      "text": "Your intuition is **100% correct**. \n\nPrompting the model with 6 different tool schemas (`exec_sqlite_fs`, `exec_isolate_codemode`, `exec_workflow`, `exec_kitesurf`, `exec_browser`, `exec_container_bash`) creates **prompt paralysis**. The LLM spends too much reasoning budget trying to decide: *\"Am I in Tier 2 or Tier 6? Do I call CodeMode or Container Bash? How do I register this CLI?\"*\n\nFoundation models (Claude 3.7, Llama 3.3, Qwen 2.5 Coder) are already pre-trained on millions of standard shell and terminal sessions. They already know how to write `grep`, `git`, `python`, `curl`, and `npm`.\n\nThe solution is the **\"Unified Terminal Façade\" (The Single-Shell Illusion)**:\n* **What the AI sees:** A clean, standard developer environment with **just 3 universal tools** (the Claude Code gold standard) [1.1.2]. It has no idea what \"Tier 1\" or \"Tier 6\" is.\n* **What Cloudflare runs under the hood:** An **invisible runtime hypervisor** that intercepts those commands and silently routes them to the cheapest, fastest tier [1.2.2, 1.2.5].\n\n---\n\n# 1. The Radical Simplification: What the AI Actually Sees\n\nYou delete all 6 tier tools from the prompt. The AI’s tool definition is reduced to **just 3 primitives** [1.1.2]:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    THE AI\u0027S MINIMALIST TOOL SURFACE                         │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1. `Bash(command)`                     │ Run terminal commands, scripts,    │\n│                                        │ CLI tools, or background jobs.     │\n├────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 2. `Read(filePath, offset?, limit?)`   │ Inspect files with line numbers.   │\n├────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 3. `Edit(filePath, oldStr, newStr)`    │ Exact AST search-and-replace.      │\n└────────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\nThat’s it. No `exec_container_bash`. No manual tier switching. No artificial friction.\n\n---\n\n# 2. How the 6 Tiers Work Invisibly Under `Bash`\n\nWhen the AI types a natural bash command, the **Cloudflare Runtime Hypervisor** inspects the command and routes it automatically [1.2.2]:\n\n```\n[ AI executes a command via `Bash({ command: \"...\" })` ]\n                           │\n                           ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                THE CLOUDFLARE RUNTIME HYPERVISOR ROUTER                     │\n└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                           │\n       ┌───────────────────┼───────────────────┬───────────────────┐\n       ▼                   ▼                   ▼                   ▼\n┌──────────────┐    ┌──────────────┐    ┌──────────────┐    ┌──────────────┐\n│ TIER 1 / 2   │    │ TIER 3       │    │ TIER 4 / 5   │    │ TIER 6       │\n│ V8 Isolate   │    │ Workflows    │    │ Browsers     │    │ Container    │\n├──────────────┤    ├──────────────┤    ├──────────────┤    ├──────────────┤\n│ • `grep`,    │    │ • `schedule` │    │ • `browse`   │    │ • `npm run   │\n│   `cat`, `ls`│    │ • `workflow` │    │ • `scrape`   │    │    build`    │\n│ • `stripe`   │    │ • `cron`     │    │ • Auto-promos│    │ • `cargo`    │\n│ • `node`     │    │   to durable │    │   to Chromium│    │ • Python ML  │\n│   scripts    │    │   background │    │   if screen- │    │ • Desktop GUI│\n│ • `git`      │    │   execution  │    │   shot needed│    │   (Xvfb)     │\n│ (\u003c5ms, $0.00)│    │ ($0/idle)    │    │ (\u003c200ms)     │    │ (Sleeps 60s) │\n└──────────────┘    └──────────────┘    └──────────────┘    └──────────────┘\n```\n\n### Trace: How the AI Uses the Ladder Without Even Knowing It Exists\n\n#### 1. Running Standard Utilities $\\rightarrow$ Routed to Tier 1/2 (`just-bash` Isolate)\n* **What the AI writes:** `Bash(\"grep -rn \u0027AUTH_SECRET\u0027 src/ | jq .\")`\n* **What happens:** The runtime executes `just-bash` and Wasm `jq` directly inside the V8 isolate against the DO SQLite filesystem.\n* **Result:** Returns in **3ms for $0.0001**. The AI thinks it ran on Linux.\n\n#### 2. Running API Commands $\\rightarrow$ Routed to Tier 2 Virtual CLI Shim\n* **What the AI writes:** `Bash(\"stripe customers list --limit 3\")`\n* **What happens:** The router intercepts the `stripe` binary, maps it to a fast HTTPS fetch with Vault credentials injected at the edge, and prints a clean ASCII table.\n* **Result:** Returns in **50ms for $0.00**. No Docker container was started.\n\n#### 3. Writing Custom Scripts (Tier 2 CodeMode) $\\rightarrow$ Routed to V8 Dynamic Worker\n* **What the AI writes:**\n  ```bash\n  cat \u003c\u003c \u0027EOF\u0027 \u003e test-payout.ts\n  import { ctx } from \"@avos/runtime\";\n  const bal \u003d await ctx.space.getWalletBalance();\n  console.log(\"Balance:\", bal);\n  EOF\n  node test-payout.ts\n  ```\n* **What happens:** The AI runs `node test-payout.ts` as it normally would. The runtime loads the TypeScript file into a **sub-millisecond Dynamic Worker Isolate**, injects `ctx`, and executes it in memory [1.2.2].\n* **Result:** Pure CodeAct execution with full access to SDK tools, without compiling inside a container.\n\n#### 4. Scheduling Background Tasks (Tier 3) $\\rightarrow$ Routed to Cloudflare Workflows\n* **What the AI writes:**\n  ```bash\n  schedule --cron \"0 9 * * 1\" --task ./workflows/weekly-report.ts\n  ```\n* **What happens:** The runtime recognizes the `schedule` CLI helper and converts it into a **Cloudflare Workflow deployment (`DynamicTaskWorkflow.ts`)** [1.2.3, 1.2.4].\n* **Result:** The task is scheduled for Monday at 9 AM; the Durable Object hibernates at **$0 compute cost** [1.2.5].\n\n#### 5. Web Browsing (Tier 4 \u0026 5) $\\rightarrow$ Routed to Kitesurf with Chromium Fallback\n* **What the AI writes:** `Bash(\"browse https://news.ycombinator.com --extract \u0027td.title\u0027\")`\n* **What happens:**\n  * The router fires **Tier 4 Kitesurf** (lightweight 30MB browser) [1.2.5].\n  * If the site requires WebGL or if the AI adds `--screenshot`, the router **auto-promotes to Tier 5 Chromium** [1.2.5].\n* **Result:** Fast DOM extraction for 80% of pages, reserving full headless browsers only for complex UI tasks [1.2.5].\n\n#### 6. Heavy Compiles (Tier 6) $\\rightarrow$ Routed to Container Sandbox\n* **What the AI writes:** `Bash(\"npm install \u0026\u0026 npm run build\")`\n* **What happens:** The router detects `npm run build` (native userland compiler). It wakes `ToolSandboxDO` via gRPC, mounts the project workspace via **`ArtifactFS` (FUSE)**, executes the build, flushes the diff, and **micro-sleeps the container after 60 seconds** [1.2.2].\n* **Result:** The build succeeds, and you pay for only 15 seconds of container compute.\n\n---\n\n# 3. How the AI Writes Its Own Custom Tools (`ctx`) Naturally\n\nInstead of teaching the AI an exotic registration syntax, rely on standard developer patterns:\n\n### Option A: The AI Writes Standard Helper Scripts\nIf the AI wants to automate something multi-step, it creates a script:\n```bash\ncat \u003c\u003c \u0027EOF\u0027 \u003e audit-docs.ts\nimport { ctx } from \"@avos/runtime\";\n\nconst files \u003d await ctx.fs.glob(\"**/*.md\");\nfor (const f of files) {\n  const content \u003d await ctx.fs.read(f);\n  if (!content.includes(\"# Summary\")) {\n    console.log(`Missing summary: ${f}`);\n  }\n}\nEOF\nnode audit-docs.ts\n```\n\n### Option B: The AI Creates a Reusable CLI Command\nIf the AI realizes it will need this tool repeatedly, it saves it into its local `$PATH` using standard Unix conventions:\n```bash\navos tool install --name audit-docs ./audit-docs.ts\n```\nFrom that moment on, the AI (or any sibling bot) can call:\n```bash\naudit-docs --fix\n```\nThe runtime automatically c