      "text": "Continuing in exact sequence with the next message files:\n* **Message File 3 (`187 - 189.txt`)**: Universal Agent Kernel (`NaelaoAgentDO`), 4-Layer Prompt Hierarchy, and Role Firewalls.\n* **Message Files 4 \u0026 5 (`190 - 192 We.txt` and `193 - 195 No.txt`)**: Unified Channel Topology (Private Executive Copilot vs. Public Customer Bots) and Project Kind Isolation.\n\nAll superseded concepts (such as the early 5-tier ceiling, static JSON tool arrays, and File 4\u0027s idea of exposing the Space Assistant\u0027s WhatsApp to public customers) have been **stripped and reconciled with the 6-tier ladder, Hermes persona bundles, and project-bound customer bots**.\n\n---\n\n# PROMPT 3: The Universal Agent Kernel, 4-Layer Prompt Hierarchy \u0026 Role Firewalls\n*(Derived from `187 - 189.txt`, reconciled with the 6-tier ladder, Hermes `SOUL.md`, and CodeAct)*\n\n```markdown\n# SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE PROMPT: UNIVERSAL AGENT KERNEL \u0026 DECLARATIVE ROLE FIREWALLS\n\nYou are architecting the universal agent execution engine (`NaelaoAgentDO`) for AVOS on Cloudflare Durable Objects.\n\nDo not write fragmented agent engines for different use cases. Maintain ONE universal execution kernel across the entire platform. Differentiate the Autonomous 24/7 CEO (Space Assistant), domain specialists (Project Dev Agents), and custom user-built bots through a declarative configuration hierarchy and hardware-enforced capability firewalls.\n\n## 1. The 4-Layer Dynamic Prompt Hierarchy\n\nTo prevent prompt drift while maintaining strict Claude Code REPL discipline, assemble the system prompt dynamically from 4 distinct, immutable layers on every turn:\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 1. UNIVERSAL OPERATING KERNEL (Immutable Engine Directives)                 │\n│    • Claude Code tool discipline: Line-numbered `Read`, exact `Edit` patches│\n│    • In-flight `compact_context` on milestones; exit-0 stdout squashing     │\n│    • Output style: Direct, technical, zero conversational fluff             │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 2. BUSINESS CONTEXT (Living Enterprise Identity)                            │\n│    • Name, active offerings, pricing plans, operational jurisdiction        │\n│    • Rendered from `SpaceDO` SQLite state: e.g., \"LexPulse Legal, $150/mo\"  │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 3. AGENT ARCHETYPE \u0026 SOUL (Persona \u0026 Mission Specification)                 │\n│    • Loaded from `/.avos/agents/:id/SOUL.md`                                │\n│    • Domain persona, assigned model, and group chat reply/pass rules        │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 4. FOUNDER CUSTOM DIRECTIVES (User-Configurable UI Overrides)              │\n│    • Live founder preferences injected from UI settings:                    │\n│      \"Always use TypeScript + Tailwind dark mode. Cite specific statutes.\"  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n## 2. Universal Agent Manifest (`packages/types/src/agent.ts`)\n\nExport the unified TypeScript manifest defining every agent entity:\n\n```typescript\nexport interface UniversalAgentManifest {\n  id: string;                      // e.g. \"space-assistant\" or \"dev-bot\"\n  name: string;                    // \"Space Assistant\" or \"Lead Edge Developer\"\n  avatar: string;                  // Custom SVG / emoji identifier\n  \n  // 1. Scoping \u0026 Workspace Boundary\n  // Space Assistant \u003d Space-wide root (`spaces/:spaceId/workspace/`)\n  // Project Agent   \u003d Project-scoped (`spaces/:spaceId/projects/:projectId/workspace/`)\n  scope: \"SPACE_WIDE\" | \"PROJECT_BOUND\";\n  projectId?: string;\n\n  // 2. Archetype Role \u0026 Security Firewall\n  role: \"SPACE_ORCHESTRATOR\" | \"DEV_OPERATOR\" | \"GROWTH_OPERATOR\" | \"CUSTOMER_SUPPORT\" | \"LEGAL_AUDITOR\" | \"CUSTOM\";\n\n  // 3. Instruction \u0026 Soul Layer\n  prompts: {\n    systemPrompt: string;            // Base technical definition\n    soulMarkdown: string;            // Persona, voice, when to reply vs pass\n    userCustomDirectives?: string;   // Founder overrides from apps/shell\n  };\n\n  // 4. Model Selection \u0026 Execution Ladder Ceiling\n  runtime: {\n    pinnedModelId: string;           // e.g. \"claude-3-7-sonnet\" or \"@cf/meta/llama-3.3-70b\"\n    maxLadderTier: 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6; // 1 (Isolate Read) to 6 (Full Container)\n    allowNativeCompilation: boolean; // Controls access to Tier 6 ToolSandboxDO\n  };\n\n  // 5. Autonomy \u0026 HITL Approval Posture\n  autonomy: {\n    approvalMode: \"always_ask\" | \"gate_unless_listed\" | \"yolo\";\n    autoApprovedActions: string[];   // Tools that run without user confirmation\n    requiresElicitationFor: string[];// Tools emitting MCP v2 Elicitation cards\n  };\n\n  // 6. Cadence \u0026 Alarms (Self-Scheduled Adaptive Wake-ups)\n  triggers: {\n    hasStandingExecutiveCron: boolean; // Daily 08:00 UTC review for Space Assistant\n    reactiveToMentions: boolean;       // Wakes on @mentions in public team channels\n    reactiveToWebhooks: boolean;       // Wakes on Stripe, WhatsApp, Git push events\n  };\n}\n```\n\n## 3. Runtime Differentiation Matrix\n\nImplement the execution routing rules inside `workers/agents/src/do/NaelaoAgentDO.ts`:\n\n| Dimension | 🏛️ Space Assistant (\"The CEO\") | ⚡ Project Specialist (\"@DevBot\") | 🛡️ Customer Support Bot |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Workspace Scope** | **Space-Wide Root** (`/workspace/`) | **Project-Bound** (`/projects/P1/`) | **Project-Bound** (`/projects/Support/`) |\n| **Trigger Cadence** | Standing daily audit (`08:00 UTC`) + webhook alerts | Reactive to `@mentions`, task DAGs, Git PR events | Reactive to incoming customer WhatsApp/webhooks |\n| **Tool Surface** | `project.create`, `wallet.balance`, `schedule`, `mcp.ca