      "text": "```markdown\n# AUTONOMOUS VENTURE \u0026 VERTICAL COWORK OPERATING SYSTEM (AVOS)\n## Master Architecture, 4-Tier Thread Model \u0026 Specialized Agent Specification\n\n---\n\n## 1. Executive Summary \u0026 Core Philosophy\n\nAVOS is a high-performance, edge-native operating system designed to run **Autonomous Businesses (1-Person Companies)** and **Vertical Cowork Studios (\"Harvey AI for X\")** natively on Cloudflare infrastructure (`@cloudflare/computer`, Durable Objects, V8 Isolates, Workflows, Artifacts, Kitesurf, Browser Rendering, and Linux Container Sandboxes).\n\n### The Operating Paradigm:\n* **No Roleplaying Chatty \"Personas\":** The platform abandons social \"chatbot personas\" in favor of **Specialized Functional Agents**—deterministic, tool-focused utility operators designed to plan, code, test, research, and execute tasks without conversational fluff.\n* **4-Tier Thread Architecture:** Human-agent collaboration is structured into four distinct execution environments (from public team rooms down to private simulation scratchpads), eliminating ghost commits and context contamination.\n* **Script-Native Execution \u0026 CodeAct:** Replaces static JSON function-calling with executable TypeScript/CodeMode running across a 6-tier execution ladder.\n* **Git-Native Versioning:** Built on **Cloudflare Artifacts (Git for Agents)** for instant micro-forking, turn rollbacks, and team Pull Request reviews.\n\n---\n\n## 2. The 4-Tier Thread \u0026 Collaboration Hierarchy\n\n```\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                    THE 4-TIER THREAD HIERARCHY                                            │\n├────────────────────┬─────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┤\n│ Tier Level         │ Audience \u0026 Visibility   │ Multi-Player Interaction   │ Workspace Write Permissions   │\n├────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Tier 1: Team**   │ **Public to Project**   │ Humans chat freely;        │ **Full Execution:**           │\n│ **Room**           │ (All team members)      │ Agents answer on `@mention`│ File edits, builds, deploys.  │\n├────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Tier 2: Task**   │ **Public to Project**   │ Focused on 1 Feature/DAG;  │ **Full Execution:**           │\n│ **Workstation**    │ (All team members)      │ Teammates + Assigned Agent │ Locks \u0026 OCC branch patches.   │\n├────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Tier 3: System** │ **Internal Background** │ Sub-agent coordination \u0026   │ **Coordination Only:**        │\n│ **Consult Lane**   │ (Collapsed/Hidden in UI)│ background task handoffs   │ Journal \u0026 state updates.      │\n├────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Tier 4: Private**│ **Strictly Private**    │ 1-on-1 between User \u0026 Agent│ **Read-Only / Simulation:**   │\n│ **Scratchpad**     │ (Only that single user) │ No `@mention` needed       │ Zero direct writes to repo.   │\n└────────────────────┴─────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Detailed Tier Mechanics:\n\n#### Tier 1: The Main Project Channel (Team Room)\n* The central room for high-level project discussion.\n* Multi-human and multi-agent. Agents **remain silent** unless explicitly addressed via `@mention` (e.g., `@DevAgent`, `@ArchitectAgent`) or when answering a `/goal` command.\n\n#### Tier 2: Task Workstations (Feature \u0026 Sprint Threads)\n* Created for specific task DAG milestones (e.g., `Thread #102: Stripe Webhook Refactor`).\n* Bound to a dedicated **Cloudflare Artifacts Git Branch** (`branch:task_102`).\n* Multiple team members can observe and review changes in real time.\n\n#### Tier 3: System Consult Lanes (Internal Multi-Agent Handoffs)\n* Hidden/collapsed background channels where the Master Architect delegates to execution agents, or where the Dev Agent passes a finished PR to the Review Agent.\n* Prevents raw multi-agent negotiation logs from cluttering the human workspace.\n\n#### Tier 4: Private 1-on-1 Scratchpads (Simulation \u0026 Personal Sandbox)\n* **Strictly Private:** Visible only to the user who created it (`created_by \u003d\u003d\u003d caller_user_id`).\n* **Read-Only / Simulation Mode:** The agent can `Read`, `Grep`, search Vectorize, run calculations, and draft proposed diffs in chat, but **direct writes to the shared project workspace are physically blocked**.\n* **The 1-Click Promotion Bridge:** When satisfied with a draft, the user clicks `[ 🚀 Promote to Team Room (Tier 1) ]` or `[ 📁 Create Task Workstation (Tier 2) ]`, creating a formal Pull Request for team review.\n* **Connector Privacy:** Personal connectors (e.g., Alice’s private Gmail) are enabled **only** in Tier 4. In public rooms, personal tools are stripped; the agent renders an inline MCP-UI card to fork the conversation into Tier 4.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Specialized Functional Agents \u0026 Capability Firewalls\n\nAgents are not chatty social personas. They are **hardened functional operators** whose tool schemas and execution ladder tiers are physically stripped at the Cloudflare Worker boundary:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                SPECIALIZED AGENT CAPABILITY MATRIX                                      │\n├──────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Functional Agent Role    │ Max Execution Ladder Tier  │ Authorized Toolset \u0026 Permissions                │\n├──────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **1. Master Architect**  │ **Tier 2 (Isolates Only)** │ `Todo`, `sub_agent.spawn`, `project_journal`,   │\n│    (`ARCHITECT_DELEGATE`)│ *(Zero direct code edits)* │ `workflow.schedule` (Emits structured DAG plans)│\n├──────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **2. Dev Operator**      │ **Tier 6 (Full Container)**│ `Edit` (AST Patch), `Read`, `Write`, `Grep`,    │\n│    (`DEV_OPERATOR`)      │                            │ `Glob`, `Bash`, `ArtifactFS`, `npm`, `cargo`    │\n├──────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **3. Growth Operator**   │ **Tier 4 (Kitesurf/Browser)│ `browser.kitesurf`, `web-search`, `resend`,     │\n│    (`GROWTH_OPERATOR`)   │ *(Tier 6 Container Blocked)│ `artifacts`, `VectorizeQuery`                   │\n├──────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **4. Customer Support**  │ **Tier 1 (DO Memory Only)**│ `knowledge.search`, `create_ticket`,            │\n│    (`CUSTOMER_SUPPORT`)  │ *(Tiers 2–6 Blocked)*      │ `calendar.check`, `calendar.book`               │\n├──────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **5. Voice Receptionist**│ **Tier 1 (Safe RAG Only)** │ `@cloudflare/voice`, `calendar.book`,           │\n│    (`VOICE_OPERATOR`)    │                            │ `transfer_call`, `knowledge.search`             │\n├──────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **6. Model Researcher**  │ **Tier 6 (Container/GPU)** │ `synthetic_data.generate`, `lora.train`,        │\n│    (`MODEL_RESEARCHER`)  │                            │ `benchmark.eval`, `model.register`              │\n└──────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. The 6-Tier Cloudflare Execution Ladder\n\nThe Execution Ladder dynamically routes every task to the cheapest, fastest compute primitive, with the **V8 Isolate acting as the primary Conductor**:\n\n```\n                                  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │ TIER 6: Sandboxed Linux Container (ToolSandboxDO / Ubuntu)  │\n                                  │ • Full OS userland: npm install, compilers, Python binaries │\n                                  └──────────────────────────────▲──────────────────────────────┘\n                                                                 │ (Promote if native compilation needed)\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │ TIER 5: Full Headless Chromium (Puppeteer / Browser Render) │\n                                  │ • Heavy browser: Visual QA snapshots, WebGL, Canvas, Bot-Def│\n                                  └──────────────────────────────▲──────────────────────────────┘\n                                                                 │ (Promote if visual QA / WebGL needed)\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │ TIER 4: Lightweight Agent Browser (Cloudflare Kitesurf)     │\n                                  │ • 3–7x cheaper/faster: DOM text extraction \u0026 form fills     │\n                                  └──────────────────────────────▲──────────────────────────────┘\n                                                                 │ (Promote if web navigation needed)\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │ TIER 3: Dynamic Workflows (Cloudflare Workflows / Cron Hub) │\n                                  │ • Durable multi-step runs, hours/days execution, sleep/pause│\n                                  │ • Step retry boundaries, scheduled crons without awake DOs │\n                                  └──────────────────────────────▲──────────────────────────────┘\n                                                                 │ (Promote if task is long-running/durable)\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │ TIER 2: Dynamic Worker Loader (V8 Isolate Shell / TS Script)│\n                                  │ • Pure code execution, HTTP fetches, MCP orchestration      │\n                                  └──────────────────────────────▲──────────────────────────────┘\n                                                                 │ (Promote if script logic needed)\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┐\n│ TIER 1: Direct In-Memory Virtual FS (@cloudflare/computer / DO SQLite)                        │\n│ • Sub-millisecond Read, Edit (AST Search \u0026 Replace), Grep, Glob, just-bash                    │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Script-Native CodeAct \u0026 Just-In-Time (JIT) Virtual CLI Synthesis\n\n### The CodeAct Action Space:\nInstead of loading dozens of static JSON tool schemas into every prompt, agents communicate via **6 Tier-Specific Universal Primitives** (`exec_sqlite_fs`, `exec_isolate_codemode`, `exec_workflow`, `exec_kitesurf`, `exec_browser`, `exec_container_bash`).\n\n### Dynamic JIT Virtual CLI Synthesis:\nWhen an agent attempts to run a terminal command for an external service (e.g. `shopify products list`, `linear issues create`, `stripe customers list`):\n1. **Interception:** The Tier 1/2 V8 Isolate router detects the command.\n2. **JIT Synthesis:** The agent writes a lightweight 12-line TypeScript parser implementing **only the requested subcommand** using `ctx.vault.fetchWithAuth`.\n3. **Persistence:** Registered into `virtual_cli_commands` in SQLite.\n4. **Execution:** Runs in **sub-5ms in a V8 isolate for $0.0001**, avoiding slow container boot-ups.\n5. **Zero-Leak Security:** Outbound HTTP requests route through **Outbound Workers \u0026 WriteGuard**, injecting credentials at the edge network boundary without exposing secrets to scripts or logs.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Cloudflare Artifacts (Git for Agents) \u0026 The PR Engine\n\nEvery project is backed by a native **Cloudflare Artifacts Git Repository (Zig-to-WASM Git in Durable Objects)**:\n\n* **Instant Zero-Copy Forking:** Creating a Tier 4 Private Scratchpad or spawning a subagent forks the repository in **10ms**.\n* **ArtifactFS FUSE Mounting:** Tier 6 Linux Containers mount `/workspace` lazily over FUSE, eliminating 90-second `git clone` delays.\n* **Inline Pull Request Cards:** Merges from branches to `main` render interactive review cards in the Tier 1 Team Room with visual AST diffs, author attribution, and one-click merge buttons.\n* **Upstream Staleness Tracking:** Scratchpads display real-time badges (`3 commits behind main`). Agents autonomously evaluate upstream diffs and rebase non-conflicting files.\n* **Turn-by-Turn Time Machine:** Every tool turn creates a Git commit, allowing 1-click workspace rollbacks from the thread timeline.\n\n---\n\n## 7. 3-Layer Hybrid Memory \u0026 Mini-AGI Scoped Knowledge\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ LAYER 1: WORKING MEMORY (Short-Term / Active Turn)                          │\n│ • Active turn buffer + Task DAG in Durable Object RAM.                      │\n│ • In-flight self-compaction (`compact_context`) + surgical payload eviction.│\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ LAYER 2: DETERMINISTIC PROJECT MEMORY (Mid-Term / Workspace Truth)          │\n│ • Autonomic `PROJECT.md` living in root of SQLite virtual filesystem.       │\n│ • Technical guidelines, schema contracts, and styling rules.                │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ LAYER 3: EPISODIC \u0026 SEMANTIC MEMORY (Long-Term / Cross-Thread Intelligence) │\n│ • Cloudflare Vectorize + D1 relational fact store.                          │\n│ • Background Workers AI hook extracts learned rules after completed runs.   │\n│ • Scoped ACLs: Space-Wide vs. Project-Scoped vs. Member Role Rank.          │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Marketplace, Business Blueprints \u0026 Monetization\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                  THE TWO-TIER DEVELOPER MARKETPLACE                                     │\n├───────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Product Type                  │ Pricing \u0026 Royalty Model               │ Feature Gating Rule             │\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **1. Tiered SaaS Templates**  │ **$0.00 Upfront (Free to Install)**   │ ✅ **Granular Feature Gating:** │\n│    *(e.g., LexPulse Legal,    │ • Developer Referral: **40% cut**     │ Features unlock as customer     │\n│     Miami Dental Voice Desk)* │ • Marketplace Organic: **20% cut**    │ upgrades ($20 ➔ $50 ➔ $150/mo)  │\n│                               │ • Lifetime on $150+; 6–12 mo on lower │                                 │\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **2. Fixed One-Off Licenses** │ **$49 – $499 One-Time Buy-Out**       │ ❌ **Zero Feature Gating:**     │\n│    *(e.g., Standalone Plugins │ • Developer receives **100% upfront** │ 100% of template features must  │\n│     or Code Packages)*        │ • Platform keeps 100% of monthly base │ be fully unlocked permanently.  │\n└───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Cumulative Plan Cycle Quota Protection:\n* On low-margin **$20/mo plans**, developer commission is paid for **6 cumulative cycles max** (preventing platform margin erosion).\n* On **$50/mo plans**, commission is paid for **12 cumulative cycles max**.\n* On **$150+/mo Pro plans**, commission is paid for **unlimited lifetime cycles**.\n* If a customer downgrades and upgrades over time, the system tracks cumulative counts per tier without being gamed.\n\n### Discover Page Live Market Radar:\nThe Discover page features the **Top 5 Market Opportunities of the Week** computed by **Cloudflare Radar Researcher** and **Pipelines/Iceberg streaming telemetry**, allowing founders to launch trending businesses with 1 click.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Enterprise Air-Gapped Local AI Engine\n\nFor defense, legal, and healthcare organizations with strict compliance requirements:\n* Companies run open weights (DeepSeek R1, Llama 3.3, Qwen 2.5 Coder) locally on **Ollama / vLLM** across on-premise GPUs.\n* Connects to Cloudflare edge workspaces via **`LocalTunnelDO`** over an encrypted outbound WebSocket.\n* **Air-Gapped Space Lock:** When enabled, all external cloud AI endpoints are disabled; 100% of prompts execute locally on the company\u0027s private GPU hardware with zero data egress.\n```",
