      "text": "This is an exceptionally strong, production-grade synthesis. It strips away the skeuomorphic \"chatty coworker\" trap and grounds AVOS as a high-performance, outcome-driven, edge-native operating system.\n\nHowever, an audit of this document against our previous breakthroughs reveals **one critical lingering contradiction in Section 5**, plus **three high-impact omissions** that need to be patched before handing this to an engineering team.\n\n---\n\n### The Critical Bug in Section 5: The \"6-Tool Prompt Paralysis\" Contradiction\n\nLook closely at **Section 5**:\n\u003e *\"Instead of loading dozens of static JSON tool schemas into every prompt, agents communicate via **6 Tier-Specific Universal Primitives** (`exec_sqlite_fs`, `exec_isolate_codemode`, `exec_workflow`, `exec_kitesurf`, `exec_browser`, `exec_container_bash`).\"*\n\n**Why this contradicts your architecture:**\nIn our earlier breakthrough, we proved that putting 6 different execution tools into the LLM\u0027s context window causes **prompt paralysis and cognitive drift**. The model has to spend reasoning tokens deciding: *\"Should I call `exec_isolate_codemode` or `exec_container_bash`? Is this a Tier 1 or Tier 2 task?\"*\n\n**The Fix:**\nThe 6 Tiers belong to the **invisible Cloudflare Runtime Hypervisor**, **NOT the AI\u0027s prompt tool definition**. \nThe AI should only see **3 Hands Primitives** (`Bash`, `Read`, `Edit`) + **2 Senses Primitives** (`Browser`, `Delegate`). When the AI runs `Bash(\"stripe customers list\")` or `Bash(\"npm run build\")`, the runtime hypervisor silently routes it to Tier 2 (Virtual CLI) or Tier 6 (Container) without the model ever having to think about tiers.\n\n---\n\n### The 3 High-Impact Omissions to Include\n\n1. **Repository Cleanliness (`/workspace` vs. `/.avos/` Namespace):**  \n   Without this explicit rule, internal agent scripts, memory files, and scratchpad drafts will pollute the user\u0027s Git repository. Project code belongs in `/workspace`, while agent meta-state belongs in `/.avos/`.\n2. **Cohere Parse 5 (`parse-v5.0`) Ingestion Layer:**  \n   The document mentions Vertical Cowork (\"Harvey AI for X\"), but leaves out the edge VLM ingestion pipeline that makes non-standard leases, medical faxes, and financial tables readable without OCR hallucinations.\n3. **The 7 Formal Project Kinds Mapping:**  \n   The document lists agent roles, but needs the explicit directory mapping them to the 7 foundational Project Kinds (`product_dev`, `doc_studio`, `voice_agent`, `customer_bot`, `model_studio`, `growth_engine`, `app_studio`).\n\n---\n\n# THE PATCHED \u0026 COMPLETE MASTER SPECIFICATION\n\nHere is the fully reconciled, contradiction-free specification with all sections harmonized:\n\n```markdown\n# AUTONOMOUS VENTURE \u0026 VERTICAL COWORK OPERATING SYSTEM (AVOS)\n## Master Architecture, 4-Tier Thread Model \u0026 Specialized Agent Specification\n\n---\n\n## 1. Executive Summary \u0026 Core Philosophy\n\nAVOS is a high-performance, edge-native operating system designed to run **Autonomous Businesses (1-Person Companies)** and **Vertical Cowork Studios (\"Harvey AI for X\")** natively on Cloudflare infrastructure (`@cloudflare/computer`, Durable Objects, V8 Isolates, Workflows, Artifacts, Kitesurf, Browser Rendering, and Linux Container Sandboxes).\n\n### The Operating Paradigm:\n* **Outcome-First, Not Persona-First:** Eliminates conversational \"social chatbot personas\" in favor of **Specialized Functional Agents**—deterministic, tool-focused utility operators designed to plan, code, test, research, and execute tasks without conversational fluff.\n* **4-Tier Thread Architecture:** Human-agent collaboration is structured into four distinct execution environments (from public team rooms down to private simulation scratchpads), eliminating ghost commits and context contamination.\n* **Minimalist Tool Interface with Invisible 6-Tier Routing:** The AI interacts through a minimalist 3-tool developer surface (`Bash`, `Read`, `Edit`), while an invisible Cloudflare edge hypervisor dynamically routes execution across a 6-tier compute ladder.\n* **Git-Native Versioning:** Built on **Cloudflare Artifacts (Git for Agents)** for instant 10ms micro-forking, turn rollbacks, and team Pull Request reviews.\n\n---\n\n## 2. The 4-Tier Thread \u0026 Collaboration Hierarchy\n\n```\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                    THE 4-TIER THREAD HIERARCHY                                            │\n├────────────────────┬─────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┤\n│ Tier Level         │ Audience \u0026 Visibility   │ Multi-Player Interaction   │ Workspace Write Permissions   │\n├────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Tier 1: Team**   │ **Public to Project**   │ Humans chat freely;        │ **Branch / PR Only:**         │\n│ **Room**           │ (All team members)      │ Agents answer on `@mention`│ Writes committed via Git PRs. │\n├────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Tier 2: Task**   │ **Public to Project**   │ Focused on 1 Feature/DAG;  │ **OCC Patches on Branch:**    │\n│ **Workstation**    │ (All team members)      │ Teammates + Assigned Agent │ Hash-checked branch commits.  │\n├────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Tier 3: System** │ **Internal Background** │ Sub-agent coordination \u0026   │ **Coordination Only:**        │\n│ **Consult Lane**   │ (Collapsed/Hidden in UI)│ background task handoffs   │ Journal \u0026 state updates.      │\n├────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Tier 4: Private**│ **Strictly Private**    │ 1-on-1 between User \u0026 Agent│ **Read-Only / Simulation:**   │\n│ **Scratchpad**     │ (Only that single user) │ No `@mention` needed       │ Zero direct writes to repo.   │\n└────────────────────┴─────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Detailed Tier Mechanics:\n\n#### Tier 1: The Main Project Channel (Team Room)\n* The central room for high-level project discussion.\n* Multi-human and multi-agent. Agents **remain silent** unless explicitly addressed via `@mention` (e.g., `@DevAgent`, `@ArchitectAgent`) or when answering a `/goal` command.\n* Changes land in `main` only via approved Pull Request cards.\n\n#### Tier 2: Task Workstations (Feature \u0026 Sprint Threads)\n* Created for specific task DAG milestones (e.g., `Thread #102: Stripe Webhook Refactor`).\n* Bound to a dedicated **Cloudflare Artifacts Git Branch** (`branch:task_102`).\n* Multiple team members can observe and review changes in real time.\n\n#### Tier 3: System Consult Lanes (Internal Multi-Agent Handoffs)\n* Hidden/collapsed background channels where the Master Architect delegates to execution agents, or where the Dev Agent passes a finished PR to the Review Agent.\n* Prevents raw multi-agent negotiation logs from cluttering the human workspace.\n\n#### Tier 4: Private 1-on-1 Scratchpads (Simulation \u0026 Personal Sandbox)\n* **Strictly Private:** Visible only to the user who created it (`created_by \u003d\u003d\u003d caller_user_id`).\n* **Read-Only / Simulation Mode:** The agent can `Read`, `Grep`, search Vectorize, run calculations, and draft proposed diffs, but **direct writes to the shared project workspace are blocked**.\n* **The Promotion Bridge:** The user clicks `[ 🚀 Promote to Team Room ]` or `[ 📁 Create Task Workstation ]`, converting the draft into an isolated Git branch and formal Pull Request card.\n* **Privacy \u0026 Credentials:** Personal connectors (e.g., Alice’s private Gmail) are enabled **only** in Tier 4. In public channels, personal tools are physically stripped; the agent renders an inline MCP-UI card to fork the conversation into Tier 4.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Specialized Functional Agents \u0026 Capability Firewalls\n\nAgents are not chatty social personas. They are **hardened functional operators** whose tool schemas and execution ladder ceilings are physically enforced at the Cloudflare Worker boundary:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                SPECIALIZED AGENT CAPABILITY MATRIX                                      │\n├──────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Functional Agent Role    │ Max Ladder Ceiling         │ Authorized Toolset \u0026 Permissions                │\n├──────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **1. Master Architect**  │ **Tier 2 (Isolates Only)** │ `Delegate`, `Read`, `Grep`, `project_journal`,  │\n│    (`ARCHITECT_DELEGATE`)│ *(Zero direct code edits)* │ `schedule` (Emits structured Task DAG plans)    │\n├──────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **2. Dev Operator**      │ **Tier 6 (Full Container)**│ `Bash`, `Edit`, `Read`, `Grep`, `Glob`,         │\n│    (`DEV_OPERATOR`)      │                            │ `ArtifactFS`, `npm`, `cargo`, `git`             │\n├──────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **3. Growth Operator**   │ **Tier 4 (Kitesurf)**      │ `Browser`, `Bash` (Virtual CLIs), `resend`,     │\n│    (`GROWTH_OPERATOR`)   │ *(Tier 6 Container Blocked)│ `VectorizeQuery`, `web-search`                  │\n├──────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **4. Customer Support**  │ **Tier 1 (Safe RAG Only)** │ `knowledge.search`, `create_ticket`,            │\n│    (`CUSTOMER_SUPPORT`)  │ *(Tiers 2–6 Blocked)*      │ `calendar.check`, `calendar.book`               │\n├──────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **5. Voice Receptionist**│ **Tier 1 (Safe RAG Only)** │ `@cloudflare/voice`, `calendar.book`,           │\n│    (`VOICE_OPERATOR`)    │                            │ `transfer_call`, `knowledge.search`             │\n├──────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **6. Model Researcher**  │ **Tier 6 (Container/GPU)** │ `synthetic_data.generate`, `lora.train`,        │\n│    (`MODEL_RESEARCHER`)  │                            │ `benchmark.eval`, `model.register`              │\n└──────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. The 6-Tier Cloudflare Execution Ladder (The Invisible Hypervisor)\n\nThe Execution Ladder dynamically routes every task to the cheapest, fastest compute primitive, with the **V8 Isolate acting as the Conductor**:\n\n```\n                                  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │ TIER 6: Sandboxed Linux Container (ToolSandboxDO / Ubuntu)  │\n                                  │ • Full OS userland: npm install, compilers, Python binaries │\n                                  │ • Visual Desktop GUI via Xvfb + noVNC WebSockets (8081)     │\n                                  └──────────────────────────────▲──────────────────────────────┘\n                                                                 │ (Promote if native compilation/GUI needed)\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │ TIER 5: Full Headless Chromium (Puppeteer / Browser Render) │\n                                  │ • Heavy browser: Visual QA snapshots, WebGL, Canvas, Bot-Def│\n                                  └──────────────────────────────▲──────────────────────────────┘\n                                                                 │ (Promote if visual QA / WebGL needed)\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │ TIER 4: Lightweight Agent Browser (Cloudflare Kitesurf)     │\n                                  │ • 3–7x cheaper/faster: DOM text extraction \u0026 form fills     │\n                                  └──────────────────────────────▲──────────────────────────────┘\n                                                                 │ (Promote if web navigation needed)\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │ TIER 3: Dynamic Workflows (Cloudflare Workflows / Cron Hub) │\n                                  │ • Durable multi-step runs, hours/days execution, sleep/pause│\n                                  │ • Step retry boundaries, scheduled crons ($0/idle compute)  │\n                                  └──────────────────────────────▲──────────────────────────────┘\n                                                                 │ (Promote if task is long-running/durable)\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │ TIER 2: Dynamic Worker Loader (V8 Isolate Shell / TS Script)│\n                                  │ • Pure code execution, HTTP fetches, MCP orchestration      │\n                                  │ • In-memory Pyodide Wasm Python (Sub-10ms, $0.00 cost)      │\n                                  └──────────────────────────────▲──────────────────────────────┘\n                                                                 │ (Promote if script logic needed)\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┐\n│ TIER 1: Direct In-Memory Virtual FS (@cloudflare/computer / DO SQLite)                        │\n│ • Sub-millisecond Read, Edit (AST Search \u0026 Replace), Grep, Glob, just-bash                    │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Minimalist AI Action Space \u0026 JIT Virtual CLI Synthesis\n\n### The Minimalist Tool Surface (What the AI Sees)\nTo eliminate prompt paralysis, the agent receives only **3 Hands Primitives** and **2 Senses Primitives**:\n1. **`Bash(command)`**: Execute shell commands, Virtual CLIs, scripts, and build tools.\n2. **`Read(filePath, offset?, limit?)`**: Windowed file reading with line numbers.\n3. **`Edit(filePath, oldString, newString)`**: Surgical AST search-and-replace patching.\n4. **`Browser(action, url, selector?)`**: Returns multimodal visual screenshots and clean accessibility DOM trees directly into the LLM context.\n5. **`Delegate(agentId, taskPayload)`**: Typed JSON-RPC communication between agents (Tier 3).\n\n### The Runtime Hypervisor \u0026 JIT Virtual CLI Synthesis\nWhen the agent executes a command via `Bash`:\n1. **POSIX Text Operations:** `grep`, `cat`, `sed`, `jq` execute natively in Tier 1/2 V8 Isolates via `just-bash` (\u003c5ms, $0.0001).\n2. **External API CLIs:** Commands like `stripe`, `gh`, `r2` are intercepted by **Virtual CLI Shims**. Outbound Workers inject credentials at the edge network boundary.\n3. **JIT Tool Synthesis:** When an agent runs an unregistered command (e.g., `shopify products list`):\n   - The router detects the missing binary and verifies vault credentials.\n   - The agent micro-synthesizes a 15-line parser using `ctx.cli.register` and `ctx.vault.fetchWithAuth`.\n   - Saved into `virtual_cli_commands` in SQLite. Future calls execute in V8 Isolates in 4ms forever.\n4. **Native Compilations:** Commands requiring native Linux userland (`npm run build`, `cargo`, `python3 -m torch`) escalate to Tier 6 via gRPC. The container boots over **ArtifactFS (FUSE)** in 200ms and **micro-sleeps after 60 seconds of inactivity**.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Workspace Layout \u0026 Repository Cleanliness\n\nTo prevent internal bot state from polluting the user\u0027s codebase:\n\n```\n/workspace/                       \u003c-- USER PROJECT CODEBASE (Tracked by Git)\n├── src/                          (Application code, components, styles)\n├── package.json\n└── astro.config.mjs\n\n/.avos/                           \u003c-- AGENT PLATFORM STATE (Git-Ignored / Internal)\n├── shared/                       (Reusable tools shared across all agents)\n│   ├── skills/                   (e.g., csv-parser.ts, delaware-linter.ts)\n│   └── workflows/                (Standing project workflow definitions)\n│\n└── agents/                       (Isolated Functional Agent States)\n    ├── dev-operator/\n    │   ├── SOUL.md               (Agent instructions, boundaries, role)\n    │   └── memory.json           (Private hindsight memory index)\n    │\n    └── growth-operator/\n        └── SOUL.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Cloudflare Artifacts (Git for Agents) \u0026 The PR Engine\n\nEvery project is backed by a native **Cloudflare Artifacts Git Repository (Zig-to-WASM Git in Durable Objects)**:\n\n* **Instant Zero-Copy Forking:** Creating a Tier 4 Private Scratchpad or spawning a subagent forks the repository in **10ms**.\n* **ArtifactFS FUSE Mounting:** Tier 6 Linux Containers mount `/workspace` lazily over FUSE, eliminating 90-second `git clone` delays.\n* **Inline Pull Request Cards:** Merges from branches to `main` render interactive review cards in the Tier 1 Team Room with visual AST diffs, author attribution, and one-click merge buttons.\n* **Upstream Staleness Tracking:** Scratchpads display real-time badges (`3 commits behind main`). Agents autonomously evaluate upstream diffs and rebase non-conflicting files.\n* **Turn-by-Turn Time Machine:** Every tool turn creates a Git commit, allowing 1-click workspace rollbacks from the thread timeline.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Enterprise Ingestion, Mini-AGI \u0026 Scoped Knowledge\n\n### Cohere Parse 5 (`parse-v5.0`) Ingestion Layer\nAll vertical cowork spaces process incoming documents through Cohere Parse 5 (2.3B Vision-Language Model) at the edge (`workers/knowledge/src/parse5Ingestion.ts`). Converts complex multi-column leases, hospital faxes, police crash reports, and financial tables into pristine Markdown prior to Vectorize indexing.\n\n### Mini-AGI Vector Access Control (Hardware-Level Pre-Filtering)\n```\nQuery Vector q ──► [ Cloudflare Vectorize Index Engine ]\n                          │\n                          ▼ (Pre-Filtering Evaluation)\n         WHERE space_id \u003d \"space_102\"\n         AND (project_id \u003d \"\" OR project_id \u003d \"proj_active\")\n         AND min_role_rank \u003c\u003d User.RoleRank (Viewer:1 -\u003e Owner:5)\n         AND (scope !\u003d \"USER_PRIVATE\" OR owner_user_id \u003d User.Id)\n                          │\n                          ▼\n             [ Returned Context Chunks ]\n                          │\n                          ▼ (Wrap in Untrusted Boundary Envelopes)\n    \u003ccontext_chunk id\u003d\"...\" access\u003d\"verified\"\u003e\n      Escaped Raw Document Text\n    \u003c/context_chunk\u003e\n```\n* Context is wrapped in `\u003ccontext_chunk\u003e` semantic envelopes, signaling to model attention layers that dynamic content cannot override operational instructions.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Marketplace, Blueprints \u0026 Monetization\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                  THE TWO-TIER DEVELOPER MARKETPLACE                                     │\n├───────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Product Type                  │ Pricing \u0026 Royalty Model               │ Feature Gating Rule             │\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **1. Tiered SaaS Templates**  │ **$0.00 Upfront (Free to Install)**   │ ✅ **Granular Feature Gating:** │\n│    *(e.g., LexPulse Legal,    │ • Developer Referral: **40% cut**     │ Features unlock as customer     │\n│     Miami Dental Voice Desk)* │ • Marketplace Organic: **20% cut**    │ upgrades ($20 ➔ $50 ➔ $150/mo)  │\n│                               │ • Lifetime on $150+; 6–12 mo on lower │                                 │\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **2. Fixed One-Off Licenses** │ **$49 – $499 One-Time Buy-Out**       │ ❌ **Zero Feature Gating:**     │\n│    *(e.g., Standalone Plugins │ • Developer receives **100% upfront** │ 100% of template features must  │\n│     or Code Packages)*        │ • Platform keeps 100% of monthly base │ be fully unlocked permanently.  │\n└───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Cumulative Plan Cycle Quota Protection:\n* **$20/mo Entry Tier:** Developer receives commission for **maximum 6 paid cycles ($48 total bounty)**. Drops to 0% thereafter (Platform captures 100%).\n* **$50/mo Growth Tier:** Developer receives commission for **maximum 12 paid cycles ($240 total bounty)**. Drops to 0% thereafter.\n* **$150+/mo Pro Tier:** **Lifetime recurring commission** for the duration of the client.\n* **Anti-Gaming Ledger:** Cumulative counters in D1 (`cycles_paid_entry_tier`, etc.) track usage across plan downgrades and upgrades.\n\n### The 95/5 Compute Arbitrage:\n* 95% of tasks execute in Tier 1/2 Isolates for $0.0001. Containers run for only ~15 min/day active CPU before micro-sleeping.\n* Enables $29/mo Starter Plans to provide unconstrained performance while maintaining **92.7% gross margins**.\n\n---\n\n## 10. The 7 Foundational Project Kinds\n\nEvery project manifests one of 7 standardized kinds:\n1. `product_dev`: Full-stack engineering canvas (`CodeWorkspaceCanvas`), T1–T6, Node/Linux container, finite lifecycle.\n2. `doc_studio`: Document Redline Studio (`DocumentRedlineCanvas`), T1–T2, Parse 5 ingestion, Delaware/HIPAA linters, finite lifecycle.\n3. `voice_agent`: 24/7 AI phone desk (`VoiceAgentCanvas`), T1–T2, `@cloudflare/voice` (WebRTC), continuous lifecycle.\n4. `customer_bot`: Inbound support messaging desk (`SupportTicketsCanvas`), T1 safe RAG only, continuous lifecycle.\n5. `model_studio`: Enterprise LoRA training studio (`ModelStudioCanvas`), T1, T2, T6, Workers AI LoRA dynamic adapters, finite lifecycle.\n6. `growth_engine`: Autonomous lead scraper (`GrowthFunnelCanvas`), T1–T5 (Kitesurf/Chromium), continuous lifecycle.\n7. `app_studio`: On-demand micro-app synthesis (`AppStudioCanvas`), T1–T2, DO Facet SQLite DBs, MCP-UI streaming, finite lifecycle.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Enterprise Air-Gapped Local AI Engine\n\n* Connects on-premise GPU clusters running **Ollama / vLLM** (DeepSeek R1, Llama 3.3, Qwen 2.5 Coder) via **`LocalTunnelDO`** over encrypted outbound WebSockets.\n* **Air-Gapped Space Lock:** When enabled, all external cloud AI endpoints are disabled at the router level; 100% of prompts execute on local hardware with zero data egress.\n```",
