      "text": "# AUTONOMOUS VENTURE \u0026 VERTICAL COWORK OPERATING SYSTEM (AVOS)\n## Definitive Master Architecture \u0026 Technical Specification\n\n---\n\n## 1. System Vision \u0026 Core Operating Philosophy\n\nAVOS is an edge-native, distributed operating system built entirely on Cloudflare\u0027s serverless primitives (`@cloudflare/computer`, Durable Objects, V8 Isolates, Workflows, Cloudflare Artifacts, Kitesurf, Browser Rendering, and Linux Container Sandboxes). It runs two complementary business models on a unified codebase:\n1. **Mode A: Autonomous Ventures (\"The 24/7 AI Operator\"):** Proactive, cron-driven, self-funding digital companies operated by autonomous agents that generate code, deploy web applications, run B2B lead scrapers, triage inbound WhatsApp leads, and process payments.\n2. **Mode B: Vertical Cowork Studios (\"Harvey AI for X\"):** Assistive, human-in-the-loop, domain-specific workspaces designed for regulated professional verticals (law, finance, healthcare, civil engineering) featuring side-by-side document redlining, live financial grids, and audit-ready citation graphs.\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                       AVOS OPERATING PARADIGM                                          │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1. OUTCOME-FIRST, NOT PERSONA-FIRST                                                                    │\n│    The platform abandons roleplaying \"chatbot personas\" talking in circles. Agents are functional,     │\n│    deterministic utility operators and background services evaluated strictly by outputs.             │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 2. THE CANVAS IS KING (NOT CHAT)                                                                       │\n│    Chat is an auxiliary drawer. The center of gravity is the Viewport: live web previews, legal diff   │\n│    canvases, spreadsheet grids, and stateful micro-apps.                                               │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 3. MINIMALIST AI INTERFACE, INVISIBLE RUNTIME HYPERVISOR                                               │\n│    The model is never confused with 6 separate tier tools. The AI receives 3 universal execution       │\n│    primitives (`Bash`, `Read`, `Edit`) and 2 sensory primitives (`Browser`, `Delegate`).               │\n│    A Cloudflare runtime hypervisor silently routes commands to the optimal compute tier.               │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 4. GIT-NATIVE ARTIFACTS \u0026 TASK DAGS                                                                    │\n│    All workspace state is version-controlled via Cloudflare Artifacts (Zig-to-WASM Git in DOs).        │\n│    Work is structured as Directed Acyclic Graphs (DAGs) in the Project Journal; changes land via PRs.  │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Enterprise Organization Hierarchy \u0026 Department Sub-Spaces\n\nAVOS structures mid-market and enterprise organizations into a strict two-level depth hierarchy: **Parent Company Space (Root Depth 0)** managing multiple departmental **Sub-Spaces** (e.g., Legal, Product Engineering, Customer Operations).\n\n```\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │     PARENT COMPANY SPACE (Root Depth 0)      │\n                                  │   Master Corporate Billing • Global Brand    │\n                                  │   Company Handbook Master Knowledge Vault    │\n                                  └──────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘\n                                                         │\n                         ┌───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┐\n                         ▼                               ▼                               ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────┐   ┌──────────────────────────────────┐   ┌──────────────────────────────────┐\n│ SUB-SPACE 1: Legal Department    │   │ SUB-SPACE 2: Product Engineering │   │ SUB-SPACE 3: Customer Operations │\n│ • Kind: `doc_studio` (Cowork)    │   │ • Kind: `product_dev` (Dev)      │   │ • Kind: `customer_bot` (Support) │\n│ • Clearance: M\u0026A / NDAs / Deeds  │   │ • Clearance: Source Code / APIs  │   │ • Clearance: Public FAQs / CRM   │\n│ • Local Spend Cap: $500 / mo     │   │ • Local Spend Cap: $2,000 / mo   │   │ • Local Spend Cap: $200 / mo     │\n└──────────────────────────────────┘   └──────────────────────────────────┘   └──────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Access \u0026 Permission Inheritance Matrix\n* **Downward Oversight (Parent Admin $\\rightarrow$ Sub-Spaces):** Parent space Owners and Admins hold full inherited visibility and management over all child department spaces.\n* **Strict Upward Isolation (Sub-Space Member $\\rightarrow$ Parent Space):** A member of a department sub-space cannot view parent financial ledgers, company-wide balance sheets, or sibling department files unless explicitly granted a row in `space_members`.\n* **Zero Lateral Access (Sibling Sub-Space A $\\leftrightarrow$ Sibling Sub-Space B):** Sibling spaces are air-gapped by default. Product Engineering cannot see Legal files. Cross-department interoperability is governed strictly via **Gatekeeper Capability Grants**.\n\n### Settings Inheritance Rules\n* **Cascading Defaults:** Master billing account, company-wide compliance rules, brand kits, and universal employee policies cascade down automatically into all sub-spaces.\n* **Local Sub-Space Overrides:** Departmental template type, local monthly token/compute spend caps, workspace viewports, and communication channels (e.g., Legal\u0027s private Telegram vs. Engineering\u0027s Slack) are managed locally.\n\n### Cross-Subspace Delegation (The Gatekeeper Capability Bridge)\nWhen a user in Department A provisions a stateful tool (e.g., an internal *QA Bug Matrix Gadget* in the PM Subspace) that Department B must use:\n1. The platform mints an attenuated **Gatekeeper Capability Grant**:\n   `grant \u003d { target: \"gadget_bug_matrix_102\", allowed_ops: [\"insert_ticket\", \"read_assigned\"], expires_at: 1774900000 }`\n2. The gadget mounts dynamically in Department B’s workspace.\n3. When developers in Department B interact with the gadget, requests route across the Cloudflare edge directly into Department A\u0027s private Durable Object SQLite database. Developers cannot view Department A\u0027s confidential roadmap files or workspace files.\n\n---\n\n## 3. The 4-Tier Thread Collaboration \u0026 Concurrency Engine\n\nAVOS eliminates flat chat clutter and race conditions by structuring all project interaction into a **4-Tier Thread Hierarchy**:\n\n```\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                    THE 4-TIER THREAD HIERARCHY                                            │\n├────────────────────┬─────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┤\n│ Tier Level         │ Audience \u0026 Visibility   │ Multi-Player Interaction   │ Workspace Write Permissions   │\n├────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Tier 1: Team**   │ **Public to Project**   │ Humans chat freely;        │ **Branch / PR Only:**         │\n│ **Room**           │ (All team members)      │ Agents answer on `@mention`│ Direct writes blocked; writes │\n│                    │                         │ or `/goal` commands.       │ merge via Pull Request cards. │\n├────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Tier 2: Task**   │ **Public to Project**   │ Focused on 1 Feature / DAG │ **OCC Patches on Branch:**    │\n│ **Workstation**    │ (All team members)      │ Milestone; teammates +     │ Hash-verified writes scoped   │\n│                    │                         │ assigned functional agents.│ to dedicated Git branch ref.  │\n├────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Tier 3: System** │ **Internal Background** │ Sub-agent coordination \u0026   │ **Coordination Only:**        │\n│ **Consult Lane**   │ (Collapsed/Hidden in UI)│ handoffs (Architect to Dev,│ Updates Task DAG status and   │\n│                    │                         │ Dev to Code Reviewer).     │ Project Journal state.        │\n├────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Tier 4: Private**│ **Strictly Private**    │ 1-on-1 between User \u0026 Agent│ **Read-Only / Simulation:**   │\n│ **Scratchpad**     │ (Creator user only)     │ Personal ideation, drafting│ Direct repo writes blocked.   │\n│                    │                         │ with personal connectors.  │ Promotes via Pull Request.    │\n└────────────────────┴─────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Solo 1-User \"Cockpit\" vs. Multi-User \"Digital Office\"\n* **Solo Projects (1 Human Founder):** The UI automatically streamlines into a **2-Tier Cockpit**. Tiers 3 and 4 are hidden; no `@mentions` are required. The founder types naturally into Command Chat; the agent commits directly to `main` and hot-reloads the live canvas in 150ms.\n* **Team Projects (2+ Humans):** The UI dynamically promotes to the full **4-Tier Digital Office**. Direct commits to `main` are locked. Changes require Git branches and inline Pull Request cards.\n\n### 3-Layer Concurrency Defense (Collision-Free Multi-Player Editing)\n1. **Layer 1: Optimistic Concurrency Control (OCC) with SHA-256 Checkpoints:**  \n   Every file in `workspace_files` carries a content hash. Mutations enforce compare-and-swap (CAS):\n   ```sql\n   UPDATE workspace_files \n   SET content \u003d ?, hash \u003d ?, size_bytes \u003d ?, updated_at \u003d datetime(\u0027now\u0027)\n   WHERE path \u003d ? AND hash \u003d ?; -- Verifies file has not changed since read!\n   ```\n   If a concurrent edit occurred mid-turn, the transaction aborts with a conflict exception and line hints, allowing the agent to self-heal.\n2. **Layer 2: Ephemeral Distributed File Mutexes (`ConcurrencyDO`):**  \n   Multi-file refactoring operations acquire a 30-second TTL lock (`lock.acquire(\"file:src/Header.astro\")`). Concurrent tasks on non-overlapping files proceed uninterrupted.\n3. **Layer 3: Cloudflare Artifacts Branching \u0026 PR Review Cards:**  \n   All significant modifications commit to dedicated Git branch forks (`branch:task_102`). The Tier 1 Team Room renders an interactive review card displaying changed lines, syntax validation status, and an `[Accept \u0026 Merge]` button that executes an atomic fast-forward merge.\n\n### Upstream Staleness Tracking \u0026 Smart Rebase\nWhen `main` updates, active branches display an inline status pill (`⚠️ 2 commits behind main`). Agents autonomously evaluate upstream diffs:\n* If upstream changes do not overlap active files, the agent executes `git.rebaseOntoMain()` automatically.\n* If an AST overlap is detected, the agent pauses, surfaces a 3-way visual diff, and requests review.\n\n---\n\n## 4. The 6-Tier Execution Ladder (Invisible Runtime Hypervisor)\n\nThe 6-tier ladder provides scalable compute escalation. The model does **not** manage these tiers in the prompt. The agent executes via `Bash`, and the Cloudflare edge hypervisor dynamically routes the workload:\n\n```\n                                  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │ TIER 6: Sandboxed Linux Container (`ToolSandboxDO` / Docker)│\n                                  │ • Full OS userland: native compilers, Python ML, GUI (Xvfb) │\n                                  └──────────────────────────────▲──────────────────────────────┘\n                                                                 │ (Promote if native compilation/GUI needed)\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │ TIER 5: Full Headless Chromium (Browser Rendering Engine)   │\n                                  │ • Heavy browser: Visual QA, WebGL, Canvas, anti-bot bypass  │\n                                  └──────────────────────────────▲──────────────────────────────┘\n                                                                 │ (Promote if visual QA/screenshots needed)\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │ TIER 4: Lightweight Agent Browser (Cloudflare Kitesurf)     │\n                                  │ • 3–7x cheaper/faster: DOM text extraction, form fills      │\n                                  └──────────────────────────────▲──────────────────────────────┘\n                                                                 │ (Promote if web navigation needed)\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │ TIER 3: Dynamic Workflows (Cloudflare Workflows / Cron Hub) │\n                                  │ • Durable multi-step runs, sleep/pause ($0/idle), cron jobs │\n                                  └──────────────────────────────▲──────────────────────────────┘\n                                                                 │ (Promote if long-running/durable task)\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │ TIER 2: Dynamic Worker Loader (V8 Isolate Shell / CodeMode) │\n                                  │ • Pure code execution, HTTP fetches, Pyodide Wasm Python    │\n                                  └──────────────────────────────▲──────────────────────────────┘\n                                                                 │ (Promote if script logic needed)\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────┐\n│ TIER 1: In-Memory Virtual Filesystem (`@cloudflare/computer` + DO SQLite)                     │\n│ • Sub-millisecond Read, Edit (AST Search \u0026 Replace), Grep, Glob, just-bash POSIX parsing     │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### 4-Dimension State Synchronization (Virtual CLI $\\leftrightarrow$ Container Sandbox)\n1. **Filesystem:** DO SQLite Virtual FS (`workspace_files`) is mounted into the Linux Container via **`ArtifactFS` (Cloudflare’s FUSE driver)**. Files hydrate lazily over the network, avoiding 90-second `git clone` delays.\n2. **Shell Session:** Working directory changes (`cd`) and environment variables (`export`) are tracked in `NaelaoAgentDO` SQLite and injected into the container\u0027s gRPC execution payload.\n3. **Git State:** Both V8 Isolates and Containers share the same Cloudflare Artifacts Zig-WASM Git commit tree and HEAD ref.\n4. **Database State:** In-memory DO Facet SQLite tables are exposed to container binaries over local RPC sockets.\n\n### 95/5 Compute Arbitrage \u0026 60-Second Micro-Sleep\n* 95% of tasks (file reading, AST editing, regex searches, API queries) execute in **Tier 1/2 V8 Isolates at $0.0001 per run**.\n* Tier 6 Linux Containers launch only when a native userland compiler (`npm run build`, `cargo`, `pip`) or GUI is required.\n* Containers undergo an **aggressive 60-second micro-sleep countdown**. If no container commands arrive within 60 seconds of completion, the container terminates immediately. Actual active container time averages under 15 minutes/day per user.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Minimalist AI Action Space \u0026 JIT Virtual CLI Synthesis\n\n### The Minimalist Tool Surface\nThe LLM is prompted with only **3 Hands Primitives** and **2 Senses Primitives**:\n\n```typescript\nexport interface MinimalistAgentTools {\n  // ── HANDS (Execution) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  Bash: {\n    description: \"Execute terminal commands, Virtual CLIs, scripts, and build tools.\";\n    parameters: { command: string };\n  };\n  Read: {\n    description: \"Inspect file contents with line numbers. Supports offset and limit.\";\n    parameters: { filePath: string; offset?: number; limit?: number };\n  };\n  Edit: {\n    description: \"Apply surgical search-and-replace patches. Never rewrite full files.\";\n    parameters: { filePath: string; oldString: string; newString: string };\n  };\n\n  // ── SENSES (Perception \u0026 Delegation) ───────────────────────────────────────\n  Browser: {\n    description: \"Navigate, inspect DOM trees, or take visual screenshot snapshots.\";\n    parameters: { action: \"navigate\" | \"click\" | \"type\" | \"screenshot\"; url?: string; selector?: string; text?: string };\n  };\n  Delegate: {\n    description: \"Dispatch a structured task DAG item to an internal specialist agent.\";\n    parameters: { targetRole: string; taskDescription: string; contextFiles: string[] };\n  };\n}\n```\n\n### The Invisible Runtime Hypervisor\nWhen the AI executes a command via `Bash`:\n1. **POSIX Text Processing:** Commands like `grep`, `cat`, `sed`, `awk`, `find`, `diff`, `jq` execute natively in Tier 1/2 V8 Isolates via `just-bash` (\u003c5ms, $0.0001).\n2. **Virtual CLI Shims:** External commands (`stripe`, `gh`, `r2`, `twilio`, `resend`) are intercepted by isolate shims that translate terminal arguments directly into edge REST API calls with Vault credentials injected at the network boundary.\n3. **In-Isolate Python (Wasm Pyodide):** `python3 -c \"...\"` runs inside WebAssembly CPython in Tier 2 (\u003c10ms, $0.00 compute cost) unless it imports native heavy libraries (PyTorch, OpenCV), which auto-escalate to Tier 6.\n4. **Native Compilation Passthrough:** Commands requiring native Linux userland (`npm run build`, `cargo build`) route over persistent gRPC to `ToolSandboxDO`.\n\n```\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │         AGENT CALLS BASH TOOL                │\n                                  │      `shopify products list --status active` │\n                                  └──────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘\n                                                         │\n                         ┌───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┐\n                         ▼                                                               ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 1. HIT: COMPILED VIRTUAL CLI SHIM                           │   │ 2. MISS: UNREGISTERED CLI COMMAND                           │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤   ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Dispatches REST call via V8 Isolate; returns ASCII table    │   │ Interceptor checks Vault for `SHOPIFY_ADMIN_TOKEN`.         │\n│ in **4ms for $0.0001**. Container stays asleep!             │   │ Prompts agent to micro-synthesize a JIT Virtual CLI.        │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   └──────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                                                                         │\n                                                                                         ▼\n                                  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │ 3. AGENT SYNTHESIZES 15-LINE PARSER (CodeMode)              │\n                                  │ Uses `ctx.cli.register` + `ctx.vault.fetchWithAuth`.        │\n                                  │ Implements ONLY `products list` (zero SDK bloat).           │\n                                  └──────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                                         │\n                                                         ▼\n                                  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │ 4. REGISTERED TO DO SQLITE (`virtual_cli_commands`)         │\n                                  │ Compiled into virtual binary bus. Future invocations        │\n                                  │ execute in V8 Isolates in 4ms forever!                      │\n                                  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Workspace Layout \u0026 Repository Cleanliness\n\nTo prevent internal agent configurations, temporary drafts, and memory states from polluting the user\u0027s production Git repository, AVOS enforces a strict namespace separation:\n\n```\n/workspace/                       \u003c-- USER REPOSITORY (Tracked by Git Artifacts)\n├── src/                          (Application source code, components, styles)\n├── public/                       (Static assets)\n├── package.json\n└── astro.config.mjs\n\n/.avos/                           \u003c-- AGENT OPERATING SYSTEM (Internal / Git-Ignored)\n├── shared/                       (Reusable across all agents in the project)\n│   ├── skills/                   (Distilled TypeScript skills, e.g., csv-parser.ts)\n│   ├── workflows/                (Standing Cloudflare Workflow definitions)\n│   └── virtual_clis/             (Auto-synthesized JIT CLI parsers)\n│\n└── agents/                       (Functional Agent State \u0026 Memory)\n    ├── dev-operator/\n    │   ├── SOUL.md               (Agent mission, role boundary, linter rules)\n    │   ├── memory.json           (Private hindsight memory indices)\n    │   └── scratchpad/           (Working files for Tier 4 private drafts)\n    │\n    └── growth-operator/\n        └── SOUL.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Skill \u0026 Video Distillation Engine\n\nAVOS enables agents to learn permanent, parameterized capabilities from demonstrations:\n\n### 1. Demonstration-to-Skill Distillation\n* An agent or human executes a task once (HTTP requests, DOM interactions, terminal commands).\n* The **Distillation Engine** parameters dynamic variables (`customerEmail`, `invoiceId`), synthesizes a clean TypeScript module (`export async function run(args, ctx)`), verifies exit code 0 in a V8 sandbox, and commits the code to `/.avos/shared/skills/{skillName}.ts`.\n* Subsequent runs execute in **100ms for $0.0001** without re-prompting the LLM.\n\n### 2. Video-to-Skill Learning\n* The user drops a 60-second screen recording (MP4/WebM) into the workspace.\n* Workers AI Whisper transcribes spoken instructions; a multimodal vision model extracts action timelines (clicks, input fields, navigation targets).\n* The compiler synthesizes parameterized TypeScript using universal `ctx` primitives, tests the code in Tier 4 Kitesurf, and saves the verified tool to the skill library.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Universal Runtime SDK (`ctx`) \u0026 Zero-Leak Credential Security\n\nEvery script executed in Tier 2 (CodeMode), Tier 3 (Workflows), or Tier 6 (Containers) receives an authoritative, scoped `ctx` object (`AVOS_SDK.d.ts`):\n\n```typescript\ndeclare namespace ctx {\n  namespace fs {\n    function read(path: string, opts?: { offset?: number; limit?: number }): Promise\u003c{ content: string; totalLines: number }\u003e;\n    function edit(path: string, oldString: string, newString: string): Promise\u003c{ ok: boolean }\u003e;\n    function write(path: string, content: string): Promise\u003c{ ok: boolean }\u003e;\n    function grep(pattern: string, path?: string): Promise\u003c{ matches: Array\u003c{ file: string; line: number; text: string }\u003e }\u003e;\n    function glob(pattern: string): Promise\u003c{ files: string[] }\u003e;\n  }\n  namespace project {\n    const id: string;\n    function getJournal(): Promise\u003c{ tasks: Array\u003c{ id: string; title: string; status: string }\u003e }\u003e;\n    function updateTaskStatus(taskId: string, status: \"PENDING\" | \"IN_PROGRESS\" | \"COMPLETED\"): Promise\u003c{ ok: boolean }\u003e;\n  }\n  namespace space {\n    const id: string; // ONLY available to Space Assistant context\n    function getWalletBalance(): Promise\u003c{ balance_cents: number }\u003e;\n    namespace calendar {\n      function checkAvailability(isoTime: string): Promise\u003c{ available: boolean }\u003e;\n      function bookSlot(params: { clientName: string; startTime: string; eventType: string }): Promise\u003c{ ok: boolean }\u003e;\n    }\n  }\n  namespace vault {\n    function fetchWithAuth(url: string, opts: { credentialName: string; method?: string; body?: any; headers?: Record\u003cstring, string\u003e }): Promise\u003cResponse\u003e;\n  }\n  namespace cli {\n    function register(name: string, def: { description: string; subcommands: Record\u003cstring, string\u003e; handlerCode: string }): Promise\u003c{ ok: boolean }\u003e;\n    function extend(name: string, subcommand: string, handlerSnippet: string): Promise\u003c{ ok: boolean }\u003e;\n    function formatTable(data: Array\u003cRecord\u003cstring, any\u003e\u003e): string;\n  }\n  namespace browser {\n    function scrape(url: string, selector?: string): Promise\u003c{ content: string; title: string }\u003e;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Zero-Leak Credential Proxy \u0026 WriteGuard Egress\n* **Outbound Workers:** Secrets are stored with AES-256-GCM encryption in `space_credentials`. Scripts write only logical names (`credentialName: \"STRIPE_SECRET\"`). The Outbound Worker proxy injects the decrypted `Authorization: Bearer` header at the edge network boundary.\n* **WriteGuard Mutation Interceptor:** Inspects SQL ASTs and tool parameters at the edge proxy, blocking destructive operations (`DROP TABLE`, `DELETE *`, `rm -rf /`) unless authorized by a signed Gatekeeper capability token.\n\n### 3-Tier Connector Scopes \u0026 Privacy Forking\n1. **Space-Shared:** Corporate credentials (company Stripe, official calendar) available to all project tools.\n2. **Project-Bound:** Tied to 1 project (clinic WhatsApp number for customer support bot).\n3. **User-Personal:** Tied to an individual human (Alice\u0027s personal Gmail/Calendar).\n   * **Public Channel Defense:** Personal tools are physically stripped in Tier 1/2 public rooms.\n   * **Privacy Bridge:** If a user requests a personal action in public, the agent outputs an interactive MCP-UI card: `[ 🚀 Continue in Private Scratchpad ]`. Clicking forks the task into a private Tier 4 thread.\n   * **Return Bridge:** When the task completes, a `[ 📢 Share Summary to Team Room ]` button posts only the sanitized result back to the public channel.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Mini-AGI Knowledge Architecture \u0026 Edge AI Search\n\n### Mathematical Pre-Filtering Vector Retrieval\nTo implement Jack Dorsey\u0027s Mini-AGI sovereign permission model, Cloudflare Vectorize applies hardware-level pre-filtering prior to similarity scoring:\n\n$$\\text{Sim}(q, c_i) \u003d \\begin{cases} \n\\frac{\\mathbf{q} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}_i}{\\|\\mathbf{q}\\| \\|\\mathbf{v}_i\\|}, \u0026 \\text{if } (\\mathbf{m}_i \\wedge \\mathbf{u}) \\neq \\mathbf{0} \\text{ and } \\text{Ten}(c_i) \u003d \\text{Ten}(q) \\\\\n-\\infty, \u0026 \\text{otherwise}\n\\end{cases}$$\n\n```typescript\nconst searchResults \u003d await env.KB_VECTORS.query(queryVector, {\n  topK: 6,\n  filter: {\n    space_id: spaceId,\n    project_id: { $in: [activeProjectId || \"\", \"\"] }, // Project-scoped OR Space-wide\n    min_role_rank: { $lte: user.roleRank }              // 1: Viewer -\u003e 2: Member -\u003e 3: Editor -\u003e 4: Admin -\u003e 5: Owner\n  }\n});\n```\n\n### XML Semantic Boundary Envelopes\nAll retrieved context chunks are wrapped in protective tags before LLM ingestion:\n$$\\mathcal{F}_{\\text{sandbox}}(c_i) \u003d \\text{\"\u003ccontext_chunk id\u003d\\\"\"} \\circ \\text{Hash}(c_i) \\circ \\text{\"\\\" access\u003d\\\"verified\\\"\u003e\"} \\circ \\text{EscapeXML}(c_i) \\circ \\text{\"\u003c/context_chunk\u003e\"}$$\n\n### Google Search AI Mode at the Edge\n1. **Sub-50ms Semantic Cache (KV):** If query embedding cosine similarity is $\u003e0.96$ against historical queries, returns the cached, verified answer in 35ms with zero LLM compute.\n2. **Dense + Sparse Hybrid RRF ($k\u003d60$):** Fuses Vectorize semantic embeddings with in-memory BM25 exact keyword matching:\n   $$\\text{Score}(d) \u003d \\sum_{m \\in \\{\\text{dense}, \\text{sparse}\\}} \\frac{1}{60 + \\text{Rank}_m(d)}$$\n3. **Interactive Numbered Citations:** Output streams with clickable citation badges (`[1] Contract §4.2`, `[2] Delaware Statute`) linking directly to source chunk coordinates in R2.\n\n### Inter-Project MCP v2 Mesh\n* Every project exposes a stateless **`https://api.avos.com/spaces/:sId/projects/:pId/mcp`** endpoint via Cloudflare MCP SDK v2 (`createMcpHandler`).\n* Projects interact as microservices over Stateless Streamable HTTP without open SSE sockets.\n* Pipedream is dropped entirely; Composio serves strictly as an external SaaS OAuth broker.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Stateful Micro-Apps (\"Cloudflare OS Gadgets\") \u0026 Dynamic UI\n\nAVOS implements Cloudflare\u0027s **Cloudflare OS (August 2026)** architecture, dividing UI deliverables into three tiers:\n\n```\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                   THE 3-TIER ARTIFACT \u0026 APP HIERARCHY                                     │\n├────────────────────┬─────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┤\n│ Tier Level         │ Execution \u0026 State       │ Underlying Cloudflare Tech │ Primary Purpose               │\n├────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Tier 1: Canvas** │ **Live Workspace View** │ `@cloudflare/computer` +   │ Deep project UI extensions    │\n│ **Viewports**      │ (Direct File Access)    │ Project SQLite Virtual FS  │ (Code Editor, Redliner, Comps)│\n├────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Tier 2: Versioned│ **Stateless Snapshots** │ Cloudflare Artifacts       │ Ephemeral deliverables (PDFs, │\n│ **Artifacts**      │ (Immutable Git Commits) │ (Zig-Wasm Git Server in DO)│ SVGs, static HTML previews)   │\n├────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Tier 3: Stateful │ **Living Mini-Apps**    │ **Dynamic Workers +**      │ Full-stack vibe-coded apps    │\n│ **Gadgets**        │ (Dedicated Database)    │ **DO Facets (SQLite DB)**  │ (Leave Tracker, Bug Matrix)   │\n└────────────────────┴─────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n* **Dedicated Database per Gadget:** Every micro-app gets its own isolated **DO Facet SQLite database** provisioned in milliseconds.\n* **Auto-Generated MCP v2 Server:** The runtime wraps every Gadget\u0027s SQLite schema into a native `/mcp` server, allowing agents to automate the application via standard tool calls.\n* **MCP-UI Bidirectional Streaming:** User interactions inside the Gadget\u0027s sandboxed iframe (button clicks, form submits) stream back to the agent\u0027s observation loop in real time.\n* **Generative In-Chat UI:** In chat streams, the AI dynamically renders interactive input widgets (Google Search AI Mode style date pickers, budget sliders) that return structured input directly into the turn.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Telephony, Voice Agents \u0026 Universal Shared State\n\n### Native Edge Voice Telephony (`@cloudflare/voice`)\nReplaces third-party brokers (Vapi, Retell) by executing duplex voice pipelines natively at Cloudflare\u0027s edge:\n```\n[ Caller Phone / WebRTC ] ──► [ Cloudflare Calls SFU ] ──► [ Workers AI Whisper STT ]\n                                                                     │\n                                                                     ▼\n[ Streaming Audio Back ] ◄── [ Workers AI TTS ] ◄── [ Workers AI Llama 3.3 70B ]\n```\n* **Latency:** Sub-300ms round-trip audio latency.\n* **Security Clamp:** Public phone callers are clamped to **Tier 1 (Safe RAG only)**; file-editing tools and shell access are physically stripped.\n* **Dual-Thread Project Architecture (`kind: \"voice_agent\"`):**\n  * *Management Threads:* User configures greetings, business hours, and phone numbers via chat or settings.\n  * *Call Session Threads (`kind: \"voice_call\"`):* Auto-spawned per inbound phone call; contains full audio recording playback, transcript, and sentiment analysis.\n* **Native Voice Dictation in `ComposerDock`:** Captures browser microphone audio and transcribes via Workers AI Whisper for $0 compute cost.\n\n### Universal Shared State Plane (`SpaceDO.space_calendar_events`)\nAll project kinds access a single shared state plane inside `SpaceDO` SQLite:\n* When a voice agent books a patient consultation, the slot commits atomically into `space_calendar_events`.\n* The booking immediately renders on the doctor\u0027s `doc_studio` schedule panel and appears in the founder\u0027s morning Telegram briefing.\n\n---\n\n## 12. The 7 Foundational Project Kinds\n\n```typescript\nexport const AVOS_PROJECT_KINDS: Record\u003cstring, BusinessFeatureKind\u