      }, {
        "text": "─────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Workspace Layout \u0026 Repository Cleanliness\n\nTo prevent internal agent"
      }, {
        "text": " configurations, temporary drafts, and memory states from polluting the user\u0027s production Git repository, AVOS enforces a strict namespace separation:\n\n"
      }, {
        "text": "```\n/workspace/                       \u003c-- USER REPOSITORY (Tracked by Git Artifacts)\n├── src/                          (Application"
      }, {
        "text": " source code, components, styles)\n├── public/                       (Static assets)\n├── package.json\n└── astro.config.mjs\n\n"
      }, {
        "text": "/.avos/                           \u003c-- AGENT OPERATING SYSTEM (Internal / Git-Ignored)\n├── shared/                       (Reusable across"
      }, {
        "text": " all agents in the project)\n│   ├── skills/                   (Distilled TypeScript skills, e.g., csv-"
      }, {
        "text": "parser.ts)\n│   ├── workflows/                (Standing Cloudflare Workflow definitions)\n│   └── virtual_clis/             "
      }, {
        "text": "(Auto-synthesized JIT CLI parsers)\n│\n└── agents/                       (Functional Agent State \u0026 Memory)"
      }, {
        "text": "\n    ├── dev-operator/\n    │   ├── SOUL.md               (Agent mission, role boundary,"
      }, {
        "text": " linter rules)\n    │   ├── memory.json           (Private hindsight memory indices)\n    │   └── scratchpad"
      }, {
        "text": "/           (Working files for Tier 4 private drafts)\n    │\n    └── growth-operator/\n        └── SOUL.md\n"
      }, {
        "text": "```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Skill \u0026 Video Distillation Engine\n\nAVOS enables agents to learn permanent, parameterized capabilities from demonstrations:"
      }, {
        "text": "\n\n### 1. Demonstration-to-Skill Distillation\n* An agent or human executes a task once (HTTP"
      }, {
        "text": " requests, DOM interactions, terminal commands).\n* The **Distillation Engine** parameters dynamic variables (`customerEmail`, `invoiceId"
      }, {
        "text": "`), synthesizes a clean TypeScript module (`export async function run(args, ctx)`), verifies exit code 0 in a V8"
      }, {
        "text": " sandbox, and commits the code to `/.avos/shared/skills/{skillName}.ts`.\n* Subsequent runs execute in"
      }, {
        "text": " **100ms for $0.0001** without re-prompting the LLM.\n\n### 2. Video-"
      }, {
        "text": "to-Skill Learning\n* The user drops a 60-second screen recording (MP4/WebM) into the workspace"
      }, {
        "text": ".\n* Workers AI Whisper transcribes spoken instructions; a multimodal vision model extracts action timelines (clicks, input fields, navigation targets)."
      }, {
        "text": "\n* The compiler synthesizes parameterized TypeScript using universal `ctx` primitives, tests the code in Tier 4 Kitesurf, and saves"
      }, {
        "text": " the verified tool to the skill library.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Universal Runtime SDK (`ctx`) \u0026 Zero-Leak Credential"
      }, {
        "text": " Security\n\nEvery script executed in Tier 2 (CodeMode), Tier 3 (Workflows), or Tier 6 ("
      }, {
        "text": "Containers) receives an authoritative, scoped `ctx` object (`AVOS_SDK.d.ts`):\n\n```typescript\ndeclare"
      }, {
        "text": " namespace ctx {\n  namespace fs {\n    function read(path: string, opts?: { offset?: number; limit?:"
      }, {
        "text": " number }): Promise\u003c{ content: string; totalLines: number }\u003e;\n    function edit(path: string, oldString: string, new"
      }, {
        "text": "String: string): Promise\u003c{ ok: boolean }\u003e;\n    function write(path: string, content: string): Promise\u003c{ ok"
      }, {
        "text": ": boolean }\u003e;\n    function grep(pattern: string, path?: string): Promise\u003c{ matches: Array\u003c{ file:"
      }, {
        "text": " string; line: number; text: string }\u003e }\u003e;\n    function glob(pattern: string): Promise\u003c{ files: string[] }\u003e;\n"
      }, {
        "text": "  }\n  namespace project {\n    const id: string;\n    function getJournal(): Promise\u003c{ tasks: Array\u003c{ id"
      }, {
        "text": ": string; title: string; status: string }\u003e }\u003e;\n    function updateTaskStatus(taskId: string, status"
      }, {
        "text": ": \"PENDING\" | \"IN_PROGRESS\" | \"COMPLETED\"): Promise\u003c{ ok: boolean }\u003e;\n  }\n  "
      }, {
        "text": "namespace space {\n    const id: string; // ONLY available to Space Assistant context\n    function getWalletBalance(): Promise\u003c{ balance_cents:"
      }, {
        "text": " number }\u003e;\n    namespace calendar {\n      function checkAvailability(isoTime: string): Promise\u003c{ available: boolean }\u003e;\n      function bookSlot("
      }, {
        "text": "params: { clientName: string; startTime: string; eventType: string }): Promise\u003c{ ok: boolean }\u003e;"
      }, {
        "text": "\n    }\n  }\n  namespace vault {\n    function fetchWithAuth(url: string, opts: {"
      }, {
        "text": " credentialName: string; method?: string; body?: any; headers?: Record\u003cstring, string\u003e }): Promise\u003cResponse\u003e;\n  "
      }, {
        "text": "}\n  namespace cli {\n    function register(name: string, def: { description: string; subcommands: Record\u003cstring"
      }, {
        "text": ", string\u003e; handlerCode: string }): Promise\u003c{ ok: boolean }\u003e;\n    function extend(name: string,"
      }, {
        "text": " subcommand: string, handlerSnippet: string): Promise\u003c{ ok: boolean }\u003e;\n    function formatTable(data: Array\u003cRecord\u003cstring, any"
      }, {
        "text": "\u003e\u003e): string;\n  }\n  namespace browser {\n    function scrape(url: string, selector?: string"
      }, {
        "text": "): Promise\u003c{ content: string; title: string }\u003e;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Zero-Leak Credential Proxy"
      }, {
        "text": " \u0026 WriteGuard Egress\n* **Outbound Workers:** Secrets are stored with AES-256-GCM encryption in `space_credentials`."
      }, {
        "text": " Scripts write only logical names (`credentialName: \"STRIPE_SECRET\"`). The Outbound Worker proxy injects the decrypted "
      }, {
        "text": "`Authorization: Bearer` header at the edge network boundary.\n* **WriteGuard Mutation Interceptor:** Inspects SQL ASTs and tool"
      }, {
        "text": " parameters at the edge proxy, blocking destructive operations (`DROP TABLE`, `DELETE *`, `rm -rf /`) unless authorized"
      }, {
        "text": " by a signed Gatekeeper capability token.\n\n### 3-Tier Connector Scopes \u0026 Privacy Forking\n1. **Space-Shared"
      }, {
        "text": ":** Corporate credentials (company Stripe, official calendar) available to all project tools.\n2. **Project-Bound:** Tied"
      }, {
        "text": " to 1 project (clinic WhatsApp number for customer support bot).\n3. **User-Personal:** Tied to an individual human"
      }, {
        "text": " (Alice\u0027s personal Gmail/Calendar).\n   * **Public Channel Defense:** Personal tools are physically stripped in Tier"
      }, {
        "text": " 1/2 public rooms.\n   * **Privacy Bridge:** If a user requests a personal action in public, the agent"
      }, {
        "text": " outputs an interactive MCP-UI card: `[ 🚀 Continue in Private Scratchpad ]`. Clicking forks the task into a private"
      }, {
        "text": " Tier 4 thread.\n   * **Return Bridge:** When the task completes, a `[ 📢 Share Summary to Team Room ]"
      }, {
        "text": "` button posts only the sanitized result back to the public channel.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Mini-AGI Knowledge Architecture \u0026 Edge"
      }, {
        "text": " AI Search\n\n### Mathematical Pre-Filtering Vector Retrieval\nTo implement Jack Dorsey\u0027s Mini-AGI sovereign permission model,"
      }, {
        "text": " Cloudflare Vectorize applies hardware-level pre-filtering prior to similarity scoring:\n\n$$\\text{Sim}(q, c_i)"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003d \\begin{cases} \n\\frac{\\mathbf{q} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}_i}{\\"
      }, {
        "text": "|\\mathbf{q}\\| \\|\\mathbf{v}_i\\|}, \u0026 \\text{if } (\\mathbf{m}_i \\wedge \\mathbf{"
      }, {
        "text": "u}) \\neq \\mathbf{0} \\text{ and } \\text{Ten}(c_i) \u003d \\"
      }, {
        "text": "text{Ten}(q) \\\\\n-\\infty, \u0026 \\text{otherwise}\n\\end{cases}$$\n\n"
      }, {
        "text": "```typescript\nconst searchResults \u003d await env.KB_VECTORS.query(queryVector, {\n  topK"
      }, {
        "text": ": 6,\n  filter: {\n    space_id: spaceId,\n    project_id:"
      }, {
        "text": " { $in: [activeProjectId || \"\", \"\"] }, // Project-scoped OR Space-wide\n    min_role_rank: {"
