      "text": "Continuing directly from where we left off, here are the reconciled, production-ready specification prompts for **Message Files 9, 10, and 11**:\n\n* **Message File 9 (`208 - 210 And.txt`)**: Demonstration-to-Skill Distillation \u0026 Tier 4 Kitesurf Agent Browser.\n* **Message File 10 (`211 - 213 What.txt`)**: Tier 3 Dynamic Workflows (Harness Pattern) \u0026 Video-to-Skill Multimodal Learning.\n* **Message File 11 (`215 - 219 With.txt`)**: Unified Filesystem Synchronization (Across All 6 Tiers) \u0026 Script-Native CodeAct Execution.\n\nAll early exploratory contradictions (such as the early 5-tier model, exposing 6 separate execution tools directly in the prompt, raw Cloudflare workflow boilerplate authoring, and saving internal skills directly into the user’s code root) have been **stripped and updated to match the final architecture**.\n\n---\n\n# PROMPT 9: Demonstration-to-Skill Distillation \u0026 Tier 4 Kitesurf Agent Browser\n*(Derived from `208 - 210 And.txt`, reconciled with the 6-tier ladder, `/.avos/` namespace, and minimalist senses)*\n\n```markdown\n# SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE PROMPT: DEMONSTRATION-TO-SKILL DISTILLATION \u0026 KITESURF BROWSER\n\nYou are architecting the demonstration distillation engine and the lightweight web perception layer for AVOS.\n\nEnable agents to record complex multi-step tasks and compile them into permanent, reusable TypeScript skills, while integrating Cloudflare Kitesurf as the lightweight, low-memory browser engine positioned right before full headless Chromium.\n\n## 1. The \"Watch Me Do It Once, Automate Forever\" Distillation Engine\n\nInstead of re-prompting foundation models from scratch on every turn, compile raw task execution traces (HTTP requests, DOM interactions, terminal commands) into deterministic, parameterized TypeScript skills stored in `/.avos/shared/skills/`:\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                 DEMONSTRATION-TO-SKILL COMPILATION PIPELINE                 │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1. Execution Trace Ingestion │ Captures raw operation log:                  │\n│                              │ `[{ op: \"fetch\", url, body }, { op: \"dom\" }]`│\n├──────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 2. Parameterization \u0026 AST    │ Identifies dynamic variables: `clientEmail`, │\n│    Synthesis (Workers AI)    │ `invoiceId`, `targetSelector`. Generates     │\n│                              │ clean TS: `export async function run(args)`. │\n├──────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 3. Isolated Sandbox Verify   │ Tests the synthesized script inside a Tier 2 │\n│                              │ V8 Isolate sandbox to verify exit code 0.    │\n├──────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 4. R2 \u0026 SQLite Registration  │ Persists to `/.avos/shared/skills/{name}.ts`.│\n│                              │ Subsequent runs execute in 5ms for $0.0001!  │\n└──────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n### Implementation: `workers/agents/src/script-engine/prebuilt/skill-distiller.ts`\n```typescript\nexport async function distillSkillFromTrace(\n  trace: Array\u003c{ op: string; input: Record\u003cstring, any\u003e; output: any }\u003e,\n  skillName: string,\n  ctx: PrebuiltOpContext\n) {\n  // 1. Synthesize parameterized TypeScript module from raw execution trace\n  const synthesizedCode \u003d await generateSkillCodeFromTrace(trace, skillName, ctx.env);\n\n  // 2. Test execution in isolated V8 sandbox\n  const verifyRun \u003d await ctx.env.codeRunner.run({\n    name: `verify_${skillName}`,\n    code: synthesizedCode,\n    tier: 2,\n    args: trace[0]?.input || {},\n    spaceId: ctx.env.spaceId,\n    agentId: ctx.env.agentId\n  });\n\n  if (verifyRun.exitCode !\u003d\u003d 0) {\n    throw new Error(`Skill distillation failed verification: ${verifyRun.stderr}`);\n  }\n\n  // 3. Persist to shared skills directory (Git-ignored from user repository)\n  await ctx.env.fs.write(`/.avos/shared/skills/${skillName}.ts`, synthesizedCode);\n\n  // 4. Index in Vectorize so agents discover it semantically\n  await indexSkillMetadata(ctx.env, {\n    name: skillName,\n    path: `/.avos/shared/skills/${skillName}.ts`,\n    description: `Distilled skill: ${skillName}`,\n    parameters: extractParametersFromTrace(trace)\n  });\n\n  return { ok: true, skillName, path: `/.avos/shared/skills/${skillName}.ts` };\n}\n```\n\n## 2. Tier 4: Cloudflare Kitesurf Agent Browser (The Fast Web Tier)\n\nPosition Cloudflare Kitesurf as Tier 4 in the execution ladder—directly before heavy Tier 5 Headless Chromium:\n* **Resource Advantage:** Consumes 30MB of RAM and starts in \u003c50ms (3–7x cheaper and faster than Chromium). Handles 85% of agent web tasks: DOM text extraction, form fills, news scraping, and API portal navigation.\n* **The Boundary:** Kitesurf does not execute heavy WebGL, canvas painting, or visual pixel-based screenshot QA.\n\n### The Transparent Kitesurf ➔ Chromium Escalation Protocol\nThe agent does not micromanage browser engines. It invokes the sensory `Browser` tool, and the runtime router automatically escalates:\n\n```\n[ Agent calls `Browser({ action: \"navigate\", url: \"https://portal.com\" })` ]\n                                │\n                                ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 1. ROUTER LAUNCHES TIER 4 KITESURF (Fast, 30MB Isolate)                     │\n│    Loads page, extracts cleaned DOM accessibility tree (AXTree) in 200ms.   │\n└───────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                │\n       ┌────────────────────────┴────────────────────────┐\n       ▼ (If normal DOM/Text)                            ▼ (If WebGL / Screenshot needed)\n┌──────────────────────────────┐          ┌──────────────────────────────────┐\n│ RETURN ACCESSIBILITY TREE    │          │ 2. AUTO-ELEVATE TO TIER 5        │\n│ Text tokens returned to LLM; │          │    Full Headless Chromium boots. │\n│ session ends. ($0.001 cost)  │          │    Captures visual PNG snapshot; │\n└──────────────────────────────┘          │    streams image into LLM context│\n                                          └──────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Router Implementation: `workers/browser/src/router.ts`\n```typescript\nexport async function executeBrowserNavigation(req: BrowserActionRequest, env: Env) {\n  // If task explicitly demands visual screenshot inspection, force Tier 5 Chromium\n  const requiresVisualQa \u003d req.action \u003d\u003d\u003d \"screenshot\" || req.requiresWebGL \u003d\u003d\u003d true;\n\n  if (!requiresVisualQa) {\n    try {\n      // Tier 4: Lightweight Kitesurf First\n      const kitesurf \u003d await launchBrowserEngine(env, \"kitesurf\");\n      return await kitesurf.executeAction(req);\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      console.warn(\"Kitesurf capability boundary hit, elevating to Tier 5 Chromium:\", err.message);\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Tier 5: Full Headless Chromium Fallback\n  const chromium \u003d await launchBrowserEngine(env, \"chromium\");\n  return await chromium.executeAction(req);\n}\n```\n\nEnsure all distilled skills save cleanly into `/.avos/shared/skills/` without polluting `/workspace`, and verify that DOM extraction routes through Tier 4 Kitesurf by default.\n```\n\n---\n\n# PROMPT 10: Tier 3 Dynamic Workflows (The Harness Pattern) \u0026 Video-to-Skill Learning\n*(Derived from `211 - 213 What.txt`, reconciled with the Workflow Harness Pattern and Multimodal Vision)*\n\n```markdown\n# SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE PROMPT: TIER 3 DYNAMIC WORKFLOWS \u0026 VIDEO-TO-SKILL LEARNING\n\nYou are architecting the durable execution layer (Cloudflare Workflows) and the multimodal video demonstration learning engine for AVOS.\n\nEnable agents to execute multi-hour background pipelines with dormant $0-cost sleeping, and allow founders to train agents by simply dropping 60-second screen recordings into the workspace.\n\n## 1. Tier 3: Dynamic Workflows \u0026 The \"Harness Pattern\"\n\nWhen a task requires multi-hour waiting, retry boundaries, or scheduled cadences (e.g. *\"Check zoning filings every 6 hours and ping me Friday\"*), keeping a synchronous Durable Object awake wastes compute.\n\n### The Failure Mode to Avoid:\nNever require the LLM to write raw Cloudflare `WorkflowEntrypoint\u003cEnv\u003e` boilerplate, serialize bindings, or manage `wrangler.jsonc`. The model will hallucinate deployment plumbing and fail.\n\n### The Solution: The Platform Harness Pattern\nThe agent authors ONLY the business logic inside a clean, standard `execute(step, ctx)` function:\n\n```typescript\n// What the AI writes in /.avos/shared/workflows/weekly-permit-audit.ts:\nexport async function execute(step: WorkflowStep, ctx: WorkflowContext) {\n  // Step 1: Scrape portal via Tier 4 Kitesurf\n  const permits \u003d await step.do(\"scrape-permits\", async () \u003d\u003e {\n    return await ctx.browser.scrape(\"https://miamidade.gov/building/permits\", \"table.permits\");\n  });\n\n  // Step 2: Dormant sleep for 6 hours ($0 compute cost during wait)\n  await step.sleep(\"wait-for-batch\", \"6 hours\");\n\n  // Step 3: Check diff and dispatch report\n  await step.do(\"compile-and-send-report\", async () \u003d\u003e {\n    const diff \u003d await ctx.fs.diff(\"src/data/permits.json\", JSON.stringify(permits));\n    if (diff.hasChanges) {\n      await ctx.notify.telegram(`Found ${diff.newCount} new municipal permits!`);\n      await ctx.fs.write(\"src/data/permits.json\", JSON.stringify(permits));\n    }\n  });\n}\n```\n\n### The Workflow Compiler (`workers/agents/src/workflows/WorkflowCompiler.ts`):\nWhen the agent executes `schedule --cron \"0 9 * * 1\" .avos/shared/workflows/weekly-permit-audit.ts`:\n1. The platform reads the raw `execute(step, ctx)` script.\n2. Injects the Cloudflare runtime harness wrapping it in `class GeneratedWorkflow extends WorkflowEntrypoint\u003cEnv\u003e`.\n3. Binds step persistence to the project\u0027s authoritative Durable Object storage.\n4. Deploys the workflow into the space\u0027s Dynamic Worker namespace and schedules the cron trigger.\n\n## 2. The Video-to-Skill Multimodal Learning Engine\n\nAllow non-technical founders to demonstrate complex browser or desktop tasks by recording their screen (MP4 / WebM) and dropping it into `/workspace/recordings/`:\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                     MULTIMODAL VIDEO DISTILLATION PIPELINE                  │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1. Video Ingestion \u0026 Stream  │ Extracts audio track (.wav) and samples      │\n│    Decomposition (R2)        │ visual keyframes on scene/click changes.     │\n├──────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 2. Audio Transcription       │ Workers AI Whisper (`@cf/openai/whisper`)    │\n│                              │ transcribes spoken instructions in 200ms.    │\n├──────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 3. Action Recognition \u0026 BBox │ Multimodal Vision LLM identifies active input│\n│    Correlation (Vision LLM)  │ selectors, button clicks, and typed values.  │\n│                              │ Maps spoken words to DOM targets.            │\n├──────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 4. TypeScript Code Synthesis │ Replaces hardcoded inputs with arguments:    │\n│                              │ `const { permitNumber, contractor } \u003d args;` │\n├──────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 5. Sandbox Verification      │ Replays action sequence in Tier 4 Kitesurf.  │\n│                              │ Confirms exit code 0, registers skill in R2. │\n└──────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n### Implementation: `workers/agents/src/script-engine/prebuilt/video-learner.ts`\n```typescript\nimport { generateObject } from \"ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nexport async function distillSkillFromVideo(\n  videoR2Key: string,\n  skillName: string,\n  ctx: PrebuiltOpContext\n) {\n  // 1. Fetch video buffer from R2 workspace\n  const videoObj \u003d await ctx.env.workspaceBucket.get(videoR2Key);\n  if (!videoObj) throw new Error(`Video file not found: ${videoR2Key}`);\n\n  // 2. Multimodal Action Extraction Schema\n  const { object: actionSequence } \u003d await generateObject({\n    model: ctx.env.AI_GATEWAY(\"claude-3-7-sonnet\"),\n    schema: z.object({\n      parameters: z.array(z.object({ name: z.string(), type: z.string(), description: z.string() })),\n      steps: z.array(z.object({\n        actionType: z.enum([\"NAVIGATE\", \"CLICK\", \"TYPE\", \"EXTRACT\", \"ASSERT\", \"BASH\"]),\n        target: z.string().describe(\"URL, CSS selector, or command\"),\n        valueExpression: z.string().describe(\"Dynamic parameter name or literal string\"),\n        description: z.string()\n      }))\n    }),\n    prompt: `Analyze this recorded video demonstration of \u0027${skillName}\u0027.\nExtract the parameterizable inputs, DOM interactions, and logic flow required to replicate this exact task programmatically.`\n  });\n\n  // 3. Synthesize clean TypeScript utilizing universal ctx primitives\n  const synthesizedCode \u003d `\n/**\n * Auto-Distilled Skill: ${skillName}\n * Generated from screen recording: ${videoR2Key}\n */\nexport async function run(args: Record\u003cstring, any\u003e, ctx: any) {\n  ${actionSequence.parameters.map(p \u003d\u003e `const ${p.name} \u003d args[\"${p.name}\"];`).join(\"\\n  \")}\n\n  // Replay synthesized action timeline\n  ${actionSequence.steps.map(s \u003d\u003e {\n    if (s.actionType \u003d\u003d\u003d \"NAVIGATE\") return `await ctx.browser.scrape(\"${s.target}\");`;\n    if (s.actionType \u003d\u003d\u003d \"CLICK\") return `await ctx.run(\"browser.click\", { selector: \"${s.target}\" });`;\n    if (s.actionType \u003d\u003d\u003d \"TYPE\") return `await ctx.run(\"browser.type\", { selector: \"${s.target}\", text: ${s.valueExpression} });`;\n    if (s.actionType \u003d\u003d\u003d \"BASH\") return `await ctx.cli.exec(${s.valueExpression});`;\n    return `// ${s.description}`;\n  }).join(\"\\n  \")}\n\n  return { ok: true, message: \"Successfully executed learned skill: ${skillName}\" };\n}\n`;\n\n  // 4. Save to project shared skills directory\n  await ctx.env.fs.write(`/.avos/shared/skills/${skillName}.ts`, synthesizedCode);\n\n  return {\n    ok: true,\n    skillName,\n    parameters: actionSequence.parameters,\n    message: `✔ Successfully learned skill \u0027${skillName}\u0027 from video demonstration.`\n  };\n}\n```\n\nVerify that all durable workflows execute via the harness pattern without leaking Cloudflare deployment complexity to the agent, and confirm that learned skills commit directly to `/.avos/shared/skills/`.\n```\n\n---\n\n# PROMPT 11: Unified Filesystem Synchronization \u0026 Script-Native CodeAct Execution\n*(Derived from `215 - 219 With.txt`, reconciled with the Minimalist 3-Tool Surface and Invisible Hypervisor)*\n\n```markdown\n# SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE PROMPT: UNIFIED FILESYSTEM SYNC \u0026 SCRIPT-NATIVE CODEACT\n\nYou are architecting the authoritative virtual filesystem synchronization engine and the script-native CodeAct execution pipeline across all 6 tiers of the AVOS ladder.\n\nEliminate the static JSON tool bloat of traditional agents. Implement an authoritative, single-source-of-truth virtual filesystem in Durable Object SQLite that synchronizes across V8 Isolates, Workflows, Headless Browsers, and Linux Containers without split-brain anomalies, while exposing a minimalist 3-tool surface to the model