│\n└─────────────────┘ └─────────────────┘ └─────────────────┘ └─────────────────┘ └─────────────────┘\n\n### How Every Tier Reads and Writes Without Data Loss:\n1. **Tier 1 \u0026 2 (In-Memory DO SQLite \u0026 V8 Dynamic Workers):** Operates directly inside the V8 isolate. `Read`, `Edit`, and `Grep` execute against SQLite in sub-milliseconds without network serialization.\n2. **Tier 3 (Dynamic Workflows):** Every `step.do()` checkpoint commits its outputs back to the project\u0027s SQLite virtual filesystem via internal RPC.\n3. **Tier 4 \u0026 5 (Kitesurf \u0026 Chromium):** Downloaded PDFs, scraped tables, and screenshot buffers stream directly into `workspace_files` under `downloads/{sessionId}/...`. The agent can immediately run `Read` or `Grep` on them in the next turn.\n4. **Tier 6 (Linux Container / `ToolSandboxDO`):**\n   - The container mounts `/workspace` lazily using **`ArtifactFS` (FUSE driver)**.\n   - Files are fetched on-demand over the edge network (zero 90-second `git clone` delays).\n   - When a build command (`npm run build`, `cargo`) completes, all modified bytes and build artifacts flush back to DO SQLite using SHA-256 hash diffs.\n\n## 2. Reconciling CodeAct: The Minimalist Tool Surface vs. Invisible Hypervisor\n\nDo not expose 6 separate tier tools in the prompt. That creates prompt paralysis. The model receives only **3 Universal Execution Primitives**:\n\n```typescript\nexport interface AgentToolPrimitives {\n  // 1. Universal Terminal \u0026 Script Execution\n  Bash: {\n    description: \"Execute terminal commands, Virtual CLIs, scripts, and build tools.\";\n    parameters: { command: string };\n  };\n  // 2. Windowed File Inspection\n  Read: {\n    description: \"Inspect file contents with line numbers. Supports offset and limit.\";\n    parameters: { filePath: string; offset?: number; limit?: number };\n  };\n  // 3. Exact AST Search-and-Replace\n  Edit: {\n    description: \"Perform surgical search-and-replace block edits. Never rewrite