 Only one bot executes at a time.\n\n```typescript\nexport function resolveTargetAgent(text: string): { primaryAgentId: string; referentAgentIds: string[] } {\n  const matches \u003d [...text.matchAll(/@([a-zA-Z0-9_-]+)(?:\u0027s)?/g)];\n  if (matches.length \u003d\u003d\u003d 0) return { primaryAgentId: \"default_assistant\", referentAgentIds: [] };\n\n  const primaryName \u003d matches[0][1].toLowerCase();\n  const referents \u003d matches.slice(1).map(m \u003d\u003e m[1].toLowerCase());\n\n  return { primaryAgentId: primaryName, referentAgentIds: referents };\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. How Hermes \u0026 Grok Bot Handle Cross-Thread Memory\n\n* **Hermes Agent (Nous Research):** Completely isolates session histories. Thread 2 starts with a clean `0-turn` context. Memory is not raw chat logs; it is **distilled semantic facts** written to `MEMORY.md` at the end of sessions.\n* **Grok Bot (xAI):** Universal workspace disk + ephemeral chat contexts. Past thread summaries index into a background vector store and are retrieved only when semantically triggered.\n\n---\n\n### 3. The AVOS Hybrid Memory Architecture\n\n```\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │           PROJECT: \"Core SaaS App\"           │\n                                  └──────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘\n                                                         │\n                         ┌───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┐\n                         ▼                                                               ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 💬 THREAD #1: \"Stripe Webhook Bug\" (50 Messages Long)        │   │ 💬 THREAD #2: \"Write CSV Export Script\" (Brand New Thread)  │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤   ├───────────────────────────────────────