      "text": "**Yes, this is completely possible**, but with one critical distinction between doing it inside the **AI Studio Web UI** versus running it through a **lightweight local runner script**.\n\n---\n\n### The Crucial Distinction: AI Studio UI vs. Local Runner\n\n1. **In the AI Studio Web Playground:**  \n   Google AI Studio allows you to define function declarations (JSON schemas). However, the web UI is **stateless and sandboxed**. When the model decides to call `push_github_diff`, AI Studio will output the function call arguments on screen and wait for *you* to manually type or paste the result back into the UI. It cannot directly connect to `api.github.com` using your private GitHub token.\n2. **In an Autonomous Local Runner (Recommended):**  \n   You use the exact same model, the Repomix output, and the Phase Plan, but run it via a small Node.js script using the **Gemini API (`@google/genai`)** and **GitHub API (`@octokit/rest`)**. The model outputs the code/diff, your script commits and pushes it to a new branch, and loops automatically until the phase is verified.\n\n---\n\n# Method 1: The Fully Autonomous Local Runner (Recommended)\n\nThis gives you a 1-click execution pipeline: **Repomix $\\rightarrow$ Gemini $\\rightarrow$ Automated GitHub Branch \u0026 Commit**.\n\n### Step 1: Configure Repomix\nIn your project root, create a `repomix.config.json` to make sure you don\u0027t burn tokens on build artifacts or lockfiles:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"output\": {\n    \"filePath\": \"repomix-output.xml\",\n    \"style\": \"xml\"\n  },\n  \"ignore\": {\n    \"useGitignore\": true,\n    \"customPatterns\": [\n      \"**/node_modules/**\",\n      \"**/.wrangler/**\",\n      \"**/dist/**\",\n      \"**/.git/**\",\n      \"package-lock.json\",\n      \"pnpm-lock.yaml\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\nRun Repomix:\n```bash\nnpx repomix\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Create the Phase Execution Runner (`run-phase.ts`)\n\nInstall the required SDKs:\n```bash\nnpm install @google/genai @octokit/rest dotenv\n```\n\nCreate `run-phase.ts`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { GoogleGenAI, Type, FunctionDeclaration } from \"@google/genai\";\nimport { Octokit } from \"@octokit/rest\";\nimport * as fs from \"fs\";\nimport * as dotenv from \"dotenv\";\n\ndotenv.config();\n\nconst ai \u003d new GoogleGenAI({ apiKey: process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY });\nconst octokit \u003d new Octokit({ auth: process.env.GITHUB_TOKEN });\n\nconst OWNER \u003d \"your-github-username\";\nconst REPO \u003d \"your-repo-name\";\nconst BASE_BRANCH \u003d \"main\";\n\n// 1. Define GitHub Tool Declarations\nconst createOrUpdateFilesTool: FunctionDeclaration \u003d {\n  name: \"commit_files_to_github\",\n  description: \"Commit new or modified files directly to a designated GitHub branch.\",\n  parameters: {\n    type: Type.OBJECT,\n    properties: {\n      branchName: {\n        type: Type.STRING,\n        description: \"The target branch (e.g., \u0027phase-01-core-storage\u0027).\",\n      },\n      commitMessage: {\n        type: Type.STRING,\n        description: \"Clear git commit message explaining the additions/modifications.\",\n      },\n      files: {\n        type: Type.ARRAY,\n        items: {\n          type: Type.OBJECT,\n          properties: {\n            path: { type: Type.STRING, description: \"File path relative to repository root.\" },\n            content: { type: Type.STRING, description: \"The full, raw text content of the file.\" },\n          },\n          required: [\"path\", \"content\"],\n        },\n      },\n    },\n    required: [\"branchName\", \"commitMessage\", \"files\"],\n  },\n};\n\n// 2. GitHub Commit Handler using Octokit Trees\nasync function handleCommitFiles(args: any) {\n  const { branchName, commitMessage, files } \u003d args;\n  console.log(`\\n🚀 Applying commit to \u0027${branchName}\u0027: \"${commitMessage}\"`);\n\n  // Get base branch SHA\n  const { data: baseRef } \u003d await octokit.git.getRef({\n    owner: OWNER,\n    repo: REPO,\n    ref: `heads/${BASE_BRANCH}`,\n  });\n  const baseSha \u003d baseRef.object.sha;\n\n  // Create or verify branch\n  try {\n    await octokit.git.getRef({ owner: OWNER, repo: REPO, ref: `heads/${branchName}` });\n  } catch {\n    await octokit.git.createRef({\n      owner: OWNER,\n      repo: REPO,\n      ref: `heads/${branchName}`,\n      sha: baseSha,\n    });\n    console.log(`✔ Created branch: ${branchName}`);\n  }\n\n  // Create tree entries\n  const tree \u003d files.map((f: any) \u003d\u003e ({\n    path: f.path,\n    mode: \"100644\" as const,\n    type: \"blob\" as const,\n    content: f.content,\n  }));\n\n  const { data: newTree } \u003d await octokit.git.createTree({\n    owner: OWNER,\n    repo: REPO,\n    base_tree: baseSha,\n    tree,\n  });\n\n  // Commit\n  const { data: newCommit } \u003d await octokit.git.createCommit({\n    owner: OWNER,\n    repo: REPO,\n    message: commitMessage,\n    tree: newTree.sha,\n    parents: [baseSha],\n  });\n\n  // Update branch ref\n  await octokit.git.updateRef({\n    owner: OWNER,\n    repo: REPO,\n    ref: `heads/${branchName}`,\n    sha: newCommit.sha,\n  });\n\n  return {\n    success: true,\n    commitSha: newCommit.sha,\n    filesCommitted: files.map((f: any) \u003d\u003e f.path),\n  };\n}\n\n// 3. Execution Pipeline\nasync function executePhase(phaseName: string, phaseSpecPrompt: string) {\n  const repoContext \u003d fs.readFileSync(\"repomix-output.xml\", \"utf-8\");\n\n  const systemInstruction \u003d `\nYou are the Principal Systems Architect implementing AVOS (Autonomous Venture \u0026 Vertical Cowork Operating System) on Cloudflare Workers and Durable Objects.\nYou are tasked with implementing: ${phaseName}.\n\nCRITICAL GUIDELINES:\n1. Adhere strictly to the codebase style and existing Cloudflare bindings found in the repository context.\n2. When creating or modifying code, emit whole, production-ready files via the \u0027commit_files_to_github\u0027 tool.\n3. Target branch should be: feature/${phaseName.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]/g, \"-\")}.\n4. Never omit code with placeholders like \u0027// ... existing code ...\u0027. Provide full, working files.\n`;\n\n  const userPrompt \u003d `\nHere is the current repository context packed by Repomix:\n${repoContext}\n\n---\n\nHERE IS THE IMPLEMENTATION SPECIFICATION FOR THIS PHASE:\n${phaseSpecPrompt}\n\nReview the existing code, implement all required features, classes, and migrations for this phase, and commit the complete files to GitHub using the provided tool.\n`;\n\n  console.log(`Analyzing codebase and generating implementation for ${phaseName}...`);\n\n  const model \u003d \"gemini-2.5-flash\"; // Or your selected Gemini model\n  const chat \u003d ai.chats.create({\n    model,\n    config: {\n      systemInstruction,\n      tools: [{ functionDeclarations: [createOrUpdateFilesTool] }],\n    },\n  });\n\n  let response \u003d await chat.sendMessage({ message: userPrompt });\n\n  // Handle autonomous tool calls\n  while (response.functionCalls \u0026\u0026 response.functionCalls.length \u003e 0) {\n    for (const call of response.functionCalls) {\n      if (call.name \u003d\u003d\u003d \"commit_files_to_github\") {\n        const result \u003d await handleCommitFiles(call.args);\n        console.log(`Commit successful (${result.commitSha.slice(0, 7)}). Feeding result back to model...`);\n\n        // Send tool response back to Gemini\n        response \u003d await chat.sendMessage({\n          message: [\n            {\n              functionResponse: {\n                name: \"commit_files_to_github\",\n                response: result,\n              },\n            },\n          ],\n        });\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  console.log(\"\\n🏁 Phase Implementation Completed!\\nSummary:\\n\", response.text);\n}\n\n// RUN PHASE 1:\nconst phase1Spec \u003d fs.readFileSync(\"PHASE_1_SPEC.md\", \"utf-8\");\nexecutePhase(\"Phase-01-Storage-Core\", phase1Spec);\n```\n\n---\n\n# Method 2: If You Prefer Using the Google AI Studi