      "text": "Being on a phone changes everything, but it actually makes this **easier and more hands-free** if you use cloud automation.\n\nSince you are on a phone, **do not try to run manual copy-paste function calling inside the AI Studio web browser**. On mobile, copying massive JSON blobs with dozens of files back and forth is clumsy and error-prone.\n\nThe cleanest way to do this from a phone—with **zero PC required**—is using **GitHub Actions as your cloud runner**.\n\n---\n\n### The Phone-Only Workflow: How It Works\n\n```\n[ Your Phone Browser (Safari / Chrome) ]\n                  │\n                  ▼ (Tap \"Run Workflow\" in GitHub Actions tab)\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ ☁️ GITHUB ACTIONS CLOUD RUNNER (Free Ubuntu VM in GitHub\u0027s Cloud)            │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1. Automatically runs `npx repomix` to bundle your entire repository.       │\n│ 2. Sends the packed repo + Phase Spec to Gemini Flash via API.              │\n│ 3. Gemini generates the full production code for that phase.                │\n│ 4. The runner creates a new branch `feature/phase-01` and commits all files.│\n│ 5. Automatically opens a Pull Request on your repo.                         │\n└─────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                      │\n                                      ▼\n[ Your Phone: Inspect the visual PR diff \u0026 tap \"Merge\" on GitHub Mobile! ]\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Add Your Gemini API Key to GitHub (On Your Phone)\n\n1. Open your browser on your phone and go to your repository on `github.com`.\n2. Go to **Settings** $\\rightarrow$ **Secrets and variables** $\\rightarrow$ **Actions**.\n3. Tap **New repository secret**:\n   * Name: `GEMINI_API_KEY`\n   * Value: *(Paste your Gemini API key from Google AI Studio)*\n4. Tap **Add secret**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Create the Phase Specs File in Your Repo\n\nCreate a folder named `specs/` in your repo with your phase prompts. You can do this directly in the GitHub web interface by tapping **Add file** $\\rightarrow$ **Create new file**:\n\nCreate `specs/phase-1.md` and paste the Phase 1 spec (Features 1 through 6):\n```markdown\nImplement Phase 1: Multi-Tenant Core, Storage \u0026 Workspace Foundation:\n1. Enterprise Depth Hierarchy (Parent Company Space -\u003e Department Sub-Spaces)\n2. Sub-Space Inheritance \u0026 Isolation Matrix (Downward oversight, upward isolation, zero lateral bleed)\n3. Public vs. Private Project Access Control (SpaceDO SQLite ACL)\n4. Cloudflare Artifacts Git-for-Agents Engine (Zig-to-WASM Git in DO)\n5. @cloudflare/computer In-Memory Virtual POSIX Shell (just-bash in V8 + DO SQLite Virtual FS)\n6. Clean Namespace Separation (/workspace User Code vs. /.avos/ Internal Agent State)\n\nAdhere to Cloudflare Workers, Durable Objects, and TypeScript standards. Write full files without truncation.\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Create the Runner Script (`scripts/run-phase.mjs`)\n\nCreate a new file at `scripts/run-phase.mjs` in your repository:\n\n```javascript\nimport { GoogleGenAI, Type } from \"@google/genai\";\nimport { Octokit } from \"@octokit/rest\";\nimport * as fs from \"fs\";\n\nconst ai \u003d new GoogleGenAI({ apiKey: process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY });\nconst octokit \u003d new Octokit({ auth: process.env.GITHUB_TOKEN });\n\nconst [owner, repo] \u003d process.env.GITHUB_REPOSITORY.split(\"/\");\nconst phaseNum \u003d process.env.PHASE_NUMBER || \"1\";\nconst branchName \u003d `feature/phase-0${phaseNum}`;\n\n// 1. Tool schema for Gemini to return complete files\nconst commitTool \u003d {\n  name: \"commit_phase_files\",\n  description: \"Commit newly created or modified files to the repository branch.\",\n  parameters: {\n    type: Type.OBJECT,\n    properties: {\n      commitMessage: { type: Type.STRING, description: \"Detailed commit message\" },\n      files: {\n        type: Type.ARRAY,\n        items: {\n          type: Type.OBJECT,\n          properties: {\n            path: { type: Type.STRING, description: \"Relative path in repo\" },\n            content: { type: Type.STRING, description: \"Full raw file content\" }\n          },\n          required: [\"path\", \"content\"]\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    required: [\"commitMessage\", \"files\"]\n  }\n};\n\nasync function main() {\n  console.log(`🚀 Starting Phase ${phaseNum} Implementation...`);\n\n  // Read repomix context and phase spec\n  const repoContext \u003d fs.readFileSync(\"repomix-output.xml\", \"utf-8\");\n  const specPath \u003d `specs/phase-${phaseNum}.md`;\n  const phaseSpec \u003d fs.existsSync(specPath) \n    ? fs.readFileSync(specPath, \"utf-8\") \n    : `Implement Phase ${phaseNum} according to the master architecture specification.`;\n\n  const systemInstruction \u003d `\nYou are the Principal Edge Architect for AVOS on Cloudflare.\nYou will receive the codebase context (packed by Repomix) and a Phase Specification.\nImplement all necessary migrations, Durable Objects, Worker routes, and TypeScript interfaces.\nReturn complete, working file contents using the \u0027commit_phase_files\u0027 tool.\nNever use ellipses like \u0027// ... existing code ...\u0027.\n`;\n\n  const userPrompt \u003d `\n\u003d\u003d\u003d REPOSITORY CONTEXT (REPOMIX) \u003d\u003d\u003d\n${repoContext}\n\n\u003d\u003d\u003d PHASE ${phaseNum} SPECIFICATION \u003d\u003d\u003d\n${phaseSpec}\n\nImplement the phase and call \u0027commit_phase_files\u0027.\n`;\n\n  const chat \u003d ai.chats.create({\n    model: \"gemini-2.5-flash\",\n    config: {\n      systemInstruction,\n      tools: [{ functionDeclarations: [commitTool] }]\n    }\n  });\n\n  console.log(\"Waiting for Gemini response...\");\n  const response \u003d await chat.sendMessage({ message: userPrompt });\n\n  const call \u003d response.functionCalls?.find(c \u003d\u003e c.name \u003d\u003d\u003d \"commit_phase_files\");\n  if (!call) {\n    console.error(\"No commit tool called. Raw response:\\n\", response.text);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  const { commitMessage, files } \u003d call.args;\n  console.log(`Received ${files.length} files to commit: \"${commitMessage}\"`);\n\n  // Get base branch SHA (main)\n  const { data: baseRef } \u003d await octokit.git.getRef({\n    owner,\n    repo,\n    ref: \"heads/main\"\n  });\n  const baseSha \u003d baseRef.object.sha;\n\n  // Create branch\n  try {\n    await octokit.git.createRef({\n      owner,\n      repo,\n      ref: `refs/heads/${branchName}`,\n      sha: baseSha\n    });\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.log(`Branch ${branchName} already exists, updating it.`);\n  }\n\n  // Build Git Tree\n  const tree \u003d files.map(f \u003d\u003e ({\n    path: f.path,\n    mode: \"100644\",\n    type: \"blob\",\n    content: f.content\n  }));\n\n  const { data: newTree } \u003d await octokit.git.createTree({\n    owner,\n    repo,\n    base_tree: baseSha,\n    tree\n  });\n\n  const { data: commit } \u003d await octokit.git.createCommit({\n    owner,\n    repo,\n    message: commitMessage,\n    tree: newTree.sha,\n    parents: [baseSha]\n  });\n\n  await octokit.git.updateRef({\n    owner,\n    repo,\n    ref: `heads/${branchName}`,\n    sha: commit.sha,\n    force: true\n  });\n\n  // Automatically create a Pull Request\n  try {\n    const { data: pr } \u003d await octokit.pulls.create({\n      owner,\n      repo,\n      title: `AVOS: Implement Phase ${phaseNum}`,\n      head: branchName,\n      base: \"main\",\n      body: `### Automated Phase ${phaseNum} Implementation\\n\\n**Commit:** ${commitMessage}\\n\\n**Files Changed (${files.length}):**\\n${files.map(f \u003d\u003e `- \\`${f.path}\\``).join(\"\\n\")}`\n    });\n    console.log(`✔ Pull Request Created: ${pr.html_url}`);\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.log(\"PR already exists or error creating PR:\", e.message);\n  }\n}\n\nmain().catch(err \u003d\u003e {\n  console.error(err);\n  process.exit(1);\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Create the GitHub Actions Workflow (`.github/workflows/run-phase.yml`)\n\nCreate a file at `.github/workflows/run-phase.yml`:\n\n```yaml\nname: Run AVOS Phase\n\non:\n  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      phase_number:\n        description: \u0027Phase number to implement (1 to 8)\u0027\n        required: true\n        default: \u00271\u0027\n\njobs:\n  implement-phase:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    permissions:\n      contents: write\n      pull-requests: write\n\n    steps:\n      - name: Checkout Code\n        uses: actions/checkout@v4\n\n      - name: Setup Node.js\n        uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 22\n\n      - name: Install Dependencies\n        run: |\n          npm install @google/genai @octokit/rest repomix\n\n      - name: Pack Repository with Repomix\n        run: |\n          npx repomix --style xml --output repomix-output.xml --ignore \"**/node_modules/**,**/.wrangler/**,**/dist/**,package-lock.json\"\n\n      - name: Run Phase with Gemini\n        env:\n          GEMINI_API_KEY: ${{ secrets.GEMINI_API_KEY }}\n          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n          PHASE_NUMBER: ${{ github.event.inputs.phase_number }}\n        run: |\n          node scripts/run-phase.mjs\n```\n\n---\n\n### How to Run Each Phase from Your Phone (In 3 Taps)\n\nOnce you commit those setup files to `main`, running any phase takes 10 seconds on your mobile browser:\n\n1. Open **GitHub** in your phone\u0027s browser and go to your repository.\n2. Tap the **Actions** tab.\n3. Tap **Run AVOS Phase** on the left menu.\n4. Tap the **Run workflow** dropdown:\n   * Input the phase number: `1` (or `2`, `3`, etc.).\n   * Tap the green **Run workflow** button.\n\n### What Happens:\n* GitHub\u0027s cloud spins up an Ubuntu VM.\n* It packs your current repo using `repomix`.\n* It calls Gemini 2.5 Flash via API.\n* Gemini generates all the files for Phase 1.\n* The script commits them to `feature/phase-01` and opens a **Pull Request**.\n* You get a notification on your phone: open the PR, review the visual diff, and tap **Merge pull request**!\n\nFor Phase 2, simply merge Phase 1, tap **Actions** $\\rightarrow$ **Run workflow**, type `2`, and run again. No PC required.",
