      "text": "Your strategy is **the gold standard for large-codebase agent orchestration**. \n\nBy splitting the process into:\n1. **Pass 1 (Discovery):** Repomix `--compress` (Tree-sitter signatures only) $\\rightarrow$ Gemini picks exact files.\n2. **Pass 2 (Targeted Repomix):** Full fidelity packing of *only* those selected files.\n3. **Pass 3 (Chunked Implementation):** Small, single-responsibility chunk files so Gemini never hits the output token ceiling (truncation).\n4. **Rate Limit Delays \u0026 Native Git:** Pausing between calls to respect RPM/TPM limits and using native `git` inside the GitHub Actions runner instead of fragile API calls.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Architecture of the Two-Pass Chunked Runner\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                          PER CHUNK PIPELINE                                 │\n└─────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                      │\n                                      ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ PASS 1: REPO MAP \u0026 FILE SELECTION                                           │\n│ 1. Run `npx repomix --compress` (Extracts outlines, 80% smaller).           │\n│ 2. Send compressed map + `chunk-0X.md` to Gemini.                           │\n│ 3. Gemini returns JSON: `{ \"includeFiles\": [\"src/do/SpaceDO.ts\", \"...\"] }`  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                      │\n                                      ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ PASS 2: TARGETED PACKING \u0026 IMPLEMENTATION                                    │\n│ 1. Run `npx repomix --include \"\u003cselected_files\u003e\"` (Full fidelity + context).│\n│ 2. Send targeted bundle + `chunk-0X.md` to Gemini.                          │\n│ 3. Gemini returns complete file contents (well within 8k output limit).     │\n│ 4. Runner writes files to disk, runs `git add . \u0026\u0026 git commit`.             │\n└─────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                      │\n                                      ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ RATE LIMIT PACING \u0026 LOOP                                                    │\n│ 1. Sleep 15–20 seconds (Guarantees staying under 15 RPM / TPM limits).      │\n│ 2. Proceed to `chunk-0(X+1).md` until all chunks for the phase are done.    │\n│ 3. Final step: `git push origin feature/phase-0X` and open PR!              │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Directory Structure in Your GitHub Repo\n\nOrganize your `specs/` directory so each phase has its own folder of atomic chunks:\n\n```\nyour-repo/\n├── specs/\n│   ├── phase-1/\n│   │   ├── chunk-01-depth-hierarchy.md\n│   │   ├── chunk-02-subspace-inheritance.md\n│   │   ├── chunk-03-project-access-acl.md\n│   │   ├── chunk-04-artifacts-git-mesh.md\n│   │   ├── chunk-05-computer-virtual-posix.md\n│   │   └── chunk-06-namespace-separation.md\n│   └── phase-2/\n│       ├── chunk-01-execution-ladder.md\n│       └── ...\n├── scripts/\n│   └── run-phase.mjs\n└── .github/\n    └── workflows/\n        └── run-phase.yml\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. The Two-Pass Runner Script (`scripts/run-phase.mjs`)\n\nThis script handles the file selection pass, targeted packaging, implementation, git commits, and API rate-limiting delays:\n\n```javascript\nimport { GoogleGenAI, Type } from \"@google/genai\";\nimport { execSync } from \"child_process\";\nimport * as fs from \"fs\";\nimport * as path from \"path\";\n\nconst ai \u003d new GoogleGenAI({ apiKey: process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY });\nconst phaseNum \u003d process.env.PHASE_NUMBER || \"1\";\nconst branchName \u003d `feature/phase-0${phaseNum}`;\nconst specsDir \u003d `specs/phase-${phaseNum}`;\n\n// Delay helper to respect RPM/TPM limits\nconst sleep \u003d (ms) \u003d\u003e new Promise((resolve) \u003d\u003e setTimeout(resolve, ms));\n\n// Tool Schema 1: File Selection Pass\nconst selectFilesTool \u003d {\n  name: \"select_relevant_files\",\n  description: \"Select the specific files needed to read and modify for this task chunk.\",\n  parameters: {\n    type: Type.OBJECT,\n    properties: {\n      includeFiles: {\n        type: Type.ARRAY,\n        items: { type: Type.STRING },\n        description: \"List of relative file paths or globs needed for this chunk.\"\n      },\n      reasoning: { type: Type.STRING, description: \"Why these files were selected.\" }\n    },\n    required: [\"includeFiles\"]\n  }\n};\n\n// Tool Schema 2: Code Implementation Pass\nconst writeCodeTool \u003d {\n  name: \"apply_chunk_code\",\n  description: \"Write complete files for this task chunk.\",\n  parameters: {\n    type: Type.OBJECT,\n    properties: {\n      commitMessage: { type: Type.STRING, description: \"Git commit message\" },\n      files: {\n        type: Type.ARRAY,\n        items: {\n          type: Type.OBJECT,\n          properties: {\n            path: { type: Type.STRING },\n            content: { type: Type.STRING, description: \"Full, untruncated file content\" }\n          },\n          required: [\"path\", \"content\"]\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    required: [\"commitMessage\", \"files\"]\n  }\n};\n\nasync function runPass1_SelectFiles(compressedMap, chunkSpec, chunkName) {\n  console.log(`\\n🔍 [Pass 1: ${chunkName}] Asking Gemini to identify relevant files...`);\n  \n  const response \u003d await ai.models.generateContent({\n    model: \"gemini-2.5-flash\",\n    contents: `\nYou are analyzing a codebase to decide which files are required to implement this specific chunk.\nDo not select the entire repository. Select ONLY the files that must be read, referenced, or modified.\n\n\u003d\u003d\u003d COMPRESSED REPOSITORY MAP (Tree-Sitter Signatures) \u003d\u003d\u003d\n${compressedMap}\n\n\u003d\u003d\u003d CHUNK SPECIFICATION \u003d\u003d\u003d\n${chunkSpec}\n`,\n    config: {\n      systemInstruction: \"You are an expert software planner. Call \u0027select_relevant_files\u0027 with the minimal set of files needed.\",\n      tools: [{ functionDeclarations: [selectFilesTool] }]\n    }\n  });\n\n  const call \u003d response.functionCalls?.find(c \u003d\u003e c.name \u003d\u003d\u003d \"select_relevant_files\");\n  if (!call || !call.args.includeFiles || call.args.includeFiles.length \u003d\u003d\u003d 0) {\n    console.log(\"No specific files selected or new files being created. Using base configuration.\");\n    return [\"package.json\", \"wrangler.toml\", \"tsconfig.json\"];\n  }\n\n  console.log(`✔ Selected ${call.args.includeFiles.length} files: ${call.args.includeFiles.join(\", \")}`);\n  return call.args.includeFiles;\n}\n\nasync function runPass2_ImplementChunk(targetedContext, chunkSpec, chunkName) {\n  console.log(`🛠️ [Pass 2: ${chunkName}] Implementing chunk code...`);\n\n  const response \u003d await ai.models.generateContent({\n    model: \"gemini-2.5-flash\",\n    contents: `\n\u003d\u003d\u003d RELEVANT CODEBASE FILES (Full Fidelity) \u003d\u003d\u003d\n${targetedContext}\n\n\u003d\u003d\u003d CHUNK SPECIFICATION TO IMPLEMENT \u003d\u003d\u003d\n${chunkSpec}\n`,\n    config: {\n      systemInstruction: `\nYou are the Principal Systems Architect implementing AVOS on Cloudflare Workers \u0026 Durable Objects.\nImplement the chunk specification completely.\nAlways provide FULL, production-ready file contents using \u0027apply_chunk_code\u0027.\nNever truncate with comments like \u0027// ... rest of code ...\u0027.\n`,\n      tools: [{ functionDeclarations: [writeCodeTool] }]\n    }\n  });\n\n  const call \u003d response.functionCalls?.find(c \u003d\u003e c.name \u003d\u003d\u003d \"apply_chunk_code\");\n  if (!call) {\n    throw new Error(`Failed to call \u0027apply_chunk_code\u0027. Output:\\n${response.text}`);\n  }\n\n  return call.args;\n}\n\nasync function main() {\n  if (!fs.existsSync(specsDir)) {\n    console.error(`Directory ${specsDir} does not exist! Please create chunk specs.`);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  const chunkFiles \u003d fs.readdirSync(specsDir)\n    .filter(f \u003d\u003e f.endsWith(\".md\"))\n    .sort();\n\n  if (chunkFiles.length \u003d\u003d\u003d 0) {\n    console.error(`No .md chunk files found in ${specsDir}`);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  console.log(`Found ${chunkFiles.length} chunks for Phase ${phaseNum}:`);\n  chunkFiles.forEach(c \u003d\u003e console.log(` - ${c}`));\n\n  // Setup Git branch\n  execSync(`git checkout -B ${branchName}`);\n\n  for (let i \u003d 0; i \u003c chunkFiles.length; i++) {\n    const chunkFile \u003d chunkFiles[i];\n    const chunkName \u003d path.basename(chunkFile, \".md\");\n    const chunkSpec \u003d fs.readFileSync(path.join(specsDir, chunkFile), \"utf-8\");\n\n    console.log(`\\n\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d`);\n    console.log(`⏩ Starting Chunk [${i + 1}/${chunkFiles.length}]: ${chunkName}`);\n    console.log(`\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d`);\n\n    // 1. Generate Compressed Repomix Map\n    console.log(\"📦 Generating compressed repo map...\");\n    execSync(`npx repomix --compress --style xml --output repomix-compressed.xml --ignore \"**/node_modules/**,**/.wrangler/**,**/dist/**,specs/**,package-lock.json\"`, { stdio: \"ignore\" });\n    const compressedMap \u003d fs.readFileSync(\"repomix-compressed.xml\", \"utf-8\");\n\n    // 2. Pass 1: Select Files\n    const includeFiles \u003d await runPass1_SelectFiles(compressedMap, chunkSpec, chunkName);\n    \n    // Rate limit sleep (10 seconds)\n    await sleep(10000);\n\n    // 3. Generate Targeted Repomix Bundle\n    console.log(\"🎯 Generating targeted repomix bundle for selected files...\");\n    const includeArg \u003d includeFiles.map(f \u003d\u003e `\"${f}\"`).join(\",\");\n    try {\n      execSync(`npx repomix --include ${includeArg} --style xml --output repomix-targeted.xml`, { stdio: \"ignore\" });\n    } catch {\n      // Fallback if globs miss\n      execSync(`npx repomix --style xml --output repomix-targeted.xml --ignore \"**/node_modules/**,**/.wrangler/**,**/dist/**,specs/**\"`, { stdio: \"ignore\" });\n    }\n    const targetedContext \u003d fs.readFileSync(\"repomix-targeted.xml\", \"utf-8\");\n\n    // 4. Pass 2: Implement Chunk\n    const { commitMessage, files } \u003d await runPass2_ImplementChunk(targetedContext, chunkSpec, chunkName);\n\n    // 5. Write Files to Disk natively\n    for (const f of files) {\n      const dir \u003d path.dirname(f.path);\n      if (!fs.existsSync(dir)) fs.mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });\n      fs.writeFileSync(f.path, f.content, \"utf-8\");\n      console.log(`  💾 Wrote: ${f.path}`);\n    }\n\n    // 6. Commit Locally via Git\n    execSync(`git add .`);\n    execSync(`git commit -m \"feat(phase-${phaseNum}): [${chunkName}] ${commitMessage}\"`);\n    console.log(`✔ Committed chunk: \"${commitMessage}\"`);\n\n    // 7. Rate limit sleep between chunks (15 seconds)\n    if (i \u003c chunkFiles.length - 1) {\n      console.log(\"⏳ Cooling down for 15s to respect Gemini RPM/TPM limits...\");\n      await sleep(15000);\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Final push of all chunk commits to GitHub\n  console.log(`\\n🚀 Pushing branch ${branchName} to GitHub...`);\n  execSync(`git push -u origin ${branchName} --force`);\n\n  // Open Pull Request via GitHub CLI (pre-installed in GitHub Actions)\n  try {\n    execSync(`gh pr create --title \"AVOS: Complete Phase ${phaseNum}\" --body \"Automated chunk-by-chunk implementation of Phase ${phaseNum}.\" --base main --head ${branchName}`);\n    console.log(\"🎉 Pull Request successfully created!\");\n  } catch {\n    console.log(\"PR already exists or created.\");\n  }\n}\n\nmain().catch(err \u003d\u003e {\n  console.error(\"Fatal Error:\", err);\n  process.exit(1);\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. The Updated GitHub Actions Workflow (`.github/workflows/run-phase.yml`)\n\nMake sure your GitHub Action grants permissions for `gh pr create` and configures the git author:\n\n```yaml\nname: Run AVOS Phase\n\non:\n  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      phase_number:\n        description: \u0027Phase number (e.g. 1)\u0027\n        required: true\n        default: \u00271\u0027\n\njobs:\n  implement-phase:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    permissions:\n      contents: write\n      pull-requests: write\n\n    steps:\n      - name: Checkout Code\n        uses: actions/checkout@v4\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 0\n\n      - name: Setup Node.js\n        uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 22\n\n      - name: Configure Git Author\n        run: |\n          git config user.name \"github-actions[bot]\"\n          git config user.email \"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\"\n\n      - name: Install Dependencies\n        run: |\n          npm install @google/genai repomix\n\n      - name: Run Chunked Phase Engine\n        env:\n          GEMINI_API_KEY: ${{ secrets.GEMINI_API_KEY }}\n          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n          PHASE_NUMBER: ${{ github.event.inputs.phase_number }}\n        run: |\n          node scripts/run-phase.mjs\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Ready-to-Commit: Phase 1 Broken Down into 6 Chunks\n\nBelow are the 6 bite-sized chunk files for **Phase 1**. You can create these files directly from your phone browser on GitHub under `specs/phase-1/`:\n\n#### Chunk 1: `specs/phase-1/chunk-01-depth-hierarchy.md`\n```markdown\n# Phase 1 - Chunk 01: Enterprise Depth Hierarchy Database Schemas\nTarget: Create or update SQLite D1 migrations and types for parent spaces and department sub-spaces.\n1. Add `parent_space_id` (NULL for root, text for sub-spaces) and `depth` (0 for parent, 1 for department) to `spaces` table.\n2. Create `sub_space_cross_grants` table for cross-subspace permissions.\n3. Export TypeScript interfaces in `packages/types/src/space-hierarchy.ts`.\n```\n\n#### Chunk 2: `specs/phase-1/chunk-02-subspace-inheritance.md`\n```markdown\n# Phase 1 - Chunk 02: Sub-Space Inheritance \u0026 Access Middleware\nTarget: Implement permission validation in `workers/spaces/src/middleware/hierarchy.ts`.\n1. Downward inheritance: Parent Owners/Admins pass authorization checks for all child spaces.\n2. Strict upward isolation: Sub-space members attempting to access parent space routes get 403 Forbidden.\n3. Zero lateral bleed: Reject sibling space requests unless a valid `cross_space_grant` token is verified.\n```\n\n#### Chunk 3: `specs/phase-1/chunk-03-project-access-acl.md`\n```markdown\n# Phase 1 - Chunk 03: Public vs Private Project Access Control\nTarget: Implement project visibility rules in `SpaceDO.ts`.\n1. Ensure `projects` table supports `visibility` (\"public\" | \"private\").\n2. Create `project_members` table in `SpaceDO` SQLite.\n3. In `readWorkspaceFile` and `listThreads`, enforce that private projects return 404 Not Found to uninvited space members.\n```\n\n#### Chunk 4: `specs/phase-1/chunk-04-artifacts-git-mesh.md`\n```markdown\n# Phase 1 - Chunk 04: Cloudflare Artifacts Git Mesh Service\nTarget: Implement `ArtifactsGitService.ts` in `workers/agents/src/services/`.\n1. Implement `createProjectRepo(project