      "text": "**Defining the Platform\u0027s Scope**\n\nI\u0027m currently focused on defining the scope of AVOS. I am analyzing the user\u0027s need for modular \"Project Kinds\" like `product_dev`, and their incorporation of \"Coding Plugins\" and a central agent engine (`NaelaoAgentDO`). I\u0027m working to fully understand how these elements function together.\n\n\n**Exploring Agent Architectures**\n\nI\u0027m now investigating how to empower users to create custom \"Coding Agents\" easily. My aim is to enable the seamless definition, publication, and swapping of different coding architectures. I am thinking about how to facilitate this process, particularly in relation to complex techniques such as Repomix. Moreover, I am focused on the platform\u0027s ability to offer advanced features and ensure that coding plugins can compete with top AI coding platforms. I must ensure the inclusion of essential capabilities like file graphs, AST indexing, and LSP integration.\n\n\n**Decomposing Agent Strategy**\n\nI\u0027m now focusing on decomposing the agent execution loop. My goal is a composable \"Cognitive Strategy Pipeline\" to define Agent behavior. This pipeline, defined by an `AgentStrategy` or `WorkflowStrategy`, should consist of a context selector, planning step, execution loop, and verification step. The idea is that these strategies can be authored as scripts or plugin bundles.\n\n\n**Analyzing Core Code Primitives**\n\nI\u0027m now diving deep into core code primitives for AVOS, focusing on AST parsing with Tree-sitter in Wasm for structural code understanding. The edge code graph, leveraging SQLite, is also a priority for efficient dependency indexing. I\u0027m exploring incremental caching with Merkle trees and hybrid search using vector embeddings and BM25 to achieve robust code analysis. Lastly, I\u0027m defining how these primitives can be used on Cloudflare Edge.\n\n\n**Constructing Plugin Bundles**\n\nI\u0027m now figuring out the architecture for \"Vertical Coding Plugin\" bundles. I\u0027m focusing on defining the structure, incorporating a `plugin.json` for viewport and strategy specifications. Each plugin would have pre-bundled tools, memory systems (like a semantic code index) and should incorporate concepts such as the \"Repomix Chunked Loop\" or \"Fast-LSP CodeAct\".\n\n\n**Defining the Code SDK**\n\nI am now structuring the `ctx.code` SDK for plugin authors, focusing on key functionalities: finding symbols, generating call graphs and repo maps, and verifying builds. I aim to create a unified interface that offers incremental AST indexing with web-tree-sitter, a relational dependency graph through SQLite, and smart context packers for robust code analysis. I\u0027m also considering the competitive advantage of this modular approach over vertical systems.\n\n\n",
