ing Orchestration Approaches**\n\nI\u0027m now investigating alternative architectures. I see that Palantir\u0027s AIP decouples data and actions from the orchestration, and I am currently figuring out how to reconcile that with Cloudflare\u0027s Workers and Agents SDK.\n\n\n**Clarifying Subagent Roles**\n\nI\u0027m now clarifying the roles. A subagent acts as an ephemeral task runner on a payload. Cloudflare\u0027s Agents SDK offers stateful Durable Objects where the Agent lives. Workflows are one tool for durable background execution. It seems I am aiming for the correct level of abstraction; the subagent shouldn\u0027t mimic the manager, it should be a pure agentic function, a job.\n\n\n**Refining `ctx` for Subagents**\n\nI\u0027m now zeroing in on a cleaner `ctx` for subagents. It seems that the Workflow will act as the durable scheduler, calling the subagent when necessary. The parent agent or SpaceDO owns the UI elements. I\u0027ll focus on keeping `ctx` functional, avoiding complex context passing, and I am exploring the use of `ctx.ai`, `ctx.fs`, `ctx.cli`, and `ctx.step` for core subagent functions. I am now refining the Repomix example with this new, clean model.\n\n\n**Constructing Subagent Functions**\n\nI\u0027m now focused on the agent\u0027s ability to create and register dynamic subagents. The agent can write a TypeScript file—let\u0027s say `/.avos/shared/workflows/repomix-builder.ts`—containing a clean multi-step workflow function. This allows for defining subagent tasks using steps, like compressing a map, selecting files via an AI model, targeted packing, and implementation.\n\n\n**Validating Core Architectural Design**\n\nI\u0027ve confirmed the initial diagnosis: equipping subagents with the full OS context is an architectural blunder. I\u0027m solidifying the rationale by highlighting four crucial flaws. Serialization issues, thread management conflicts, latency spikes, and potential prompt failures underscore the need for a more streamlined approach. I\u0027m now comparing this with how Palantir AIP and Cloudflare Agents actually work to avoid these problems.\n\n\n",
