      "text": "Here is the complete, reconciled **Master Implementation Plan (Phases 1–8)** incorporating every finalized breakthrough—including **Background Gadget Indexers**, **Declarative Step Pipelines**, and the **Asymmetric Subagent Workflow Engine**—followed by the complete **Step-by-Step Mobile Implementation Flow** (running the entire build from your phone via GitHub Actions).\n\n---\n\n# PART 1: THE UPDATED MASTER IMPLEMENTATION PHASES (1–8)\n\nEach phase is strictly sequenced so that no feature is implemented before its dependencies exist.\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                   CHRONOLOGICAL IMPLEMENTATION PHASES                                  │\n├─────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 1 │ Multi-Tenant Core \u0026 Storage Foundation     │ Durable Objects, SQLite FS, Git Mesh, Subspaces │\n├─────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 2 │ Compute Ladder \u0026 Runtime Hypervisor        │ 6-Tier Execution, FUSE Sync, Containers, Wasm   │\n├─────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 3 │ Action Space, Virtual CLI \u0026 Edge Security  │ `ctx` SDK, JIT CLIs, Outbound Workers, Vault    │\n├─────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 4 │ Cognition, Memory, Knowledge \u0026 Ingestion   │ Dual-Tier DAGs, Vectorize ACLs, Parse 5, Search │\n├─────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 5 │ 4-Tier Thread Hierarchy \u0026 Concurrency      │ Team/Task/Scratchpad Threads, OCC, Git PR Engine│\n├─────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 6 │ Project Kinds, Viewports \u0026 Stateful Gadgets│ 7 Studio Kinds, Background Indexers, DO Facets  │\n├─────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 7 │ Asymmetric Workflows, Telephony \u0026 Voice    │ Slim Subagent Workflows, Crons, Calls WebRTC    │\n├─────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 8 │ Billing, Marketplace, Distribution \u0026 Shell │ Credits, Subscriptions, Exporter, Radar, UI     │\n└─────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### PHASE 1: Multi-Tenant Core, Storage \u0026 Workspace Foundation (Items 1–6)\n*Prerequisite: Clean repository. Bedrock database and filesystem layer.*\n\n1. **Enterprise Depth Hierarchy:** Parent Company Space (Depth 0) $\\rightarrow$ Department Sub-Spaces (Depth 1) in D1 schema.\n2. **Sub-Space Inheritance \u0026 Isolation Matrix:** Downward admin oversight, strict upward isolation, and zero lateral bleed.\n3. **Public vs. Private Project Access Control:** In-DO SQLite project visibility and access-list verification.\n4. **Cloudflare Artifacts Git-for-Agents Engine:** Zig-to-WASM Git server running in Durable Objects for 10ms branching and commit trees.\n5. **`@cloudflare/computer` Virtual POSIX Shell:** In-memory `just-bash` parser executing against DO SQLite `workspace_files`.\n6. **Clean Namespace Separation:** Strict isolation between `/workspace/` (user code) and `/.avos/` (internal agent state).\n\n---\n\n### PHASE 2: Compute Ladder \u0026 Invisible Runtime Hypervisor (Items 7–18)\n*Prerequisite: Phase 1 (Requires the SQLite VFS and Git Artifacts engine).*\n\n7. **6-Tier Cloudflare Execution Ladder:** Dynamic escalation routing (T1 Virtual FS $\\rightarrow$ T6 Container).\n8. **Invisible Runtime Hypervisor:** Minimalist tool surface (`Bash`, `Read`, `Edit`, `Browser`, `Delegate`) routing transparently.\n9. **`ArtifactFS` FUSE Driver:** Lazy, on-demand hydration of repository files into Linux Containers in 5ms.\n10. **4-Dimension State Synchronization Engine:** Bidirectional sync across Filesystem, Shell CWD/Env, Git HEAD, and SQLite DB.\n11. **95/5 Compute Arbitrage:** Sub-5ms V8 Isolate execution for 95% of tasks + 60-second container micro-sleep countdown.\n12. **In-Isolate WebAssembly Python (Pyodide):** Lightweight Python runs in V8; auto-elevates to Tier 6 only for native C-extensions.\n13. **Tier 4 Cloudflare Kitesurf Agent Browser:** 30MB low-memory DOM extraction with transparent Tier 5 Chromium fallback.\n14. **Virtual Display Container Automation:** Xvfb + Fluxbox + noVNC WebSockets for desktop GUI automation.\n15. **Multiplexed Persistent gRPC Bridge:** Sub-5ms binary communication between Durable Objects and Containers over TCP sockets.\n16. **Instant Zero-Copy Branch Micro-Forking:** Programmatic 10ms repository forks for subagents and private scratchpads.\n17. **Turn-by-Turn Git Time Machine:** Automatic commit generation per tool turn with 1-click historical rollback.\n18. **Reasoning-Aware Git Blame:** Front-matter commit attribution storing the technical rationale behind every code change.\n\n---\n\n### PHASE 3: Action Space, Virtual CLI \u0026 Zero-Trust Security (Items 19–32)\n*Prerequisite: Phase 2 (Requires execution primitives and hypervisor router).*\n\n19. **Universal Runtime SDK (`ctx`):** Typed API exposed to scripts (`fs`, `project`, `space`, `vault`, `cli`, `browser`).\n20. **Universal Vault Layer \u0026 Outbound Workers:** Zero-leak secret injection at the edge network boundary.\n21. **WriteGuard Mutation Interceptor:** Edge proxy SQL AST and destructive tool filter.\n22. **Virtual CLI Interception Engine:** Translates CLI commands (`stripe`, `gh`, `r2`, `jq`) into edge REST/Wasm calls in \u003c5ms.\n23. **Just-In-Time (JIT) Virtual CLI Synthesis:** Agent micro-synthesizes missing CLI commands using `ctx.cli.register`.\n24. **Gatekeeper Capability-Based Cross-Subspace Delegation:** Cryptographically signed, attenuated resource grants.\n25. **3-Tier Connector Scoping:** Space-Shared, Project-Bound, and User-Personal credential separation.\n26. **Public Channel Tool Stripping \u0026 MCP-UI Privacy Bridge:** Strips personal tools in public rooms; forks to private scratchpads.\n27. **Single-Use Ephemeral Action Grants:** In-channel 15-second capability signing via MCP v2 Elicitation cards.\n28. **Turn-Holder vs. Referent Mention Router:** First `@mention` gets the turn lock; subsequent mentions become context references.\n29. **Sequential Turn Delegation (`ctx.agent.delegate`):** Orderly handoffs between agents preventing multi-agent collision.\n30. **Demonstration-to-Skill Distillation Engine:** Execution traces parameterize into TypeScript skills in `/.avos/shared/skills/`.\n31. **Zero-Turn Tool Catalog in Prompt:** Injects available CLI index into system prompt; implementation fetched on-demand.\n32. **Declarative Step Pipelines (Execution Hooks):** Pre-flight context hooks and verification gates configured via JSON.\n\n---\n\n### PHASE 4: Cognition, Memory, Knowledge \u0026 Ingestion (Items 33–47)\n*Prerequisite: Phase 3 (Requires security boundaries, Vault, and SDK tools).*\n\n33. **Universal Agent Execution Kernel (`NaelaoAgentDO`):** Single REPL engine powering all functional roles.\n34. **Dynamic 4-Layer System Prompt Assembly:** Universal Kernel $\\rightarrow$ Business Identity $\\rightarrow$ `SOUL.md` $\\rightarrow$ User Overrides.\n35. **Hardware-Enforced Role Firewalls (`AgentFirewall`):** Physical schema stripping based on declared functional role.\n36. **Dual-Tier Planner-Worker Asymmetry Engine:** `/goal` command creates a clean Task DAG; anonymous workers execute code.\n37. **3-Layer Hybrid Memory Architecture:** Active Turn RAM $\\rightarrow$ Deterministic `PROJECT.md` $\\rightarrow$ Vectorize Long-Term Semantic.\n38. **Cross-Thread Context Isolation:** Pristine context per thread; past thread message logs are never carried over.\n39. **Semantic Fact Gating (Hindsight Memory):** Learnings distilled to atomic rules; retrieved only if cosine similarity is $\u003e0.80$.\n40. **In-Flight Milestone Squashing (`compact_context`):** Archives older message history to D1 while preserving active task state.\n41. **Jack Dorsey Mini-AGI Sovereign Permission Model:** Decentralized, role-clamped intelligence per employee.\n42. **Hardware-Level Vector Pre-Filtering:** Integer role ranks (1–5) and bitmasks evaluated directly inside Cloudflare Vectorize.\n43. **Mathematical Bitmask Evaluation \u0026 XML Envelopes:** Wraps dynamic retrieval chunks in `\u003ccontext_chunk\u003e` untrusted tags.\n44. **Cohere Parse 5 (`parse-v5.0`) Edge Ingestion Pipeline:** Converts enterprise PDFs, faxes, and complex tables into Markdown.\n45. **Google Search AI Mode at the Edge:** Sub-50ms KV semantic caching + Dense/Sparse Hybrid Reciprocal Rank Fusion ($k\u003d60$).\n46. **Interactive Numbered Citation Footnotes:** Markdown stream anchored directly to verified chunk coordinates in R2.\n47. **Inter-Project Stateless MCP v2 Mesh:** Every project exposes `/mcp` via `createMcpHandler` over Streamable HTTP.\n\n---\n\n### PHASE 5: 4-Tier Thread Hierarchy, Concurrency \u0026 Collaboration (Items 48–61)\n*Prerequisite: Phase 4 (Requires agent kernel, memory boundaries, and Git mesh).*\n\n48. **4-Tier Thread Hierarchy:** Team Rooms, Task Workstations, System Consult Lanes, and Private Scratchpads.\n49. **Solo 2-Tier Cockpit vs. Multi-User 4-Tier Digital Office:** Dynamic elevation when a teammate is invited.\n50. **Optimistic Concurrency Control (OCC):** Atomic Compare-And-Swap file writes verified against SHA-256 base hashes.\n51. **Distributed File-Level Mutex Locks:** 30-second TTL locks in `ConcurrencyDO` for multi-file refactoring runs.\n52. **Inline Pull Request (PR) Review Cards:** Interactive visual AST diff cards with 1-click fast-forward merges.\n53. **Upstream Staleness Detection \u0026 Auto-Rebase:** Real-time divergence detection and automated conflict-free rebasing.\n54. **Multi-Branch Parallel Model Benchmarking Races:** Forks 3 branches for 3 models in parallel; merges the winning test code.\n55. **Real-Time Multiplayer Presence via `WsHubDO`:** WebSockets broadcast active file editing and presence cursors.\n56. **Invoker-Attested Split-Actor Model:** Thread-isolated DO actors prevent cross-user conversation and credential bleed.\n57. **Vertical-Scoped Certified Model Whitelist (`whitelist_only`):** Server-side compliance gate enforcing approved models.\n58. **Private LoRA Model Dynamic Edge Loading:** Routes `custom/*` models to Workers AI with dynamic LoRA adapter injection.\n59. **Sovereign Enterprise Air-Gapped Local AI Engine:** `LocalTunnelDO` connects on-premise Ollama/vLLM GPUs over WebSockets.\n60. **Strict Air-Gapped Space Compliance Lock:** Physically blocks external cloud AI endpoints when compliance mode is active.\n61. **Finite Task Project Auto-Sleep:** Hibernates Durable Objects and clears alarms when the Task DAG reaches 100%.\n\n---\n\n### PHASE 6: Project Kinds, Viewports \u0026 Stateful Gadgets (Items 62–74)\n*Prerequisite: Phase 5 (Requires collaborative threads, viewports, and execution engine).*\n\n62. **Dual-Mode Operating System:** Declarative switch between `autonomous_venture` and `vertical_cowork`.\n63. **Canvas-First / Domain Viewport Architecture:** Center canvas mounts live code editors, redline diffs, or financial grids.\n64. **Full-Stack Product Engineering Studio (`product_dev`):** CodeWorkspaceCanvas with Node/Linux container backend.\n65. **Document Redline \u0026 Contract Studio (`doc_studio`):** DocumentRedlineCanvas with Parse 5 and legal linters.\n66. **Inbound Customer Messaging Desk (`customer_bot`):** SupportTicketsCanvas clamped strictly to Tier 1 Safe RAG.\n67. **Model Training \u0026 LoRA Studio (`model_studio`):** ModelStudioCanvas with autonomous dataset synthesis and eval playground.\n68. **Autonomous Growth \u0026 Scraping Desk (`growth_engine`):** GrowthFunnelCanvas with Tier 4 Kitesurf scraping runners.\n69. **On-Demand Micro-App Studio (`app_studio`):** AppStudioCanvas for prompt-to-application full-stack builds.\n70. **Cloudflare OS Stateful Gadgets:** Micro-apps running on Dynamic Workers with dedicated DO Facet SQLite databases.\n71. **Background Stateful Gadget Indexers:** Domain indexers (Code Graph, Ledger Reconciler) running silently as gadgets.\n72. **Auto-Generated Stateless MCP v2 Endpoints for Gadgets:** Automatically wraps gadget SQLite tables into `/mcp` tools.\n73. **Bidirectional MCP-UI Real-Time Canvas Streaming:** UI iframe actions stream into the agent loop in real time.\n74. **Generative In-Chat Dynamic UI Widgets:** AI streams interactive input cards (date pickers, sliders) directly in chat.\n\n---\n\n### PHASE 7: Asymmetric Subagents, Telephony \u0026 Voice (Items 75–86)\n*Prerequisite: Phase 6 (Requires project studios, micro-apps, and workflows).*\n\n75. **Asymmetric Subagent Topology:** Subagents are ephemeral functions in workflows; only Parent Agents own threads and UI.\n76. **Slimmed-Down `SubagentContext`:** Strips thread/session bloat, exposing only `ai`, `fs`, `cli`, `vault`, and `step`.\n77. **Repomix-Style Chunked Subagent Workflow:** Multi-step durable workflow packing and committing code chunk by chunk.\n78. **Cloudflare Workflows Harness Pattern:** Pure `execute(step, ctx)` functions auto-compile to `WorkflowEntrypoint`.\n79. **Project-Universal, Bot-Attributed Scheduled Crons:** Registered in `SpaceDO` SQLite; decoupled from chat context.\n80. **Compact Background Job Receipt Cards:** 2-line expandable cards in thread timeline; heavy stdout offloaded to R2.\n81. **Unified Space-Wide Shared Calendar \u0026 CRM Plane:** Authoritative booking table in `SpaceDO` shared by all projects.\n82. **Native Duplex Telephony via `@cloudflare/voice`:** Cloudflare Calls WebRTC SFU + Workers AI Whisper + Llama 3.3.\n83. **24/7 AI Phone Receptionist Call Desk (`kind: \"voice_agent\"`):** Handles phone appointments, clamped to Tier 1 RAG.\n84. **Dual-Thread Voice Structure:** Management Threads (config chat) vs. Call Session Threads (audio playback, transcripts).\n85. **Automated Outbound Telephony Reminder Workflows:** Crons query tomorrow\u0027s appointments and trigger confirmation calls.\n86. **Native In-Composer Voice Dictation:** Mic button in chat transcribes spoken audio via Workers AI Whisper for $0 compute.\n\n---\n\n### PHASE 8: Billing, Marketplace, Distribution \u0026 Shell (Items 87–100)\n*Prerequisite: Phase 7 (The entire OS must be functional before selling and billing).*\n\n87. **Standardized Credit Metering:** Unified consumption unit (1 Credit \u003d $0.01 USD).\n88. **Unified SaaS Subscription Plans:** Free BYOK, Starter ($29/mo), Pro ($99–$150/mo), Enterprise ($299+/mo).\n89. **Self-Funding Autonomous Business Loop:** Storefront sales settle to `wallet_ledger`; compute debits automatically.\n90. **1-Click Venture Exporter:** Serializes live business into clean, sanitized `blueprint.json` in R2.\n91. **Automated PII \u0026 Vault Secret Scrubber:** Strips live credentials, emails, and transaction logs on export.\n92. **Automated Security Rating \u0026 Sandbox Test Gate:** Background workflow boots template in test DO and issues rating.\n93. **2-Tier Developer Marketplace:** Freemium Tiered SaaS ($0 install, feature-gated) vs. Fixed One-Off License (Buy-Out).\n94. **Mutual Exclusivity Marketplace Pricing Rule:** Fixed-price templates must unlock all features permanently.\n95. **Attribution-Based Commission Split:** 40% Developer Referral / 20% Organic Marketplace / 100% Upfront Buy-Out.\n96. **Cumulative Per-Tier Cycle Quotas:** $20 plan capped at 6 months ($48); $50 plan at 12 months; $150+ lifetime recurring.\n97. **Anti-Plan-Hopping D1 Ledger:** Tracks cumulative usage per tier (`cycles_paid_entry_tier`), immune to plan switching.\n98. **Dynamic First-Month Price Floor Formula Protection:** Enforces `Min Month 1 Price \u003d Base Plan + ∑ Plugin Wholesale Fees`.\n99. **Discover Page Live Market Radar:** Analyzes real-time global traffic surges via Cloudflare Pipelines and Apache Iceberg on R2.\n100. **Progressive Disclosure Interface:** \"Business Mode\" (Apple simplicity) default vs. \"Developer Mode\" (full Git observability).\n\n---\n\n# PART 2: THE MOBILE-FIRST STEP-BY-STEP IMPLEMENTATION FLOW\n\nBecause you are working exclusively from a mobile phone, this workflow eliminates local terminal commands, manual copy-pasting, and long-context output limits. **GitHub Actions acts as your automated cloud developer.**\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Initial Phone Setup (One-Time)\n\n1. Open your mobile browser, go to your repository on GitHub, and navigate to **Settings** $\\rightarrow$ **Secrets and variables** $\\rightarrow$ **Actions**.\n2. Tap **New repository secret**:\n   * Name: `GEMINI_API_KEY`\n   * Value: *(Your Gemini API key from Google AI Studio)*\n3. Tap **Add secret**.\n4. Scroll down to **Workflow permissions** (in **Actions** $\\rightarrow$ **General**):\n   * Select **Read and write permissions**.\n   * Check **Allow GitHub Actions to create and approve pull requests**.\n   * Tap **Save**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Create the Workflow File on GitHub Mobile\n\nUsing the GitHub mobile web interface, tap **Add file** $\\rightarrow$ **Create new file** at `.github/workflows/run-phase.yml`:\n\n```yaml\nname: Run AVOS Phase\n\non:\n  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      phase_number:\n        description: \u0027Phase number to implement (1 to 8)\u0027\n        required: true\n        default: \u00271\u0027\n\njobs:\n  implement-phase:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    permissions:\n      contents: write\n      pull-requests: write\n\n    steps:\n      - name: Checkout Code\n        uses: actions/checkout@v4\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 0\n\n      - name: Setup Node.js\n        uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: 22\n\n      - name: Configure Git Author\n        run: |\n          git config user.name \"github-actions[bot]\"\n          git config user.email \"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\"\n\n      - name: Install Dependencies\n        run: |\n          npm install @google/genai repomix\n\n      - name: Run Two-Pass Chunked Engine\n        env:\n          GEMINI_API_KEY: ${{ secrets.GEMINI_API_KEY }}\n          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n          GH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n          PHASE_NUMBER: ${{ github.event.inputs.phase_number }}\n        run: |\n          node scripts/run-phase.mjs\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Create the Two-Pass Runner Script (`scripts/run-phase.mjs`)\n\nCreate `scripts/run-phase.mjs` in your repository:\n\n```javascript\nimport { GoogleGenAI, Type } from \"@google/genai\";\nimport { execSync } from \"child_process\";\nimport * as fs from \"fs\";\nimport * as path from \"path\";\n\nconst ai \u003d new GoogleGenAI({ apiKey: process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY });\nconst phaseNum \u003d process.env.PHASE_NUMBER || \"1\";\nconst branchName \u003d `feature/phase-0${phaseNum}`;\nconst specsDir \u003d `specs/phase-${phaseNum}`;\n\nconst sleep \u003d (ms) \u003d\u003e new Promise((resolve) \u003d\u003e setTimeout(resolve, ms));\n\n// Schema 1: File Selection Pass (Pass 1)\nconst selectFilesTool \u003d {\n  name: \"select_relevant_files\",\n  description: \"Select the minimal set of files needed to read, reference, or modify for this chunk.\",\n  parameters: {\n    type: Type.OBJECT,\n    properties: {\n      includeFiles: {\n        type: Type.ARRAY,\n        items: { type: Type.STRING },\n        description: \"List of relative file paths needed.\"\n      },\n      reasoning: { type: Type.STRING, description: \"Why these files were selected.\" }\n    },\n    required: [\"includeFiles\"]\n  }\n};\n\n// Schema 2: Code Implementation Pass (Pass 2)\nconst writeCodeTool \u003d {\n  name: \"apply_chunk_code\",\n  description: \"Emit complete, working, production-ready files for this chunk.\",\n  parameters: {\n    type: Type.OBJECT,\n    properties: {\n      commitMessage: { type: Type.STRING, description: \"Descriptive git commit message\" },\n      files: {\n        type: Type.ARRAY,\n        items: {\n          type: Type.OBJECT,\n          properties: {\n            path: { type: Type.STRING },\n            content: { type: Type.STRING, description: \"Full file content without truncation\" }\n          },\n          required: [\"path\", \"content\"]\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    required: [\"commitMessage\", \"files\"]\n  }\n};\n\nasync function runPass1_SelectFiles(compressedMap, chunkSpec, chunkName) {\n  console.log(`\\n🔍 [Pass 1: ${chunkName}] Requesting file selection from Gemini...`);\n  \n  const response \u003d await ai.models.generateContent({\n    model: \"gemini-2.5-flash\",\n    contents: `\nYou are analyzing a codebase to select ONLY the files necessary to implement this task chunk.\nDo not select irrelevant files.\n\n\u003d\u003d\u003d COMPRESSED REPOSITORY MAP (Tree-Sitter Signatures) \u003d\u003d\u003d\n${compressedMap}\n\n\u003d\u003d\u003d CHUNK SPECIFICATION \u003d\u003d\u003d\n${chunkSpec}\n`,\n    config: {\n      systemInstruction: \"You are an expert software architect. Call \u0027select_relevant_files\u0027.\",\n      tools: [{ functionDeclarations: [selectFilesTool] }]\n    }\n  });\n\n  const call \u003d response.functionCalls?.find(c \u003d\u003e c.name \u003d\u003d\u003d \"select_relevant_files\");\n  if (!call || !call.args.includeFiles || call.args.includeFiles.length \u003d\u003d\u003d 0) {\n    console.log(\"No specific files selected. Defaulting to project configuration files.\");\n    return [\"package.json\", \"wrangler.toml\", \"tsconfig.json\"];\n  }\n\n  console.log(`✔ Selected ${call.args.includeFiles.length} files: ${call.args.includeFiles.join(\", \")}`);\n  return call.args.includeFiles;\n}\n\nasync function runPass2_ImplementChunk(targetedContext, chunkSpec, chunkName) {\n  console.log(`🛠️ [Pass 2: ${chunkName}] Implementing production code...`);\n\n  const response \u003d await ai.models.generateContent({\n    model: \"gemini-2.5-flash\",\n    contents: `\n\u003d\u003d\u003d TARGETED CODEBASE FILES \u003d\u003d\u003d\n${targetedContext}\n\n\u003d\u003d\u003d CHUNK SPECIFICATION \u003d\u003d\u003d\n${chunkSpec}\n`,\n    config: {\n      systemInstruction: `\nYou are the Principal Systems Architect implementing AVOS on Cloudflare Workers \u0026 Durable Objects.\nImplement the chunk completely. Provide full, working files using \u0027apply_chunk_code\u0027.\nNever truncate with comments like \u0027// ... existing code ...\u0027.\n`,\n      tools: [{ functionDeclarations: [writeCodeTool] }]\n    }\n  });\n\n  const call \u003d response.functionCalls?.find(c \u003d\u003e c.name \u003d\u003d\u003d \"apply_chunk_code\");\n  if (!call) {\n    throw new Error(`Failed to call \u0027apply_chunk_code\u0027. Raw response:\\n${response.text}`);\n  }\n\n  return call.args;\n}\n\nasync function main() {\n  if (!fs.existsSync(specsDir)) {\n    console.error(`Directory ${specsDir} does not exist! Please create chunk spec files.`);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  const chunkFiles \u003d fs.readdirSync(specsDir)\n    .filter(f \u003d\u003e f.endsWith(\".md\"))\n    .sort();\n\n  if (chunkFiles.length \u003d\u003d\u003d 0) {\n    console.error(`No .md chunk files found in ${specsDir}`);\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  console.log(`Found ${chunkFiles.length} chunks for Phase ${phaseNum}`);\n\n  // Ensure target branch exists\n  execSync(`git checkout -B ${branchName}`);\n\n  for (let i \u003d 0; i \u003c chunkFiles.length; i++) {\n    const chunkFile \u003d chunkFiles[i];\n    const chunkName \u003d path.basename(chunkFile, \".md\");\n    const chunkSpec \u003d fs.readFileSync(path.join(specsDir, chunkFile), \"utf-8\");\n\n    console.log(`\\n\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d`);\n    console.log(`⏩ Processing Chunk [${i + 1}/${chunkFiles.length}]: ${chunkName}`);\n    console.log(`\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d`);\n\n    // 1. Pack compressed repository outline (Tree-sitter signatures)\n    execSync(`npx repomix --compress --style xml --output repomix-compressed.xml --ignore \"**/node_modules/**,**/.wrangler/**,**/dist/**,specs/**,package-lock.json\"`, { stdio: \"ignore\" });\n    const compressedMap \u003d fs.readFileSync(\"repomix-compressed.xml\", \"utf-8\");\n\n    // 2. Pass 1: Select Files\n    const includeFiles \u003d await runPass1_SelectFiles(compressedMap, chunkSpec, chunkName);\n    await sleep(10000); // 10s cooldown\n\n    // 3. Pack targeted slice\n    const includeArg \u003d includeFiles.map(f \u003d\u003e `\"${f}\"`).join(\",\");\n    try {\n      execSync(`npx repomix --include ${includeArg} --style xml --output repomix-targeted.xml`, { stdio: \"ignore\" });\n    } catch {\n      execSync(`npx repomix --style xml --output repomix-targeted.xml --ignore \"**/node_modules/**,**/.wrangler/**,**/dist/**,specs/**\"`, { stdio: \"ignore\" });\n    }\n    const targetedContext \u003d fs.readFileSync(\"repomix-targeted.xml\", \"utf-8\");\n\n    // 4. Pass 2: Generate code\n    const { commitMessage, files } \u003d await runPass2_ImplementChunk(targetedContext, chunkSpec, chunkName);\n\n    // 5. Write files to workspace disk\n    for (const f of files) {\n      const d