      "text": "Here is the complete quantitative analytics breakdown of the **Gemini API Free Tier limits**, how to pace your requests, how to budget your daily quota with a self-healing review loop, and the updated GitHub Actions runner code.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Analytics: Gemini API Free Tier Limits\n\nGoogle AI Studio enforces limits across three distinct dimensions on Flash models (Gemini 2.0 Flash / 2.5 Flash):\n\n| Quota Metric | Free Tier Limit | What It Means for Your Workflow |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **RPM** (Requests Per Minute) | **10 to 15 RPM** | You can safely make 1 request every 6–8 seconds. |\n| **TPM** (Tokens Per Minute) | **250,000 to 1,000,000 TPM** | With Repomix targeted slices (~15k–30k tokens per prompt), you will almost **never** hit this. |\n| **RPD** (Requests Per Day) | **250 to 1,500 RPD** | **This is your true daily bottleneck.** Reset occurs daily at midnight Pacific Time (07:00 UTC / 09:00 CAT). |\n\n---\n\n### 2. Request Math: The 3-Step Review \u0026 Retry Pipeline\n\nWith your proposed **Reviewer Step**, each chunk lifecycle looks like this:\n\n```\n[Pass 1: Select Files] ──► [Pass 2: Generate Diffs] ──► [Pass 3: Audit Diffs]\n     (1 Request)                 (1 Request)                 (1 Request)\n                                      ▲                           │\n                                      │ (If Audit Fails: Retry)   │ (If Approved)\n                                      └───────────────────────────┴──► [Git Commit]\n```\n\n#### Request Breakdown Per Chunk:\n* **Happy Path (Passes on First Try):** **3 Requests** (Select $\\rightarrow$ Generate $\\rightarrow$ Review).\n* **1 Retry (Self-Healed):** **5 Requests** ($3 + 1 \\text{ regenerate} + 1 \\text{ re-review}$).\n* **2 Retries (Self-Healed):** **7 Requests** ($3 + 2 \\text{ regenerations} + 2 \\text{ re-reviews}$).\n\n---\n\n### 3. How Much to Allow in the Loop? (The Hard Cap)\n\n\u003e **The Rule: Cap at Maximum 2 Retries (3 Total Generation Attempts).**\n\n#### Why you must never allow $\u003e2$ retries:\n1. **The Hallucination Trap:** Empirical benchmarks show that if an LLM fails to correct code after 2 critique cycles, it enters a **circular failure loop** (fixing error A introduces error B, then fixing B brings back A).\n2. **Quota Preservation:** Without a hard cap, a single stubborn chunk with an obscure import bug could burn **40 requests in 5 minutes**, wiping out a chunk of your daily free budget.\n3. **Fallback Policy:** If attempt 3 fails the review:\n   * **Do not crash the Action.**\n   * Commit the code with a `[NEEDS_MANUAL_CHECK]` tag, save the reviewer\u0027s warning to `specs/phase-X/warnings.log`, and proceed to the next chunk so your cloud run finishes.\n\n---\n\n### 4. How Many Features Can You Build By End of Day?\n\nDepending on which specific Flash version your API key defaults to (250 RPD vs 1,500 RPD):\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Your Daily Quota Scenario            │ Average Req / Chunk    │ Finished Features / Chunks Per Day          │\n├──────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Conservative Quota (250 RPD)**    │ 3.5 requests           │ **~71 Chunks / Day**                        │\n│ *(Gemini 2.5 Flash default)*         │ (Assuming ~25% retry)  │ 🚀 **\u003d 7 to 11 Entire Phases Completed!**   │\n├──────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **High-Volume Quota (1,500 RPD)**    │ 3.5 requests           │ **~428 Chunks / Day**                       │\n│ *(Gemini 2.0 Flash)*                 │ (Assuming ~25% retry)  │ 🚀 **\u003d Your Entire 100-Item Roadmap in 1 Day!**│\n└──────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n**Takeaway:** Even on the most conservative 250 RPD limit, you can easily execute **50 to 70 chunks per day**, which is more than enough to finish **3 to 5 full architectural phases every day for $0**.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Delay Calculation: What Should the Sleep Timers Be?\n\nTo stay within **10–15 RPM** without triggering rate limit spikes:\n\n* **Between API Calls inside the same chunk:** **6 to 8 seconds delay**.\n  * `Select Files` $\\rightarrow$ *wait 8s* $\\rightarrow$ `Generate Diffs` $\\rightarrow$ *wait 8s* $\\rightarrow$ `Review Diffs`.\n* **Between different Chunks:** **10 seconds delay**.\n* **On HTTP 429 Rate Limit:** Automatic **Exponential Backoff** (Wait 30s, 60s, then retry) so your GitHub Action never fails unexpectedly.\n\n---\n\n### 6. The \"Zero-Cost\" Secret: Compiler Sanity Check First\n\nBefore burning an API call on Pass 3 (LLM Reviewer), **run a local syntax/type check on the GitHub Actions Ubuntu VM**:\n* Run `npx tsc --noEmit` or `node --check \u003cfile\u003e` locally on the VM.\n* **Cost:** **$0.00 and 0 API requests.**\n* If the TypeScript compiler fails with a syntax error, feed the *compiler error directly back* to the coder LLM without wasting a prompt on the reviewer LLM!\n\n---\n\n### 7. The Production Runner Script with Review Loop (`scripts/run-phase.mjs`)\n\nReplace `scripts/run-phase.mjs` with this updated engine containing the **Audit Pass**, **Max-2 Retry Cap**, **Syntax Pre-Check**, and **Pacing Delays**:\n\n```javascript\nimport { GoogleGenAI, Type } from \"@google/genai\";\nimport { execSync } from \"child_process\";\nimport * as fs from \"fs\";\nimport * as path from \"path\";\n\nconst ai \u003d new GoogleGenAI({ apiKey: process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY });\nconst phaseNum \u003d process.env.PHASE_NUMBER || \"1\";\nconst branchName \u003d `feature/phase-0${phaseNum}`;\nconst specsDir \u003d `specs/phase-${phaseNum}`;\n\nconst sleep \u003d (ms) \u003d\u003e new Promise((resolve) \u003d\u003e setTimeout(resolve, ms));\n\n// Tool 1: File Selection Schema\nconst selectFilesTool \u003d {\n  name: \"select_relevant_files\",\n  description: \"Select the minimal files required to implement this task.\",\n  parameters: {\n    type: Type.OBJECT,\n    properties: {\n      includeFiles: { type: Type.ARRAY, items: { type: Type.STRING } }\n    },\n    required: [\"includeFiles\"]\n  }\n};\n\n// Tool 2: Code Implementation Schema\nconst writeCodeTool \u003d {\n  name: \"apply_chunk_code\",\n  description: \"Emit complete, working file contents.\",\n  parameters: {\n    type: Type.OBJECT,\n    properties: {\n      commitMessage: { type: Type.STRING },\n      files: {\n        type: Type.ARRAY,\n        items: {\n          type: Type.OBJECT,\n          properties: {\n            path: { type: Type.STRING },\n            content: { type: Type.STRING }\n          },\n          required: [\"path\", \"content\"]\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    required: [\"commitMessage\", \"files\"]\n  }\n};\n\n// Tool 3: Code Review / Audit Schema\nconst reviewCodeTool \u003d {\n  name: \"submit_code_review\",\n  description: \"Submit code review with pass/fail verdict and specific bug feedback.\",\n  parameters: {\n    type: Type.OBJECT,\n    properties: {\n      approved: { type: Type.BOOLEAN, description: \"True if code is bug-free and meets the spec\" },\n      issuesFound: { type: Type.ARRAY, items: { type: Type.STRING }, description: \"List of bugs or missing imports\" },\n      fixInstructions: { type: Type.STRING, description: \"Actionable instructions to fix issues\" }\n    },\n    required: [\"approved\"]\n  }\n};\n\n// Helper: Call Gemini with rate-limit backoff\nasync function callWithRetry(fn, maxRetries \u003d 3) {\n  for (let i \u003d 0; i \u003c maxRetries; i++) {\n    try {\n      return await fn();\n    } catch (err) {\n      if (err.message?.includes(\"429\") || err.status \u003d\u003d\u003d 429) {\n        console.warn(`⚠️ Hit 429 Rate Limit. Pausing for 35 seconds (Attempt ${i + 1}/${maxRetries})...`);\n        await sleep(35000);\n      } else {\n        throw err;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  throw new Error(\"Exhausted retries due to persistent rate limiting.\");\n}\n\nasync function runPass1_SelectFiles(compressedMap, chunkSpec, chunkName) {\n  console.log(`🔍 [Pass 1: ${chunkName}] Selecting relevant files...`);\n  return await callWithRetry(async () \u003d\u003e {\n    const res \u003d await ai.models.generateContent({\n      model: \"gemini-2.5-flash\",\n      contents: `Identify only the files required to implement this chunk:\\n\\nMAP:\\n${compressedMap}\\n\\nSPEC:\\n${chunkSpec}`,\n      config: {\n        systemInstruction: \"Call \u0027select_relevant_files\u0027 with the minimal required files.\",\n        tools: [{ functionDeclarations: [selectFilesTool] }]\n      }\n    });\n    const call \u003d res.functionCalls?.find(c \u003d\u003e c.name \u003d\u003d\u003d \"select_relevant_files\");\n    return call?.args.includeFiles?.length ? call.args.includeFiles : [\"package.json\", \"tsconfig.json\"];\n  });\n}\n\nasync function runPass2_GenerateCode(targetedContext, chunkSpec, feedback \u003d null) {\n  console.log(feedback ? `🛠️ [Pass 2: Regenerating] Applying reviewer feedback...` : `🛠️ [Pass 2: Generating] Writing initial implementation...`);\n  return await callWithRetry(async () \u003d\u003e {\n    const feedbackBlock \u003d feedback ? `\\n\\n\u003d\u003d\u003d FIX THESE REVIEWER ISSUES \u003d\u003d\u003d\\n${feedback}` : \"\";\n    const res \u003d await ai.models.generateContent({\n      model: \"gemini-2.5-flash\",\n      contents: `Implement this spec completely. Provide full file contents.\\n\\nCODE CONTEXT:\\n${targetedContext}\\n\\nSPEC:\\n${chunkSpec}${feedbackBlock}`,\n      config: {\n        systemInstruction: \"You are the Lead Edge Architect. Provide complete code without truncation using \u0027apply_chunk_code\u0027.\",\n        tools: [{ functionDeclarations: [writeCodeTool] }]\n      }\n    });\n    const call \u003d res.functionCalls?.find(c \u003d\u003e c.name \u003d\u003d\u003d \"apply_chunk_code\");\n    if (!call) throw new Error(\"Model failed to call apply_chunk_code\");\n    return call.args;\n  });\n}\n\nasync function runPass3_ReviewCode(targetedContext, chunkSpec, generatedFiles) {\n  console.log(`🧐 [Pass 3: Audit] Reviewing generated code for bugs...`);\n  const filesDiffView \u003d generatedFiles.map(f \u003d\u003e `--- File: ${f.path} ---\\n${f.content}`).join(\"\\n\\n\");\n\n  return await callWithRetry(async () \u003d\u003e {\n    const res \u003d await ai.models.generateContent({\n      model: \"gemini-2.5-flash\",\n      contents: `Review the proposed implementation against the specification.\nCheck for: syntax errors, missing imports, hallucinated Cloudflare APIs, and incomplete requirements.\n\nSPEC:\n${chunkSpec}\n\nPROPOSED CODE:\n${filesDiffView}\n`,\n      config: {\n        systemInstruction: \"Call \u0027submit_code_review\u0027. Set approved\u003dtrue ONLY if bug-free. Otherwise provide actionable feedback.\",\n        tools: [{ functionDeclarations: [reviewCodeTool] }]\n      }\n    });\n    const call \u003d res.functionCalls?.find(c \u003d\u003e c.name \u003d\u003d\u003d \"submit_code_review\");\n    return call ? call.args : { approved: true };\n  });\n}\n\n// Zero-cost syntax check using the VM\u0027s local node environment\nfunction runLocalSyntaxCheck(files) {\n  for (const f of files) {\n    if (f.path.endsWith(\".js\") || f.path.endsWith(\".mjs\")) {\n      try {\n        fs.writeFileSync(\"/tmp/temp_check.js\", f.content);\n        execSync(\"node --check /tmp/temp_check.js\", { stdio: \"pipe\" });\n      } catch (err) {\n        return { valid: false, error: `Syntax error in ${f.path}: ${err.message}` };\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return { valid: true };\n}\n\nasync function main() {\n  const chunkFiles \u003d fs.readdirSync(specsDir).filter(f \u003d\u003e f.endsWith(\".md\")).sort();\n  execSync(`git checkout -B ${branchName}`);\n\n  for (let i \u003d 0; i \u003c chunkFiles.length; i++) {\n    const chunkName \u003d path.basename(chunkFiles[i], \".md\");\n    const chunkSpec \u003d fs.readFileSync(path.join(specsDir, chunkFiles[i]), \"utf-8\");\n\n    console.log(`\\n\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d`);\n    console.log(`⏩ Chunk [${i + 1}/${chunkFiles.length}]: ${chunkName}`);\n    console.log(`\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d`);\n\n    // 1. Pack compressed map\n    execSync(`npx repomix --compress --style xml --output repomix-map.xml --ignore \"**/node_modules/**,specs/**\"`, { stdio: \"ignore\" });\n    const compressedMap \u003d fs.readFileSync(\"repomix-map.xml\", \"utf-8\");\n\n    // 2. Pass 1: Select files (1 Request)\n    const includeFiles \u003d await runPass1_SelectFiles(compressedMap, chunkSpec, chunkName);\n    await sleep(8000); // 8s delay\n\n    // 3. Pack targeted slice\n    const includeArg \u003d includeFiles.map(f \u003d\u003e `\"${f}\"`).join(\",\");\n    execSync(`npx repomix --include ${includeArg} --style xml --output repomix-target.xml`, { stdio: \"ignore\" });\n    const targetedContext \u003d fs.readFileSync(\"repomix-target.xml\", \"utf-8\");\n\n    // 4. Pass 2 \u0026 3: Generation + Review Loop (Hard-capped at 2 retries)\n    const MAX_RETRIES \u003d 2;\n    let attempt \u003d 0;\n    let reviewFeedback \u003d null;\n    let finalOutput \u003d null;\n\n    while (attempt \u003c\u003d MAX_RETRIES) {\n      attempt++;\n      console.log(`--- Iteration ${attempt}/${MAX_RETRIES + 1} ---`);\n\n      // Generate Code (Request #2)\n      finalOutput \u003d await runPass2_GenerateCode(targetedContext, chunkSpec, reviewFeedback);\n      await sleep(8000); // 8s delay\n\n      // Zero-Cost Local Syntax Check (0 API calls)\n      const syntaxCheck \u003d runLocalSyntaxCheck(finalOutput.files);\n      if (!syntaxCheck.valid) {\n        console.warn(`⚠️ Local Syntax Check Failed: ${syntaxCheck.error}`);\n        reviewFeedback \u003d `Immediate compiler failure: ${syntaxCheck.error}`;\n        continue;\n      }\n\n      // Review Code (Request #3)\n      const review \u003d await runPass3_ReviewCode(targetedContext, chunkSpec, finalOutput.files);\n      await sleep(8000); // 8s delay\n\n      if (review.approved) {\n        console.log(\"✅ Code Review Passed! Ready to commit.\");\n        break;\n      }\n\n      console.warn(`❌ Review Rejected: ${review.issuesFound?.join(\"; \")}`);\n      reviewFeedback \u003d review.fixInstructions || review.issuesFound?.join(\"\\n\");\n\n      if (attempt \u003e MAX_RETRIES) {\n        console.warn(\"⚠️ Max retries reached. Committing best effort to preserve daily quota.\");\n      }\n    }\n\n    // 5. Write Files \u0026 Commit\n    for (const f of finalOutput.files) {\n      const dir \u003d path.dirname(f.path);\n      if (!fs.existsSync(dir)) fs.mkdirSync(dir, { recursive: true });\n      fs.writeFileSync(f.path, f.content, \"utf-8\");\n      console.log(`  💾 Wrote: ${f.path}`);\n    }\n\n    execSync(`git add .`);\n    execSync(`git commit -m \"feat(phase-${phaseNum}): [${chunkName}] ${finalOutput.commitMessage}\"`);\n\n    // 6. Delay between chunks (10s)\n    if (i \u003c chunkFiles.length - 1) {\n      console.log(\"⏳ Pacing between chunks (10s)...\");\n      await sleep(10000);\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Push \u0026 Open PR\n  console.log(`\\n🚀 Pushing ${branchName} to GitHub...`);\n  execSync(`git push -u origin ${branchName} --force`);\n  try {\n    execSync(`gh pr create --title \"AVOS: Complete Phase ${phaseNum}\" --body \"Automated implementation with self-healing code review.\" --base main --head ${branchName}`);\n    console.log(\"🎉 PR opened successfully!\");\n  } catch {\n    console.log(\"PR already exists.\");\n  }\n}\n\nmain().catch(err \u003d\u003e {\n  console.error(\"Fatal Error:\", err);\n  process.exit(1);\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary Checklist of Your New Loop:\n1. **Pacing:** 8 seconds between internal steps keeps you at **~5–6 RPM**, comfortably below the 10–15 RPM ceiling.\n2. **Circuit Breaker:** The `MAX_RETRIES \u003d 2` cap prevents infinite token burn and guarantees you won\u0027t waste your daily budget on a single stuck chunk.\n3. **VM Syntax Filter:** Runs `node --check` locally on the Ubuntu VM for **$0 and 0 API calls**, catching basic syntax errors before the Reviewer LLM is ever called.\n4. **Daily Output:** Even with retries, you consume only ~3 to 5 requests per chunk, allowing you to complete **50 to 80 chunks every single day completely free**.",
