      "parts": [{
        "text": "Here is the complete quantitative analytics breakdown of the **Gemini API Free Tier limits**,"
      }, {
        "text": " how to pace your requests, how to budget your daily quota with a self-healing review loop, and the updated GitHub"
      }, {
        "text": " Actions runner code.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Analytics: Gemini API Free Tier Limits\n\nGoogle AI Studio enforces limits across"
      }, {
        "text": " three distinct dimensions on Flash models (Gemini 2.0 Flash / 2.5 Flash):\n\n| Qu"
      }, {
        "text": "ota Metric | Free Tier Limit | What It Means for Your Workflow |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n"
      }, {
        "text": "| **RPM** (Requests Per Minute) | **10 to 15 RPM**"
      }, {
        "text": " | You can safely make 1 request every 6–8 seconds. |\n"
      }, {
        "text": "| **TPM** (Tokens Per Minute) | **250,000 to 1,000,0"
      }, {
        "text": "00 TPM** | With Repomix targeted"
      }, {
        "text": " slices (~15k–30k tokens per prompt), you will almost **never** hit this. |\n|"
      }, {
        "text": " **RPD** (Requests Per Day) | **250 to 1,500 RPD**"
      }, {
        "text": " | **This is your true daily bottleneck.** Reset occurs"
      }, {
        "text": " daily at midnight Pacific Time (07:00 UTC / 09:00 CAT)."
      }, {
        "text": " |\n\n---\n\n### 2. Request Math: The 3-Step Review \u0026 Retry Pipeline\n\nWith your proposed **Review"
      }, {
        "text": "er Step**, each chunk lifecycle looks like this:\n\n```\n[Pass 1: Select Files] ──►"
      }, {
        "text": " [Pass 2: Generate Diffs] ──► [Pass 3: Audit Diffs]\n     (1 Request)                 "
      }, {
        "text": "(1 Request)                 (1 Request)\n                                      ▲                           │\n                                      │ (If Audit Fails:"
      }, {
        "text": " Retry)   │ (If Approved)\n                                      └───────────────────────────┴──► [Git Commit]\n```\n\n####"
      }, {
        "text": " Request Breakdown Per Chunk:\n* **Happy Path (Passes on First Try):** **3 Requests** (Select"
      }, {
        "text": " $\\rightarrow$ Generate $\\rightarrow$ Review).\n* **1 Retry (Self-Healed):** **5 Requests** ($3 + 1"
      }, {
        "text": " \\text{ regenerate} + 1 \\text{ re-review}$).\n* **2 Retries (Self-Healed):** **7 Requests"
      }, {
        "text": "** ($3 + 2 \\text{ regenerations} + 2 \\text{ re-reviews}$).\n\n---"
      }, {
        "text": "\n\n### 3. How Much to Allow in the Loop? (The Hard Cap)\n\n\u003e **The Rule:"
      }, {
        "text": " Cap at Maximum 2 Retries (3 Total Generation Attempts).**\n\n#### Why you must never allow $\u003e2$ retries:\n1."
      }, {
        "text": " **The Hallucination Trap:** Empirical benchmarks show that if an LLM fails to correct code after 2 critique cycles"
      }, {
        "text": ", it enters a **circular failure loop** (fixing error A introduces error B, then fixing B brings back A).\n2. **Quota Preservation"
      }, {
        "text": ":** Without a hard cap, a single stubborn chunk with an obscure import bug could burn **40 requests in 5 minutes**, wiping"
      }, {
        "text": " out a chunk of your daily free budget.\n3. **Fallback Policy:** If attempt 3 fails the review:"
      }, {
        "text": "\n   * **Do not crash the Action.**\n   * Commit the code with a `"
      }, {
        "text": "[NEEDS_MANUAL_CHECK]` tag, save the reviewer\u0027s warning to `specs/phase-X/warnings.log`, and proceed"
      }, {
        "text": " to the next chunk so your cloud run finishes.\n\n---\n\n### 4. How Many Features Can You Build By End of Day?\n\nDepending on"
      }, {
        "text": " which specific Flash version your API key defaults to (250 RPD vs 1,500 RPD"
      }, {
        "text": "):\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────"
      }, {
        "text": "┬─────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Your Daily Quota Scenario            │ Average Req / Chunk    │ Finished Features / Chunks Per"
      }, {
        "text": " Day          │\n├──────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Conservative Quota (250 RPD)**"
      }, {
        "text": "    │ 3.5 requests           │ **~71 Chunks / Day**                        │\n│ *(Gem"
      }, {
        "text": "ini 2.5 Flash default)*         │ (Assuming ~25% retry)  │ 🚀 **\u003d 7 to 1"
      }, {
        "text": "1 Entire Phases Completed!**   │\n├──────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **High"
      }, {
        "text": "-Volume Quota (1,500 RPD)**    │ 3.5 requests           │ **~4"
      }, {
        "text": "28 Chunks / Day**                       │\n│ *(Gemini 2.0 Flash)*                 │ (Assuming"
      }, {
        "text": " ~25% retry)  │ 🚀 **\u003d Your Entire 100-Item Roadmap in 1 Day!**│\n└"
      }, {
        "text": "──────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n**Takeaway:** Even on the most conservative 250 R"
      }, {
        "text": "PD limit, you can easily execute **50 to 70 chunks per day**, which is"
      }, {
        "text": " more than enough to finish **3 to 5 full architectural phases every day for $0**.\n\n---\n\n### "
      }, {
        "text": "5. Delay Calculation: What Should the Sleep Timers Be?\n\nTo stay within **10–15 RPM**"
      }, {
        "text": " without triggering rate limit spikes:\n\n* **Between API Calls inside the same"
      }, {
        "text": " chunk:** **6 to 8 seconds delay**.\n  * `Select Files` $\\rightarrow$ *wait 8s* $\\rightarrow$ "
      }, {
        "text": "`Generate Diffs` $\\rightarrow$ *wait 8s* $\\rightarrow$ `Review Diffs`.\n* **Between different"
      }, {
        "text": " Chunks:** **10 seconds delay**.\n* **On HTTP 429 Rate Limit:** Automatic **Exponential Backoff**"
      }, {
        "text": " (Wait 30s, 60s, then retry) so your GitHub Action never fails unexpectedly.\n\n---"
      }, {
        "text": "\n\n### 6. The \"Zero-Cost\" Secret: Compiler Sanity Check First\n\nBefore burning an API call on"
      }, {
        "text": " Pass 3 (LLM Reviewer), **run a local syntax/type check on the GitHub Actions Ubuntu VM**:"
      }, {
        "text": "\n* Run `npx tsc --noEmit` or `node --check \u003cfile\u003e` locally on the VM"
      }, {
        "text": ".\n* **Cost:** **$0.00 and 0 API requests.**\n* If the TypeScript compiler fails with"
      }, {
        "text": " a syntax error, feed the *compiler error directly back* to the coder LLM without wasting a prompt on the reviewer LLM!\n\n---\n\n###"
      }, {
