      "text": "This approach provides a significant efficiency advantage. By analyzing your compressed codebase map **directly in this chat session once**, you eliminate Pass 1 (File Selection) from your GitHub Actions pipeline entirely.\n\nThis reduces your API consumption from **3 requests down to 2 requests per chunk** (a **33% reduction in API calls**), prevents rate-limit delays, and eliminates the risk of an automated model missing an important file during file selection.\n\n---\n\n### 1. How We Solve the \"Newly Created Files\" Problem\n\nWhen Chunk 1 creates a new file (for example, `packages/types/src/space-hierarchy.ts`), Chunk 2 and Chunk 3 will need to import and reference it.\n\nInstead of re-running a full `repomix --compress`, the runner script uses the **\"Branch Accumulator Pattern\"**:\n\n```\n[ Chunk 1: Reads existing SpaceDO.ts ]\n                 │\n                 ▼\n[ Chunk 1 creates `space-hierarchy.ts` \u0026 commits to branch ]\n                 │\n                 ▼\n[ Chunk 2 starts: ]\nBase Files (from spec): `workers/spaces/src/middleware/hierarchy.ts`\n        +\nAccumulated Branch Files (`git diff --name-only origin/main`): `space-hierarchy.ts`\n                 │\n                 ▼\n[ Targeted Repomix packs BOTH existing and newly created files! ]\n```\n\nBecause an entire phase only creates or touches 5 to 10 files total, automatically including **all files created or modified on the active branch so far** in subsequent chunks costs almost nothing in tokens (\u003c 1,500 tokens) and **guarantees that newly created types, classes, and DB schemas are immediately visible to later chunks.**\n\n---\n\n### 2. The Streamlined Chunk Spec Format\n\nEach chunk spec will have a simple `include_files:` header at the top:\n\n```markdown\n---\ninclude_files:\n  - workers/spaces/src/do/SpaceDO.ts\n  - packages/types/src/spaces.ts\nexpected_outputs:\n  - packages/types/src/space-hierarchy.ts\n---\n\n# Phase 1 - Chunk 01: Enterprise Depth Hierarchy\nTarget: Implement parent_space_id, depth, and cross-grant schemas.\n...\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. The Streamlined Runner Script (`scripts/run-phase.mjs`)\n\nBecause file selection is handled upfront here, `scripts/run-phase.mjs` no longer needs Pass 1. It directly parses the chunk\u0027s `include_files`, merges any newly created branch files, and proceeds straight to code generation:\n\n```javascript\nimport { GoogleGenAI, Type } from \"@google/genai\";\nimport { execSync } from \"child_process\";\nimport * as fs from \"fs\";\nimport * as path from \"path\";\n\n// 1. Key Pool Management\nconst rawKeys \u003d process.env.GEMINI_API_KEYS || process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY || \"\";\nconst API_KEYS \u003d rawKeys.split(\",\").map(k \u003d\u003e k.trim()).filter(Boolean);\n\nif (API_KEYS.length \u003d\u003d\u003d 0) {\n  console.error(\"❌ No GEMINI_API_KEYS found!\");\n  process.exit(1);\n}\n\nlet currentKeyIndex \u003d 0;\nfunction getActiveAIClient() {\n  const key \u003d API_KEYS[currentKeyIndex];\n  return { ai: new GoogleGenAI({ apiKey: key }), keyIndex: currentKeyIndex + 1 };\n}\n\nfunction rotateToNextKey(reason \u003d \"rate_limit\") {\n  const prev \u003d currentKeyIndex + 1;\n  currentKeyIndex \u003d (currentKeyIndex + 1) % API_KEYS.length;\n  console.warn(`🔄 Rotating Key [${prev} ➔ ${currentKeyIndex + 1}/${API_KEYS.length}]: ${reason}`);\n}\n\nconst sleep \u003d (ms) \u003d\u003e new Promise((res) \u003d\u003e setTimeout(res, ms));\nconst phaseNum \u003d process.env.PHASE_NUMBER || \"1\";\nconst branchName \u003d `feature/phase-0${phaseNum}`;\nconst specsDir \u003d `specs/phase-${phaseNum}`;\n\nasync function callWithKeyPool(fn, maxAttempts \u003d API_KEYS.length * 2) {\n  for (let attempt \u003d 0; attempt \u003c maxAttempts; attempt++) {\n    try {\n      const { ai, keyIndex } \u003d getActiveAIClient();\n      return await fn(ai, keyIndex);\n    } catch (err) {\n      if (err.message?.includes(\"429\") || err.status \u003d\u003d\u003d 429 || err.message?.includes(\"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\")) {\n        rotateToNextKey(\"Quota/429\");\n        await sleep(4000);\n      } else {\n        throw err;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  throw new Error(\"❌ All API keys in rotation exhausted.\");\n}\n\n// Tool: Emit Complete Files\nconst writeCodeTool \u003d {\n  name: \"apply_chunk_code\",\n  description: \"Emit complete, working, production-ready files for this chunk.\",\n  parameters: {\n    type: Type.OBJECT,\n    properties: {\n      commitMessage: { type: Type.STRING },\n      files: {\n        type: Type.ARRAY,\n        items: {\n          type: Type.OBJECT,\n          properties: {\n            path: { type: Type.STRING },\n            content: { type: Type.STRING }\n          },\n          required: [\"path\", \"content\"]\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    required: [\"commitMessage\", \"files\"]\n  }\n};\n\n// Tool: Review\nconst reviewCodeTool \u003d {\n  name: \"submit_code_review\",\n  description: \"Review implementation against spec.\",\n  parameters: {\n    type: Type.OBJECT,\n    properties: {\n      approved: { type: Type.BOOLEAN },\n      issuesFound: { type: Type.ARRAY, items: { type: Type.STRING } },\n      fixInstructions: { type: Type.STRING }\n    },\n    required: [\"approved\"]\n  }\n};\n\n// Helper: Parse YAML-style frontmatter headers from chunk spec\nfunction parseChunkHeader(content) {\n  const match \u003d content.match(/^---\\s*([\\s\\S]*?)\\s*---/);\n  if (!match) return { baseFiles: [] };\n  const lines \u003d match[1].split(\"\\n\");\n  const baseFiles \u003d [];\n  let inInclude \u003d false;\n  for (const line of lines) {\n    if (line.startsWith(\"include_files:\")) {\n      inInclude \u003d true;\n      continue;\n    }\n    if (inInclude \u0026\u0026 line.trim().startsWith(\"-\")) {\n      baseFiles.push(line.replace(/^[-\\s]+/, \"\").trim());\n    } else if (inInclude \u0026\u0026 line.match(/^[a-zA-Z_]+:/)) {\n      break;\n    }\n  }\n  return { baseFiles };\n}\n\n// Helper: Get all files modified/creat