      "text": "**Defining the Core System**\n\nI\u0027m now zeroing in on the AVOS platform itself. My focus is on its core architecture, specifically understanding how Cloudflare\u0027s edge capabilities (Workers, Durable Objects, etc.) are integrated within its 6-tier execution ladder, background gadgets, and associated components like Parse 5 and Mini. I\u0027m aiming for a concise definition of the system.\n\n\n**Exploring FDE Integration**\n\nI\u0027m now investigating the potential for AVOS to serve as a platform for Forward Deployed Engineers (FDEs). The aim is to understand whether the platform can enable these engineers to build vertical cowork templates, effectively creating \"Harvey for X\" solutions. This involves creating custom domain studios with pre-configured project setups, tools, and background indexers. I\u0027m exploring if this capability can be a valuable tool for FDEs.\n\n\n**Mapping FDE Needs**\n\nI\u0027m now identifying FDE challenges: legacy infrastructure, messy data, the need for rapid prototypes that quickly become secure systems, client resistance to generic tools, and high operational costs. I’m thinking AVOS can be the *ideal* solution, specifically as \"FDE-as-a-Service\". AVOS features align directly with FDE requirements for rapid vertical prototyping.\n\n\n**Defining the Solutions**\n\nI\u0027m now thinking about specific \"Harvey for X\" examples, like a hospital or law firm, and how an FDE could rapidly deploy a tailored solution using AVOS. An FDE could load a blueprint, trigger an indexer gadget, connect client data with Parse 5, and deliver a \"Harvey for Hospital X\" in just two days.\n\nI\u0027m also considering the implications of air-gapped data and sovereign data lock, enabled by `LocalTunnelDO`. Clients can keep their data secure while still benefiting from AVOS functionality with `LocalTunnelDO`\u0027s bridging ability. Another key aspect I\u0027m working on is dealing with unstructured data ingestion using Cohere Parse 5.\nI see these Sub-Spaces as fitting into the hierarchy of enterprise departments and governance.\n\n\n**Refining Template Reusability**\n\nI am now focusing on the practical application of reusable templates. My thinking centers around a 1-click exporter to sanitize sensitive data, allowing FDEs to deploy a customized setup, like \"Hospital A,\" to \"Hospital B\" quickly. This offers the potential to convert consulting services into high-margin, scalable software solutions, and I am particularly interested in the economic implications of such an approach.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Architecting the Thread \u0026 Canvas**\n\nI\u0027m now designing an outcome-focused, 4-tier model for AVOS that incorporates thread and canvas elements. The key is to move away from generic chatbots, and deliver configurable workspace views (Redline for legal, finance grids for M\u0026A, plan specs for construction). I want the FDE to configure these canvas viewports, mirroring the legacy workflow of each client.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Evaluating the Economics**\n\nI\u0027m now working through the financial model for an FDE or agency deploying AVOS. A Developer Partner program with upfront deployment fees ($5,000–$50,000) is being planned, alongside recurring retainers ($150–$500/month/user) for ongoing support and maintenance. This is the model being examined, and the aim is to create a sustainable revenue stream.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Exploring Token Gatekeepers**\n\nI\u0027m now thinking about how the AVOS platform might fit within an enterprise organizational chart. My focus is on the possibility of a Root holding company with Legal, Risk, and Trading Subspaces. Gatekeeper capability tokens could enable data sharing across departments in a secure way, without the risk of leaks.\n\n\n**Defining the Toolkit**\n\nI\u0027m now concretizing the idea of AVOS as an FDE toolkit, moving past mere templates to a complete \"Boutique AI Foundry.\" This involves a clear comparison: the existing high-cost Palantir approach vs. the AVOS model, which enables rapid deployment. I\u0027m focusing on defining the six key \"superpowers\" that give AVOS an edge, and working out the specific value of each. I\u0027m looking at real-world deployment scenarios.\n\n\n",
