ke SQLite), dynamic workflows (durable pipelines for tasks such as ETL, reconciliation, CI/CD), and AI capabilities. I\u0027m imagining a `product_dev` coding example featuring micro-apps and workflows for continuous builds, testing, security audits, and a `doc_studio` legal example with data referencing and monitoring workflows. This could be a B2B SaaS killer.\n\n\n**Confirming Core Concepts**\n\nI now understand that AVOS can replace several external SaaS subscriptions by enabling Dynamic Workflows and Micro-Apps to handle deterministic logic and AI augmentation. I\u0027m focusing on the 80/20 rule, where most business automation is pure code, while a smaller portion leverages LLMs. Cloudflare Workflows offers native handling for these diverse tasks, with code steps and AI steps seamlessly integrated. I\u0027m excited by this approach.\n\n\n**Defining System Frameworks**\n\nI\u0027m now detailing the four key components: Viewport Canvas for the UI, Background Micro-Apps for state and database management, Dynamic Workflows as durable pipelines for automation, and Agent Skills and Primitives for LLM reasoning. I\u0027m developing specific use case examples. I\u0027m focusing on defining and comparing two case studies, one for an AI Coding Platform plugin, the other for Enterprise Legal/Financial plugins. I\u0027m also actively clarifying the deterministic versus agentic workflow balance and cost implications.\n\n\n",
