      "text": "**Limiting Dynamic Workflows only to \"AI agent chat tasks\" would be a massive mistake.** \n\nIn fact, allowing Dynamic Workflows to solve **real company business problems and background software automations** is the exact bridge that transforms your platform from a simple \"AI wrapper\" into a **true Vertical Software Engine** (competing directly with dedicated vertical SaaS, Palantir AIP, and internal engineering tools).\n\nA company does not buy software just to chat with a bot. They buy software to **automate operations**:\n* They need nightly reconciliation pipelines.\n* In coding projects, they need continuous integration (CI/CD) runners, background code indexers, and automated issue-to-PR pipelines (like Cursor, Codex, or Claude Code).\n* In legal and finance, they need multi-step due diligence batch processors that ingest 2,000 files, normalize balance sheets, and notify partners.\n\nBy allowing **Plugins to bundle both Background Micro-Apps (Gadgets) AND Dynamic Workflows**, any plugin author can turn a project into a **complete, bespoke software product**.\n\n---\n\n# 1. The Realization: Workflows as \"Company Software Pipelines,\" Not Just \"Agent Scaffolding\"\n\nTraditional AI frameworks (LangChain, CrewAI) treat workflows purely as *agent execution loops* (\"Agent thinks $\\rightarrow$ calls tool $\\rightarrow$ thinks\"). This wastes compute and burns unnecessary tokens.\n\nIn AVOS on Cloudflare, a **Dynamic Workflow is a Durable State Machine** that combines **deterministic code** (90% of the work) with **AI reasoning** (10% of the work):\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        THE MODERN DUAL-ROLE WORKFLOW ARCHITECTURE                                      │\n├──────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Role 1: Agent Task Runner            │ Role 2: Standalone Company Software Automations                 │\n├──────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ • Used *by* the AI agent.            │ • Solves direct business operations without needing a human.    │\n│ • Long-running tool execution.       │ • Replaces Zapier, Make, Temporal, and custom backend servers.  │\n│ • Example: Agent runs a 15-minute    │ • Example: E-commerce Order-to-Fulfillment pipeline, nightly    │\n│   web research crawl across 50 URLs. │   Stripe sync, continuous automated test runners on Git push.   │\n└──────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n# 2. How This Makes Projects Feel Like Bespoke Vertical Platforms\n\nLook at how top vertical systems (like Claude Code, Cursor, or Harvey) work. They are **not just chat boxes**—they have complex background pipelines constantly running.\n\nWith this architecture, **a Plugin is a 4-Part Vertical Software Package**:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                       THE 4-PART VERTICAL PLUGIN BUNDLE                     │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1. 🖥️ VIEWPORT CANVAS (Frontend)                                            │\n│    • Interactive visual UI (e.g. Code Editor, Legal Redliner, Finance Grid).│\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 2. 📱 STATEFUL MICRO-APPS / GADGETS (Relational Data \u0026 State)               │\n│    • Dedicated DO Facet SQLite databases holding domain-specific graphs     │\n│      (Symbol tables, double-entry GL ledgers, statute cross-references).    │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 3. ⚡ DYNAMIC WORKFLOWS (Durable Background Pipelines)                       │\n│    • Long-running automations, ETL batch processing, and event sentinels.   │\n│    • Replaces backend worker servers and cron daemons.                      │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 4. 🧠 FUNCTIONAL OPERATORS (AI Senses \u0026 Execution)                          │\n│    • Tailored prompts (`SOUL.md`), domain linters, and CodeAct primitives.  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n# 3. Real-World Case Study: The \"Cursor / Claude Code\" Coding Plugin\n\nIf a developer builds a coding plugin (`plugin_edge_ide_v1`) for `product_dev`, they can bundle **three dedicated Dynamic Workflows** that turn the project into an autonomous software engineering platform:\n\n```\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │   PROJECT: `product_dev` (Astro SaaS App)    │\n                                  └──────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘\n                                                         │\n                         ┌───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┐\n                         ▼                               ▼                               ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────┐   ┌──────────────────────────────────┐   ┌──────────────────────────────────┐\n│ WORKFLOW A: Continuous CI/CD     │   │ WORKFLOW B: Background AST       │   │ WORKFLOW C: Autonomous Issue     │\n│ Pipeline (`ci-runner.ts`)        │   │ Deep Indexer (`ast-indexer.ts`)  │   │ Resolver (`issue-to-pr.ts`)      │\n├──────────────────────────────────┤   ├──────────────────────────────────┤   ├──────────────────────────────────┤\n│ • Trigger: Commit on Git branch. │   │ • Trigger: Weekly or on-demand.  │   │ • Trigger: Webhook from GitHub/  │\n│ • Runs `npm test` and build in   │   │ • Runs Tree-sitter Wasm across   │   │   Linear when a bug is tagged.   │\n│   Tier 6 Container sandbox.      │   │   the entire repo in background. │   │ • Spawns isolated branch, writes │\n│ • Captures visual screenshots of │   │ • Updates `gadget_code_graph`    │   │   the fix, runs tests, and opens │\n│   UI preview via Tier 5 Chromium.│   │   DO Facet SQLite symbol table.  │   │   a PR without human awake time! │\n│ • Posts PR status card to chat!  │   │ • Zero chat thread slowdown!     │   │ • Human just clicks [Merge].     │\n└──────────────────────────────────┘   └──────────────────────────────────┘   └──────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Why this bridges the gap:\nIn standard tools, the user has to ask the AI to test every single change. In this setup, **the project acts like a real engineering platform**: the moment a change is pushed, the background CI workflow runs automatically, checks for regressions, and reports back.\n\n---\n\n# 4. Real-World Case Study: The \"Harvey / Hebbia\" Vertical Cowork Plugin\n\nIn a legal or financial cowork project (`doc_studio` or `finance_grid`), the plugin bundles company automations that replace entire software suites:\n\n* **Workflow 1: Bulk Data Room ETL Pipeline:**  \n  When an M\u0026A client uploads a zip file with 200 scanned contracts, a Dynamic Workflow spins up, calls Cohere Parse 5 in parallel batches across 50 workers, normalizes all indemnification terms into SQLite, and builds the deal index in 10 minutes.\n* **Workflow 2: Standing Regulatory Watcher (Weekly Cron):**  \n  Every Sunday night, a Tier 2 workflow wakes up at $0 cost, crawls the Delaware Chancery Court docket and SEC filings using Tier 4 Kitesurf, extracts relevant precedents, and leaves a clean briefing in the partners\u0027 private Telegram channel.\n\n---\n\n# 5. The \"Economic Shield\": Deterministic Logic Saves Massive Money\n\nOne of the biggest reasons to use Dynamic Workflows for company automations is **unit economics**:\n\n$$\\text{Pure AI Agent Chat Turn} \\approx \\$0.02 - \\$0.10 \\quad \\text{vs.} \\quad \\text{Deterministic Workflow Step} \\approx \\$0.00005$$\n\nMost company automations don\u0027t need an LLM for 90% of their logic:\n```typescript\n// Inside a Plugin\u0027s Workflow:\nexport async function run(event: WorkflowEvent, step: WorkflowStep) {\n  // Step 1: Pure deterministic code (Cost: $0.00001, No LLM!)\n  const rawData \u003d await step.do(\"fetch-transactions\", async () \u003d\u003e {\n    return await fetchFromStripeAPI();\n  });\n\n  // Step 2: Pure deterministic database filter (Cost: $0.00001, No LLM!)\n  const flaggedItems \u003d await step.do(\"filter-anomalies\", async () \u003d\u003e {\n    return rawData.filter(tx \u003d\u003e tx.amount \u003e 10000 \u0026\u0026 !tx.verified);\n  });\n\n  // Step 3: ONLY call the AI LLM if an anomaly actually exists!\n  if (flaggedItems.length \u003e 0) {\n    await step.do(\"ai-risk-summary\", async () \u003d\u003e {\n      // Calls cheap Workers AI Llama 3.3 for a 2-sentence summary\n      return await generateRiskBrief(flaggedItems);\n    });\n  }\n}\n```\n\nBy allowing plugins to define workflows that run **pure code for routine steps and invoke AI only for complex reasoning**, you deliver enterprise-grade software automations at **99% lower cost than competitors**.\n\n---\n\n# 6. Updated Declarative Plugin Manifest (`plugin.json`)\n\nTo enable developers to package these capabilities cleanly, expand the Plugin manifest:\n\n```typescript\nexport interface AvosPluginManifest {\n  id: string; // e.g. \"plugin_legal_due_diligence_pro\"\n  name: string;\n  version: string;\n  category: \"CODING\" | \"LEGAL\" | \"FINANCE\" | \"HEALTHCARE\" | \"OPS\";\n\n  // 1. UI Extension Viewport\n  viewport: {\n    componentName: string; // e.g. \"DocumentRedlineCanvas\"\n    entrypointUrl: string;\n  };\n\n  // 2. Bundled Background Micro-Apps (Stateful Gadgets)\n  gadgets?: Array\u003c{\n    id: string; // e.g. \"gadget_citation_matrix\"\n    description: string;\n    database: \"do_facet_sqlite\";\n    autoMcpEndpoint: boolean; // Auto-exposes /mcp to agents\n  }\u003e;\n\n  // 3. Bundled Company Workflows \u0026 Automations\n  workflows?: Array\u003c{\n    id: string; // e.g. \"batch_lease_etl\"\n    name: string;\n    scriptPath: string; // e.g. \"./workflows/batch-etl.ts\"\n    trigger: {\n      type: \"manual\" | \"cron\" | \"webhook\" | \"git_push\";\n      cronExpression?: string; // e.g. \"0 8 * * 1\"\n      webhookEvent?: string;   // e.g. \"document.uploaded\"\n    };\n    maxStepCeiling: number;    // e.g. 50 steps\n  }\u003e;\n\n  // 4. Domain Directives \u0026 Linters\n  directives: {\n    systemPromptSupplement: string;\n    linterRules: string[];\n  };\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary: What This Achieves\n\n1. **Not Just for Agent Tasks:** Dynamic Workflows are the **general-purpose software and automation engine** of the enterprise, handling both long-running agent tools and routine company business processes.\n2. **True Vertical Parity:** Plugins become full-featured vertical platforms (like Cursor for code or Harvey for law) by bundling **Canvas UI + Background Gadgets (Data) + Dynamic Workflows (Automation)**.\n3. **Massive Cost Protection:** 90% of business automation executes as fast, deterministic code in workflow steps for fractions of a cent, calling AI models only when semantic interpretation is strictly required.\n4. **Huge Developer Incentive:** A developer is no longer just selling a \"prompt template\"; they are selling an **autonomous, end-to-end operational software product** that commands high B2B subscription prices.",
