      "text": "Your insight connects the organizational and operational layers: **Company Automations should not float in an unorganized void; they should be anchored inside dedicated Company Projects.** \n\nWhen every company automation has a \"home project,\" it automatically inherits a **Git repository (Cloudflare Artifacts)**, **version control**, **testing harnesses**, and **access control lists (ACLs)**.\n\nHowever, having multiple employees—each with their own personal Space Assistant—working in the same shared company space creates the **\"Dual-Assistant Collision Problem\"**:\n* An automation fails at 03:00 AM.\n* Both Alice\u0027s assistant and Bob\u0027s assistant notice the failure.\n* Both assistants fork branches, burn LLM tokens, generate conflicting code patches, and submit duplicate Pull Requests.\n\nHere is the exact architectural solution: **The Atomic Task Lease Protocol**, **Sibling Spectator Mode**, and **Semantic Intent Deduplication**.\n\n---\n\n# 1. The Project-Anchored Automation Architecture\n\nInstead of floating unmanaged, all three classes of Dynamic Workflows live inside specific, version-controlled projects:\n\n```\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │      PARENT COMPANY SPACE (Root Depth 0)     │\n                                  └──────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘\n                                                         │\n                         ┌───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┐\n                         ▼                                                               ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 📁 PROJECT: \"Corporate Treasury \u0026 Billing\"       │   │ 📁 PROJECT: \"Customer Ops \u0026 Dispatch\"            │\n│ Kind: `finance_grid`                             │   │ Kind: `customer_bot`                             │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────┤   ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ ⚡ BUNDLED COMPANY AUTOMATIONS:                   │   │ ⚡ BUNDLED COMPANY AUTOMATIONS:                   │\n│ • `wf_stripe_nightly_reconciler.ts` (Class 1)    │   │ • `wf_lead_triage_router.ts` (Class 1)          │\n│ • `wf_partner_payout_settlement.ts` (Class 1)    │   │ • `wf_churn_risk_sentinel.ts` (Class 1)          │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────┤   ├──────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ ⚙️ BUNDLED VERTICAL EXTENSIONS:                   │   │ ⚙️ BUNDLED VERTICAL EXTENSIONS:                   │\n│ • `wf_ledger_discrepancy_indexer.ts` (Class 2)   │   │ • `wf_sla_response_tracker.ts` (Class 2)        │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   └──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Why this is powerful:\n1. **Clear Code Ownership:** If the Space Assistant needs to update the Stripe reconciler, it doesn\u0027t edit a mysterious cloud script. It targets `Project: Treasury`, checks out a branch on Cloudflare Artifacts, and directs the project\u0027s developer agent to make the edit.\n2. **Clear Permissions:** Only users with `Editor` or `Admin` rank in `Project: Treasury` can modify its company automations.\n\n---\n\n# 2. The Collision Trap: The \"Double-Fix Token Burn\"\n\n```\n[ 03:00 AM: `wf_stripe_reconciler` throws 500 error in Project: Treasury ]\n                                    │\n                                    ▼\n       ┌────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────┐\n       ▼                                                         ▼\n[ 👩‍💻 Alice\u0027s Personal Assistant ]         [ 👨‍💻 Bob\u0027s Personal Assistant ]\n• Detects error.                           • Detects error.\n• Fires Claude 3.7 ($0.15).                • Fires Claude 3.7 ($0.15).\n• Forks branch `alice_fix`.                • Forks branch `bob_fix`.\n• Writes patch.                            • Writes patch.\n• Opens PR #18.                            • Opens PR #19 (CONFLICT!).\n       │                                                         │\n       └────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┘\n                                    ▼\n                   💸 RESULT: Double Credits Burned!\n                   💥 Merge Conflicts on Main!\n```\n\n---\n\n# 3. The Solution: The Atomic Task Lease Protocol (`SpaceDO.tasks`)\n\nTo prevent duplicate work and wasted credits, AVOS uses **Single-Writer Task Leases** enforced at the single-threaded **Durable Object SQLite layer (`SpaceDO.ts`)**.\n\nWhen an automation fails or a task is created, `SpaceDO` generates an **Authoritative Incident Record** in the Project Journal:\n\n```sql\n-- Project Journal Tasks \u0026 Incident Table in SpaceDO\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS project_tasks (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,                       -- e.g. \"inc_stripe_fail_042\"\n  project_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  title TEXT NOT NULL,\n  status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT \u0027OPEN\u0027 CHECK (status IN (\u0027OPEN\u0027, \u0027CLAIMED\u0027, \u0027IN_REVIEW\u0027, \u0027COMPLETED\u0027)),\n  claimed_by_user_id TEXT,                  -- \"usr_alice\"\n  claimed_by_assistant_id TEXT,             -- \"asst_alice\"\n  branch_name TEXT,                          -- \"fix/inc_stripe_fail_042\"\n  lease_expires_at TEXT,                    -- ISO-8601 UTC timestamp\n  created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime(\u0027now\u0027))\n);\n```\n\n### The Atomic Compare-And-Swap (CAS) Lease Claim:\nWhen Alice\u0027s assistant detects the failure, it **must acquire the lease** before generating any code:\n\n```sql\n-- Atomic CAS Write in SpaceDO SQLite\nUPDATE project_tasks\nSET status \u003d \u0027CLAIMED\u0027,\n    claimed_by_user_id \u003d ?,\n    claimed_by_assistant_id \u003d ?,\n    branch_name \u003d ?,\n    lease_expires_at \u003d datetime(\u0027now\u0027, \u0027+15 minutes\u0027)\nWHERE id \u003d ? \n  AND (status \u003d \u0027OPEN\u0027 OR lease_expires_at \u003c datetime(\u0027now\u0027));\n```\n\n#### What Happens at the Edge:\n1. **Alice\u0027s Assistant gets `changes \u003d\u003d\u003d 1`:**  \n   * **Lease GRANTED.**  \n   * Alice\u0027s assistant forks `branch:fix/inc_stripe_fail_042` on Cloudflare Artifacts.\n   * Spawns an isolated V8 run, patches the code, runs `npm test`, and opens PR #18.\n2. **Bob\u0027s Assistant executes 10ms later and gets `changes \u003d\u003d\u003d 0`:**  \n   * **Lease DENIED (Already claimed by Alice\u0027s Assistant).**  \n   * Bob\u0027s assistant **aborts execution immediately**. Zero LLM tokens burned! Zero duplicate branches created!\n\n### The Crash-Proof 15-Minute TTL:\nIf Alice\u0027s assistant crashes or runs out of credits midway, the lease expires after 15 minutes (`lease_expires_at \u003c datetime(\u0027now\u0027)`). Bob\u0027s assistant can then cleanly claim the task without getting deadlocked forever.\n\n---\n\n# 4. Sibling Assistant Collaboration: \"Spectator \u0026 Review\" Mode\n\nInstead of Bob\u0027s assistant doing nothing or acting blind, it transitions into **Collaborative Spectator Mode**:\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 👥 SIBLING ASSISTANT SPECTATOR FLOW                                                                    │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1. Bob\u0027s Assistant checks `project_tasks`: Sees `claimed_by_user_id \u003d \u0027usr_alice\u0027`.                    │\n│ 2. Bob\u0027s Assistant sends an ambient update to Bob\u0027s notification feed:                                │\n│    \"⚠️ Incident in Project Treasury: Stripe Reconciler failed.                                         │\n│     Alice\u0027s Assistant has claimed the task and is drafting a fix on `branch:fix-stripe-042`.\"          │\n│ 3. Alice\u0027s Assistant opens PR #18.                                                                     │\n│ 4. Bob\u0027s Assistant notifies Bob:                                                                       │\n│    \"PR #18 opened by Alice\u0027s team. [ 🔍 Would you like me to audit the diff for you? ]\"               │\n│ 5. If Bob clicks [Audit], Bob\u0027s assistant runs an AST review without ever touching the code itself!   │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n# 5. Semantic Intent Deduplication (Human Collision Defense)\n\nWhat happens when two humans independently ask their assistants to do the exact same thing in different chats?\n* **10:00 AM (Alice in Thread #1):** *\"Add Google OAuth login to our auth routes.\"*\n* **10:02 AM (Bob in Thread #2):** *\"We need Google sign-in supported on the login page.\"*\n\nWithout coordination, both assistants will write duplicate, clashing code.\n\n### The Semantic Deduplication Gate (`SpaceDO.ts`):\nBefore any assistant spawns an execution run for a feature, it calls `ctx.project.claimOrJoinGoal()`:\n\n```typescript\n// workers/spaces/src/engine/GoalDeduplicator.ts\nexport async function claimOrJoinGoal(\n  projectId: string,\n  userPrompt: string,\n  callingUserId: string,\n  env: Env\n) {\n  // 1. Embed the prompt in 15ms via Workers AI (@cf/baai/bge-small-en-v1.5)\n  const queryEmbedding \u003d await env.AI.run(\"@cf/baai/bge-small-en-v1.5\", { text: [userPrompt] });\n\n  // 2. Query active IN_PROGRESS tasks in this project\n  const activeTasks \u003d await getActiveTasksFromSpaceDO(projectId);\n\n  // 3. Check for high semantic collision (Cosine Similarity \u003e 0.85)\n  for (const task of activeTasks) {\n    const similarity \u003d cosineSimilarity(queryEmbedding.data[0], task.embedding);\n    if (similarity \u003e 0.85) {\n      // DUPLICATE DETECTED!\n      return {\n        isDuplicate: true,\n        existingTask: task,\n        message: `Task already underway by @${task.claimedByUserName} on branch \u0027${task.branchName}\u0027.`\n      };\n    }\n  }\n\n  // 4. If no collision, register new task and grant lease\n  return await createAndClaimNewTask(projectId, userPrompt, callingUserId);\n}\n```\n\n#### What Bob Experiences:\nBob’s assistant stops before generating code and returns a clean, collaborative card:\n\u003e *\"I noticed Alice\u0027s assistant is already working on **Google OAuth Authentication** on `branch:alice_oauth` (started 2 minutes ago).  \n\u003e **[ Join Alice\u0027s Task Thread #104 ]** or **[ View Her Active Branch ]**\"*\n\n---\n\n# 6. Strict RBAC \u0026 Mini-AGI Permission Enforcement\n\nAn assistant **cannot claim work or view automations that the human user is not cleared to access**:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                 AUTOMATION EDIT PERMISSION MATRIX                                       │\n├───────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ User Role in Project          │ Can View Automation?      │ Can Assistant Claim/Edit Automation?        │\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Owner / Admin (Rank 4–5)**  │ ✅ Yes                    │ ✅ **Full Access:** Auto-claims fixes;      │\n│                               │                           │    merges PRs directly to `main`.           │\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Editor / Dev (Rank 3)**     │ ✅ Yes                    │ ✅ **Branch Access:** Can claim and fix on  │\n│                               │                           │    isolated branches; requires PR review.   │\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Member / Viewer (Rank 1–2)**│ ❌ No (404 Not Found)     │ ❌ **HARD BLOCKED:** Assistant receives     │\n│                               │                           │    `Permission Denied: Insufficient Rank`.  │\n└───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n* If a junior contractor asks their assistant: *\"Fix the Stripe billing automation\"*, the assistant queries `SpaceDO` SQLite.\n* `SpaceDO` evaluates `user.role_rank \u003c 3`.\n* Result: The assistant replies:  \n  \u003e *\"You do not have edit clearance for Project Treasury\u0027s financial automations. Please contact a project admin.\"*  \n  Zero code is run. Zero files are exposed.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Guarantees\n\n1. **Automations are Project-Anchored:** Every company automation lives inside a specific project, giving it a Git repo, versioned history, and access control.\n2. **Zero Duplicate Token Burn:** The **Atomic Task Lease Protocol** ensures that when an automation breaks, only **one assistant wins the right to fix it**; all others abort execution instantly.\n3. **No Deadlocks:** Leases carry a 15-minute TTL; if an assistant crashes, another assistant can seamlessly take over.\n4. **No Clashing PRs:** Sibling assistants act as **reviewers and spectators**, keeping team members informed without generating conflicting code branches.\n5. **Semantic Collision Prevention:** If two users ask for the same feature, the system detects the semantic match (\u003e0.85 cosine similarity) and links them to the existing task instead of re-building it twice.",
