      "text": "Combining a stateful database (Micro-App / Gadget) with an automated processing loop (Dynamic Workflow) creates a complete, self-contained serverless micro-backend that lives and breathes on the edge. \n\nInstead of treating them as separate concepts, fusing state + logic into a single cohesive unit represents a powerful architectural primitive. Several terms fit this combination depending on the context:\n\n---\n\n### Top Naming Candidates for this Combination\n\n#### 1. **Durable Daemon** (Recommended for the Technical Stack)\n* *Why it fits:* In systems architecture, a \"daemon\" is a background process that runs continuously or triggers on events without direct human intervention. Because it uses Cloudflare Workflows, it is *durable* (survives restarts, sleeps at $0 cost), and because it uses DO Facets, it has its own *state*. \n* *Example:* The `code_indexer_daemon` watches file changes, updates its SQLite symbol graph, and sleeps.\n\n#### 2. **Active Service** (Recommended for Enterprise / Cowork Mode)\n* *Why it fits:* A standard micro-app/gadget is *passive* (it sits there waiting for an HTTP request or an MCP tool call). Adding a Dynamic Workflow makes it *proactive*. It is a micro-service that serves APIs **and** runs its own background routines.\n* *Example:* The `stripe_reconciliation_service` syncs ledgers every night at midnight *and* serves query endpoints to the agent.\n\n#### 3. **Edge Reactor** (Recommended for Event-Driven Automations)\n* *Why it fits:* It \"reacts\" to inbound webhooks, GitHub pushes, or calendar events, processes them through durable workflow steps, and mutates its private SQLite state.\n* *Example:* The `github_issue_reactor` listens for webhook events and automatically schedules bug-fix workflows.\n\n---\n\n### How to Position It in AVOS\n\nTo keep the naming hierarchy clean for builders and developers:\n1. **Templates** \u003d The whole-space building (e.g., *Harvey for Law*).\n2. **Extensions** \u003d The modular add-ons.\n3. **Gadgets** \u003d User-facing, interactive micro-apps with UI viewports and SQLite DBs.\n4. **Daemons** (or **Active Services**) \u003d The background, autonomous data-processors combining a DO SQLite database with Dynamic Workflows.",
