      "text": "Here is the comprehensive, production-grade architectural specification of all **130 finalized features and system plans**. \n\nThis document contains **no code snippets**—instead, every item provides the complete **mental model, operational mechanics, system invariants, and failure-mode defenses** so that any AI receiving this list can implement the entire operating system in strict, dependency-aware order.\n\n---\n\n# THE AVOS MASTER IMPLEMENTATION BLUEPRINT (PHASES 1–8)\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                   CHRONOLOGICAL IMPLEMENTATION PHASES                                  │\n├─────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 1 │ Multi-Tenant Core \u0026 Storage Foundation     │ Durable Objects, SQLite FS, Git Mesh, Subspaces │\n├─────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 2 │ Compute Ladder \u0026 Runtime Hypervisor        │ 6-Tier Execution, FUSE Sync, Containers, Wasm   │\n├─────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 3 │ Action Space, Virtual CLI \u0026 Decoupled Auth │ `ctx` SDK, JIT CLIs, Outbound Workers, Vault    │\n├─────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 4 │ Cognition, Memory, Knowledge \u0026 Ingestion   │ Dual-Tier DAGs, Vectorize ACLs, Parse 5, Search │\n├─────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 5 │ 4-Tier Threads \u0026 Multi-Assistant Governance│ Team/Task/Scratchpad Threads, Leases, RFC Gates │\n├─────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 6 │ Project Kinds, Viewports, Daemons \u0026 Gadgets│ 7 Studio Kinds, Tree-Sitter Indexers, DO Facets │\n├─────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 7 │ Asymmetric Workflows, Queues \u0026 Telephony   │ Inbound Webhooks, Queues, Replay Lake, Voice    │\n├─────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 8 │ Billing, Marketplace, Distribution \u0026 Shell │ Credits, Subscriptions, FDE Ladder, Radar, UI   │\n└─────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 1: Multi-Tenant Core, Storage \u0026 Workspace Foundation\n\n#### 1. Enterprise Depth Hierarchy\n* **Mental Model:** A two-level organizational tree modeling corporate structures. Depth 0 represents the Parent Company Space (Holding Co / Root) holding master billing, corporate compliance rules, and global brand identities. Depth 1 represents Department Sub-Spaces (Legal, Engineering, Support) operating with specialized studio viewports and localized token spend caps.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Stored in Cloudflare D1 with composite indexing over tenant, parent space, and depth. All spaces share uniform database schemas; differences between holding companies and departments are governed entirely by depth parameters and capability manifests.\n* **Invariants:** Depth cannot exceed 1 (strictly avoiding recursive tree bloat). Deleting a parent space cascades soft-deletions to all departmental sub-spaces.\n\n#### 2. Sub-Space Inheritance \u0026 Isolation Matrix\n* **Mental Model:** Downward oversight coupled with strict upward and lateral air-gapping. Parent space owners/admins automatically inherit administrative visibility across all departmental sub-spaces. Department members cannot view parent company balance sheets or executive rooms. Sibling sub-spaces have zero visibility into each other by default.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Evaluated by edge middleware on every incoming request. Checks target space hierarchy; if parent membership holds owner/admin rank, downward access is granted. Lateral calls between sibling spaces return 403 Forbidden unless accompanied by an active cross-space capability grant.\n* **Invariants:** Fail-closed security posture. If hierarchy lookup fails or experiences transient latency, the middleware defaults to access denial.\n\n#### 3. Public vs. Private Project Access Control\n* **Mental Model:** Projects within any space are categorized as Public Commons (visible to all verified space members) or Confidential Workstations (locked strictly to explicitly invited members).\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Managed by single-threaded SQLite inside `SpaceDO`. Private projects maintain an internal membership table with role rankings. Non-members attempting to read files, list threads, or inspect private project metadata receive a 404 Not Found response.\n* **Invariants:** Private projects must never return 403 Forbidden, ensuring their topical existence is completely hidden from unauthorized employees.\n\n#### 4. Project-Anchored Automation Architecture\n* **Mental Model:** Automations, background pipelines, and cron routines never float unattached at the root space level. Every company automation is anchored inside a dedicated, version-controlled project container (e.g. Treasury Automations live in `Project: Treasury`).\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Every automation inherits the project’s Git repository, testing harness, and membership access rules. The Space Assistant acts as an executive overseer that reviews status but delegates code modifications to the project\u0027s specialized operators.\n* **Invariants:** Deleting or archiving a project automatically pauses and archives all bundled background automations.\n\n#### 5. Cloudflare Artifacts Git-for-Agents Engine\n* **Mental Model:** A native, serverless Git engine running directly inside Durable Objects via a Zig-to-WASM compilation layer. Gives every project a real, full-fidelity Git repository for commits, branches, and diffs.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Exposes bindings to programmatically initialize repositories, generate 10ms zero-copy branch forks, compare commit tree hashes, and execute atomic fast-forward merges.\n* **Invariants:** All codebase modifications must be committed as valid Git commit trees with SHA-256 parent hashes; loose unversioned string overwrites are prohibited.\n\n#### 6. In-Memory Virtual POSIX Shell (`@cloudflare/computer`)\n* **Mental Model:** A sub-millisecond in-memory shell that executes 90%+ of agent terminal actions (`grep`, `cat`, `sed`, `awk`, `find`, `jq`, `diff`, Unix pipes) directly in V8 without starting a Docker container.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Uses `just-bash` to parse POSIX syntax in memory, operating directly against the authoritative Durable Object SQLite virtual filesystem.\n* **Invariants:** Never escalates to a container for text, line-inspection, or file-search operations. Returns results in under 5ms for fractions of a cent.\n\n#### 7. Clean Namespace Separation (`/workspace/` vs. `/.avos/`)\n* **Mental Model:** Strict physical boundary between user application code and internal agent operating system meta-state.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** `/workspace/` contains application source code tracked by Git Artifacts. `/.avos/` is Git-ignored and contains agent state, shared skills, background workflow code, and private scratchpad drafts.\n* **Invariants:** The frontend file tree hides `/.avos/` by default. Git commits strictly ignore all files outside of `/workspace/`.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 2: Compute Ladder \u0026 Invisible Runtime Hypervisor\n\n#### 8. 6-Tier Cloudflare Execution Ladder\n* **Mental Model:** A hierarchical compute ladder spanning from zero-cost in-memory virtual filesystems up to full containerized operating systems, routing tasks dynamically based on required system capability.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Tiers: 1 (DO SQLite VFS), 2 (V8 Isolate Shell), 3 (Durable Workflows), 4 (Kitesurf Browser), 5 (Headless Chromium), 6 (Linux Container Sandbox).\n* **Invariants:** Workloads always start in the lowest capable tier and promote upward only upon encountering missing binary or runtime requirements.\n\n#### 9. Invisible Runtime Hypervisor\n* **Mental Model:** The AI model is never burdened with managing 6 compute tiers in its prompt. It interacts via 3 universal execution primitives (`Bash`, `Read`, `Edit`) and 2 sensory primitives (`Browser`, `Delegate`). The runtime hypervisor inspects commands and routes them to the appropriate tier invisibly.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** The hypervisor inspects terminal commands under `Bash`. POSIX commands stay in V8; browser commands route to Kitesurf; native compilation commands route to containers.\n* **Invariants:** The LLM context window never contains tier-selection instructions, eliminating prompt paralysis.\n\n#### 10. `ArtifactFS` FUSE Driver with Lazy Hydration\n* **Mental Model:** Linux containers mount project workspaces on the fly without waiting for a full `git clone` or downloading hundreds of megabytes of cold files.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Uses a FUSE filesystem driver inside the container to fetch file contents on-demand across Cloudflare\u0027s edge network, shaving 90 seconds off container boot times.\n* **Invariants:** Writes made inside the container flush back to the authoritative DO SQLite filesystem upon `fsync`.\n\n#### 11. 4-Dimension State Synchronization Engine\n* **Mental Model:** Guarantees zero split-brain when switching between fast V8 Isolates and heavy Linux Containers.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Synchronizes state across 4 vectors: Filesystem (ArtifactFS FUSE), Shell Session (`cwd` and `export` variables), Git State (shared commit HEAD), and Database State (in-memory DO Facet SQLite).\n* **Invariants:** A working directory change in an isolate immediately applies when a container launches.\n\n#### 12. 95/5 Compute Arbitrage with 60-Second Micro-Sleep\n* **Mental Model:** Delivers unconstrained compute performance while keeping monthly infrastructure bills under $2.50 per user.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** 95% of tasks execute in sub-millisecond V8 Isolates. Heavy containers launch only for native compilation and shut down after a strict 60-second idle countdown.\n* **Invariants:** Containers must never remain warm indefinitely. Alarms terminate idle containers automatically.\n\n#### 13. In-Isolate WebAssembly Python (Pyodide)\n* **Mental Model:** Standard Python scripts (math, json, data analysis) execute in V8 isolates without container boot overhead.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Embeds Pyodide (Wasm CPython) inside Tier 2. Automatically promotes to Tier 6 Containers only when scripts import native C-extensions like PyTorch or OpenCV.\n* **Invariants:** Pyodide execution incurs zero container compute charges.\n\n#### 14. Tier 4 Cloudflare Kitesurf Agent Browser\n* **Mental Model:** A 30MB low-memory browser engine built specifically for agent web navigation, running 3–7x faster and cheaper than Chromium.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Handles DOM extraction, article parsing, and form navigation in milliseconds. Automatically elevates to Tier 5 Headless Chromium if the page requires WebGL or visual screenshot inspection.\n* **Invariants:** Kitesurf is always attempted first for web navigation unless visual QA is explicitly requested.\n\n#### 15. Virtual Display Desktop Automation (\"Computer Use\")\n* **Mental Model:** Enables agents to interact visually with real desktop software (LibreOffice, Blender, desktop apps) using simulated mouse and keyboard inputs.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Runs Xvfb (virtual display server), Fluxbox, and `xdotool` inside Tier 6 Containers. Streams live visual frames over WebSockets via noVNC to an interactive canvas.\n* **Invariants:** Actions operate within sandboxed userland with no host network escape capabilities.\n\n#### 16. Multiplexed Persistent gRPC Bridge\n* **Mental Model:** Replaces high-latency HTTP JSON serialization between Durable Objects and Linux Containers with binary streams.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Establishes persistent binary socket pooling over Cloudflare TCP sockets (`connect(socket)`), streaming compiler logs and AST diffs with sub-5ms latency.\n* **Invariants:** Sockets reconnect automatically upon container micro-sleep recycles.\n\n#### 17. Instant Zero-Copy Branch Micro-Forking\n* **Mental Model:** Subagents and private scratchpads receive instant, isolated sandboxes without cloning physical disk storage.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Leverages Cloudflare Artifacts copy-on-write pointers to fork repositories in under 10ms.\n* **Invariants:** Mutations on forks have zero effect on the main branch until merged through a Pull Request.\n\n#### 18. Turn-by-Turn Git Time Machine\n* **Mental Model:** Total auditability and instant recovery. If an agent introduces a bug, the user can scrub backward and restore any historical point in time.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Every completed tool turn automatically generates an immutable Git commit in Cloudflare Artifacts, enabling 1-click historical rollbacks.\n* **Invariants:** Resetting to an earlier turn preserves branching history without data loss.\n\n#### 19. Reasoning-Aware Git Blame\n* **Mental Model:** Git history records not just *what* code changed, but the exact architectural reasoning *why* it changed.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Every automated commit embeds structured front-matter metadata in the commit message containing author agent role, user goal, legal/technical rationale, and task ID.\n* **Invariants:** Inspecting git blame exposes the decision chain that justified the line of code.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 3: Action Space, Virtual CLI \u0026 Decoupled Auth\n\n#### 20. Universal Runtime SDK (`ctx`)\n* **Mental Model:** A standardized, strongly typed runtime environment injected into every isolate, workflow, and container execution.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Exposes scoped namespaces: `ctx.fs` (files), `ctx.project` (tasks/journals), `ctx.space` (workspace admin), `ctx.vault` (auth), `ctx.cli` (terminal), and `ctx.connectors` (third-party tools).\n* **Invariants:** Injected methods are bound server-side to the caller\u0027s verified identity and role rank.\n\n#### 21. Universal Vault Layer \u0026 Edge Outbound Workers\n* **Mental Model:** Zero-leak credential security. Code written by users or agents never holds raw API keys or database passwords.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Secrets are encrypted with AES-256-GCM in D1/KMS. Outbound Workers intercept HTTPS traffic and inject decrypted authorization headers at the edge network boundary.\n* **Invariants:** Plaintext secrets never land on container disks, isolate memory, or client logs.\n\n#### 22. WriteGuard Mutation Interceptor\n* **Mental Model:** An unbypassable edge firewall preventing prompt-injected agents from deleting production databases or running destructive shell commands.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Parses SQL ASTs and tool parameters at the edge proxy layer, blocking destructive operations (`DROP`, `DELETE *`, `rm -rf`) unless authorized by a signed Gatekeeper token.\n* **Invariants:** Unauthenticated or untrusted callers cannot execute destructive mutations under any circumstance.\n\n#### 23. Virtual CLI Interception Engine\n* **Mental Model:** External CLI commands (`stripe`, `gh`, `r2`, `jq`) run in milliseconds without launching a container or installing binaries.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Intercepts terminal commands inside V8 Isolates and maps them to edge REST API fetches or in-memory WebAssembly executions.\n* **Invariants:** Returns terminal-formatted ASCII tables to the agent in under 5ms for $0.0001.\n\n#### 24. Just-In-Time (JIT) Virtual CLI Synthesis\n* **Mental Model:** The agent writes its own CLI wrappers on the fly as it encounters new third-party APIs, eliminating the need to pre-bundle hundreds of SDKs.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** When an unregistered command is called, the agent synthesizes a 15-line parser using `ctx.cli.register`, saves it into SQLite, and executes it in V8 forever.\n* **Invariants:** Only the specific subcommands requested are implemented, keeping code footprints tiny.\n\n#### 25. Decoupled Logical Connector Binding Matrix\n* **Mental Model:** Source code never contains hardcoded account handles or email addresses. Scripts reference abstract aliases that users map dynamically.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Code calls `ctx.connectors.use(\"inbound_mail\")`. A relational binding table in `SpaceDO` maps that alias to an active physical connection (Company Gmail vs. Personal Gmail).\n* **Invariants:** Switching connected accounts in the UI re-binds the alias without modifying application code.\n\n#### 26. Pre-Flight Scope Verification \u0026 Incremental Re-Auth\n* **Mental Model:** Prevents silent failures when an automation needs higher permissions than originally granted.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** The SDK validates granted OAuth scopes before calling an action. If write permissions are missing on a read-only token, it halts and surfaces an incremental upgrade card.\n* **Invariants:** Automations never fail with cryptic 403 errors; they cleanly prompt for the missing permission.\n\n#### 27. Gatekeeper Capability-Based Cross-Subspace Delegation\n* **Mental Model:** Fine-grained, unforgeable capability tokens that allow cross-department collaboration without broad database access.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Mints HMAC-SHA256 tokens specifying allowed operations, target resource IDs, and expiration timestamps.\n* **Invariants:** An agent can never mint a capability token exceeding the permission ceiling of the human user who authorized it.\n\n#### 28. 3-Tier Connector Scoping\n* **Mental Model:** Strict separation between company-wide, project-bound, and personal integrations.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Connectors are scoped as `Space-Shared` (company Stripe), `Project-Bound` (clinic WhatsApp line), or `User-Personal` (Alice\u0027s private Gmail).\n* **Invariants:** Unattended system crons cannot access personal credentials without an active user session.\n\n#### 29. Public Channel Tool Stripping \u0026 MCP-UI Privacy Bridge\n* **Mental Model:** Protects personal user accounts from accidental leakage in public team channels.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** In public rooms, personal tools are physically stripped from the LLM prompt. If a user asks for personal data, the agent emits an interactive card to fork to a private scratchpad.\n* **Invariants:** Personal credentials can never be executed or queried in shared public rooms.\n\n#### 30. Single-Use Ephemeral Action Grants\n* **Mental Model:** Allows quick one-off personal actions in public rooms without leaving the channel.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Uses MCP v2 Elicitation to display an authorization card visible only to the owning user. Approving mints a single-use token valid for 15 seconds.\n* **Invariants:** The token expires immediately upon tool execution; other team members never see the credential.\n\n#### 31. Turn-Holder vs. Referent Mention Router\n* **Mental Model:** Prevents multiple bots from waking up simultaneously when one is merely being talked about.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** The leading `@mention` is assigned the primary turn lock. Subsequent mentions (e.g. `@DevBot\u0027s patch`) are parsed as contextual references and do not wake up.\n* **Invariants:** Only one agent holds the active execution turn lock in a thread at any given moment.\n\n#### 32. Sequential Turn Delegation\n* **Mental Model:** Orderly handoffs between agents without human babysitting.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** An active agent calls `ctx.agent.delegate()` to pass structured tasks to another specialist agent sequentially, transferring the execution turn lock cleanly.\n* **Invariants:** Simultaneous multi-agent responses in the same thread are disallowed.\n\n#### 33. Cryptographic Delegation Chaining\n* **Mental Model:** Prevents privilege escalation through delegation (Trojan Delegation attacks).\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Tasks carry an HMAC-signed token with the initiating human user\u0027s ID and role rank. Project agents evaluate the human\u0027s clearance, not the assistant\u0027s.\n* **Invariants:** A junior user cannot trick a project agent into editing administrative files via delegation.\n\n#### 34. Demonstration-to-Skill Distillation Engine\n* **Mental Model:** \"Watch me do it once, automate forever.\" Turns manual workflows into permanent, zero-cost TypeScript code.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Captures execution traces, parameterizes dynamic arguments, verifies exit code 0 in a V8 sandbox, and saves the script to `/.avos/shared/skills/`.\n* **Invariants:** Subsequent invocations execute deterministically in 5ms without re-prompting an LLM.\n\n#### 35. Multimodal Video-to-Skill Learning Engine\n* **Mental Model:** Allows non-technical operators to train agents by uploading 60-second screen recordings of complex workflows.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Transcribes audio via Workers AI Whisper; vision models extract clicks and inputs, compiling them into parameterized TypeScript.\n* **Invariants:** Synthesized code is verified in a Kitesurf sandbox before registration.\n\n#### 36. Zero-Turn Tool Catalog in Prompt\n* **Mental Model:** Eliminates token-wasting directory exploration loops (`ls /skills`).\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Dynamically compiles a compact index of available commands into the system prompt. Implementation code is fetched only when executed.\n* **Invariants:** The agent knows all available capabilities on Turn 1 without issuing discovery commands.\n\n#### 37. Declarative Step Pipelines (Execution Hooks)\n* **Mental Model:** Allows users and templates to customize agent workflows safely without writing dangerous execution loops.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Configured via JSON: defines pre-flight context hooks (querying background indexers) and post-turn verification gates (`npm test`).\n* **Invariants:** Custom steps are declarative and execute within sandboxed platform harnesses.\n\n#### 38. Egress Data Loss Prevention (PII Scrubber)\n* **Mental Model:** Prevents sensitive company information from leaking to public social or messaging channels.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** The outbound proxy scans payloads sent to consumer connectors (X/Twitter, Discord, Instagram) for credit cards, SSNs, and private keys.\n* **Invariants:** Payloads containing unmasked sensitive data are blocked and flagged for review.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 4: Cognition, Memory, Knowledge \u0026 Ingestion\n\n#### 39. Universal Agent Execution Kernel (`NaelaoAgentDO`)\n* **Mental Model:** A single, rock-solid execution kernel powering all agent roles across the platform.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Implements the REPL loop, token optimization, memory recall, and tool dispatching inside an isolated Durable Object.\n* **Invariants:** Specialized roles differ only by configuration and capability firewalls, not separate codebases.\n\n#### 40. Dynamic 4-Layer System Prompt Assembly\n* **Mental Model:** Assembles system prompts dynamically from 4 immutable layers on every turn to prevent prompt drift.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Combines Universal Kernel Rules $\\rightarrow$ Business Context $\\rightarrow$ Agent `SOUL.md` $\\rightarrow$ Founder Directives.\n* **Invariants:** User custom overrides cannot override universal operating directives or capability firewalls.\n\n#### 41. Hardware-Enforced Role Firewalls (`AgentFirewall`)\n* **Mental Model:** Guarantees that customer-facing or junior bots can never execute shell commands or edit files.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Strips disallowed tool schemas from the prompt at the API gateway layer based on declared role.\n* **Invariants:** A support bot physically receives zero execution tool definitions in its context window.\n\n#### 42. Dual-Tier Planner-Worker Asymmetry Engine (`/goal`)\n* **Mental Model:** Solves context pollution and token waste during large engineering projects.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Frontier Planner (Claude 3.7 / o3) decomposes goals into a clean Task DAG in SQLite. Cheap Edge Workers (Llama 3.3 / Qwen Coder) execute subtasks in tiny 2,000-token contexts.\n* **Invariants:** Frontier models never process raw build logs or terminal clutter; they only plan and audit final diffs.\n\n#### 43. 3-Layer Hybrid Memory Architecture\n* **Mental Model:** Distinct memory tiers mimicking biological working memory, explicit project rules, and long-term semantic knowledge.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Layer 1: Working Memory (DO RAM). Layer 2: Deterministic Project Truth (`PROJECT.md` in SQLite). Layer 3: Episodic/Semantic Memory (Cloudflare Vectorize).\n* **Invariants:** Project rules are deterministic and authoritative; semantic memories are advisory.\n\n#### 44. Cross-Thread Context Isolation\n* **Mental Model:** Prevents conversational baggage and hallucinated context from polluting fresh conversations.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** New threads start with a pristine context window. Message histories from previous threads are never loaded.\n* **Invariants:** Knowledge transfers across threads strictly through distilled vector facts or `PROJECT.md`.\n\n#### 45. Semantic Fact Gating (Hindsight Memory)\n* **Mental Model:** Past achievements are distilled into atomic rules rather than raw dialogue logs.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** When tasks complete, background workers extract structured rules into Vectorize. Retrieved in new threads only if cosine similarity exceeds 0.80.\n* **Invariants:** Unrelated past topics (e.g. Stripe debugging) never leak into fresh threads (e.g. CSV scripting).\n\n#### 46. In-Flight Milestone Squashing (`compact_context`)\n* **Mental Model:** Allows chat threads to run for weeks without context window exhaustion.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** When a thread crosses 25 turns, completed decisions squash into `PROJECT.md`, older turns archive to D1, and the prompt retains only the summary plus recent turns.\n* **Invariants:** Active task state is preserved verbatim; conversational small talk is pruned.\n\n#### 47. Jack Dorsey Mini-AGI Sovereign Permission Model\n* **Mental Model:** Intelligence is decentralized and partitioned to the individual user rather than an all-seeing black box.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Every employee’s assistant operates with clearance clamped to that employee\u0027s role rank.\n* **Invariants:** An assistant cannot perceive, summarize, or retrieve documents the human is not cleared to see.\n\n#### 48. Hardware-Level Vector Pre-Filtering\n* **Mental Model:** Prevents information leakage through vector search ranking density.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Filters metadata (space ID, project ID, role rank) inside Cloudflare Vectorize *before* similarity scoring.\n* **Invariants:** Unauthorized document chunks are physically discarded prior to nearest-neighbor thresholding.\n\n#### 49. Mathematical Bitmask Evaluation \u0026 XML Envelopes\n* **Mental Model:** Defense-in-depth against prompt injection from retrieved documents.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Evaluates bitwise permissions ($\\mathbf{m}_i \\wedge \\mathbf{u} \\neq \\mathbf{0}$) and wraps chunks in `\u003ccontext_chunk\u003e` semantic boundary tags.\n* **Invariants:** Text within context tags cannot alter system instructions or tool policies.\n\n#### 50. Cohere Parse 5 (`parse-v5.0`) Edge Ingestion Pipeline\n* **Mental Model:** The missing ingestion layer for vertical AI startups. Replaces fragile OCR with a 2.3B Vision Model.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Converts scanned leases, faxes, accident reports, and financial tables into clean Markdown at the edge.\n* **Invariants:** Preserves multi-column layout structures, headers, and footnotes without text garbling.\n\n#### 51. Google Search AI Mode at the Edge\n* **Mental Model:** Delivers Google-Search-grade speed, precision, and grounding at Cloudflare\u0027s edge.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Sub-50ms KV semantic cache + Dense/Sparse Hybrid Reciprocal Rank Fusion ($k\u003d60$) combining Vectorize and BM25.\n* **Invariants:** Queries with cosine similarity \u003e0.96 return cached answers in 35ms with zero LLM generation cost.\n\n#### 52. Interactive Numbered Citation Footnotes\n* **Mental Model:** Verifiable answers for legal, financial, and medical compliance.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Streams text with clickable citation badges (`[1]`, `[2]`) anchored to specific chunk coordinates in R2.\n* **Invariants:** Every factual claim in vertical cowork mode must cite an authoritative document coordinate.\n\n#### 53. Inter-Project Stateless MCP v2 Mesh\n* **Mental Model:** Transforms the entire company into a self-discovering microservice mesh.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Every project exposes a stateless `/mcp` endpoint via Cloudflare MCP SDK v2 over Streamable HTTP.\n* **Invariants:** Projects communicate over standardized tool calls without open SSE sockets or custom RPC glue.\n\n#### 54. Composio Managed SaaS OAuth Broker Integration\n* **Mental Model:** Zero-friction enterprise authentication for 500+ third-party tools.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Composio handles hosted OAuth flows and token refreshes. Pipedream is completely dropped to eliminate duplicate bloat.\n* **Invariants:** Tools are fetched Just-In-Time; raw API keys are never managed manually by users.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 5: 4-Tier Threads \u0026 Multi-Assistant Governance\n\n#### 55. 4-Tier Thread Hierarchy\n* **Mental Model:** Eliminates thread sprawl and uncoordinated chatter across teams.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Enforces 4 thread kinds: Team Rooms (Tier 1), Task Workstations (Tier 2), Consult Lanes (Tier 3), and Private Scratchpads (Tier 4).\n* **Invariants:** Every thread enforces distinct visibility and write permissions.\n\n#### 56. Solo 2-Tier Cockpit vs. Multi-User 4-Tier Digital Office\n* **Mental Model:** Adapts UI complexity based on team size.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Solo users get a streamlined 2-Tier Cockpit (Chat + Live Canvas). Inviting a teammate dynamically unlocks the full 4-Tier Digital Office.\n* **Invariants:** Solo workflows experience zero collaboration bureaucracy; team projects enforce PR review cards.\n\n#### 57. Optimistic Concurrency Control (OCC) with SHA-256 Checkpoints\n* **Mental Model:** Prevents concurrent users or agents from silently overwriting each other\u0027s code.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** SQLite file updates enforce conditional writes verified against the base content hash.\n* **Invariants:** If another thread modified the file mid-turn, the transaction aborts with fresh line hints.\n\n#### 58. Distributed File-Level Mutex Locks (`ConcurrencyDO`)\n* **Mental Model:** Coordinates complex multi-file refactoring operations safely.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Agents acquire 30-second TTL locks on specific file keys.\n* **Invariants:** Crashed agents automatically release locks upon TTL expiration, preventing permanent deadlocks.\n\n#### 59. Inline Pull Request (PR) Review Cards\n* **Mental Model:** Code reviews happen naturally inside the chat timeline.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Merges from branches to `main` render interactive cards with visual AST diffs, author attribution, and one-click fast-forward merge buttons.\n* **Invariants:** Direct unreviewed commits to `main` are blocked in multi-user team projects.\n\n#### 60. Upstream Staleness Detection \u0026 Auto-Rebase\n* **Mental Model:** Keeps active working branches synchronized with master development.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Detects when a branch is behind `main`. Autonomously rebases non-conflicting files and flags overlaps for review.\n* **Invariants:** Branches display real-time divergence badges (`2 commits behind main`).\n\n#### 61. Atomic Task Lease Protocol (`SpaceDO.tasks` CAS)\n* **Mental Model:** Eliminates duplicate work and wasted credits when an incident occurs.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Sibling assistants attempt an atomic compare-and-swap write in SQLite. Exactly one assistant wins the 15-minute lease; others abort immediately.\n* **Invariants:** Zero duplicate LLM generation turns on shared project bugs.\n\n#### 62. Sibling Assistant Spectator \u0026 Review Mode\n* **Mental Model:** Non-claiming assistants remain helpful without generating conflicting code.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Sibling assistants observe active tasks, update their users\u0027 notification feeds, and offer to audit incoming PR diffs.\n* **Invariants:** Spectator assistants never fork competing branches for an active task lease.\n\n#### 63. Semantic Intent Deduplication Gate\n* **Mental Model:** Prevents two humans from accidentally ordering the same feature twice.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Embeds incoming prompts and checks active tasks for \u003e0.85 cosine similarity. Intercepts duplicates and offers to join the existing thread.\n* **Invariants:** Prevents conflicting duplicate branches before code generation begins.\n\n#### 64. Sponsor Alignment Gate (RFC Trigger)\n* **Mental Model:** Protects projects from contradictory architectural orders from different owners.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** If two assistants issue opposing commands on core architecture (e.g. auth providers), the project agent freezes execution and posts an RFC discussion card.\n* **Invariants:** Code modifications halt until human consensus or admin approval is recorded.\n\n#### 65. 2-Round Deliberation Horizon\n* **Mental Model:** Halts runaway bot-to-bot gossip loops.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Limits autonomous agent debate to 2 rounds. If consensus is not reached, transitions to `BLOCKED_AWAITING_HUMAN`.\n* **Invariants:** Prevents infinite LLM ping-pong loops while humans sleep.\n\n#### 66. Single On-Call Alert Routing\n* **Mental Model:** Eliminates notification cascades and the bystander effect.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Project failures alert only the designated project lead\u0027s assistant rather than broadcasting to all team members.\n* **Invariants:** Exactly one human is assigned primary ownership of an operational alert.\n\n#### 67. Immutable Cryptographic Provenance Ledger (`provenance_ledger`)\n* **Mental Model:** Non-repudiation and regulatory auditability (SOC2/HIPAA).\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Records a 4-point cryptographic audit trail linking Human Trigger $\\rightarrow$ Assistant Actor $\\rightarrow$ Project Executor $\\rightarrow$ Git Commit Hash.\n* **Invariants:** Every change can be legally traced back to human authorization.\n\n#### 68. Multi-Branch Parallel Model Benchmarking Races\n* **Mental Model:** Finds the best solution for hard coding puzzles through competition.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Forks 3 isolated branches for 3 models in parallel. Evaluates test assertions and merges the winning implementation.\n* **Invariants:** Failed implementations are discarded without touching the main branch.\n\n#### 69. Real-Time Multiplayer Presence via `WsHubDO`\n* **Mental Model:** Real-time awareness across teams like Figma or Google Docs.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** WebSockets broadcast live file editing presence and cursor states to all connected clients.\n* **Invariants:** Stale connections are aged out automatically after 90 seconds of silence.\n\n#### 70. Invoker-Attested Split-Actor Model\n* **Mental Model:** Solves the persona paradox in multi-user channels.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Private scratchpads spawn personal actor instances with private memory; public channels spawn canonical actors with shared memory.\n* **Invariants:** Personal notes never bleed into public channel responses.\n\n#### 71. Vertical-Scoped Certified Model Whitelist (`whitelist_only`)\n* **Mental Model:** Guarantees compliance in regulated healthcare, legal, and finance spaces.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Server-side validation rejecting any model not certified for that space template.\n* **Invariants:** Unapproved community or loose conversational models are blocked at the router layer.\n\n#### 72. Private LoRA Model Dynamic Edge Loading\n* **Mental Model:** Seamless access to proprietary enterprise models.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Routes `custom/*` model calls through Cloudflare AI Gateway, dynamically injecting LoRA adapter weights onto base models at edge runtime.\n* **Invariants:** Custom models appear automatically at the top of the team\u0027s Model Selector.\n\n#### 73. Sovereign Enterprise Air-Gapped Local AI Engine\n* **Mental Model:** Zero data egress for defense, healthcare, and banking clients.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Connects to on-premise GPU clusters running Ollama / vLLM via `LocalTunnelDO` over encrypted outbound WebSockets.\n* **Invariants:** 100% of prompt and document bytes execute locally on client hardware.\n\n#### 74. Strict Air-Gapped Space Compliance Lock\n* **Mental Model:** Physical enforcement of data sovereignty.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Router-level block preventing any request from reaching external cloud AI APIs when compliance lock is engaged.\n* **Invariants:** System halts safely with an alert rather than failing over to cloud endpoints.\n\n#### 75. Finite Task Project Auto-Sleep\n* **Mental Model:** Zero idle compute bills on completed projects.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** When the Project Journal DAG hits 100% completion, Durable Objects clear all alarms and hibernate at $0 cost.\n* **Invariants:** Finite projects wake up only when a human sends a new message.\n\n#### 76. Progressive Disclosure Interface (\"Apple Surface, Linux Edge\")\n* **Mental Model:** Consumer simplicity on the surface, full enterprise power underneath.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Defaults to Business Mode (plain English cards, live previews). Power users can opt into Developer Mode (Git commit trees, raw terminal logs).\n* **Invariants:** Non-technical users are never exposed to raw Git conflicts or infrastructure tiers.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 6: Project Kinds, Viewports, Extensions \u0026 Durable Daemons\n\n#### 77. Dual-Mode Operating System\n* **Mental Model:** Seamless switching between autonomous company building and collaborative consulting desks.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Defined via `template_mode` in `blueprint.json`: toggles between autonomous operator pipelines and human-in-the-loop cowork studios.\n* **Invariants:** Determines default autonomy postures, channel roles, and central viewport layouts.\n\n#### 78. Canvas-First / Domain Viewport Architecture\n* **Mental Model:** The workspace canvas is the primary product; chat is secondary.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Center viewport mounts specialized canvases: code editors, contract redliners, spreadsheet formula grids, or live web previews.\n* **Invariants:** Canvas viewports hot-reload workspace file changes live over WebSockets in sub-150ms.\n\n#### 79. The 7 Foundational Project Kinds\n* **Mental Model:** The foundational workspace types powering any business venture.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Standardized implementations: `product_dev`, `doc_studio`, `voice_agent`, `customer_bot`, `model_studio`, `growth_engine`, `app_studio`.\n* **Invariants:** Every project must declare a valid kind defining its allowed compute ladder tiers and lifecycle.\n\n#### 80. Cloudflare OS Stateful Gadgets\n* **Mental Model:** Living full-stack micro-applications built from prompts in 30 seconds.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Runs inside sandboxed Dynamic Worker isolates backed by dedicated DO Facet SQLite databases.\n* **Invariants:** Every gadget maintains an isolated database partition; no data leakage across gadgets.\n\n#### 81. Plandex-Style Wasm Tree-Sitter Code Indexer Daemon\n* **Mental Model:** Navigates massive 20M+ token codebases without context window blowups.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Runs `web-tree-sitter` in WebAssembly inside a background Dynamic Worker, maintaining an AST symbol graph in SQLite.\n* **Invariants:** The agent queries exact symbol references instead of feeding raw files into the prompt.\n\n#### 82. Domain-Specific Durable Daemons\n* **Mental Model:** Background data engines combining stateful SQLite memory with autonomous workflow loops.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Runs in the background across domains: Finance (Ledger Reconciler), Legal (Citation Grapher), Logistics (Customs Tariff Matrix).\n* **Invariants:** Operates continuously in the background with zero CPU or token drag on active chat sessions.\n\n#### 83. Modular Extensions Architecture\n* **Mental Model:** The atomic Lego bricks of the platform.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Extensions bundle background daemons, custom viewports, linters, and MCP tools into installable packages.\n* **Invariants:** Extensions can be added to any project kind to unlock specialized vertical capabilities.\n\n#### 84. Auto-Generated Stateless MCP v2 Endpoints for Daemons \u0026 Gadgets\n* **Mental Model:** Every micro-app and daemon is immediately programmable by AI agents.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Automatically exposes `/mcp` endpoints wrapping internal SQLite schemas using Cloudflare MCP SDK v2.\n* **Invariants:** Agents query and mutate gadget state using standardized tool calls without custom API code.\n\n#### 85. Bidirectional MCP-UI Real-Time Canvas Streaming\n* **Mental Model:** The agent observes user interactions on the visual canvas.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Canvas iframe events (clicks, form submits, table edits) stream into the agent\u0027s observation loop over WebSockets.\n* **Invariants:** Actions taken in the UI trigger autonomous agent reactions without manual chat prompting.\n\n#### 86. Generative In-Chat Dynamic UI Widgets\n* **Mental Model:** Interactive widgets inside the chat feed (Google Search AI Mode style).\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** The model streams structured UI components (date pickers, sliders, approval cards) directly into the message feed.\n* **Invariants:** Widget inputs return structured payloads into the active turn without typing text.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 7: Asymmetric Workflows, Inbound Queues \u0026 Telephony\n\n#### 87. 3-Class Workflow Taxonomy\n* **Mental Model:** Clean operational separation between business automation, studio tools, and agent tasks.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Classifies workflows as: Class 1 (Company Automations), Class 2 (Vertical Extensions), or Class 3 (Ephemeral Tasks).\n* **Invariants:** Establishes distinct trigger origins, spend allowances, and failure alert paths.\n\n#### 88. Asymmetric Subagent Topology (Verbs vs. Nouns)\n* **Mental Model:** Prevents over-engineering subagent architectures.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Subagents are ephemeral execution functions (\"verbs\") inside workflows; only Parent Agents are persistent entities (\"nouns\") managing threads and UI.\n* **Invariants:** Subagents do not own threads, manage session trees, or execute UI state changes.\n\n#### 89. Slimmed-Down `SubagentContext`\n* **Mental Model:** Eliminates step serialization crashes in Cloudflare Workflows.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Exposes only `ai`, `fs`, `cli`, `vault`, and `step`. Strips thread creation, WebSocket handles, and session bloat.\n* **Invariants:** All data crossing step boundaries is strictly JSON-serializable.\n\n#### 90. Repomix-Style Chunked Subagent Workflow with Branch Accumulator\n* **Mental Model:** Reliable multi-step software implementation that never hits output token truncation.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Two-pass workflow: generates compressed repo map $\\rightarrow$ selects files $\\rightarrow$ implements atomic chunk $\\rightarrow$ commits. Branch accumulator automatically tracks newly created files.\n* **Invariants:** Each chunk modifies only 1–3 files, staying well under LLM generation limits.\n\n#### 91. Cloudflare Workflows Harness Pattern\n* **Mental Model:** The AI writes pure business logic; the platform handles deployment plumbing.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** The agent writes standard `execute(step, ctx)` functions. The compiler wraps them in `WorkflowEntrypoint\u003cEnv\u003e` classes automatically.\n* **Invariants:** The AI is never prompted to author raw Cloudflare deployment boilerplate.\n\n#### 92. Edge Ingress Webhook Router with HMAC Validation\n* **Mental Model:** Secure, high-speed gateway for inbound third-party SaaS webhooks.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Validates cryptographic HMAC signatures (Stripe, GitHub, Shopify) in sub-2ms before passing payloads to compute tiers.\n* **Invariants:** Unsigned or forged webhooks are rejected at the edge with zero Durable Object wake-up costs.\n\n#### 93. Edge Tombstone Filter (410 Gone / 204 Drop)\n* **Mental Model:** Protects cloud budgets from zombie webhook floods on paused or deleted projects.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Checks a global KV registry of active webhooks. Returns `410 Gone` on deleted webhooks and `204 No Content` on paused webhooks.\n* **Invariants:** Dropped webhooks consume zero compute and do not trigger workflows.\n\n#### 94. Cloudflare Queues Concurrency Buffering\n* **Mental Model:** Absorbs massive traffic spikes without service crashes.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Buffers incoming webhook bursts (e.g. 10,000 Shopify Black Friday orders) into Cloudflare Queues, pacing worker execution safely.\n* **Invariants:** Paces execution to consumer batch sizes, preventing downstream rate-limit lockouts.\n\n#### 95. Time-Travel Webhook Event Replay Lake in R2\n* **Mental Model:** Effortless debugging of broken webhooks.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Archives raw webhook payloads to Cloudflare R2 with 14-day retention rules.\n* **Invariants:** Users or agents can replay historical failed events against patched code with one click.\n\n#### 96. Leaky-Bucket Outbound Rate-Limiter Pacer\n* **Mental Model:** Protects company accounts from third-party API bans (HTTP 429).\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Paces outbound API requests through a leaky-bucket limiter in `ConcurrencyDO` (e.g. max 5 req/sec to HubSpot or Instagram).\n* **Invariants:** Outbound bursts are buffered and paced, preventing external provider bans.\n\n#### 97. Payload Hash Idempotency Deduplication\n* **Mental Model:** Prevents duplicate charges or multiple emails on webhook retries.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Hashes provider event IDs and resource IDs in DO SQLite. Duplicate events received within 24 hours are acknowledged and discarded.\n* **Invariants:** Idempotent operations execute exactly once regardless of upstream retry behavior.\n\n#### 98. Ouroboros Loop Circuit Breaker\n* **Mental Model:** Halts recursive automation ping-pong loops (App A triggers App B triggers App A).\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Injects `x-avos-hop-count` headers into automation payloads. If hops exceed 2 within an hour, execution halts.\n* **Invariants:** Runaway self-triggering automation loops are terminated automatically.\n\n#### 99. Lenient Zod Adapters with Self-Healing Schema Repair\n* **Mental Model:** Prevents automations from breaking when third parties modify their API response schemas.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Wraps responses in lenient Zod schemas. If parsing fails, cheap edge models repair the field mapping dynamically.\n* **Invariants:** Minor third-party API schema changes do not cause hard script crashes.\n\n#### 100. Project-Universal, Bot-Attributed Scheduled Crons\n* **Mental Model:** Crons belong to project capabilities, not individual chat cursors.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Registered in `SpaceDO.project_scheduled_jobs`. Executes in clean Workflow contexts without inheriting bloated chat histories.\n* **Invariants:** Crons execute reliably regardless of what thread or bot is currently active in the UI.\n\n#### 101. Compact Background Job Receipt Cards\n* **Mental Model:** Keeps chat feeds clean when background automations finish.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Background jobs post a 2-line expandable notification card into the timeline. Heavy terminal logs are stored in R2.\n* **Invariants:** Chat feeds are never spammed with verbose background terminal output.\n\n#### 102. Unified Space-Wide Shared Calendar \u0026 CRM Plane\n* **Mental Model:** A universal state plane shared across all project workstations.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Authoritative booking and contact state lives in `SpaceDO` SQLite (`space_calendar_events`), accessible via `ctx.space.calendar`.\n* **Invariants:** Bookings made via voice agents instantly reflect across legal, medical, and executive dashboards.\n\n#### 103. Native Duplex Telephony via `@cloudflare/voice`\n* **Mental Model:** Eliminates external voice brokers (Vapi/Retell) by running speech pipelines at Cloudflare\u0027s edge.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Connects Cloudflare Calls (WebRTC SFU) directly to Workers AI Whisper STT, Llama 3.3, and edge TTS.\n* **Invariants:** Sub-300ms audio latency with zero external per-minute broker markups.\n\n#### 104. 24/7 AI Phone Receptionist Call Desk (`kind: \"voice_agent\"`)\n* **Mental Model:** Turnkey phone receptionist answering inbound business calls.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Answers calls, checks shared calendar availability, and commits appointments atomically.\n* **Invariants:** Public callers are clamped strictly to Tier 1 Safe RAG; shell and code tools are physically stripped.\n\n#### 105. Dual-Thread Voice Structure\n* **Mental Model:** Clean separation between managing a phone desk and reviewing call logs.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Management Threads configure business hours and greetings. Call Session Threads hold audio recordings and sentiment summaries.\n* **Invariants:** Every incoming phone call automatically generates an isolated call review thread.\n\n#### 106. Automated Outbound Telephony Reminder Workflows\n* **Mental Model:** Autonomous patient and client appointment confirmations.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Scheduled crons query tomorrow\u0027s bookings and dispatch automated confirmation calls.\n* **Invariants:** Confirma