      {
      "text": "This maps directly to Cloudflare’s **Cloudflare OS (August 2026)** release, which introduced **Gadgets** (isolated, per-document/per-tool sandboxes on Dynamic Workers with DO Facets), **Blueprints** (shareable gadget templates), and **Gatekeepers** (the capability-based security model).\n\nHere is how we integrate **Project Canvas Viewports**, **Stateless Versioned Artifacts**, and **On-Demand Stateful Gadgets**, complete with **MCP-UI streaming** and **Cross-Subspace/Cross-Department permission delegation**.\n\n---\n\n# 1. The 3-Tier Canvas, Artifact, \u0026 Micro-App Hierarchy\n\n```\n┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                   THE 3-TIER ARTIFACT \u0026 APP HIERARCHY                                     │\n├────────────────────┬─────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┤\n│ Tier Level         │ Execution \u0026 State       │ Underlying Cloudflare Tech │ Primary Purpose               │\n├────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Tier 1: Canvas** │ **Live Workspace View** │ `@cloudflare/computer` +   │ Deep project UI extensions    │\n│ **Viewports**      │ (Direct File Access)    │ Project SQLite Virtual FS  │ (Code Editor, Redliner, Comps)│\n├────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Tier 2: Versioned│ **Stateless Snapshots** │ Cloudflare Artifacts       │ Ephemeral deliverables (PDFs, │\n│ **Artifacts**      │ (Immutable Git Commits) │ (Zig-Wasm Git Server in DO)│ SVGs, static HTML previews)   │\n├────────────────────┼─────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Tier 3: Stateful │ **Living Mini-Apps**    │ **Dynamic Workers +**      │ Full-stack vibe-coded apps    │\n│ **Gadgets**        │ (Dedicated Database)    │ **DO Facets (SQLite DB)**  │ (Leave Tracker, Bug Matrix)   │\n└────────────────────┴─────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Tier 1: Project Canvas Viewports (Workspace-Bound UI)\n* **What it is:** Extends the Project Kind\u0027s main workspace viewport (e.g. `CodeWorkspace` for `product_dev`, `DocumentRedlineCanvas` for `doc_studio`, `SpreadsheetFormulaGrid` for `finance_grid`).\n* **Storage \u0026 Access:** Directly attached to the project\u0027s **authoritative SQLite Virtual Filesystem** (`@cloudflare/computer`).\n* **Behavior:** When an agent runs `Edit` or `Write`, this canvas hot-reloads the changes live over WebSockets in sub-150ms.\n\n---\n\n### Tier 2: Stateless / Versioned Artifacts (Claude Artifacts on Cloudflare)\n* **What it is:** Ephemeral, versioned deliverables generated during conversation turns (e.g., a static SVG flowchart, a compiled PDF invoice, or an interactive React chart).\n* **Storage \u0026 Versioning:** Stored as immutable commits inside **Cloudflare Artifacts (Git for Agents)**.\n* **Behavior:** Users can scrub the thread history like a time machine and click **[Fork Artifact]** or **[Revert Workspace to this Commit]**.\n\n---\n\n### Tier 3: On-Demand Stateful Micro-Apps (\"Cloudflare OS Gadgets\")\n* **What it is:** A full-stack, living micro-application (built from a prompt in 30 seconds) that holds **its own private database and business logic**.\n* **Storage \u0026 Execution:**\n  * **Frontend:** Sandboxed in a null-origin `\u003ciframe\u003e` that communicates with the server via **Cap\u0027n Web RPC / MCP-UI**.\n  * **Backend \u0026 Database:** Runs inside a **Dynamic Worker isolate** backed by an isolated **Durable Object Facet SQLite database**.\n  * **Self-Exposing API:** Automatically gets an **MCP v2 `/mcp` endpoint**, allowing AI agents to read, query, or automate the gadget natively!\n\n---\n\n# 2. The 4 Scopes: Who Can Access \u0026 Install Gadgets?\n\nGadgets can be provisioned at four distinct organizational boundaries with zero security leakage:\n\n```\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │           PARENT COMPANY SPACE (Root)        │\n                                  └──────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘\n                                                         │\n                         ┌───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┐\n                         ▼                                                               ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 🏢 SCOPE 3: SPACE-WIDE GADGET (Company Commons)             │   │ 🏢 CROSS-SUBSPACE DELEGATION (PM ──► Dev Subspace)          │\n│ • Installed for the entire organization.                    │   │ • PM creates \"Bug Intake Gadget\" in PM Subspace.            │\n│ • Example: *Company-Wide PTO Leave Approval Tracker*.       │   │ • Shares delegated Gatekeeper token to Dev Subspace.        │\n│ • All members across all departments see and use it.        │   │ • Devs log tickets directly into PM\u0027s private DO database!  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                         │                                                               │\n                         ▼                                                               ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 📁 SCOPE 2: PROJECT-BOUND GADGET                            │   │ 👤 SCOPE 1: PERSONAL USER GADGET (Private Sandbox)          │\n│ • Bound strictly to 1 Project (e.g. `Project: Warehouse`).  │   │ • Created by Alice for her own use.                         │\n│ • Example: *Barcode Equipment Scanner \u0026 Return Ledger*.     │   │ • Example: *Alice\u0027s Private Pomodoro Timer \u0026 Scratchpad*.   │\n│ • Shared only among teammates inside that specific project. │   │ • Completely invisible to Bob, PMs, and other coworkers.    │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Cross-Subspace Delegation: PM Subspace $\\rightarrow$ Dev Subspace\n\n\u003e **The Real-World Enterprise Scenario:**  \n\u003e A Project Manager in the **PM Department Subspace** prompts the AI to build a *\"QA Bug Reporting \u0026 Acceptance Matrix Gadget\"*. The PM wants developers in the **Engineering Department Subspace** to use it without giving developers full access to the PM\u0027s confidential space.\n\n#### How It Works via Gatekeepers (Zero Auth Boilerplate):\n1. **The PM builds the Gadget:** The Gadget is created inside the PM Subspace with its own **DO Facet SQLite database**.\n2. **The PM clicks `[Share Gadget with Engineering Subspace]`:**\n   * The platform mints an attenuated **Gatekeeper Capability Grant**:\n     `grant \u003d { target: \"gadget_bug_matrix_102\", allowed_ops: [\"insert_ticket\", \"read_assigned_tickets\"] }`.\n3. **The Gadget mounts in the Dev Subspace:**\n   * Developers open the gadget inside their Engineering space.\n   * When a developer logs a bug, the request routes across the Cloudflare edge to the PM\u0027s DO Facet SQLite database!\n   * Developers **cannot** see the PM\u0027s other private roadmap files or parent space ledgers.\n\n---\n\n# 3. How Auth Works (Zero Code Written by Users)\n\nIn Cloudflare OS Gadgets, **the application code never handles authentication or user logins**.\n\n* The UI runs in a secure, sandboxed null-origin `\u003ciframe\u003e`.\n* The platform\u0027s edge proxy authenticates the user via **Cloudflare Zero Trust / AVOS JWT Session**.\n* The runtime injects the authenticated caller context directly into the Gadget\u0027s backend:\n\n```typescript\n// Inside the Gadget\u0027s Backend Dynamic Worker:\nexport async function handleGadgetRequest(request: Request, ctx: GadgetContext) {\n  // `ctx.caller` is injected by the platform edge — 100% tamper-proof!\n  const { userId, userRole, spaceId, permissions } \u003d ctx.caller;\n\n  if (request.method \u003d\u003d\u003d \"POST\" \u0026\u0026 request.url.endsWith(\"/submit-ticket\")) {\n    const body \u003d await request.json() as any;\n    \n    // Write to private DO Facet SQLite\n    ctx.storage.sql.exec(`\n      INSERT INTO tickets (id, reporter_user_id, title, status, space_id)\n      VALUES (?, ?, ?, \u0027OPEN\u0027, ?)\n    `, `tick_${Date.now()}`, userId, body.title, spaceId);\n\n    // Stream action event to observing agents via MCP-UI\n    ctx.mcp.emitUiAction({ action: \"TICKET_CREATED\", ticketId: `tick_${Date.now()}`, author: userId });\n    \n    return Response.json({ ok: true });\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n# 4. The Complete Declarative Gadget Manifest (`gadget.json`)\n\n```typescript\nexport interface AvosGadgetManifest {\n  id: string; // e.g. \"gadget_bug_tracker_v1\"\n  name: string;\n  description: string;\n  \n  // 1. Scoping \u0026 Installation Boundary\n  scope: \"USER_PRIVATE\" | \"PROJECT_BOUND\" | \"SPACE_WIDE\" | \"CROSS_SUBSPACE_DELEGATED\";\n  ownerSpaceId: string;\n  ownerUserId: string;\n  \n  // Target Subspaces (For Cross-Subspace Sharing)\n  delegatedTargetSpaceIds?: string[];\n\n  // 2. Storage \u0026 Compute\n  runtime: {\n    engine: \"dynamic_worker_isolate\"; // Runs in sub-ms V8 isolate\n    database: \"do_facet_sqlite\";       // Private dedicated SQLite DB\n    enableMcpV2Api: boolean;          // Exposes auto-generated /mcp endpoint\n  };\n\n  // 3. Gatekeeper Security Policy\n  gatekeeperGrants: Array\u003c{\n    resource: \"sqlite_db\" | \"notifications\" | \"slack\";\n    operations: Array\u003c\"read\" | \"write\" | \"notify\"\u003e;\n  }\u003e;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary of What This Establishes\n\n1. **Clean 3-Tier Separation:**  \n   * **Canvas Viewports:** Live workspace file editors.  \n   * **Artifacts:** Stateless versioned Git deliverables (Cloudflare Artifacts).  \n   * **Gadgets:** Stateful, sandboxed full-stack mini-apps with dedicated **DO Facet SQLite databases**.\n2. **MCP-UI Real-Time Streaming:** User actions inside any Gadget (button clicks, form submits) stream back to the agent\u0027s observation loop in real time.\n3. **Cross-Subspace Interoperability:** A PM in Department A can build a tool and delegate it to Developers in Department B with **Gatekeeper capability tokens**, enabling cross-firm workflows with zero data leaks.\n4. **Zero-Trust Auth by Construction:** Users vibe-code gadgets with zero authentication logic; Cloudflare\u0027s edge runtime securely validates user identities and roles before requests ever reach the database.",
