     │ 👩‍💻 **Alice:** \"Hey team, we need to add the new Stripe webhook.\"   │\n│ ├── 💬 # Team Room (Public)       │                                                                     │\n│ └── 📋 Active Tasks \u0026 PRs:        │ 👩‍💻 **Alice:** \"@DevBot please implement the signature check in      │\n│     ├── 📌 #102: Stripe Webhooks  │                `src/api/webhook.ts` and test with `npm run build`.\" │\n│     └── 📌 #103: Dark Mode Navbar │                                                                     │\n│                                   │ 🤖 **@DevBot [⚙️ Dev Operator]:**                                    │\n│ 🔒 **My Private Drafts (Tier 4):**│ \"On it, Alice! I\u0027ve created branch `dev-stripe-fix`, applied the    │\n│ └── 📝 Scratchpad with @DevBot    │  AST patch, and opened PR #15 for @ReviewBot to inspect.\"           │\n│                                   │                                                                     │\n│ ⚙️ **Bot Wakes (Tier 3 Hidden):** │ ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │\n│ └── [x] Show 3 Heartbeat Runs     │ │ 📬 **Pull Request #15: \"Stripe Webhook Signature Verification\"** │ │\n│                                   │ │ 🤖 @ReviewBot: \"AST syntax checks passed (Exit Code 0).\"        │ │\n│                                   │ │ [ ✅ Merge to Main Workspace ]           [ 🔍 View Git Diff ]   │ │\n│                                   │ └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │\n└───────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. How the Agent Roster \u0026 Thread Tiers Harmonize\n\nThe **Agent Roster** (The *\"Who\"*) and the **Thread Tiers** (The *\"Where \u0026 What\"*) work together with zero conceptual friction:\n\n```\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │           THE PROJECT AGENT ROSTER           │\n                                  │    [@ArchitectBot, @DevBot, @ReviewBot...]   │\n                                  └──────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘\n                                                         │\n                         ┌───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┐\n                         ▼                                                               ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 💬 TIER 1 \u0026 TIER 2: PUBLIC COLLABORATIVE ROOMS              │   │ 🔒 TIER 4: PRIVATE 1-ON-1 SCRATCHPAD                        │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤   ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ • **Interaction:** Slack-style multi-player room.           │   │ • **Interaction:** Alice clicks `[ 💬 Private Chat ]` on   │\n│ • **How Bots Respond:** Only when explicitly `@mentioned`   │   │   `@DevBot` in the top roster bar.                          │\n│   (e.g., `@DevBot fix the styling`).                        │   │ • **Isolation:** Spawns a private Tier 4 scratchpad.       │\n│ • **Multi-Human Concurrency:** Handled by single-threaded   │   │ • **Safety:** Read-only simulation sandbox. Zero risk of   │\n│   Durable Object FIFO queues with live `[Queued...]` tags.  │   │   silent unreviewed commits to the shared workspace.        │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Implementation: The Roster Header Component (`apps/shell`)\n\nHere is how we implement the **Project Roster Bar** in `apps/shell/src/components/ProjectRosterHeader.tsx`:\n\n```tsx\n// apps/shell/src/components/ProjectRosterHeader.tsx\nimport { Badge, Button } from \"@naelao/ui\";\nimport { useState } from \"react\";\n\nexport interface ProjectAgentMember {\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  avatar: string;\n  role: \"ARCHITECT\" | \"DEV\" | \"REVIEW\" | \"GROWTH\" | \"HUMAN\";\n  status: \"ACTIVE\" | \"CODING\" | \"REVIEWING\" | \"SLEEPING\" | \"IDLE\";\n  activeTask?: string;\n  currentBranch?: string;\n}\n\nexport function ProjectRosterHeader({\n  members,\n  onStartPrivateScratchpad,\n  onMentionInChat\n}: {\n  members: ProjectAgentMember[];\n  onStartPrivateScratchpad: (agentId: string) \u003d\u003e void;\n  onMentionInChat: (agentName: string) \u003d\u003e void;\n}) {\n  const [selectedAgent, setSelectedAgent] \u003d useState\u003cProjectAgentMember | null\u003e(null);\n\n  return (\n    \u003cdiv className\u003d\"project-roster-bar\" style\u003d{{ display: \"flex\", gap: \"10px\", padding: \"10px 16px\", background: \"var(--surface2)\", borderBottom: \"1px solid var(--border)\", overflowX: \"auto\" }}\u003e\n      {members.map(member \u003d\u003e (\n        \u003cdiv\n          key\u003d{member.id}\n          className\u003d\"roster-member-card\"\n          onClick\u003d{() \u003d\u003e setSelectedAgent(member)}\n          style\u003d{{ display: \"flex\", alignItems: \"center\", gap: \"8px\", padding: \"6px 12px\", background: \"var(--bg)\", borderRadius: \"8px\", border: \"1px solid var(--border)\", cursor: \"pointer\" }}\n        \u003e\n          \u003cspan style\u003d{{ fontSize: \"16px\" }}\u003e{member.avatar}\u003c/span\u003e\n          \u003cdiv style\u003d{{ display: \"flex\", flexDirection: \"column\" }}\u003e\n            \u003cspan style\u003d{{ fontSize: \"12.5px\", fontWeight: 600, color: \"var(--text)\" }}\u003e@{member.name}\u003c/span\u003e\n            \u003cspan style\u003d{{ fontSize: \"10.5px\", color: \"var(--text3)\" }}\u003e\n              {member.status \u003d\u003d\u003d \"CODING\" \u0026\u0026 \"🟢 Coding...\"}\n              {member.status \u003d\u003d\u003d \"REVIEWING\" \u0026\u0026 \"🟡 Reviewing PR\"}\n              {member.status \u003d\u003d\u003d \"SLEEPING\" \u0026\u0026 \"💤 Sleeping\"}\n              {member.status \u003d\u003d\u003d \"IDLE\" \u0026\u0026 \"⚪ Ready\"}\n            \u003c/span\u003e\n          \u003c/div\u003e\n        \u003c/div\u003e\n      ))}\n\n      {/* Quick Action Drawer when clicking a Bot */}\n      {selectedAgent \u0026\u0026 selectedAgent.role !\u003d\u003d \"HUMAN\" \u0026\u0026 (\n        \u003cdiv className\u003d\"roster-action-modal\"\u003e\n          \u003ch4\u003e🤖 {selectedAgent.name}\u003c/h4\u003e\n          \u003cp style\u003d{{ fontSize: \"12px\", color: \"var(--text2)\" }}\u003e{selectedAgent.activeTask || \"Standing by for project instructions.\"}\u003c/p\u003e\n          \u003cdiv style\u003d{{ display: \"flex\", gap: \"8px\", marginTop: \"10px\" }}\u003e\n            \u003cButton size\u003d\"sm\" variant\u003d\"primary\" onClick\u003d{() \u003d\u003e onStartPrivateScratchpad(selectedAgent.id)}\u003e\n              🔒 Start Private 1-on-1 Draft (Tier 4)\n            \u003c/Button\u003e\n            \u003cButton size\u003d\"sm\" variant\u003d\"ghost\" onClick\u003d{() \u003d\u003e onMentionInChat(selectedAgent.name)}\u003e\n              💬 Mention in Team Room\n            \u003c/Button\u003e\n          \u003c/div\u003e\n        \u003c/div\u003e\n      )}\n    \u003c/div\u003e\n  );\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Instant Autocomplete `@mentions` in `ComposerDock.tsx`\n\nWhen a user types `@` in `ComposerDock.tsx`, an autocomplete popup dynamically shows the active project roster (humans + bots):\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ @dev                                                        │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 🤖 **@DevBot**      [⚙️ Lead Full-Stack Edge Developer]     │\n│ 🤖 **@ReviewBot**   [🔍 Automated AST Code Reviewer]        │\n│ 🤖 **@ArchitectBot** [📐 System Planner \u0026 DAG Dispatcher]   │\n│ 👩‍💻 **@Alice**        [Project Owner]                         │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary of What to Adopt:\n\n1. **Replace the \"Chat Sessions\" Mental Model:** The project sidebar and header now display the **Project Team Roster** (the persistent AI and human coworkers assigned to that workspace).\n2. **Harmonized with Thread Tiers:**\n   * In **Team Rooms (Tier 1/2)**: Multi-human conversation; bots respond on `@mention` [1.3.17].\n   * In **Private Scratchpads (Tier 4)**: Initiated by clicking *\"Private Chat\"* on any bot in the roster, creating an isolated simulation sandbox.\n3. **Apple-Grade Experience:** The user feels like they are leading an active, talented team of digital specialists with clear statuses, avatars, and one-click action cards [1.1.2].",
