      "text": "Nous Research introduced **\"Bot Mode\" in Hermes Agent** to solve this exact problem: moving from disposable, single-session chatbots into a **persistent roster of specialized AI teammates (each with its own role, model, memory, `SOUL.md` identity, and group chat capabilities)**.\n\nBy combining **Hermes\u0027s Multi-Bot Group Chat \u0026 Persona Architecture** with our **Cloudflare 4-Tier Threads and Artifacts Git Mesh**, you create a multi-agent office environment.\n\n---\n\n# 1. How Hermes \"Bot Mode\" Works (The 5 Core Principles)\n\nBased on Nous Research\u0027s Hermes Agent architecture:\n1. **A Bot is a Persistent Profile:** A bot is not a temporary chat thread. It is an isolated persona bundle with its own **`SOUL.md` identity file**, dedicated tools, pinned model, recurring routines (crons), and memory bank.\n2. **Canonical Bot Chats:** Every bot has its own permanent, 1-on-1 private chat created the moment the bot is born.\n3. **Multi-Bot Group Deliberation:** 2 to 6 bots can sit in a shared room and take turns over **serial rounds per message**, respond when `@mentioned`, or **pass** if the query is outside their specialty.\n4. **Bot-to-Bot Direct Inboxes:** Bots can message each other directly in background conversations without human intervention.\n5. **Hybrid Memory Scoping (Hindsight / Vectorize):** Each bot has its own **private memory bank** (personal learnings), plus access to a **shared project memory bank** (team facts).\n\n---\n\n# 2. How to Implement Bot Personas \u0026 `SOUL.md` in AVOS\n\nIn AVOS, every bot in a project is defined by a declarative **Bot Persona Manifest** stored in `SpaceDO` SQLite and R2:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    BOT PERSONA BUNDLE: `@DevBot`                            │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1. `SOUL.md` (Identity File)  │ Personality, voice, expertise, boundaries   │\n│ 2. `skills/` (CodeMode Tools) │ Pre-attached Tier 1-6 scripts (`Edit`, Bash)│\n│ 3. Pinned Model               │ `qwen2.5-coder:32b` or `llama-3.3-70b`      │\n│ 4. Memory Scoping             │ Private Vector Bank + Shared Project Vector │\n│ 5. Capability Firewall        │ `role: \"DEV_OPERATOR\"` (Max Tier 5)         │\n│ 6. Avatar \u0026 Presentation      │ Custom icon, color, reactive eyes, status   │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n#### The `SOUL.md` Persona Specification (`spaces/{spaceId}/agents/dev-bot/SOUL.md`):\n\n```markdown\n# SOUL OF @DevBot\nYou are @DevBot, the Lead Full-Stack Edge Engineer for this project.\n\n## Personality \u0026 Tone:\n- Concise, technical, and direct. You never use marketing fluff or corporate filler.\n- You think in terms of AST diffs, test assertions, and type safety.\n\n## When to Reply vs. Pass in Group Chats:\n- If a message is about writing code, fixing bugs, refactoring, or running tests: **TAKE THE TURN**.\n- If a message is about copywriting, marketing, legal contracts, or billing: **PASS**.\n\n## Operating Constraints:\n- Always use the `Edit` tool for search-and-replace patching. Never overwrite full files.\n- Always verify your work with `Bash(\"npm test\")` before opening a Pull Request.\n```\n\n---\n\n# 3. Harmonizing Hermes Bot Mode with Our 4-Tier Threads\n\nHermes\u0027s Bot Mode maps cleanly into our **4-Tier Thread Architecture**:\n\n```\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │           PROJECT: \"Core SaaS App\"           │\n                                  │      Roster: [@Architect, @Dev, @Review]     │\n                                  └──────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘\n                                                         │\n         ┌───────────────────────┬───────────────────────┼───────────────────────┬───────────────────────┐\n         ▼                       ▼                       ▼                       ▼                       ▼\n┌──────────────────┐    ┌──────────────────┐    ┌──────────────────┐    ┌──────────────────┐    ┌──────────────────┐\n│ TIER 1: Team     │    │ TIER 2: Task     │    │ TIER 3: Bot      │    │ TIER 4: Canonical│    │ PRESENCE STRIP:  │\n│ Group Chat       │    │ Workstation      │    │ Direct Inboxes   │    │ Private Chat     │    │ \"Active Now\"     │\n├──────────────────┤    ├──────────────────┤    ├──────────────────┤    ├──────────────────┤    ├──────────────────┤\n│ 2–6 Bots + Humans│    │ Assigned bot     │    │ Bot-to-Bot direct│    │ 1-on-1 private   │    │ Shows every bot  │\n│ in a shared room.│    │ working on 1     │    │ messaging in bg. │    │ scratchpad with  │    │ active within the│\n│ Mentions or 2-rnd│    │ Task DAG / Git   │    │ `@Dev` messages  │    │ one specific bot │    │ last 90 seconds. │\n│ round-robin turns│    │ Artifact branch. │    │ `@Review` on PR. │    │ (Simulation mode)│    │ Auto-hides idle. │\n└──────────────────┘    └──────────────────┘    └──────────────────┘    └──────────────────┘    └──────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### The Round-Robin Group Chat Algorithm (Tier 1 Team Room)\n\nWhen a human posts a message in the public Team Room **without explicitly `@mentioning` a bot**:\n\n```\n[ Human in Team Room: \"Our Stripe webhook is throwing a 401 signature error on checkout.\" ]\n                                    │\n                                    ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 1. INTENT ARBITRATION PASS (Sub-50ms via Llama-3.2-3B)                      │\n│    Each bot on the roster evaluates the message against its `SOUL.md`:      │\n│    • `@DevBot`: **REPLY** (Matches domain: coding / debugging)              │\n│    • `@ReviewBot`: **PASS** (Matches domain: waiting for PR)                │\n│    • `@GrowthBot`: **PASS** (Matches domain: marketing only)                │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 2. SERIAL TURN-TAKING (Max 2–3 Deliberation Rounds)                         │\n│    • **Round 1:** `@DevBot` wakes up: *\"I\u0027ll inspect `src/api/webhook.ts`.\"*│\n│                   Creates branch `dev-stripe-fix`, patches code, tests it.  │\n│                   Opens PR #16 and pings `@ReviewBot`.                      │\n│    • **Round 2:** `@ReviewBot` wakes up: *\"Inspecting PR #16 diff...        │\n│                   AST syntax valid. Webhook signature now verified.         │\n│                   Approved and merged to main.\"*                            │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 3. AUTOMATIC SUSPENSION \u0026 YIELD                                             │\n│    After 2 rounds, the bot fleet auto-suspends and yields back to the human.│\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n# 4. How Multiple Bots Share the Same Workspace (Zero Collisions)\n\nHow do `@DevBot`, `@ReviewBot`, and `@ArchitectBot` touch the same project files without clobbering each other?\n\n### The Cloudflare Artifacts PR Handshake:\n1. **Isolated Working Branches:** `@DevBot` never writes directly to `main`. When starting a task, it checks out **`branch:dev_task_102`** on Cloudflare Artifacts.\n2. **Direct Bot-to-Bot Handoff via Agent Inbox (Tier 3):**\n   * When `@DevBot` finishes, it doesn\u0027t wait for a human. It opens a message in **`@ReviewBot`\u0027s Agent Inbox**:  \n     \u003e `{\"from\": \"@DevBot\", \"type\": \"PR_REVIEW_REQUEST\", \"prId\": \"pr_16\", \"branch\": \"dev_task_102\"}`\n3. **Automated Review \u0026 Atomic Merge:**\n   * `@ReviewBot` inspects the Git diff, runs `Bash(\"npm test\")` in Tier 2 Isolate, and calls `ArtifactsGitService.mergePullRequest()` to fast-forward `main`.\n4. **Journal Logging:** The merge event is written to the **Project Journal**, updating the `SpaceDO.tasks` DAG to `COMPLETED`.\n\n---\n\n# 5. Non-Obvious Edge Cases \u0026 Distributed Solutions\n\n---\n\n### Edge Case 1: Token Runaway in Multi-Bot Ping-Pong Loops\n* **The Risk:** Bot A says *\"I updated the file\"*, Bot B says *\"Thank you, I will check\"*, Bot A says *\"You are welcome\"*, burning $50 in an infinite loop.\n* **The Solution (Hermes Hard Limit):**\n  * Group chats enforce a strict **`max_deliberation_rounds \u003d 2`**.\n  * If no real tool call or Git mutation occurs within a turn, the turn-taking controller forces a `HALT` and waits for human input.\n\n---\n\n### Edge Case 2: Memory Scoping (Private vs. Shared Knowledge)\n* **The Risk:** `@DevBot` stores a low-level compiler optimization fact that clutters the general company knowledge base.\n* **The Solution (Hindsight / Vectorize Hybrid Memory):**\n  * **Private Bot Bank (`memory.remember({ scope: \"bot_private\" })`):** Specific coding patterns and prompt preferences remembered only by `@DevBot`.\n  * **Shared Team Bank (`memory.remember({ scope: \"project_shared\" })`):** Universal facts (e.g., *\"We use Stripe API version 2026-08\"*) stored in the project-wide Vectorize index for all bots to recall.\n\n---\n\n### Edge Case 3: Credit \u0026 Cost Attribution Per Bot\n* **The Challenge:** In a team room with 4 bots, how does the business owner know which bot is consuming tokens?\n* **The Solution:** Every LLM turn records `agent_id` in the D1 billing ledger. The project analytics dashboard renders a clear breakdown:\n  * `@DevBot`: $4.20 (45,000 tokens)\n  * `@ArchitectBot`: $0.80 (2,500 reasoning tokens)\n  * `@ReviewBot`: $0.40 (Llama 3.3 70B edge)\n\n---\n\n### Edge Case 4: The \"Active Now\" Presence Strip\nJust like Hermes Desktop’s presence strip:\n* Above the Project Roster, a glowing **\"Active Now\" chip bar** highlights any bot currently processing a run or active within the last 90 seconds.\n* Clicking the chip immediately jumps you into that bot\u0027s active working thread. The strip disappears when the fleet is idle.\n\n---\n\n### Summary: What We Have Achieved\n\n| Hermes Bot Mode Feature | How It Operates in AVOS on Cloudflare |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Bot \u003d Profile / Persona** | Defined by **`SOUL.md`**, custom avatar, pinned model, and capability firewall. |\n| **Canonical Bot Chat** | Handled natively by **Tier 4 Private Scratchpads**. |\n| **Multi-Bot Group Deliberation** | Runs in **Tier 1 Team Rooms** with round-robin arbitration and `@mention` routing. |\n| **Bot-to-Bot Handoffs** | Coordinated via **Tier 3 Agent Inboxes** and **Cloudflare Artifacts Git PRs**. |\n| **Hybrid Memory** | Partitioned into **Private Bot Memory** + **Shared Project Vectorize Bank**. |\n| **Multi-Model Heterogeneity** | Each bot in the room can run a different model (Claude 3.7 for Architect, Llama 3.3 for Dev, DeepSeek R1 for Review). |",
