      "text": "Here is the definitive **Mental Model and User Journey** for AVOS projects.\n\nThe architecture adapts dynamically based on whether a project is a **Private 1-User Cockpit** (zero collaboration overhead) or a **Multi-User Collaborative Office** (full multi-player governance).\n\n---\n\n# 1. The Two Mental Models\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 🚀 1. SOLO 1-USER PROJECT (\"The Supercharged Cockpit\")       │ 🏢 2. MULTI-USER PROJECT (\"The Digital Office\")             │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ • **Who:** 1 Human (Founder) + Dedicated Bot Team.          │ • **Who:** 2+ Humans (Alice, Bob) + Bot Roster.             │\n│ • **Philosophy:** **Maximum Velocity, Zero Bureaucracy.**   │ • **Philosophy:** **Safe Collaboration, Zero Collisions.**  │\n│ • **Tiers Active:** **Streamlined 2-Tier UI** (No private   │ • **Tiers Active:** **Full 4-Tier Hierarchy** (Team Room,   │\n│   scratchpad needed—you are the only human!).               │   Task Workstations, Consult Lanes, Private Scratchpads).   │\n│ • **Git Workflow:** Direct commits \u0026 auto-merges to `main`. │ • **Git Workflow:** Isolated branch forks \u0026 PR review gates.│\n│ • **Chat Style:** Talk naturally (No `@mentions` needed).   │ • **Chat Style:** Slack-style multi-player (`@mention` bots)│\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n# PART A: The Solo 1-User Project Journey (The \"Cockpit\")\n\nIn a 1-user project, there are no other teammates to step on your toes or read your private thoughts. Tiers 3 and 4 are **completely hidden**, collapsing the project into a **direct, high-speed 2-tier interface**:\n\n```\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │      SOLO PROJECT: \"My Micro-SaaS\"           │\n                                  └──────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘\n                                                         │\n                         ┌───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┐\n                         ▼                                                               ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 💬 TIER 1: THE UNIFIED COMMAND CHAT                         │   │ ⚡ TIER 2: ASYNC BACKGROUND SPRINTS                         │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤   ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ • The primary workspace. Chat on left, live canvas on right.│   │ • Created automatically for long-running heavy tasks        │\n│ • You talk naturally: *\"Add Stripe checkout to the site.\"*  │   │   (e.g., scraping 500 leads, training a LoRA model).        │\n│ • Direct Execution: Agent patches files directly to `main`  │   │ • Runs quietly in background without locking your main chat.│\n│   and compiles the live edge preview in 2 seconds.          │   │ • Logs completion directly to your Project Journal.         │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### The Solo Founder\u0027s 5-Step Journey:\n\n1. **Entry:** You open your project. The screen shows your **Live Canvas Preview** on the right and your **Command Chat** on the left.\n2. **Natural Prompting:** You type:  \n   \u003e *\"Add a dark mode toggle to the navbar and connect our contact form to the SQLite database.\"*\n3. **Instant Action (Zero `@mentions`):** Your bot reads the prompt, applies AST search-and-replace patches to `src/Header.astro` in the Tier 1 SQLite virtual FS, and compiles the preview.\n4. **Live Canvas Feedback:** The edge preview hot-reloads in **150ms**. You click the new dark mode toggle on the screen; it works.\n5. **Sleep \u0026 Auto-Advancement:** You close your laptop. If you scheduled a cron, the bot wakes up on its alarm, runs its background task, updates the Project Journal, and goes back to sleep at **$0 cost**.\n\n---\n\n# PART B: The Multi-User Project Journey (The \"Digital Office\")\n\nWhen a project has 2 or more humans (e.g. Alice and Bob), the interface unlocks the **Full 4-Tier Collaboration \u0026 Roster System** to prevent accidental code clobbering, secret memory leaks, and communication chaos:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                   THE MULTI-USER WORKSPACE CANVAS                                       │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 👥 **PROJECT ROSTER BAR (Top Header):**                                                                 │\n│ [ 🤖 @ArchitectBot (🟡 Planning) ]  [ 🤖 @DevBot (🟢 Coding) ]  [ 👩‍💻 Alice (Lead) ]  [ 👨‍💻 Bob (Dev) ]       │\n├───────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 📁 **TIERED NAVIGATION (Sidebar)** │ 💬 **ACTIVE WORKSTATION VIEW**                                      │\n│                                   │                                                                     │\n│ 💬 **Tier 1: Team Room** (Public) │ 👩‍💻 **Alice:** \"Hey @DevBot, let\u0027s test a new pricing layout.\"      │\n│                                   │                                                                     │\n│ 📋 **Tier 2: Task Workstations**  │ 🤖 **@DevBot:** \"I\u0027ve created Task #104. Let\u0027s move to that thread  │\n│ ├── 📌 #104: Pricing Redesign     │                 to keep the team room clear.\"                       │\n│ └── 📌 #105: Stripe Webhook Fix   │                                                                     │\n│                                   │ ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │\n│ 🔒 **Tier 4: My Private Drafts**  │ │ 📬 **Pull Request #16 (by Alice \u0026 @DevBot): \"New Pricing Tier\"**│ │\n│ └── 📝 Alice\u0027s 1-on-1 with @DevBot│ │ • AST syntax valid. 0 build errors.                             │ │\n│                                   │ │ 👨‍💻 **Bob:** \"Looks clean. Approved.\"                             │ │\n│ ⚙️ **Tier 3: Bot Consults (Hidden)│ │ [ ✅ Merge to Main Workspace ]           [ 🔍 View Git Diff ]   │ │\n│ └── [x] Show 2 Bot Conversations  │ └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │\n└───────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### The Multi-User Team Lifecycle (A Real Collaborative Sprint):\n\n```\n1. PRIVATE BRAINSTORMING (Tier 4 Private Scratchpad)\n   • Alice clicks `@DevBot` in the top Roster: `[ 💬 Start Private Draft ]`.\n   • She enters her isolated sandbox. She tests a radical new pricing layout.\n   • The bot applies patches to a private Git branch (`branch:alice_test`).\n   • Bob CANNOT see this thread, and the shared `main` workspace is 100% untouched.\n\n2. TEAM PROMOTION (Tier 2 Task Workstation)\n   • Alice is happy with the result. She clicks `[ 🚀 Promote to Task Thread ]`.\n   • The system creates **Task Workstation #104: Pricing Redesign** in the sidebar.\n   • A Pull Request card is automatically submitted to the team.\n\n3. MULTI-PLAYER COLLABORATION \u0026 BOT REVIEW (Tier 1 \u0026 Tier 3)\n   • Bob opens Task #104 and inspects the live visual diff.\n   • Behind the scenes, `@ReviewBot` wakes up in a **Tier 3 System Consult Lane**,\n     runs the automated test suite on Cloudflare Artifacts, and posts:\n     *\"All 8 test assertions passed (Exit Code 0).\"*\n   • Bob types: *\"Approved!\"* and clicks `[ ✅ Merge to Main Workspace ]`.\n\n4. ATOMIC MERGE \u0026 SHARED JOURNAL COMMIT\n   • Cloudflare Artifacts fast-forwards `main`.\n   • The live website preview updates for all teammates.\n   • The **Project Journal** logs the commit with full author attribution:\n     `c_8f12 by Alice \u0026 @DevBot (Reviewed by Bob \u0026 @ReviewBot)`.\n```\n\n---\n\n# 3. Solo vs. Team Project Mechanics\n\n| Dimension | 🚀 Solo 1-User Project | 🏢 Multi-User Collaborative Project |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Visible Tiers** | **2 Tiers** (Main Chat + Background Sprints) | **4 Tiers** (Team Room, Tasks, Inboxes, Scratchpads) |\n| **Invoking Bots** | **Zero `@mentions`:** Talk naturally to the project | **Slack Style:** Bots speak only when `@mentioned` |\n| **Git Writes** | **Direct \u0026 Fast:** Commits straight to `main` | **Branch \u0026 PR:** Requires review / OCC merge gates |\n| **Scratchpads** | **Disabled:** (Everything is already private to you) | **Enabled:** Private 1-on-1 sandboxes per teammate |\n| **Roster UI** | Shows your personal AI assistants | Shows full team (Humans + AI Coworkers + Statuses) |\n| **Cognitive Load** | **Ultra-Low:** Feels like ChatGPT/Cursor | **Structured:** Feels like Slack/Linear with AI teammates |\n\n---\n\n# 4. What Happens When a Solo Project Invites a Teammate?\n\nIf a solo founder starts a project alone and later clicks **`[+ Invite Teammate]`** to bring on a developer or partner:\n\n1. **Instant, Zero-Downtime Elevation:** The project dynamically transitions from **Solo Cockpit Mode** to **Digital Office Mode**.\n2. **Branch Protection Activates:** The system locks direct commits to `main` and turns on **Pull Request Review Cards**.\n3. **Roster Expands:** The top bar updates to show both team members alongside the bot fleet.\n4. **Zero Workflow Interruption:** All existing files, journal tasks, and Git commit histories remain 100% intact.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\n* **For Solo Founders:** It is as fast and simple as Cursor or ChatGPT—you type what you want, and your AI team builds and deploys it immediately to the edge.\n* **For Teams \u0026 Agencies:** It becomes a structured digital office—private sandboxes for drafting, public workstations for collaborative tasks, and automated bot reviews to keep the codebase pristine.",
