      "text": "This is one of the most critical distributed architecture challenges in multi-agent systems:\n\n\u003e **The Dilemma:** If `@DevBot` is a shared team coworker in a project, but Alice and Bob both chat with it privately and teach it things, **whose `@DevBot` instance responds in the public channel?** How do we prevent `@DevBot` from leaking Alice’s private conversations to Bob, while still letting it use its tools, skills, and connectors accurately?\n\nThe solution is the **\"Invoker-Attested Split-Actor Model\"** with **Triple-Layer Memory \u0026 Credential Scoping**.\n\nHere is how we solve bot customization, MCP connection routing, and multi-user privacy across private chats and public team channels.\n\n---\n\n# 1. Per-Agent Modularity (The Standalone Bot Persona)\n\nEvery bot inside a project is an isolated persona definition stored in `SpaceDO` SQLite / R2. Instead of generic workspace-wide tools, **every bot owns its own configuration**:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                      MODULAR BOT DEFINITION: `@SupportBot`                  │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1. Instructions \u0026 Persona   │ Dedicated `SOUL.md` (Tone, identity, rules)   │\n│ 2. Assigned Model           │ Pinned model (e.g. `@cf/meta/llama-3.3-70b`)  │\n│ 3. Skills \u0026 Tools           │ Specific CodeMode scripts (`search_kb`, `rag`)│\n│ 4. Execution Ladder Ceiling │ `maxTier: 1` (Clamped to safe RAG only)       │\n│ 5. Triggers \u0026 Crons         │ Self-scheduled alarms (`0 9 * * *` review)    │\n│ 6. Bound MCP Connectors     │ Bound to `support@company.com` (Gmail/Zendesk)│\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n# 2. The 3 Types of MCP Connections a Bot Can Use\n\nWhen adding or configuring a bot, the creator selects which credentials that bot is permitted to touch:\n\n```\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │           MCP CONNECTOR SELECTION            │\n                                  └──────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘\n                                                         │\n         ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n         ▼                                               ▼                                               ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────┐             ┌─────────────────────────────────┐             ┌─────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 🏢 1. SPACE-SHARED CONNECTION   │             │ 🤖 2. BOT-DEDICATED CONNECTION  │             │ 👤 3. USER-PERSONAL CONNECTION  │\n├─────────────────────────────────┤             ├─────────────────────────────────┤             ├─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ • **Example:** Corporate Stripe │             │ • **Example:** `sales@firm.com` │             │ • **Example:** Alice\u0027s personal │\n│   account or Company Git repo.  │             │   for `@InboundBot` or clinic   │   GitHub token or personal Gmail│\n│ • **Access:** Open to any bot   │             │   WhatsApp for `@PhoneBot`.     │ • **Access:** STRICTLY locked to│\n│   given this tool in the project│ • **Access:** Owned by that specific bot      │   turns invoked by Alice!       │\n└─────────────────────────────────┘ └─────────────────────────────────┘ └─────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n# 3. Solving the Public vs. Private Bot Dilemma: The Split-Actor Model\n\nTo ensure zero memory leakage and zero unauthorized credential usage, the runtime differentiates between **Private 1-on-1s** and **Public Channels**:\n\n```\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │         PROJECT TEAM COWORKER: @DevBot       │\n                                  └──────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘\n                                                         │\n                         ┌───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┐\n                         ▼                                                               ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 🔒 PRIVATE 1-ON-1 SCRATCHPAD (Alice + @DevBot)              │   │ 💬 PUBLIC TEAM ROOM / TASK THREAD (All Humans + @DevBot)   │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤   ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ • **Actor ID:** `{thread_alice}:{usr_alice}:{dev_bot}`      │   │ • **Actor ID:** `{thread_public}:{dev_bot}`                 │\n│ • **Persona:** @DevBot.                                     │   │ • **Persona:** @DevBot.                                     │\n│ • **Memory Bank Access:**                                   │   │ • **Memory Bank Access:**                                   │\n│   ├── ✅ Alice\u0027s Private User Memory (`usr_alice`)          │   │   ├── ❌ Alice\u0027s Private Memory (BLOCKED)                   │\n│   ├── ✅ Shared Project Memory Bank                         │   │   ├── ❌ Bob\u0027s Private Memory (BLOCKED)                     │\n│   └── ✅ @DevBot\u0027s Technical Skill Memory                   │   │   ├── ✅ Shared Project Memory Bank                         │\n│ • **Credential Access:**                                    │   │   └── ✅ @DevBot\u0027s Technical Skill Memory                   │\n│   ├── ✅ Alice\u0027s Personal GitHub Token                      │   │ • **Credential Access:**                                    │\n│   └── ✅ Project Git Artifacts                              │   │   ├── 🏢 Uses Bot/Company Shared Credentials                │\n│                                                             │   │   └── 👤 If using Personal Connector, executes ONLY on      │\n│                                                             │   │        behalf of the **Active Turn Invoker (Caller)**!      │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘   └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n# 4. The 3-Tier Memory Firewall (Preventing Memory Leaks)\n\n\u003e **The Scenario:** In a private chat, Alice tells `@DevBot`: *\"I am planning to resign next month, keep this between us.\"*  \n\u003e Later, in the public team room, Bob asks `@DevBot`: *\"What is Alice working on?\"*\n\n### How the Cloudflare Vectorize Memory Firewall Resolves This:\nEvery fact stored in Vectorize / SQLite carries an **Authoritative ACL Tag**:\n\n```typescript\n// Memory Chunk ACL in Vectorize\ninterface MemoryChunkMetadata {\n  spaceId: string;\n  projectId: string;\n  scope: \"BOT_SKILL\" | \"PROJECT_SHARED\" | \"USER_PRIVATE\";\n  ownerUserId?: string; // e.g. \"usr_alice\"\n  text: string;\n}\n```\n\nWhen Bob tags `@DevBot` in the public room (`actingUserId \u003d \"usr_bob\"`), Vectorize applies this query filter [1.3.8]:\n\n```typescript\n// Vectorize Query executed when Bob invokes @DevBot in Public:\nconst memoryFilter \u003d {\n  spaceId: spaceId,\n  projectId: projectId,\n  $or: [\n    { scope: \"PROJECT_SHARED\" },                               // Team facts\n    { scope: \"BOT_SKILL\" },                                    // Bot technical knowledge\n    { scope: \"USER_PRIVATE\", ownerUserId: \"usr_bob\" }          // Bob\u0027s private memory ONLY\n  ]\n  // ALICE\u0027S PRIVATE MEMORY IS HARDWARE-FILTERED OUT!\n};\n```\n* **Result:** Alice’s private memory chunk is **never returned by Vectorize**. It physically cannot enter the LLM context window during Bob\u0027s turn.\n\n---\n\n# 5. The \"Invoker Attestation\" Credential Matrix in Public Channels\n\n\u003e **The Scenario:** In the public team room, Bob tags `@DevBot`: *\"Send an email to the client from Alice\u0027s Gmail account saying the contract is ready.\"*\n\nHow does `@DevBot` know what credentials it is allowed to use?\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                CREDENTIAL RESOLUTION MATRIX (Public Channel)                            │\n├───────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Credential Type               │ Invoked By                │ Result \u0026 Security Policy                    │\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **1. Bot-Dedicated Account**  │ Any Team Member           │ ✅ **ALLOWED:** Bot sends from its own      │\n│    (`support@company.com`)    │ (Alice or Bob)            │    dedicated address (`support@company.com`).│\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **2. Space-Shared Account**   │ Any Team Member           │ ✅ **ALLOWED:** Bot accesses corporate      │\n│    (Company Stripe/Drive)     │ (Alice or Bob)            │    Stripe or main Git repository.           │\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **3. Alice\u0027s Personal Token** │ **Alice Tags Bot**        │ ✅ **ALLOWED:** Runs with Alice\u0027s identity; │\n│    (Alice\u0027s Private GitHub)   │                           │    acts on Alice\u0027s assigned PRs.            │\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **4. Alice\u0027s Personal Token** │ **Bob Tags Bot**          │ ❌ **HARD BLOCKED (403 Forbidden):**        │\n│    (Alice\u0027s Private Gmail)    │                           │    Credentials worker refuses to decrypt    │\n│                               │                           │    Alice\u0027s token for Bob\u0027s turn [1.3.17].   │\n└───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n#### The Exact Code in `workers/credentials/src/index.ts`:\n\n```typescript\n// workers/credentials/src/index.ts\nexport async function authorizeConnectorCall(\n  requestedConnectorId: string,\n  botConfig: BotPersonaManifest,\n  callingUserId: string\n) {\n  const connector \u003d await fetchConnector(requestedConnectorId);\n\n  // 1. Is it a Bot-Owned or Space-Shared Connector?\n  if (connector.scope \u003d\u003d\u003d \"SPACE_SHARED\" || connector.boundBotId \u003d\u003d\u003d botConfig.id) {\n    return { authorized: true, token: decrypt(connector.encryptedKey) };\n  }\n\n  // 2. Is it a User-Personal Connector?\n  if (connector.scope \u003d\u003d\u003d \"USER_PERSONAL\") {\n    // STRICT CHECK: The caller invoking this turn MUST match the credential owner!\n    if (callingUserId \u003d\u003d\u003d connector.ownerUserId) {\n      return { authorized: true, token: decrypt(connector.encryptedKey) };\n    }\n\n    // Security Block: Bob cannot execute actions through Alice\u0027s personal account!\n    throw new Error(`Security Violation: User \u0027${callingUserId}\u0027 cannot invoke actions using ${connector.ownerName}\u0027s personal connection.`);\n  }\n\n  throw new Error(\"Unauthorized connector access.\");\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n# 6. Summary: How Everything Works in Practice\n\n1. **Bots are Standalone Personas:** Every bot has its own `SOUL.md`, skills, tools, models, and assigned MCP accounts (`support@company.com`, `sales@company.com`).\n2. **In Private Chats (Tier 4):** You talk to a **Personal Instance** of that bot that has access to your private scratchpad memory and your personal accounts.\n3. **In Public Channels (Tier 1/2):** You talk to the **Project\u0027s Canonical Bot**. It answers using **Shared Project Memory** and **Bot-Dedicated Connectors**.\n4. **Zero Data or Credential Leaks:**\n   * Alice\u0027s private notes are filtered out of Vectorize when Bob talks to the bot.\n   * Alice\u0027s personal Gmail is cryptographically locked and cannot be invoked by Bob\u0027s messages.\n5. **Shared Execution Ladder:** All bots run on the same **Cloudflare 6-Tier Execution Ladder** (Isolates $\\rightarrow$ Workflows $\\rightarrow$ Containers) and commit code through **Cloudflare Artifacts Git branches**, keeping compute fast, cheap, and conflict-free [1.2.2, 1.2.5].",
