      "text": "This is a clean and secure UX pattern.\n\nBy completely **stripping personal credentials from public channels** and providing an **interactive MCP-UI bridge that forks the conversation into a private scratchpad**, you achieve **zero credential leakage** while maintaining a smooth user experience.\n\nTo make this system completely bulletproof and seamless, here are the **5 additional architectural components** needed:\n\n---\n\n# 1. The End-to-End \"Channel-to-Scratchpad\" Forking Lifecycle\n\n```\n[ In Public Team Room (Tier 1): Alice types: \"@DevBot, check my personal Gmail for the Acme NDA and summarize it\" ]\n                                    │\n                                    ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 1. BOT DETECTS PERSONAL TOOL REQUIREMENT                                    │\n│    `@DevBot` identifies that `gmail.search` requires Alice\u0027s Personal Auth. │\n│    Because this is a Public Team Channel, personal tools are physically     │\n│    stripped from the schema.                                                │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 2. BOT EMITS INTERACTIVE MCP-UI PRIVACY BRIDGE (In Public Channel)          │\n│ ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │\n│ │ 🔒 **Personal Integration Required**                                    │ │\n│ │ To protect your privacy and email credentials in team channels,         │ │\n│ │ personal Gmail access is restricted to private workspaces.              │ │\n│ │                                                                         │ │\n│ │ [ 🚀 Continue in Private Scratchpad (Fork This Task) ]                 │ │\n│ └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │\n└───────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                    │ (Alice clicks \"Continue in Private Scratchpad\")\n                                    ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 3. INSTANT CONTEXT-PRESERVING THREAD FORK (Tier 4 Scratchpad)               │\n│    • A new private Tier 4 thread is created: `#scratchpad-alice-gmail-nda`. │\n│    • Inherits the exact prompt + relevant project context (`PROJECT.md`).   │\n│    • Alice\u0027s Personal Gmail MCP tool is **now active**.                     │\n│    • `@DevBot` immediately executes the query without Alice retyping!       │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 4. THE RETURN BRIDGE: SHARE SANITIZED SUMMARY BACK TO TEAM                  │\n│    `@DevBot` finds the NDA, summarizes it, and renders an action card:      │\n│ ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │\n│ │ 📬 **Task Complete:** \"Acme NDA requires mutual indemnity under DE law.\"│ │\n│ │                                                                         │ │\n│ │ [ 📢 Share Summary Back to Team Room ]      [ Keep Private in Scratchpad]│ │\n│ └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │\n│                                   │ (Alice clicks \"Share Summary\")          │\n│                                   ▼                                         │\n│    • ONLY the clean summary is posted back to the Tier 1 Team Room.         │\n│    • Alice\u0027s raw emails, headers, and tokens stay 100% private!             │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n# 2. The 5 Missing Architectural Components Needed\n\n---\n\n### Component 1: Context-Preserving Thread Forking (The \"Handoff Token\")\nWhen Alice clicks **`[ Continue in Private Scratchpad ]`**, she shouldn\u0027t have to re-explain the task to the bot.\n\nThe platform creates a **Handoff Snapshot** in `SpaceDO`:\n\n```typescript\n// workers/spaces/src/do/SpaceDO.ts\nexport async function forkChannelToPrivateScratchpad(\n  spaceId: string,\n  projectId: string,\n  sourceThreadId: string,\n  userPrompt: string,\n  callingUserId: string\n) {\n  // 1. Create a new Tier 4 Private Scratchpad thread\n  const privateThread \u003d await createThread({\n    spaceId,\n    projectId,\n    title: `🔒 Private Task: ${userPrompt.slice(0, 35)}...`,\n    threadKind: \"private_scratchpad\",\n    createdBy: callingUserId // Locked strictly to Alice!\n  });\n\n  // 2. Seed the initial turn with the handoff prompt\n  await appendMessage(privateThread.sessionId, {\n    role: \"user\",\n    content: userPrompt,\n    metadata: {\n      forkedFromThreadId: sourceThreadId,\n      autoExecuteOnBoot: true // Tells @DevBot to run immediately upon opening!\n    }\n  });\n\n  return { ok: true, privateThreadId: privateThread.id };\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Component 2: The Return Bridge (\"Share Sanitized Result to Team\")\nOnce an agent runs in private, the user usually wants to bring the **result** (not the private inbox or raw credentials) back to their colleagues.\n\n* In the Tier 4 Scratchpad, when the bot completes the task, it automatically attaches a **`ShareToTeam` action card** to its response.\n* Clicking **`[ Share Summary to Team Room ]`** executes a cross-thread message dispatch that posts the distilled output back into the public channel where the request originated.\n\n---\n\n### Component 3: Elicitation \u0026 One-Time Ephemeral Action Grants (In-Channel Action)\nWhat if Alice is in the team channel and just wants the bot to perform a **quick 1-second action** (e.g. *\"@DevBot create a GitHub issue on my behalf with my personal token\"*), and she doesn\u0027t want to leave the channel?\n\nUsing **MCP v2 Elicitation [1.2.2]**, the bot renders a **Private One-Time Confirmation Card** visible only to Alice in the public channel:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 🔐 **One-Time Personal Action Authorization** (Visible only to @alice)      │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ `@DevBot` is requesting permission to use your **Personal GitHub Account**  │\n│ to perform this single action in this channel:                              │\n│ • **Action:** Create Issue in `repo/acme-webapp`                            │\n│ • **Title:** *\"Fix Stripe webhook signature verification\"*                  │\n│                                                                             │\n│ [ ✅ Authorize 1-Time Action ]                             [ ❌ Deny ]       │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n* **Security Rule:** Alice clicks **`[ Authorize 1-Time Action ]`**. The runtime mints a **single-use ephemeral capability token** (valid for 15 seconds) [1.2.2].\n* The bot executes the creation, posts the issue link to the team, and the token expires immediately. Bob never sees Alice\u0027s credentials.\n\n---\n\n### Component 4: Physical Tool Schema Stripping (Hardware-Level Defense)\nDo not rely on prompt instructions (*\"Please don\u0027t use personal tools in public rooms\"*). An adversarial prompt injection could bypass this.\n\nIn `workers/agents/src/script-engine/tool-surface.ts`, enforce **Physical Schema Pruning**:\n\n```typescript\n// workers/agents/src/script-engine/tool-surface.ts\nexport function assembleToolSchemasForThread(\n  allTools: ToolDefinition[],\n  threadKind: \"primary\" | \"task_workstation\" | \"private_scratchpad\",\n  actingUserId: string\n) {\n  if (threadKind !\u003d\u003d \"private_scratchpad\") {\n    // In Public Channels: Physically filter out all tools flagged as USER_PERSONAL\n    return allTools.filter(tool \u003d\u003e tool.scope !\u003d\u003d \"USER_PERSONAL\");\n  }\n\n  // In Private Scratchpads: Include personal tools belonging strictly to this user\n  return allTools.filter(tool \u003d\u003e \n    tool.scope \u003d\u003d\u003d \"SPACE_SHARED\" || \n    (tool.scope \u003d\u003d\u003d \"USER_PERSONAL\" \u0026\u0026 tool.ownerUserId \u003d\u003d\u003d actingUserId)\n  );\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Component 5: Explicit Scope Management \u0026 Live Audit Ledger in Settings\n\nIn `apps/shell` under **Space Settings $\\rightarrow$ Connected Accounts**, users have complete visibility and control over how their connectors are shared:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 🔌 CONNECTED ACCOUNTS \u0026 MCP INTEGRATIONS                                    │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 📬 **Google Workspace (Alice\u0027s Gmail \u0026 Calendar)**                          │\n│ • Connected by: **Alice (@alice)**                                          │\n│ • Current Scope: **🔒 Personal (Only Me in Private Scratchpads)**           │\n│ • Change Scope: `[ (•) Personal Only  ( ) Share with Space  ( ) Share with Project ]` │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 📜 **Recent Access Audit Log:**                                             │\n│ • [Today 18:24 UTC] @DevBot accessed Gmail in `#scratchpad-alice` (Searched NDA)│\n│ • [Yesterday 14:10 UTC] @DevBot accessed Calendar in `#scratchpad-alice`    │\n│ • [Yesterday 09:00 UTC] 🛡️ Blocked attempt from public channel (Redirected) │\n│                                                                             │\n│ [ 🔄 Re-authenticate ]                                 [ ❌ Disconnect ]     │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary of What This Achieves:\n\n| Scenario | Behavior \u0026 Security Guarantee |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **User asks for personal data in a public room** | The bot is physically incapable of running the tool. It returns an interactive **MCP-UI card** with a 1-click button to fork to a private scratchpad. |\n| **Context transfer to private scratchpad** | A new private Tier 4 thread is spawned automatically, carrying the prompt and project context so the bot executes immediately without retyping. |\n| **Sharing results back to the team** | When the private task finishes, a **`Share Summary to Team`** button allows the user to post only the sanitized output back to the public room. |\n| **Quick one-time actions in public** | Handled via **MCP v2 Elicitation cards** where the user signs a single-use 15-second ephemeral grant. |\n| **Hardware-level protection** | Personal tool schemas are **physically removed** from the LLM prompt in public channels, making prompt injection attacks impossible. |",
