─────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Why the User Experiences Zero Limits:\nTo the user, there is **zero artificial throttling or waiting**. Whenever they type a command, inspect a file, click their live canvas, or run a build, the system answers in milliseconds. \n\nBecause Cloudflare’s **`ArtifactFS` FUSE driver** mounts the project workspace lazily into the container in **5ms**, the user never feels a cold-start delay [1.2.2].\n\n---\n\n# 2. Container Allocation Policy Across Plans\n\nEvery plan includes **1 Default Container per project** tailored to that project’s Kind, with additional specialized containers billed at low micro-credit rates:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                   CONTAINER ALLOCATION MATRIX                                           │\n├───────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Project Kind                  │ 1 Included Default Container          │ Add-on Specialized Containers   │\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **`product_dev` (General)**   │ **Standard Linux / Node 22 / Python** │ + GUI Desktop Container (3 cr/m)│\n│                               │ (Handles npm, pip, builds, tests)     │ + Rust/C++ High-Memory (5 cr/m) │\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **`doc_studio` (Legal/Docs)** │ **Document Engine (Parse 5 / Pandoc)**│ + Heavy OCR Scanner (2 cr/m)    │\n│                               │ (Fast Markdown conversion \u0026 PDF export│                                 │\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **`growth_engine`**           │ **Lightweight Kitesurf Browser (T4)** │ + Chromium Puppeteer (2 cr/m)   │\n│                               │ (Fast DOM scraping \u0026 form fills)      │                                 │\n└───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n# 3. The 4 Engineering Rules That Prevent You From Losing Money\n\n---\n\n### Rule 1: Aggressive 60-Second Micro-Sleep (Scale-to-Zero)\n* When a developer asks the AI to run `npm install \u0026\u0026 npm run build`, the container wakes up, executes the command in 18 seconds, flushes file diffs to SQLite, and begins a **60-second countdown**.\n* If the user sends another command within 60 seconds, the container stays warm.\n* If 60 seconds pass with no container commands, **the container sleeps immediately**. You pay **zero idle compute fees**.\n\n---\n\n### Rule 2: Dynamic Workload Filtering (Isolate-First Gate)\nNever let the agent route a simple file search or string patch to the Linux container.\n* The tool router (`tool-surface.ts`) checks the command:\n  * Is it `read`, `grep`, `edit`, `patch`, `git diff`? $\\rightarrow$ **Force Tier 1/2 Isolate ($0.00)**.\n  * Is it `npm run build`, `python script.py`, `pip install`? $\\rightarrow$ **Route to Tier 6 Container**.\n\n---\n\n### Rule 3: Shared Golden Edge Layer Caching\n* Cloudflare caches the base rootfs image (Ubuntu + Node.js 22 + Python 3.11 + standard build tools) globally across edge nodes.\n* Your containers don\u0027t download 1GB OS layers on every run. They boot on top of the shared cached layer instantly.\n\n---\n\n### Rule 4: Micro-Credit Add-ons for Heavy / Multi-Containers\nIf a user adds a **2nd or 3rd specialized container** (or a heavy **GUI Desktop / Xvfb container**) to the same project:\n* The system charges a small per-minute credit fee **only while that extra container is actively processing CPU instructions**:\n  * Specialized C++ Compiler: **2 Credits / min ($0.02 / min)**.\n  * GUI Visual Desktop (noVNC): **5 Credits / min ($0.05 / min)**.\n* Because the container sleeps after 60s of inactivity, running a 5-minute desktop task costs the user only **25 cents**, while your actual Cloudflare cost is **less than 2 cents (92% margin)**.\n\n---\n\n# 4. The Exact Math: Unit Economics on a $29 Plan\n\nHere is the financial breakdown of a heavy developer using your **$29 / month Starter Plan**:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 💵 MONTHLY USER REVENUE:                                           $29.00   │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 📉 REAL CLOUDFLARE EDGE COSTS (Heavy Daily Usage):                          │\n│ • Tier 1/2 V8 Isolates (15,000 file reads/patches/greps):          -$0.15   │\n│ • Tier 6 Container CPU (20 minutes/day active build time \u003d 10 hrs): -$0.60   │\n│ • Tier 4 Kitesurf Browser Scrapes (500 pages/mo):                  -$0.50   │\n│ • Prompt Caching Tokens via AI Gateway (with Ephemeral Caching):   -$0.85   │\n│ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── │\n│ 🧾 **TOTAL CLOUDFLARE INFRASTRUCTURE COST:**                       **-$2.10**│\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 🚀 **YOUR NET PROFIT PER $29 USER:**                               **$26.90**│\n│ 📊 **GROSS PROFIT MARGIN:**                                        **92.7%**│\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n# 5. Plugin Builders Monetizing Custom Containers\n\nDevelopers in your marketplace can build and publish **Custom Specialized Container Images**:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 🧩 MARKETPLACE CONTAINER PLUGIN: \"@GodotGameDevSandbox\"                     │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ • **Author:** GameDev Studio (@alex)                                        │\n│ • **What It Bundles:** Ubuntu + Godot 4.3 Engine + WebAssembly Export Tools │\n│ • **Pricing:** **Free to Install** + **3 Credits / min of active build time**│\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 💰 Payout Split:                                                            │\n│ • 40% of the active container credits go to the Plugin Creator.             │\n│ • 60% retained by your platform.                                            │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\n1. **How $29 feels like $300:** Sub-millisecond V8 Isolates handle 95% of tasks instantly, while the included container only wakes for active compiles and **sleeps after 60 seconds**, delivering unconstrained performance without server bills.\n2. **1 Included Container per Project:** Covers standard full-stack development, while heavy multi-containers (GUI Desktops, CUDA ML) use small, metered micro-credits.\n3. **92%+ Gross Profit Margins:** You collect $29/mo while paying Cloudflare ~$2.10/mo in actual metered compute.\n4. **Extensible Container Marketplace:** Third-party developers can package custom container images (Rust, Godot, PyTorch) and earn royalties on active compute usage.",
