      "text": "Here is the exact credit math for the **$29 Plan** and the architectural blueprint for delivering long-running, extreme GUI container workloads (like installing a desktop app or automating a game for hours) at **fractions of a cent**.\n\n---\n\n# 1. The $29 Plan Credit Allocation \u0026 Unit Economics\n\nEvery **$29 / month Starter Plan** comes with an included monthly allowance of **1,200 Platform Credits ($12.00 retail value)** [1 credit \u003d $0.01 USD]:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 💵 $29 / MONTH PLAN BREAKDOWN                                               │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ • **Included Credit Allowance:** **1,200 Credits ($12.00 Retail Value)**   │\n│ • **Platform Software \u0026 Edge Retainer:** **$17.00** (Pure Gross Margin)     │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 📦 WHAT 1,200 CREDITS DELIVERS TO THE USER:                                 │\n│ • **If BYOK (Bring Your Own Key):** 100% of credits go to Cloudflare compute│\n│   ➡️ **240 active minutes (4 hours) of heavy Linux GUI container time**, or │\n│   ➡️ **12,000 Tier 1/2 V8 Isolate file edits \u0026 code runs**, or             │\n│   ➡️ **1,200 Tier 4 Kitesurf web scrapes**.                                 │\n│                                                                             │\n│ • **If Using Platform AI Models:** Covers ~1.5 million prompt-cached tokens │\n│   plus standard container builds and daily cron runs.                       │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 💳 **Top-Up Credit Packs (When Users Need More):**                          │\n│ • **$10 Pack:** 1,000 Credits                                               │\n│ • **$25 Pack:** 2,800 Credits (+12% Bonus)                                  │\n│ • **$50 Pack:** 6,000 Credits (+20% Bonus)                                  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n# 2. The Extreme Scenario: Running a GUI Container for Hours\n\n\u003e **The Stress Test:** A user tasks the AI: *\"Install desktop game X, launch it in the visual container, play through all 20 levels, and win.\"*\n\n### Why the Naive Way Fails \u0026 Burns $50/Hour:\nIf an agent blindly streams 30 FPS video frames to Claude 3.7 or GPT-4o and calls `mouse_click(x, y)` on every single frame:\n* 3,600 screenshots/hour $\\times$ $0.01/screenshot \u003d **$36.00/hour in Vision LLM tokens alone.**\n* 10,000 conversational round-trips over the network introduce lag and context overflow.\n\n---\n\n### How AVOS Delivers 4 Hours of GUI Automation for Under $0.50\n\nWe solve this using **5 Engineering Layers** inside the Tier 6 Container:\n\n```\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │      LONG-RUNNING GUI TASK: \"Win Game X\"     │\n                                  └──────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘\n                                                         │\n                         ┌───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┐\n                         ▼                                                               ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 1. LOCAL IN-CONTAINER CODEACT SCRIPTING (99% Token Cut)     │   │ 2. PERCEPTUAL SCREEN DIFFING \u0026 EVENT SAMPLING               │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤   ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ The AI writes a local Python/PyAutoGUI script that runs     │   │ • The container does NOT stream 30 FPS to the LLM.          │\n│ directly inside the Linux container at 60 FPS:              │   │ • It captures a screenshot ONLY when:                       │\n│ `while not gameOver(): pressKey(\u0027right\u0027); if obstacle: jump()`   ├── A new level screen appears (Perceptual SSIM diff \u003e 20%)  │\n│ ➡️ Runs locally for 15 minutes without calling LLM once!    │   │   └── The local script hits an unexpected stuck state.      │\n└──────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┘   └──────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────┘\n                               │                                                                 │\n                               └───────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┘\n                                                               │\n                                                               ▼\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 3. CASCADE TO WORKERS AI VISION AT THE EDGE ($0.00 Model Cost)                                         │\n│ Periodic UI state inspections (reading level number, health bar, score) are processed by               │\n│ **Cloudflare Workers AI Llama 3.2 Vision (11B)** running at Cloudflare\u0027s edge for **$0.00**.           │\n│ Only complex strategic puzzles escalate to the Frontier Model (Claude 3.7).                            │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 4. EPHEMERAL FRAME SCRUBBING (Zero Context Memory Bloat)                                               │\n│ Previous screenshots are purged from LLM context immediately after inspection. Active context is kept  │\n│ strictly to: `Current Screen State` + `Game Progress Summary` (\u003c 2,000 tokens).                        │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Financial Comparison: Naive Agent vs. AVOS on a 4-Hour GUI Run\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                4-HOUR CONTINUOUS GUI AUTOMATION BENCHMARK                               │\n├───────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Cost Vector                   │ Naive Cloud Agent (Grok / Devin style) │ AVOS Optimized Edge Engine      │\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Vision Tokens Billed**      │ 14,400 Screenshots \u003d **$144.00**      │ 40 Event Keyframes \u003d **$0.40**  │\n│ **Reasoning Turns**           │ 14,400 Network Calls \u003d **$43.20**     │ 8 Strategic Turns \u003d **$0.08**   │\n│ **Container Runtime Cost**    │ Dedicated Cloud VM \u003d **$1.20**        │ Cloudflare Container \u003d **$0.20**│\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 🧾 **TOTAL REAL COST:**       │ **$188.40** (Bankrupts standard plans)│ **$0.68** (99.6% Cost Reduction)│\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 💳 **Credits Deducted:**      │ 18,840 Credits (Exceeds allowance)   │ **68 Credits (Out of 1,200)**   │\n└───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. User Budget Guardrails in `apps/shell`\n\nTo protect users from accidentally draining their 1,200 monthly credits on an infinite background loop, `apps/shell` enforces **Task Budget Ceilings**:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ ⚙️ START LONG-RUNNING DESKTOP TASK                                          │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Task: *\"Install Game X and play through all levels\"*                        │\n│                                                                             │\n│ 🛑 **Safety Credit Limit for this Run:**                                    │\n│ [ (•) 50 Credits ($0.50)  ( ) 150 Credits ($1.50)  ( ) Custom Limit ]       │\n│                                                                             │\n│ ⏰ **Max Wall-Time Execution Ceiling:**                                     │\n│ [ 2 Hours ▼ ]  *(Container auto-pauses and checkpoints state if reached)*   │\n│                                                                             │\n│ [ 🚀 Launch Autonomous Desktop Run ]                               [ Cancel ] │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n* If the task hits 50 credits or the 2-hour mark, the container takes an **Artifacts Git snapshot of the game state**, pauses execution, and pings the user on Telegram:\n  \u003e *\"I reached Level 12 and hit the 50-credit safety limit. Would you like me to continue to Level 20? [Continue] [Finish]\"*\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\n1. **The $29 Plan gives 1,200 Credits ($12 retail value):** More than enough for standard daily development, hundreds of web scrapes, and hours of container time.\n2. **Long GUI Runs Cost Pennies, Not Dollars:** By having the AI write **in-container Python/PyAutoGUI loops**, using **Workers AI Vision at the edge**, and **evicting old screenshot frames**, a 4-hour game automation runs for **~$0.68 instead of $180+**.\n3. **Task Safety Caps:** Users can set maximum credit caps per long-running run so they never experience bill shock.",
