      "text": "To prevent state divergence (where a virtual CLI command runs in a V8 isolate, but the Linux container has stale files, a different working directory, or missing environment variables), the platform implements a **4-Dimension State Synchronization Engine** and a **Unified Cross-Layer Execution Pipeline**.\n\n---\n\n# PART 1: Bidirectional Virtual CLI $\\leftrightarrow$ Container State Sync\n\nState is synchronized across **4 distinct operational dimensions** so that switching between a fast V8 isolate and a heavy Linux container is 100% seamless and split-brain proof:\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        4-DIMENSION VIRTUAL CLI ◄═══► CONTAINER CLI SYNC ENGINE                          │\n├────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ State Dimension    │ Handled in Tier 1/2 V8 Isolate       │ Synchronized in Tier 6 Container Sandbox   │\n├────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **1. Filesystem**  │ DO SQLite Virtual FS (`workspace_files`│ **ArtifactFS (FUSE):** Hydrates on-demand  │\n│                    │ modified in-memory via AST `Edit`)   │ into `/workspace`; auto-flushes on `fsync`.│\n├────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **2. Shell Session**│ `cd src/` and `export VAR\u003dval` stored │ Passed as `cwd` and `env_vars` payload     │\n│                    │ in `NaelaoAgentDO` SQLite session.   │ directly into container gRPC exec headers. │\n├────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **3. Git State**   │ Cloudflare Artifacts WASM Git Engine │ Container Git client points to the **same  │\n│                    │ (Branches, staging, HEAD commits).   │ Artifacts remote URL \u0026 SHA-256 commit tree│\n├────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **4. SQLite DB**   │ Direct in-memory DO Facet query      │ Mounted `.sqlite` file over FUSE or direct │\n│                    │ (`sqlite3 db.sqlite \"SELECT...\"`).   │ gRPC socket query to the DO storage.       │\n└────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### How Each State Dimension Syncs in Practice\n\n#### 1. Shell Environment \u0026 Working Directory Sync (`cwd` \u0026 `export`)\n* When an agent runs a Virtual CLI command in Tier 2:\n  ```bash\n  cd src/api \u0026\u0026 export STRIPE_MODE\u003dtest\n  ```\n* `NaelaoAgentDO` captures this in its persistent SQLite session state:\n  `session_state \u003d { cwd: \"src/api\", env: { STRIPE_MODE: \"test\" } }`.\n* When the agent later runs a heavy Tier 6 Container command:\n  ```bash\n  npm test\n  ```\n* The gRPC execution bridge dispatches the command directly to `/workspace/src/api` with `process.env.STRIPE_MODE \u003d \"test\"` pre-injected.\n\n#### 2. Git Branch \u0026 Tree Synchronization\n* If the Virtual CLI runs `git checkout -b feature-darkmode` and makes an AST commit in Tier 2 via **Cloudflare Artifacts WASM Git**, the branch ref updates in the Durable Object.\n* When the Tier 6 Container runs `git status` or `cargo build`, **`ArtifactFS` (the FUSE driver) invalidates its cache and presents the exact new branch files inside `/workspace` in 5ms**.\n\n---\n\n# PART 2: Cross-Layer Execution (The Isolate as Conductor)\n\nIn this architecture, **the AI Agent never lives inside the slow, expensive container.** \n\nThe Agent’s brain, memory, and reasoning loop reside in **Tier 1/2 (V8 Isolate in Durable Object)**. The isolate acts as the **Puppeteer / Conductor**, executing fast logic at the edge and calling other tiers (Kitesurf, Chromium, Linux Containers, and Workflows) on the fly within a single script:\n\n```\n[ NaelaoAgentDO in V8 Isolate (The Conductor) ]\n                         │\n                         ├──► 1. TIER 1/2: Virtual CLI patches code \u0026 creates Git branch (Sub-5ms, $0.0001)\n                         │\n                         ├──► 2. TIER 4: Kitesurf scrapes live market data at edge (Sub-200ms, $0.001)\n                         │\n                         ├──► 3. TIER 6: Linux Container compiles native Rust/Node binary over gRPC ($0.05/hr)\n                         │               (Wakes for 12 seconds, flushes diffs, and immediately sleeps!)\n                         │\n                         ├──► 4. TIER 5: Headless Chromium takes visual QA snapshot of live UI ($0.01)\n                         │\n                         └──► 5. TIER 3: Dynamic Workflow schedules weekly cron for recurring execution ($0.00)\n```\n\n---\n\n### Real-World Code: A Single Script Orchestrating Across All 6 Tiers\n\nAn agent in **Tier 2 CodeMode** can write and execute this self-authored TypeScript block that crosses all layers seamlessly:\n\n```typescript\n// Single Tier-2 CodeMode Script Orchestrating Across All 6 Layers\nexport async function run(args: any, ctx: AvosRuntimeContext) {\n  // ── LAYER 1 \u0026 2: Virtual CLI in V8 Isolate (Sub-5ms) ──────────────────────\n  // Branch git repository and patch frontend configuration\n  await ctx.cli.exec(\"git checkout -b feature-payment-v2\");\n  await ctx.fs.edit(\"src/config.ts\", \"MODE \u003d \u0027dev\u0027\", \"MODE \u003d \u0027production\u0027\");\n\n  // ── LAYER 4: Lightweight Kitesurf Browser ──────────────────────────────────\n  // Scrapes latest regulatory tax rates from government portal at edge\n  const taxRates \u003d await ctx.browser.kitesurf(\"https://revenue.state.gov/rates\", [\n    { type: \"extract\", selector: \"table#current-rates\" }\n  ]);\n  await ctx.fs.write(\"src/data/rates.json\", JSON.stringify(taxRates));\n\n  // ── LAYER 6: Heavy Linux Container Sandbox via gRPC ────────────────────────\n  // Wakes container for 15 seconds to run native compilation \u0026 test suite\n  const testRun \u003d await ctx.container.exec(\"npm install \u0026\u0026 npm run test:ci\", {\n    timeoutMs: 30000,\n    syncWorkspaceFiles: true // Ensures FUSE flushes latest rates.json before test\n  });\n\n  if (testRun.exitCode !\u003d\u003d 0) {\n    throw new Error(`Build failed in Linux container: ${testRun.stderr.slice(-500)}`);\n  }\n\n  // ── LAYER 5: Visual QA with Headless Chromium ──────────────────────────────\n  // Takes high-res DOM snapshot to verify checkout button is rendered\n  const qaSnapshot \u003d await ctx.browser.chromium(\"https://preview.edge.app/checkout\", {\n    takeScreenshot: true,\n    assertSelectorExists: \"button#stripe-checkout-btn\"\n  });\n\n  // ── LAYER 3: Dynamic Durable Workflows ─────────────────────────────────────\n  // If all layers pass, register a recurring weekly audit cron\n  await ctx.workflows.schedule({\n    cron: \"0 9 * * 1\", // Every Monday at 9 AM\n    workflowPath: \"workflows/weekly-tax-audit.ts\"\n  });\n\n  return {\n    ok: true,\n    gitCommit: await ctx.cli.exec(\"git rev-parse HEAD\"),\n    qaPassed: qaSnapshot.assertionPassed,\n    message: \"✔ Cross-layer execution completed: Code patched, native build passed, visual QA verified, and weekly cron scheduled.\"\n  };\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n# PART 3: Implementation: The Unified Shell Session \u0026 gRPC Bridge\n\nIn `workers/agents/src/do/NaelaoAgentDO.ts`:\n\n```typescript\n// Persistent Session State inside Durable Object SQLite\nexport interface ShellSessionState {\n  cwd: string;                      // e.g. \"src/components\"\n  envVars: Record\u003cstring, string\u003e;   // e.g. { NODE_ENV: \"production\" }\n  activeGitBranch: string;          // e.g. \"feature-darkmode\"\n}\n\nexport class NaelaoAgentDO extends DurableObject {\n  private sessionState: ShellSessionState \u003d {\n    cwd: \"\",\n    envVars: {},\n    activeGitBranch: \"main\"\n  };\n\n  async executeCrossLayerCommand(command: string) {\n    const trimmed \u003d command.trim();\n\n    // 1. STATEFUL COMMAND INTERCEPTION (Handled in Isolate SQLite)\n    if (trimmed.startsWith(\"cd \")) {\n      const targetDir \u003d trimmed.replace(\"cd \", \"\").trim();\n      this.sessionState.cwd \u003d resolvePath(this.sessionState.cwd, targetDir);\n      return { stdout: `✔ Changed directory to ${this.sessionState.cwd}`, exitCode: 0 };\n    }\n\n    if (trimmed.startsWith(\"export \")) {\n      const [key, val] \u003d trimmed.replace(\"export \", \"\").split(\"\u003d\");\n      this.sessionState.envVars[key.trim()] \u003d val.trim();\n      return { stdout: `✔ Set environment variable ${key}\u003d${val}`, exitCode: 0 };\n    }\n\n    // 2. VIRTUAL CLI SHIMS (Stripe, GitHub, JQ, R2 - Executed in V8 Isolate)\n    if (isVirtualCliCommand(trimmed)) {\n      return await executeVirtualBashShim(trimmed, this.sessionState, this.ctx);\n    }\n\n    // 3. NATIVE CONTAINER EXECUTION VIA gRPC (Tier 6 Pass-Through)\n    // Synchronizes the exact session state (cwd, env, branch) into the container!\n    const sandboxDO \u003d this.env.TOOL_SANDBOX.get(this.env.TOOL_SANDBOX.idFromName(this.ctx.id.toString()));\n    \n    return await sandboxDO.fetch(\"http://internal/exec-grpc\", {\n      method: \"POST\",\n      headers: { \"content-type\": \"application/json\" },\n      body: JSON.stringify({\n        command: trimmed,\n        cwd: `/workspace/${this.sessionState.cwd}`,\n        envVars: this.sessionState.envVars,\n        branch: this.sessionState.activeGitBranch\n      })\n    });\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Summary of What This Establishes\n\n1. **Zero Split-Brain Across Tiers:** Files modified via AST search-and-replace in a V8 isolate immediately appear in the Linux container’s `/workspace` over **ArtifactFS FUSE** without manual copy scripts.\n2. **Session State Continuity:** Shell navigation (`cd`), environment variables (`export`), and active Git branches are tracked in **DO SQLite** and injected into container executions automatically.\n3. **The Isolate as the Conductor:** The agent runs in a cheap, sub-millisecond V8 isolate, orchestrating Virtual CLIs, Kitesurf scrapers, Container builds, and Chromium QA snapshots in a **single turn**.\n4. **95%+ Cost Savings:** Heavy Linux containers are only woken for the exact 10–20 seconds required to compile native code, keeping compute costs at **fractions of a cent**.",
