027m exploring an example of how an agent runs a command, and then the isolate router takes over by checking if the command is pre-registered, synthesized or missing. If the command is missing, the suggestion signal will be passed to the model.\n\n\n**Registering New Commands**\n\nI\u0027ve moved on to the next iteration. I\u0027ve formulated how the agent crafts a 15-line parser using libraries such as `args-parser` or `simple regex/flags`, along with `ctx.vault.fetchWithAuth`. This means that only required components are registered for use. I\u0027m focusing on registering and saving these commands into the `virtual_cli_commands` in `NaelaoAgentDO`. I am ready to incrementally enhance the CLI with more functionality.\n\n\n**Defining the Lifecycle**\n\nMy focus is now on structuring a comprehensive explanation. I\u0027m articulating the \"Just-In-Time (JIT) Virtual CLI Synthesis\" paradigm, highlighting its advantages over monolithic approaches and Docker. I\u0027m breaking down the 3-step lifecycle: command detection and signal, then micro-synthesis, and finally, incremental evolution. I\u0027m also planning to outline the `ctx.cli` runtime SDK interface, detailing what\u0027s exposed to the agent.\n\n\n",
