      "text": "### 1. Unified Authentication State Across All Layers\n\nWhen a user completes an OAuth flow (via Composio, direct OAuth, or API key vault) for a connector like **Google Drive, GitHub, Stripe, Linear, or Shopify**, that authentication state is **automatically shared and active across every layer of the execution ladder**:\n\n```\n[ User completes Composio / Google OAuth in Settings ]\n                          │\n                          ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 🔐 THE UNIVERSAL VAULT LAYER (SpaceDO SQLite / Cloudflare KMS)              │\n│ Stores encrypted OAuth refresh tokens \u0026 connection IDs under `space_102`.   │\n└─────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                          │\n       ┌──────────────────┼──────────────────┬──────────────────┐\n       ▼                  ▼                  ▼                  ▼\n┌──────────────┐   ┌──────────────┐   ┌──────────────┐   ┌──────────────┐\n│ 1. MCP Tools │   │ 2. Virtual   │   │ 3. Raw V8    │   │ 4. Tier 6    │\n│    (/mcp v2) │   │    CLI Shims │   │    HTTP      │   │    Container │\n├──────────────┤   ├──────────────┤   ├──────────────┤   ├──────────────┤\n│ Injected by  │   │ Injected by  │   │ Injected by  │   │ Injected by  │\n│ `mcp-hub`    │   │ Outbound     │   │ `ctx.vault.  │   │ Cloudflare   │\n│ for LLM      │   │ Worker proxy │   │  fetchWith   │   │ Outbound     │\n│ function     │   │ into bash    │   │  Auth()`     │   │ Egress Proxy │\n│ calls│   │ shims│   │      │   │\n└──────────────┘   └──────────────┘   └──────────────┘   └──────────────┘\n```\n\n#### How Each Layer Uses the Same Auth State with Zero Leaks:\n\n1. **Virtual CLI Shims (Tier 1/2 V8 Isolate):**\n   * The agent runs `Bash(\"gh pr create\")` or `Bash(\"stripe customers list\")`.\n   * The V8 isolate shim routes the request through the **Outbound Worker**, attaching `Authorization: Bearer \u003ctoken\u003e` at the edge network boundary.\n2. **Raw V8 HTTP Calls (`ctx.vault.fetchWithAuth` in CodeMode):**\n   * When an agent writes a TypeScript script that calls `ctx.vault.fetchWithAuth(\"https://api.github.com/...\", { credentialName: \"GITHUB_TOKEN\" })`, the runtime attaches the active token directly to the `Request` headers.\n3. **Real Linux Container CLI (Tier 6 Sandbox / `ToolSandboxDO`):**\n   * When the agent runs a native binary inside the container (e.g. native `git push` or `gh` CLI):\n   * Cloudflare’s **Sandbox Outbound Worker** intercepts the container\u0027s outbound TLS traffic via an ephemeral Certificate Authority.\n   * It injects the `Authorization` header transparently as the packet leaves the container.\n   * **Result:** The native Linux `git` binary authenticates successfully, but `cat ~/.gitconfig` inside the container shows **zero raw secrets**, preventing code-injection attacks from stealing credentials.\n\n---\n\n# 2. Industry Research, Articles \u0026 Cloudflare Sources\n\nThis exact paradigm—**Virtual CLI Shims, Isolate-first Execution, Outbound Zero-Trust Credential Proxies, and CodeAct**—is backed by official Cloudflare releases, industry engineering write-ups, and academic papers:\n\n---\n\n### A. Primary Cloudflare Architecture \u0026 Blog Sources\n\n#### 1. \"Your agent needs a computer, not a container — introducing `@cloudflare/computer`\"\n* **Source:** *Cloudflare Official Blog (August 3, 2026)*\n* **Link:** `https://blog.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-computer/`\n* **Core Takeaway:** Explains why 90%+ of agent operations never need a Linux container. Demonstrates how `@cloudflare/computer` combines a **Durable Object SQLite virtual filesystem** with a **`just-bash` Dynamic Worker isolate shell** and an on-demand **FUSE-mounted Linux Container backend**.\n\n#### 2. \"Secure Credential Injection and Dynamic Egress Policies for Sandboxes\"\n* **Source:** *Cloudflare Platform Changelog \u0026 Architecture (April 13 \u0026 August 2026)*\n* **Link:** `https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/2026-04-13-sandbox-egress-policies/`\n* **Core Takeaway:** Introduces **Outbound Workers for Sandboxes and Containers**. Shows how to run untrusted agent-written code while injecting OAuth tokens and API secrets at the edge proxy layer so the sandboxed code never holds raw keys.\n\n#### 3. \"Enterprise AI Vibe Coding Platform Reference Architecture\"\n* **Source:** *Cloudflare Reference Architecture (August 28, 2026)*\n* **Link:** `https://developers.cloudflare.com/reference-architecture/architectures/enterprise-vibe-coding/`\n* **Core Takeaway:** Details the governance, per-app isolation, DO Facets, and zero-trust credential model for user-generated micro-apps and autonomous coding agents.\n\n---\n\n### B. Industry Systems \u0026 Research Sources\n\n#### 4. \"Making MCP Cheaper via CLI (The `mcpshim` Architecture)\"\n* **Source:** *Hacker News \u0026 Engineering Systems Discussion (2026)*\n* **Core Takeaway:** Demonstrates why loading 20–50 full JSON tool schemas into LLM context on every turn causes severe token bloat and context rot. Proves that **wrapping API/MCP capabilities into lightweight CLI shims that support Unix piping (`| jq`, `| grep`, `| tail`)** slashes agent token overhead by **70–80%** while making tasks composable in 1 turn.\n\n#### 5. \"Executable Code Actions Elicit Better LLM Agents (CodeAct)\"\n* **Source:** *Xingyao Wang et al. — ICML 2024 (arXiv:2402.01030)*\n* **Core Takeaway:** The foundational academic paper proving that **code and CLI execution outperforms static JSON tool calling by up to 20% on complex benchmarks** while requiring 30% fewer conversational turns, because code allows the model to implement loops, error handling, and multi-step composition in a single action turn.\n\n#### 6. \"Test-Time Tool Evolution (TTE)\"\n* **Source:** *Jiaxuan Lu et al. — arXiv 2026 (arXiv:2601.07641)*\n* **Core Takeaway:** Proves the viability of **on-demand tool synthesis**, where agents dynamically author their own specialized CLI shims and function handlers at runtime, test them in sandboxes, and register them into their persistent skill library.\n\n---\n\n### Summary Matrix of the Universal Execution Engine\n\n| Layer | Compute Engine | How Auth Token is Injected | State Storage |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Tier 1/2 Virtual CLI** | V8 Isolate (`just-bash`) | Outbound Worker Proxy (`ctx.vault`) | In-Memory DO SQLite Virtual FS |\n| **Tier 2 CodeMode Script** | Dynamic Worker (TypeScript) | `ctx.vault.fetchWithAuth()` | In-Memory DO SQLite Virtual FS |\n| **Tier 3 Dynamic Workflow** | Cloudflare Workflows | Workflow Environment Secrets | Checkpointed Step State in DO |\n| **Tier 4/5 Browser** | Kitesurf / Chromium Puppeteer | Session Cookies / Header Injection | Download buffer stream to DO SQLite |\n| **Tier 6 Linux Container** | Container Sandbox (`ToolSandboxDO`) | **Outbound Worker TLS Interception** | **`ArtifactFS` (FUSE Mount)** |\n\nThis confirms that the **Virtual CLI $\\leftrightarrow$ Real CLI $\\leftrightarrow$ Universal Vault** design aligns directly with Cloudflare\u0027s 2026 developer platform architecture.",
