  <div class="sec" id="foundation">
    <span class="sec-ey">01 — Foundation</span>
    <h2>What Naelao Is Built From</h2>
    <div class="bar"></div>
    <p class="lead">Naelao is a fork of <strong>kortix-ai/suna</strong> (Apache 2.0). Every product concept — threads,
      projects, agents, the marketplace, billing — is preserved. Every infrastructure component is replaced with
      Cloudflare-native equivalents. A user migrating from Suna sees the same product. The stack underneath is
      completely different and dramatically cheaper to operate.</p>

    <h3>The Core Architecture Philosophy</h3>
    <p>The original Suna kortix runs on a traditional server stack: a Python FastAPI backend, Redis for queuing and
      pub/sub, Docker containers managed by Daytona for agent sandboxes, and Supabase for persistence (suna kortix original). This stack costs
      significant money even when idle — containers running, Redis paying for memory, a FastAPI server billing for
      uptime regardless of traffic.</p>
    <p>Naelao's philosophy inverts this: <strong>compute exists only when it is doing compute</strong>. The Durable
      Object is the agent's brain — it costs nothing when the conversation is idle. The container is the agent's hands —
      it boots when needed and stops when done. R2 is the agent's memory — it never sleeps but never computes either.
      Cloudflare Workflows are the agent's long-running tasks — they checkpoint between steps and hibernate for free.
    </p>

    <h3>Complete Suna → Naelao Technology Map</h3>
