  <div class="sec" id="agentdo">
    <span class="sec-ey">03 — AgentDO</span>
    <h2>NaelaoAgentDO — The Agent Brain</h2>
    <div class="bar"></div>
    <p class="lead">The <span class="ic">NaelaoAgentDO</span> is the most critical Durable Object in the entire system.
      It is the agent's persistent brain — everything the agent knows, is doing, and has done lives here. Understanding
      this DO fully before writing anything else is mandatory. Get this wrong and every feature built on top of it will
      be wrong.</p>

    <h3>Why a Durable Object Is the Agent Brain</h3>
    <p>A Durable Object has properties that make it uniquely suited for an agent runtime. It has <strong>strong
        consistency</strong> — single-threaded execution, no race conditions when two requests arrive simultaneously. It
      has <strong>zero idle cost</strong> — when no requests are coming in, the DO hibernates and you pay nothing. It
      has <strong>built-in SQLite</strong> — persistent relational storage in the same process as the request handler,
      no network hop. It has <strong>WebSocket Hibernation</strong> — WebSocket connections survive across the DO
      sleeping and waking, costing nothing while idle. It has <strong>Alarm API</strong> — built-in scheduling without
      any external cron infrastructure.</p>

    <p>The agent is a state machine. Between turns (user messages), it is idle. A traditional server-based agent (like
      Suna kortix's Docker approach) pays full server cost during idle. NaelaoAgentDO pays zero. The agent wakes when a
      message arrives, processes it, dispatches work, and hibernates again. On a platform with thousands of agents most
      of which are idle at any moment, this is an enormous cost difference.</p>

    <h3>DO Identity and Naming</h3>
    <pre><code><span class="cm">// durable-objects/agent-do.ts
// The DO ID determines which agent instance handles which request.
// Critical: this must be stable — the same inputs always produce the same ID.
// If the ID changes, a new DO is created and all state is lost.</span>

<span class="cm">// CORRECT — stable, deterministic ID</span>
const agentId = env.NAELAO_AGENT_DO.idFromName(
  `${spaceId}:${projectId}:${threadId}`
);
const agentDO = env.NAELAO_AGENT_DO.get(agentId);

<span class="cm">// WRONG — random ID creates a new DO every time</span>
const agentId = env.NAELAO_AGENT_DO.newUniqueId(); <span class="cm">// ❌ Never do this for agents</span>

<span class="cm">// WRONG — missing spaceId means different spaces share the same agent brain</span>
const agentId = env.NAELAO_AGENT_DO.idFromName(`${projectId}:${threadId}`); <span class="cm">// ❌ Security violation</span></code></pre>

    <h3>Complete DO SQLite Schema</h3>
    <p>Every table the NaelaoAgentDO creates in its built-in SQLite storage. Run these in the DO's constructor, wrapped
      in a transaction, using <span class="ic">this.ctx.storage.sql.exec()</span>. If you use <span
        class="ic">this.ctx.storage.put()</span> instead of SQL for structured data, you will regret it — SQL is faster,
      queryable, and supports migrations.</p>
    <pre><code><span class="cm">// durable-objects/agent-do.ts
// Run in constructor — idempotent (IF NOT EXISTS on all tables)</span>

export class NaelaoAgentDO extends DurableObject {
  constructor(ctx: DurableObjectState, env: Env) {
    super(ctx, env);
    
    <span class="cm">// Initialize schema — runs on first request after DO creation</span>
    ctx.blockConcurrencyWhile(async () => {
      await this.initSchema();
    });
  }

  private async initSchema() {
    this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(`
      <span class="cm">-- Run WAL: write before execute for crash recovery</span>
      CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS run_wal (
        id          TEXT PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT (lower(hex(randomblob(16)))),
        run_id      TEXT NOT NULL,
        tool_name   TEXT NOT NULL,
        tool_args   TEXT NOT NULL,   <span class="cm">-- JSON</span>
        status      TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending',  <span class="cm">-- pending|complete|failed</span>
        result      TEXT,            <span class="cm">-- JSON, null while pending</span>
        started_at  INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT (unixepoch('now') * 1000),
        finished_at INTEGER,
        CONSTRAINT valid_status CHECK (status IN ('pending', 'complete', 'failed'))
      );

      <span class="cm">-- Current active fiber (background run)</span>
      CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS fibers (
        id          TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
        name        TEXT NOT NULL,
        status      TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'running',  <span class="cm">-- running|complete|failed|cancelled</span>
        snapshot    TEXT,            <span class="cm">-- JSON checkpoint state from ctx.stash()</span>
        created_at  INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT (unixepoch('now') * 1000),
        updated_at  INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT (unixepoch('now') * 1000)
      );

      <span class="cm">-- Session: conversation messages as a tree (Project Think)</span>
      CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sessions (
        id          TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
        thread_id   TEXT NOT NULL,
        created_at  INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT (unixepoch('now') * 1000)
      );

      CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS messages (
        id          TEXT PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT (lower(hex(randomblob(16)))),
        session_id  TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES sessions(id),
        parent_id   TEXT REFERENCES messages(id),   <span class="cm">-- tree structure</span>
        role        TEXT NOT NULL,                   <span class="cm">-- user|assistant|tool|system</span>
        content     TEXT NOT NULL,                   <span class="cm">-- raw text or JSON</span>
        tool_name   TEXT,                            <span class="cm">-- if role=tool</span>
        token_count INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
        created_at  INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT (unixepoch('now') * 1000),
        CONSTRAINT valid_role CHECK (role IN ('user', 'assistant', 'tool', 'system'))
      );
      CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_messages_session ON messages(session_id, created_at);
      CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE IF NOT EXISTS messages_fts USING fts5(
        content, session_id UNINDEXED,
        content=messages, content_rowid=rowid
      );

      <span class="cm">-- Token buffer for reconnect replay (last 1000 tokens)</span>
      CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS token_buffer (
        id          INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
        run_id      TEXT NOT NULL,
        delta       TEXT NOT NULL,  <span class="cm">-- streaming token text</span>
        created_at  INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT (unixepoch('now') * 1000)
      );

      <span class="cm">-- Context cache control points</span>
      CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS context_cache (
        key         TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
        value       TEXT NOT NULL,
        expires_at  INTEGER
      );

      <span class="cm">-- Agent memory (typed JSON, never flat Markdown)</span>
      CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS agent_memory (
        key         TEXT NOT NULL,
        category    TEXT NOT NULL,  <span class="cm">-- preference|fact|context|task</span>
        value       TEXT NOT NULL,  <span class="cm">-- JSON</span>
        confidence  REAL DEFAULT 1.0,
        created_at  INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT (unixepoch('now') * 1000),
        updated_at  INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT (unixepoch('now') * 1000),
        PRIMARY KEY (key, category)
      );

      <span class="cm">-- Plan steps (todo.md mirror in SQL for fast queries)</span>
      CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS plan_steps (
        id          INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
        run_id      TEXT NOT NULL,
        step_text   TEXT NOT NULL,
        status      TEXT DEFAULT 'pending',  <span class="cm">-- pending|done|skipped</span>
        order_idx   INTEGER NOT NULL,
        updated_at  INTEGER DEFAULT (unixepoch('now') * 1000)
      );
    `);
  }
}</code></pre>

    <h3>The Full Agent Run() Method</h3>
    <p>This is the most important method in the entire codebase. It orchestrates the entire agent execution loop. Study
      every line — each decision here has a reason.</p>
    <pre><code><span class="cm">// durable-objects/agent-do.ts (continued)</span>

async run(request: Request): Promise&lt;Response&gt; {
  const body = await request.json() as AgentRunRequest;
  const { threadId, input, backgroundMode, runId, spaceId } = body;

  <span class="cm">// 1. Verify space isolation — NEVER skip this</span>
  if (this.spaceId !== spaceId) {
    return new Response('Forbidden: space mismatch', { status: 403 });
  }

  <span class="cm">// 2. Create or load session (Project Think SessionManager)</span>
  let sessionId = this.ctx.storage.sql
    .exec('SELECT id FROM sessions WHERE thread_id = ?', threadId)
    .one()?.id as string | null;
  
  if (!sessionId) {
    sessionId = crypto.randomUUID();
    this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(
      'INSERT INTO sessions (id, thread_id) VALUES (?, ?)',
      sessionId, threadId
    );
  }

  <span class="cm">// 3. Add user message to session tree</span>
  const userMsgId = crypto.randomUUID();
  this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(
    'INSERT INTO messages (id, session_id, role, content) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)',
    userMsgId, sessionId, 'user', input
  );

  <span class="cm">// 4. Background mode → runFiber() for durable execution</span>
  if (backgroundMode) {
    <span class="cm">// Register fiber BEFORE starting execution
    // If we crash between registration and execution start, the sweeper finds
    // a 'running' fiber with no recent heartbeat and marks it failed.
    // This is intentional — better to mark failed than to hang forever.</span>
    const fiberId = runId ?? crypto.randomUUID();
    this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(
      'INSERT INTO fibers (id, name, status) VALUES (?, ?, ?)',
      fiberId, 'agent-run', 'running'
    );

    <span class="cm">// runFiber() — Project Think primitive for durable execution
    // The fiber is registered in SQLite. If the DO is evicted, onFiberRecovered()
    // is called with the last snapshot. The agent resumes from the last checkpoint.</span>
    void this.runFiber(`agent-run-${fiberId}`, async (ctx) => {
      await this.executeAgentLoop(sessionId!, userMsgId, ctx);
      this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(
        'UPDATE fibers SET status = ? WHERE id = ?', 'complete', fiberId
      );
    });

    return Response.json({ status: 'background', fiberId });
  }

  <span class="cm">// 5. Foreground mode — direct execution, WS-tied</span>
  <span class="cm">// If the user closes the browser, the WS closes, the DO hibernates,
  // and the run stops cleanly. No orphaned state.</span>
  await this.executeAgentLoop(sessionId, userMsgId, null);
  return Response.json({ status: 'complete' });
}

private async executeAgentLoop(
  sessionId: string,
  startMsgId: string,
  fiberCtx: FiberContext | null
) {
  const agentPress = new AgentPress(this.env, {
    spaceId: this.spaceId,
    sessionId,
    onToken: (delta: string, runId: string) => {
      <span class="cm">// Buffer tokens for reconnect replay</span>
      this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(
        'INSERT INTO token_buffer (run_id, delta) VALUES (?, ?)', runId, delta
      );
      <span class="cm">// Broadcast to all connected WebSocket clients</span>
      this.ctx.getWebSockets().forEach(ws => {
        ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'token', delta, runId }));
      });
    }
  });

  let iteration = 0;
  const MAX_ITERATIONS = 50; <span class="cm">// prevent infinite loops</span>

  while (iteration < MAX_ITERATIONS) {
    iteration++;

    <span class="cm">// Checkpoint fiber state every iteration (Project Think)</span>
    if (fiberCtx) {
      fiberCtx.stash({ iteration, sessionId, lastMsgId: startMsgId });
    }

    <span class="cm">// Build context from session messages</span>
    const messages = await agentPress.buildContext(sessionId);
    
    <span class="cm">// LLM call via CF AI Gateway</span>
    const response = await agentPress.callLLM(messages);

    <span class="cm">// Persist assistant message</span>
    const assistantMsgId = crypto.randomUUID();
    this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(
      'INSERT INTO messages (id, session_id, parent_id, role, content, token_count) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)',
      assistantMsgId, sessionId, startMsgId, 'assistant', 
      response.content, response.usage.output_tokens
    );

    <span class="cm">// Record billing — every LLM response, no exceptions</span>
    await this.env.NAELAO_BILLING.recordTokens({
      spaceId: this.spaceId,
      inputTokens: response.usage.input_tokens,
      outputTokens: response.usage.output_tokens,
      cacheReadTokens: response.usage.cache_read_input_tokens ?? 0,
      cacheWriteTokens: response.usage.cache_creation_input_tokens ?? 0,
      model: response.model,
    });

    <span class="cm">// If no tool calls, the agent is done</span>
    if (!response.toolCalls || response.toolCalls.length === 0) {
      if (response.stopReason === 'end_turn') break;
      if (response.stopReason === 'max_tokens') {
        <span class="cm">// Context full — trigger compaction before next iteration</span>
        await agentPress.compactContext(sessionId);
        continue;
      }
      break;
    }

    <span class="cm">// Execute tools — parallel for CF-native, serial for containers</span>
    const toolResults = await agentPress.executeTools(
      response.toolCalls,
      { sessionId, assistantMsgId, fiberCtx }
    );

    <span class="cm">// Persist tool results</span>
    for (const result of toolResults) {
      this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(
        'INSERT INTO messages (id, session_id, parent_id, role, content, tool_name) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)',
        crypto.randomUUID(), sessionId, assistantMsgId,
        'tool', JSON.stringify(result.output), result.toolName
      );
    }

    <span class="cm">// Update todo.md in R2 if plan changed</span>
    await this.syncTodoMd(sessionId);
  }

  <span class="cm">// Broadcast completion to connected clients</span>
  this.ctx.getWebSockets().forEach(ws => {
    ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'run_complete', sessionId }));
  });
}

<span class="cm">// Called by CF runtime when DO is recovered after eviction
// The fiber's last stash() snapshot is in ctx.snapshot</span>
async onFiberRecovered(ctx: FiberContext) {
  if (!ctx.snapshot) return; <span class="cm">// new fiber, nothing to recover</span>
  
  const { iteration, sessionId, lastMsgId } = ctx.snapshot;
  
  <span class="cm">// Resume from last checkpoint
  // We don't replay the completed iterations — only resume from the last stash point
  // The session messages already contain everything up to the checkpoint</span>
  await this.executeAgentLoop(sessionId, lastMsgId, ctx);
}</code></pre>

    <h3>WebSocket Hibernation — How Streaming Works</h3>
    <p>WebSocket Hibernation is what makes real-time streaming cost-efficient. Without it, keeping a WebSocket open
      would keep the DO active and billing. With Hibernation, the DO can hibernate between messages and the WebSocket
      connection survives — the client sees a continuous stream.</p>
    <pre><code><span class="cm">// The DO handles WebSocket upgrades in its fetch() handler</span>
async fetch(request: Request): Promise&lt;Response&gt; {
  const url = new URL(request.url);
  
  if (request.headers.get('Upgrade') === 'websocket') {
    <span class="cm">// SECURITY: Always validate origin before upgrading
    // CVE-2026-25253 happened because OpenClaw skipped this check</span>
    const origin = request.headers.get('Origin') ?? '';
    const allowed = ['https://app.naelao.dev', 'https://naelao.dev'];
    if (!allowed.some(a => origin.startsWith(a))) {
      return new Response('Forbidden: invalid origin', { status: 403 });
    }

    <span class="cm">// CF WebSocket Hibernation — the correct way to create hibernated WS</span>
    const pair = new WebSocketPair();
    const [client, server] = Object.values(pair);
    
    <span class="cm">// acceptWebSocket() registers the WS for hibernation
    // The DO can now sleep between messages — zero cost while idle
    // When client sends a message, DO wakes and webSocketMessage() fires</span>
    this.ctx.acceptWebSocket(server);
    
    return new Response(null, { status: 101, webSocket: client });
  }

  <span class="cm">// Route non-WS requests to appropriate handler</span>
  if (url.pathname === '/run') return this.run(request);
  if (url.pathname === '/replay') return this.replayBuffer(request);
  return new Response('Not Found', { status: 404 });
}

<span class="cm">// Called by CF runtime when a hibernated WS receives a message</span>
async webSocketMessage(ws: WebSocket, message: string | ArrayBuffer) {
  const data = JSON.parse(message as string);
  
  if (data.type === 'ping') {
    ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'pong' }));
    return;
  }
  if (data.type === 'cancel') {
    await this.cancelCurrentRun();
    return;
  }
}

<span class="cm">// Reconnect: replay buffered tokens so user sees full history</span>
async replayBuffer(request: Request): Promise&lt;Response&gt; {
  const { runId } = await request.json();
  const tokens = this.ctx.storage.sql
    .exec('SELECT delta FROM token_buffer WHERE run_id = ? ORDER BY id', runId)
    .toArray();
  return Response.json({ tokens: tokens.map(r => r.delta) });
}</code></pre>

    <h3>The WAL (Write-Ahead Log) — Crash Recovery</h3>
    <p>The WAL is one of the most important patterns in Naelao. Every tool call is written to the WAL <em>before</em> it
      executes. If the DO crashes mid-execution, the sweeper finds pending WAL entries and replays them. Without the
      WAL, a crash loses all in-progress work. With it, the agent can always resume.</p>
    <pre><code><span class="cm">// agentpress/wal.ts
// Every tool execution MUST go through this. No exceptions.
// If you call a tool without WAL, a crash loses the result and the loop hangs.</span>

export class WAL {
  constructor(private sql: SqlStorage) {}

  async executeWithWAL&lt;T&gt;(
    runId: string,
    toolName: string,
    args: unknown,
    executor: () => Promise&lt;T&gt;
  ): Promise&lt;T&gt; {
    const walId = crypto.randomUUID();
    
    <span class="cm">// WRITE BEFORE EXECUTE — this is the entire point of WAL
    // If we crash after this line but before the executor, the sweeper
    // finds this 'pending' entry and knows to either retry or mark failed.</span>
    this.sql.exec(
      `INSERT INTO run_wal (id, run_id, tool_name, tool_args, status) 
       VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, 'pending')`,
      walId, runId, toolName, JSON.stringify(args)
    );

    try {
      const result = await executor();
      
      <span class="cm">// Mark complete AFTER successful execution</span>
      this.sql.exec(
        `UPDATE run_wal SET status = 'complete', result = ?, finished_at = ?
         WHERE id = ?`,
        JSON.stringify(result), Date.now(), walId
      );
      
      return result;
    } catch (error) {
      <span class="cm">// Mark failed — the error is preserved for debugging</span>
      this.sql.exec(
        `UPDATE run_wal SET status = 'failed', result = ?, finished_at = ?
         WHERE id = ?`,
        JSON.stringify({ error: (error as Error).message }), Date.now(), walId
      );
      throw error;
    }
  }

  async getPendingEntries(runId: string): Promise&lt;WALEntry[]&gt; {
    return this.sql
      .exec(`SELECT * FROM run_wal WHERE run_id = ? AND status = 'pending'`, runId)
      .toArray() as WALEntry[];
  }
}</code></pre>

