    <h2>Naelao OS — The Foundation That Makes All Space Types Possible</h2>
    <div class="bar"></div>
    <p class="lead">The insight behind "no more building Space Types from scratch" is this: every Space Type —
      Launchpad, Sites, Verticals, Enterprise, Workers, Mini-AGI — is made of the same primitives configured
      differently. Naelao OS is the name for the layer that provides these primitives so a developer (or the AI itself)
      can compose any Space Type without touching platform code.</p>

    <div class="box box-or">
      <div class="box-lbl">The Whop Analogy — But For Agents</div>
      <p>Whop lets users build plugin apps so Whop doesn't have to ship features every day. The user builds exactly the
        feature they need using Whop's developer tools. Naelao OS is this, but the "apps" are <strong>MCP
          servers</strong> consumed by both users (via UI) and agents (via tool calls). The "developer tools" are CF
        Dynamic Workers, Dynamic Workflows, Naelao's agent SDK, and the skill system. Any Space Type is just a
        composition of these primitives with specific defaults and UI templates.</p>
    </div>

