    <h3>Common Implementation Errors — The Junior Developer Error Handbook</h3>
    <p>These are the 15 most common mistakes made when implementing Naelao. Read all of them before writing any code.
      Memorize them.</p>

    <table class="t">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>#</th>
          <th>Error</th>
          <th>Symptom</th>
          <th>Correct Approach</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">1</td>
          <td class="tr">Testing in Node.js instead of workerd</td>
          <td>Tests pass locally, fail in production. WebSocket API different. DO SQLite missing.</td>
          <td>Configure vitest with @cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers from day 1. Never write tests that run in Node.js.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">2</td>
          <td class="tr">Using newUniqueId() for agent DOs</td>
          <td>New DO created on every request. Previous conversation state lost.</td>
          <td>Always use idFromName() with a deterministic key. The key must be the same for every request to the same
            agent.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">3</td>
          <td class="tr">Calling SpaceDO with wrong rootSpaceId or bypassing SpaceDO with raw DO SQL</td>
          <td>Queries return all rows across all spaces. Data leak. RLS catches it (0 rows returned instead of wrong
            rows).</td>
          <td>Every data access must go through SpaceDO typed methods — never construct raw SQL in Workers. Use ESLint rule to
            enforce.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">4</td>
          <td class="tr">WAL entry written after tool execution</td>
          <td>If DO evicts between tool execution and WAL write, tool ran but no record. Loop hangs on recovery.</td>
          <td>WAL entry must be written BEFORE the tool executes. See wal.ts — executeWithWAL() enforces this pattern.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">5</td>
          <td class="tr">Two-query debit instead of atomic SQL</td>
          <td>Race condition. Two simultaneous agent runs both read balance=100, both debit 80, balance goes to -60.
          </td>
          <td>DO is single-threaded — no race conditions. Use a single SQL UPDATE for the deduction. See
            WalletDO.deductCredits().</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">6</td>
          <td class="tr">StreamingXMLParser not handling partial chunks</td>
          <td>Tool calls silently dropped when tag is split across chunks. Agent loops forever or stops prematurely.
          </td>
          <td>Buffer incomplete tags. Only emit when closing tag arrives. See xml-parser.ts — the while(true) loop
            pattern.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">7</td>
          <td class="tr">Skipping WebSocket origin validation</td>
          <td>CVE-2026-25253 class vulnerability. Any attacker can steal auth tokens via a malicious WebSocket URL.</td>
          <td>ALWAYS validate Origin header before accepting WebSocket upgrade. See handleWebSocketUpgrade() in security
            section.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">8</td>
          <td class="tr">Skills loading from R2 on every LLM call</td>
          <td>300-500ms added to every LLM turn from R2 latency. Agent feels slow.</td>
          <td>Load skills ONCE at agent run start. Cache in AgentDO SQLite context_cache table with TTL. Invalidate only
            on skill changes.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">9</td>
          <td class="tr">Missing cf-aig-metadata header</td>
          <td>All LLM costs billed to single account, no per-space analytics, rate limits don't work correctly.</td>
          <td>Use createAnthropicClient() factory for every LLM call. It always includes the metadata headers.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">10</td>
          <td class="tr">Reading credentials from process.env in agents</td>
          <td>Credentials exposed in agent logs. Agents can read each other's secrets.</td>
          <td>All credentials go through naelao-credentials Worker. It decrypts and injects at request time. Never in
            env vars accessible to agent code.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">11</td>
          <td class="tr">Skipping security scanner on agent-created skills</td>
          <td>Agent can write malicious skill that exfiltrates data. ClawHavoc equivalent inside your platform.</td>
          <td>ALL skills go through scanSkillContent() before writing to R2. No exceptions. Scanner runs even for
            assistant self-authored skills.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">12</td>
          <td class="tr">Adding a second DynamicWorkflow binding</td>
          <td>Breaks tenant isolation. Wrong workflow code loaded for wrong tenant.</td>
          <td>ONE binding. Always. The spaceId in metadata determines which tenant's code runs. See naelao-workflows
            Worker Loader.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">13</td>
          <td class="tr">Using fetch() for internal service calls</td>
          <td>HTTP round-trip between Workers in same data center. 5-50ms unnecessary latency on every call.</td>
          <td>Use Service Bindings. env.NAELAO_AUTH.fetch() goes direct, no network hop. Orders of magnitude faster.
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">14</td>
          <td class="tr">Memory poisoning via flat Markdown</td>
          <td>Attacker injects persistent instructions into assistant memory. Instructions activate on next session
            silently.</td>
          <td>Memory MUST be typed JSON in DO SQLite with schema validation. See writeMemory() in AssistantDO. Never
            flat Markdown.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">15</td>
          <td class="tr">Federated learning without LLM judge</td>
          <td>Company data (names, revenues, strategies) leaks through skill patterns to Worker definition. Legal
            liability.</td>
          <td>EVERY proposed learning goes through the LLM judge in WorkerDefinitionDO.proposeLearning(). 0.95
            confidence threshold. Non-negotiable.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>


