    <span class="sec-ey">23 — Developer Space Type</span>
    <h2>Developer Space — The Builder's Environment</h2>
    <div class="bar"></div>
    <p class="lead">The Developer Space Type is where developers build everything else on Naelao: new Space Types, new
      Naelao Apps (MCP servers), new agent definitions, fine-tuning pipelines, and custom integrations. It combines the
      capabilities of Lovable (AI-generated UI) and Claude Code (agentic coding) into an environment where Naelao agents
      write Naelao code, deployed to Naelao infrastructure — a complete build loop.</p>

    <h3>Who Developer Space Is For</h3>
    <ul class="fl">
      <li><strong>Platform developers</strong> building new Space Types that will be available to other builders via
        the Space Type picker in the Builder Dashboard Product Creation Wizard</li>
      <li><strong>App developers</strong> building Naelao Apps (MCP servers) to publish to the Naelao Apps marketplace
      </li>
      <li><strong>Agency developers</strong> building custom agent definitions and workflow templates for their clients
      </li>
      <li><strong>Internal platform teams</strong> at Enterprise companies building internal tools and automations on
        Naelao</li>
      <li><strong>Researchers</strong> building fine-tuning pipelines, evaluation frameworks, and dataset management
        tools</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>What Developer Space Adds on Top of Standard Space</h3>
    <div class="g2">
      <div class="box box-pu">
        <div class="box-lbl">Development Primitives</div>
        <p><strong>Code Agent (Claude Code-style):</strong> NaelaoAgentDO configured for agentic coding. Reads/writes
          files in the developer's R2 workspace, runs tests in the container, commits and pushes to GitHub via git-ops
          skill, deploys to CF via wrangler CLI in container.</p>
        <p><strong>UI Agent (Lovable-style):</strong> NaelaoAgentDO configured for UI generation. Creates React
          components, styles them with Tailwind, previews via Artifacts (Dynamic Worker Loader), iterates based on user
          feedback.</p>
        <p><strong>Live Preview:</strong> Every code change can be previewed via spin_artifact() within 5ms. No separate
          preview server needed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="box box-cy">
        <div class="box-lbl">Publishing Pipeline</div>
        <p><strong>Space Type Publisher:</strong> Agent generates a NaelaoSpaceTypeManifest, validates it, and submits
          it to the platform registry. After review, it appears in the Space Type picker in the Builder Dashboard Product Creation Wizard — available for other builders to use when configuring their products.</p>
        <p><strong>App Publisher:</strong> Agent generates naelao-app.json, writes MCP server TypeScript, deploys via
          wrangler, registers with naelao-apps-registry. App appears in marketplace immediately.</p>
        <p><strong>Agent Definition Publisher:</strong> Agent generates agent definition JSON, validates against schema,
          submits to naelao-agents marketplace. Other builders can install it into their products via the Builder Dashboard.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

