  <div class="sep"></div>
  <div class="sec" id="user-journeys">
    <span class="sec-ey">25 — User Journeys</span>
    <h2>Complete User Journeys — From Sign-Up to Production</h2>
    <div class="bar"></div>
    <p class="lead">These are the exact flows a user goes through for each major interaction. Every step maps to a
      specific API call, Worker, or Durable Object. Junior developers can use these flows to verify their implementation
      is correct end-to-end.</p>

    <h3>Journey 1A — Builder Onboards and Ships Their First Product</h3>
    <p style="font-size:0.9rem;opacity:0.75;margin-top:-0.5rem;margin-bottom:1rem;">Builders are Tier 1. They access <code>dashboard.naelao.app</code> — never the end-user product surface. End users never interact with Naelao directly; they interact with the builder's product.</p>
    <div class="flow">
      <div class="fstep">
        <div class="fn">1</div>
        <div class="ft"><strong>Builder signs up</strong> at <code>dashboard.naelao.app</code> via Naelao-native auth (CF Access + JWT). naelao-auth issues a builder-scoped JWT. BuilderAccountDO initialized (one DO per builder org).</div>
      </div>
      <div class="fstep">
        <div class="fn">2</div>
        <div class="ft"><strong>Builder opens the Product Creation Wizard.</strong> Selects a space type (e.g. Team, Launchpad, Verticals) or picks a Temple for a pre-configured starting point. No space type is ever chosen by end users — the builder fixes it here.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="fstep">
        <div class="fn">3</div>
        <div class="ft"><strong>Builder configures auth, pricing, and branding.</strong> Picks auth provider (Naelao-native, Clerk, custom OIDC, or SAML SSO), sets pricing model (free / credits / subscription / seats), uploads logo, sets brand color, and enters their custom domain.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="fstep">
        <div class="fn">4</div>
        <div class="ft"><strong>Builder launches.</strong> POST /builder/products → naelao-spaces creates the Space with the chosen manifest, naelao-agents installs default agents, CF Pages project is provisioned for the product frontend, domain registered in KV. <code>NaelaoProduct</code> record written to SpaceDO SQLite (root space's product DB) and indexed in KV for fast lookup.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="fstep">
