    <span class="sec-ey">27 — Worker Deep Dive: naelao-threads</span>
    <h2>naelao-threads — Thread & Message Management</h2>
    <div class="bar"></div>
    <p class="lead">naelao-threads is responsible for every thread and message in the platform. It is one of the most
      frequently called Workers — every agent run, every user message, and every streaming response passes through it.
      Getting this Worker wrong causes data loss, incorrect billing, and broken streaming. This section documents every
      endpoint, every SQL query, and every edge case.</p>

    <h3>What naelao-threads Does</h3>
    <ul class="fl">
      <li><strong>Thread CRUD:</strong> Create, read, update, list, archive threads. All queries include <span
          class="ic">WHERE space_id = $1</span> via withSpace() middleware.</li>
      <li><strong>Message persistence:</strong> Persist user messages before the agent runs. Persist agent responses
        after. Persist tool results. All with space_id, thread_id, and created_at.</li>
      <li><strong>SSE streaming:</strong> For clients that can't use WebSockets (certain mobile browsers),
        naelao-threads provides an SSE fallback endpoint that proxies tokens from the AgentDO WebSocket.</li>
      <li><strong>Message search:</strong> Full-text search across a user's threads using SpaceDO SQLite FTS5 (messages_fts virtual table)
        (tsvector). Useful for the "search my conversations" feature.</li>
      <li><strong>Thread metadata:</strong> Title, summary (AI-generated after run completes), tags (auto-assigned by
        naelao-categorizer), and project association.</li>
    </ul>

