    <h2>Complete Workspace Setup — From Zero to First Worker</h2>
    <div class="bar"></div>
    <p class="lead">This section walks a junior developer through setting up the complete Naelao development environment
      from a blank machine. Every command is exact. Every config value is explained. Follow these steps in order and you
      will have a working local development environment in under 2 hours.</p>

    <h3>Prerequisites</h3>
    <ul class="fl">
      <li>Node.js 22+ (use nvm: <span class="ic">nvm install 22 && nvm use 22</span>)</li>
      <li>A Cloudflare account (free tier is fine for development)</li>
      <li>Cloudflare account with Workers, Durable Objects, R2, KV, and Vectorize enabled (no Supabase required)</li>
      <li>Git configured with your credentials</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Step 1 — Fork and Clone</h3>
    <pre><code><span class="cm"># Fork kortix-ai/suna on GitHub first, then:</span>
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_ORG/naelao.git
cd naelao

<span class="cm"># Install all workspace dependencies</span>
npm install

<span class="cm"># Run the rebrand script ONCE — never run it again</span>
chmod +x scripts/rename-to-naelao.sh
./scripts/rename-to-naelao.sh

<span class="cm"># Verify the rename</span>
git diff --stat
<span class="cm"># Should show changes only in Worker names, package.json, wrangler.jsonc, env vars</span>
<span class="cm"># Should NOT show changes in: LICENSE, agentpress Python original comments, kortix attribution</span></code></pre>

    <h3>Step 2 — Cloudflare Resources</h3>
    <pre><code><span class="cm"># Login to Cloudflare</span>
npx wrangler login

<span class="cm"># Create R2 buckets</span>
npx wrangler r2 bucket create naelao-workspace
npx wrangler r2 bucket create naelao-assets

<span class="cm"># Create KV namespaces (copy the IDs printed to your wrangler.jsonc)</span>
npx wrangler kv namespace create naelao-config
npx wrangler kv namespace create naelao-circuit
npx wrangler kv namespace create naelao-artifact

<span class="cm"># Create Queues</span>
npx wrangler queues create naelao-agent-runs
npx wrangler queues create naelao-analytics
npx wrangler queues create naelao-notifications
npx wrangler queues create naelao-dlq

<span class="cm"># Create AI Gateway (do this in CF dashboard: AI Gateway > Create)
# Copy ACCOUNT_ID and GATEWAY_ID to your .dev.vars</span>

<span class="cm"># Create Vectorize index for knowledge base</span>
npx wrangler vectorize create naelao-kb   --dimensions=768   --metric=cosine</code></pre>

    <h3>Step 3 — SpaceDO Configuration</h3>
    <pre><code><span class="cm"># No Supabase CLI, no Hyperdrive, no external DB to configure.
