    <span class="sec-ey">40 — Execution Ladder Deep Dive</span>
    <h2>The 5-Tier Execution Ladder — Complete Specification</h2>
    <div class="bar"></div>
    <p class="lead">The execution ladder is a Project Think concept that defines five tiers of compute, from
      cheapest/fastest (direct R2 reads) to most expensive/capable (full Linux container). The agent automatically
      selects the right tier for each tool call. This section documents every tier with exact cost, boot time,
      capability limits, and the code that routes between them.</p>

    <h3>The 5 Tiers — Complete Specification</h3>

    <h4>Tier 1 — Workspace (Direct R2)</h4>
    <div class="box box-gr">
      <div class="box-lbl">Tier 1: Workspace — Direct R2 Operations</div>
      <p><strong>Boot time:</strong> ~0ms (no isolate created). <strong>Cost:</strong> R2 read/write pricing only
        (~$0.00004 per 1k operations). <strong>No CPU billing</strong> for the operation itself.</p>
      <p><strong>Capabilities:</strong> Read files, write files, list directories, delete files, copy files within R2.
        Nothing else. Cannot execute code. Cannot make HTTP requests. Cannot access system resources.</p>
      <p><strong>When to use:</strong> read_file, write_file, list_directory, delete_file, todo-workflow updates. Any
        operation that is purely a file read or write.</p>
      <p><strong>When NOT to use:</strong> Any computation on file contents (use Tier 2). Any file format conversion
        (use Tier 5). Any HTTP request (use Tier 2).</p>
    </div>
    <pre><code><span class="cm">// agentpress/orchestrator.ts — Tier 1 execution
// No isolate created. Direct R2 API call via SpaceR2 helper.
// This is why workspace-tier tools are parallelized — they're pure I/O.</span>

private async executeWorkspaceTool(tc: ParsedToolCall, spaceId: string, projectId: string): Promise&lt;ToolResult&gt; {
  const r2 = new SpaceR2(this.env.NAELAO_WORKSPACE, spaceId);
  const prefix = `projects/${projectId}/workspace/`;

  switch (tc.toolName) {
    case 'read_file': {
      const obj = await r2.get(`${prefix}${tc.parameters.path}`);
      if (!obj) return { toolName: tc.toolName, output: { error: 'File not found', path: tc.parameters.path } };
      return { toolName: tc.toolName, output: { content: await obj.text(), size: obj.size } };
    }
    case 'write_file': {
      await r2.put(`${prefix}${tc.parameters.path}`, tc.parameters.content ?? '');
      return { toolName: tc.toolName, output: { success: true, path: tc.parameters.path } };
    }
    case 'list_directory': {
      const listing = await r2.list(`${prefix}${tc.parameters.path ?? ''}`);
      return { toolName: tc.toolName, output: {
        files: listing.objects.map(o => ({
          name: o.key.replace(`spaces/${spaceId}/${prefix}`, ''),
          size: o.size
        })),
        count: listing.objects.length
      }};
    }
    default:
      throw new Error(`Unknown workspace tool: ${tc.toolName}`);
  }
}</code></pre>

    <h4>Tier 2 — Isolate (Dynamic Worker)</h4>
    <div class="box box-bl">
      <div class="box-lbl">Tier 2: Isolate — V8 Dynamic Worker</div>
      <p><strong>Boot time:</strong> &lt;5ms (V8 isolate, no OS overhead). <strong>Cost:</strong> CF Workers billing
        (~$0.50 per 1M requests + $0.02 per GB-second CPU). Typical tool call: &lt;$0.000001.</p>
      <p><strong>Capabilities:</strong> Full TypeScript/JavaScript execution. Fetch to external HTTP endpoints
        (sandboxed). Web Crypto. No filesystem access. No native binaries. No npm at runtime (packages must be bundled
        at deploy time).</p>
      <p><strong>When to use:</strong> web_search (Tavily API call), api_caller (REST/GraphQL), data_transform
        (JS-based), render_artifact (HTML generation), any TypeScript computation that doesn't need filesystem access.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Implementation:</strong> The agent's tool call code is a TypeScript function. The orchestrator sends it
        to a pre-deployed Dynamic Worker via Service Binding. The Worker executes the function and returns the result.
      </p>
    </div>
    <pre><code><span class="cm">// agentpress/orchestrator.ts — Tier 2 execution via Dynamic Worker</span>
private async executeIsolateTool(tc: ParsedToolCall): Promise&lt;ToolResult&gt; {
  <span class="cm">// Route to the appropriate platform skill Worker via naelao-mcp-hub</span>
  const response = await this.env.NAELAO_MCP_HUB.fetch(
    new Request('http://mcp-hub/execute', {
      method: 'POST',
      body: JSON.stringify({
        toolName: tc.toolName,
        parameters: tc.parameters,
        spaceId: this.spaceId,
        tier: 'isolate'
      })
    })
  );
  const result = await response.json();
  return { toolName: tc.toolName, output: result };
}</code></pre>

    <h4>Tier 3 — npm (Isolate + Package Resolution)</h4>
    <div class="box box-tl">
      <div class="box-lbl">Tier 3: npm — Dynamic Worker with Package Resolution</div>
      <p><strong>Boot time:</strong> &lt;10ms (npm resolution cached by Cloudflare). <strong>Cost:</strong> Same as Tier
        2 plus npm package fetching (minimal).</p>
      <p><strong>Capabilities:</strong> Everything in Tier 2 plus ability to import npm packages not bundled at deploy
        time. Used for: markdown parsing, PDF text extraction (pure JS), JSON schema validation, date parsing libraries.
      </p>
      <p><strong>When to use:</strong> Tasks that need a specific npm package but no filesystem access or native
        binaries. Example: parsing a YAML string with <span class="ic">js-yaml</span>, validating JSON with <span
          class="ic">ajv</span>, generating CSV with <span class="ic">papaparse</span>.</p>
      <p><strong>Note:</strong> Most platform skills are at Tier 2 (bundled) not Tier 3. Tier 3 is primarily for
        agent-authored codemode programs that need to import packages at runtime.</p>
    </div>

    <h4>Tier 4 — Browser (CF Browser Rendering)</h4>
    <div class="box box-am">
      <div class="box-lbl">Tier 4: Browser — Cloudflare Browser Rendering</div>
      <p><strong>Boot time:</strong> ~200ms (Chrome instance cold start). <strong>Cost:</strong> CF Browser Rendering
        billing (currently included in Workers plans up to certain limits). ~$0.002 per page load at scale.</p>
      <p><strong>Capabilities:</strong> Full Chrome browser. JavaScript execution on pages. DOM manipulation. Screenshot
        capture. Form filling. Cookie management. Network request interception. Everything Playwright can do.</p>
      <p><strong>When to use:</strong> browser_navigate, browser_click, browser_fill_form, browser_screenshot,
        browser_scrape for JS-rendered pages. Any page that requires JavaScript execution to render its content.</p>
      <p><strong>Critical implementation detail:</strong> The CDP proxy (naelao-browser Worker) runs as a Moltworker — a
        single persistent Worker that proxies CDP protocol messages to the CF Browser Rendering API. Agents never get
        direct CDP access. All browser automation goes through the proxy, which enforces security limits.</p>
    </div>
    <pre><code><span class="cm">// workers/browser/index.ts — CDP proxy for agents
// Agents call this via MCP tool, get HTML/screenshot back.
// They never touch CDP directly.</span>

export default {
  async fetch(request: Request, env: Env): Promise&lt;Response&gt; {
    const { action, url, selector, value, spaceId } = await request.json();

    <span class="cm">// Security: validate the URL is not a private/internal address</span>
    const parsedUrl = new URL(url);
    if (BLOCKED_IP_RANGES.some(p => p.test(parsedUrl.hostname))) {
      return Response.json({ error: 'Blocked: private IP address' }, { status: 403 });
    }
    if (parsedUrl.protocol !== 'https:' && parsedUrl.protocol !== 'http:') {
      return Response.json({ error: 'Only http/https URLs allowed' }, { status: 403 });
    }

    const browser = await puppeteer.launch(env.NAELAO_BROWSER);
    const page = await browser.newPage();

    try {
      await page.goto(url, { waitUntil: 'networkidle0', timeout: 30000 });

      let result: unknown;
      switch (action) {
        case 'get_content':
          result = {
            html: await page.content(),
            title: await page.title(),
            url: page.url()
          };
          break;
        case 'screenshot':
          const screenshot = await page.screenshot({ type: 'png', fullPage: false });
          result = { image: Buffer.from(screenshot).toString('base64'), mimeType: 'image/png' };
          break;
        case 'click':
          await page.click(selector);
          result = { success: true, clicked: selector };
          break;
        case 'fill':
          await page.type(selector, value);
          result = { success: true, filled: selector };
          break;
        case 'extract_text':
          const text = await page.evaluate(() => document.body.innerText);
          result = { text };
          break;
        default:
          return Response.json({ error: `Unknown action: ${action}` }, { status: 400 });
      }

      return Response.json({ success: true, result });
    } finally {
      await browser.close();
    }
  }
};</code></pre>

    <h4>Tier 5 — Sandbox (Full CF Container)</h4>
    <div class="box box-rd">
      <div class="box-lbl">Tier 5: Sandbox — Full Linux Container</div>
      <p><strong>Boot time:</strong> 2-3 seconds cold, &lt;100ms warm (after first start, stays warm for 10 minutes).
        <strong>Cost:</strong> CF Containers pricing (~$0.015/hr for standard-1, billed per-second). Most agent runs use
        &lt;5 minutes of container time.</p>
      <p><strong>Capabilities:</strong> Full Ubuntu Linux. Python 3.12 with pip. Node.js 22. Git. Any bash command. Any
        installed package. File access at /workspace (R2 mounted). Port exposure for dev servers.</p>
      <p><strong>When to use:</strong> execute_python, execute_bash, git_clone, install_package, run_jupyter,
        compile_code, generate_pdf. Any task that requires native binaries, system calls, or Python packages.</p>
      <p><strong>Cost optimization tips:</strong> (1) Check if Tier 1-4 can do the same thing first. (2) Batch multiple
        Tier 5 commands into one container session — container stays warm for 10 minutes. (3) Do file reads/writes in
        Tier 1 even if a container is running — R2 reads from Tier 1 don't require an exec() call.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Execution Ladder Router — Complete Implementation</h3>
    <pre><code><span class="cm">// agentpress/orchestrator.ts — complete routing logic
// This is called for every tool call the LLM emits.
// The router determines which tier handles each tool.</span>

export async function routeAndExecuteTools(
  toolCalls: ParsedToolCall[],
  context: ExecutionContext,
  env: Env
): Promise&lt;ToolResult[]&gt; {
  const orchestrator = new Orchestrator(env, context);

  <span class="cm">// Group tool calls by their required execution tier</span>
  const grouped = groupByTier(toolCalls);
  const results: ToolResult[] = [];

  <span class="cm">// Tier 1: Workspace — always parallel (pure I/O, no resource contention)</span>
  if (grouped.workspace?.length) {
    const t1Results = await Promise.all(
      grouped.workspace.map(tc =>
        orchestrator.wal.executeWithWAL(context.runId, tc.toolName, tc.parameters, () =>
          orchestrator.executeWorkspaceTool(tc)
        )
      )
    );
    results.push(...t1Results);
  }

  <span class="cm">// Tier 2 + 3: Isolate/npm — parallel for independent tools</span>
  const isolateTools = [...(grouped.isolate ?? []), ...(grouped.npm ?? [])];
  if (isolateTools.length) {
    <span class="cm">// Tools marked parallel=true can run concurrently</span>
    const parallelTools = isolateTools.filter(tc => TOOL_TIERS[tc.toolName]?.parallel !== false);
    const serialTools = isolateTools.filter(tc => TOOL_TIERS[tc.toolName]?.parallel === false);

    const t2Results = await Promise.all(
      parallelTools.map(tc =>
        orchestrator.wal.executeWithWAL(context.runId, tc.toolName, tc.parameters, () =>
          orchestrator.executeIsolateTool(tc)
        )
      )
    );
    results.push(...t2Results);

    for (const tc of serialTools) {
      const result = await orchestrator.wal.executeWithWAL(
        context.runId, tc.toolName, tc.parameters, () =>
          orchestrator.executeIsolateTool(tc)
      );
      results.push(result);
    }
  }

  <span class="cm">// Tier 4: Browser — serial (shared browser resource)</span>
  if (grouped.browser?.length) {
    for (const tc of grouped.browser) {
      const result = await orchestrator.wal.executeWithWAL(
        context.runId, tc.toolName, tc.parameters, () =>
          orchestrator.executeBrowserTool(tc)
      );
      results.push(result);
    }
  }

  <span class="cm">// Tier 5: Sandbox — ensure container running ONCE, then serial commands
  // DO NOT call ensureRunning() inside the loop — it would restart the container each time</span>
  if (grouped.sandbox?.length) {
    await orchestrator.ensureContainerRunning();
    for (const tc of grouped.sandbox) {
      const result = await orchestrator.wal.executeWithWAL(
        context.runId, tc.toolName, tc.parameters, () =>
          orchestrator.executeSandboxTool(tc)
      );
      results.push(result);
    }
  }

  return results;
}

<span class="cm">// Tool tier assignment — every platform tool mapped to its tier
// Junior dev: add your new tools here when you add them to the skill system</span>
export const TOOL_TIERS: Record&lt;string, { tier: ExecutionTier; parallel: boolean }&gt; = {
  <span class="cm">// Tier 1 — Workspace (R2 direct)</span>
  read_file:         { tier: 'workspace', parallel: true },
  write_file:        { tier: 'workspace', parallel: false }, <span class="cm">// writes are serial (lock needed)</span>
  list_directory:    { tier: 'workspace', parallel: true },
  delete_file:       { tier: 'workspace', parallel: false },
  update_todo:       { tier: 'workspace', parallel: false },

  <span class="cm">// Tier 2 — Isolate (Dynamic Worker)</span>
  web_search:        { tier: 'isolate', parallel: true },
  api_call:          { tier: 'isolate', parallel: true },
  render_artifact:   { tier: 'isolate', parallel: false },
  data_transform:    { tier: 'isolate', parallel: true },
  validate_json:     { tier: 'isolate', parallel: true },
  create_workflow:   { tier: 'isolate', parallel: false },
  get_weather:       { tier: 'isolate', parallel: true },

  <span class="cm">// Tier 4 — Browser (CF Browser Rendering)</span>
  browser_navigate:  { tier: 'browser', parallel: false },
  browser_click:     { tier: 'browser', parallel: false },
  browser_fill:      { tier: 'browser', parallel: false },
  browser_screenshot:{ tier: 'browser', parallel: false },
  browser_scrape:    { tier: 'browser', parallel: false },
  browser_extract:   { tier: 'browser', parallel: false },

  <span class="cm">// Tier 5 — Sandbox (CF Container)</span>
  execute_python:    { tier: 'sandbox', parallel: false },
  execute_bash:      { tier: 'sandbox', parallel: false },
  execute_node:      { tier: 'sandbox', parallel: false },
  git_clone:         { tier: 'sandbox', parallel: false },
  git_commit:        { tier: 'sandbox', parallel: false },
  install_package:   { tier: 'sandbox', parallel: false },
  generate_pdf:      { tier: 'sandbox', parallel: false },
  generate_pptx:     { tier: 'sandbox', parallel: false },
  run_tests:         { tier: 'sandbox', parallel: false },
  wrangler_deploy:   { tier: 'sandbox', parallel: false },
};</code></pre>
  </div>

