    <h2>Mini-AGI — From Jack Dorsey's Vision to Running Code</h2>
    <div class="bar"></div>
    <p class="lead">Jack Dorsey's insight: every company now has access to AI that can process, understand, and act on
      every piece of data it generates. The company that wires its internal data to an intelligence layer becomes a
      Mini-AGI — able to answer complex questions about itself, route decisions intelligently, and coordinate action
      across departments. This section implements that vision completely on Cloudflare.</p>

    <h3>The Mini-AGI Mental Model</h3>
    <p>Think of a company with three layers: (1) data scattered across CRM, ERP, Slack, email, documents; (2) employees
      who understand pieces of that data in isolation; (3) a CEO who needs to make decisions requiring cross-functional
      synthesis. A Mini-AGI is the intelligence layer that sits between the data and the decision-makers — it can answer
      "what's happening across the whole company right now?" in seconds, not weeks.</p>

    <div class="g3">
