  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     §50 — WHAT NAELAO IS NOT: ARCHITECTURAL CLARITY
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <div class="sep"></div>
  <div class="sec" id="what-naelao-is-not">
    <span class="sec-ey">50 — Architectural Clarity</span>
    <h2>What Naelao Is NOT — Preventing Architecture Drift</h2>
    <div class="bar"></div>
    <p class="lead">As a platform grows, new features get added in ways that violate the original design intent. This
      section documents what Naelao is not — the things that should never be built in Naelao the way they're described —
      to prevent architectural drift that creates technical debt, security vulnerabilities, and operational complexity.
    </p>

    <div class="g2">
      <div class="box box-rd">
        <div class="box-lbl">❌ Naelao Is NOT a Traditional SaaS</div>
        <p>Naelao does not have always-on application servers. There is no FastAPI process, no Node.js server, no EC2
          instance. If you find yourself wanting to add a "background worker process" or a "cron server," stop — use CF
          Cron Triggers, DO Alarms, or Dynamic Workflows instead. The entire platform is event-driven and serverless.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="box box-rd">
        <div class="box-lbl">❌ Naelao Is NOT a Single-Tenant Platform</div>
        <p>Every feature must work for multiple isolated tenants simultaneously. If you add a feature that requires a
          shared global state (a global counter, a global list, a global queue), you've introduced a cross-tenant
          surface area. Every new feature must carry a spaceId and every data access must be scoped to that spaceId. No
          exceptions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="box box-rd">
        <div class="box-lbl">❌ Agents Are NOT Always Running</div>
        <p>NaelaoAgentDO is not an always-on process. It wakes when a message arrives and sleeps between turns. Features
          that require "the agent is always watching" should use the Space Assistant (AssistantDO) instead — that's what
          it's for. Don't make agents continuously poll external services; use webhooks and channel integrations
          instead.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="box box-rd">
        <div class="box-lbl">❌ R2 Is NOT a Database</div>
        <p>R2 is object storage — files, not records. For structured data (user preferences, agent memory,
          configuration), use SpaceDO SQLite. For large files (documents, datasets, training files), use R2.
          Never try to implement relational queries on R2 keys — that's what SpaceDO SQLite is for. The correct question is
          always: "Is this a file or a record?"</p>
      </div>
      <div class="box box-rd">
        <div class="box-lbl">❌ Containers Are NOT the Default</div>
        <p>Container execution (Tier 5) is the slowest, most expensive, and most complex option. It should be the last
          resort, not the first choice. Before using a container, ask: Can this be done with a direct R2 operation (Tier
          1)? Can this be done in a Dynamic Worker (Tier 2)? Can this be done via CF Browser Rendering (Tier 4)? Only
          use a container when none of the lighter tiers can accomplish the task.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="box box-rd">
        <div class="box-lbl">❌ Service Bindings Are NOT fetch()</div>
        <p>Internal Worker-to-Worker calls use Service Bindings, not fetch(). If you write <span class="ic">await
            fetch('https://naelao-auth.workers.dev/validate')</span>, you're adding 5-50ms latency and paying for an
          external request. Write <span class="ic">await env.NAELAO_AUTH.fetch(...)</span> instead. This is not optional
          — it's a performance and cost requirement enforced by code review.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3>Architectural Drift Detection — Code Review Checklist</h3>
    <p>Every pull request should be checked against these questions:</p>
    <ol class="nl">
      <li>Does this feature add any always-on compute? If yes, refactor to event-driven.</li>
      <li>Does every new DB query include space_id via withSpace()? If not, fix before merge.</li>
      <li>Does any new Worker communicate with another Worker via fetch() instead of Service Binding? Fix it.</li>
      <li>Does this feature store structured data in R2 instead of SpaceDO SQLite? Move it to the right store.
      </li>
      <li>Does this feature require a container when Tier 1-4 would suffice? Refactor to a lower tier.</li>
      <li>Does any new DO use newUniqueId() for business data? Change to idFromName() with spaceId prefix.</li>
      <li>Does any new test run in Node.js instead of workerd? Move it to vitest-pool-workers.</li>
      <li>Does any new skill or agent-generated code skip the security scanner? Add scanner before any code runs.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     §51 — COMPLETE GLOSSARY
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <div class="sep"></div>
  <div class="sec" id="glossary">
    <span class="sec-ey">51 — Glossary</span>
    <h2>Naelao Glossary — Every Term Defined</h2>
    <div class="bar"></div>
    <p class="lead">A junior developer reading this document for the first time will encounter many terms that need
      precise definitions. This glossary defines every domain-specific term used in this specification.</p>

    <table class="t">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Term</th>
          <th>Definition</th>
          <th>Where Defined</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">AgentDO / NaelaoAgentDO</td>
          <td>The Cloudflare Durable Object that serves as an agent's "brain." Persistent, single-threaded, has built-in
            SQLite. One instance per (spaceId, projectId, threadId) combination. Zero idle cost via DO hibernation.</td>
          <td>§03</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">AgentPress</td>
          <td>The execution engine ported from Suna kortix (agentpress/ Python package). Handles: context building, XML
            parsing, tool orchestration, WAL, billing, and caching. Lives inside NaelaoAgentDO.</td>
          <td>§04</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">AssistantDO</td>
          <td>The Durable Object brain for Space Assistants. One per (spaceId, userId). Contains: session management,
            memory, channel configs, permission manifest, self-modification log. More capable than AgentDO — includes
            wallets and channels.</td>
          <td>§05</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">Bootstrap Mode</td>
          <td>The cold-start flywheel for Vertical Spaces. Expert annotators label edge cases → training data → LoRA
            fine-tuning via Together AI → domain-specific model → Autopilot mode. Named for the "pull yourself up by
            your bootstraps" self-funding loop.</td>
          <td>§12</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl">codemode</td>
