  <div class="sep"></div>
  <div class="sec" id="analytics">
    <span class="sec-ey">56 — naelao-analytics Deep Dive</span>
    <h2>Analytics Engine — All Analytics Events (Never Written to SpaceDO)</h2>
    <div class="bar"></div>
    <p class="lead">Naelao replaces all analytics tables from Suna kortix with Cloudflare Workers Analytics Engine. This
      gives structured event ingestion with SQL-queryable output at essentially zero cost. Every agent run, every tool
      call, every billing event, every error — structured, queryable, per-Space. This section documents the complete
      event schema and query patterns.</p>

    <h3>Why Workers Analytics Engine Instead of SpaceDO Tables</h3>
    <div class="g2">
      <div class="box box-or">
        <div class="box-lbl">Inline Analytics Tables — Old Pattern (Do Not Use)</div>
        <p>Suna kortix stores analytics in PostgreSQL tables: <span class="ic">agent_run_analytics</span>, <span
            class="ic">token_usage</span>, <span class="ic">conversation_metrics</span>. This creates write
          amplification on every agent action (every token usage = a DB write), fills storage quickly (1M agent runs =
          millions of rows), and requires expensive analytic queries on OLTP storage.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="box box-gr">
        <div class="box-lbl">CF Workers Analytics Engine (Naelao)</div>
        <p>Workers Analytics Engine is a time-series columnar store optimized for event ingestion and analytics queries.
          Writes are fire-and-forget (non-blocking). Queries use SQL against a columnar store (100x faster for
          aggregations). No storage cost beyond $0.25/million events above free tier. Perfect fit for event analytics.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3>Complete Event Schema</h3>
    <pre><code><span class="cm">// types/analytics-events.ts
// Every event type that flows through naelao-analytics-queue and into Analytics Engine.
// All events MUST include: spaceId, timestamp, type.
// All events SHOULD include: userId, agentId, threadId where relevant.</span>

export type NaelaoAnalyticsEvent =
  | AgentRunEvent
  | ToolExecutionEvent
  | TokenUsageEvent
  | ErrorEvent
  | BillingEvent
  | UserActionEvent
  | SecurityEvent
