    <h3>The Admin Health Dashboard</h3>
    <pre><code><span class="cm">// Workers Analytics Engine queries that power the admin health dashboard
// Accessible at: /_admin/health (CF Access protected)</span>

<span class="cm">// Last 1 hour: key platform metrics</span>
const PLATFORM_HEALTH_QUERY = `
  SELECT
    COUNT(CASE WHEN blob1 = 'agent_run_start' THEN 1 END) as runs_started,
    COUNT(CASE WHEN blob1 = 'agent_run_complete' THEN 1 END) as runs_completed,
    COUNT(CASE WHEN blob1 = 'agent_run_failed' THEN 1 END) as runs_failed,
    AVG(CASE WHEN blob1 = 'agent_run_complete' THEN double1 END) as avg_run_duration_ms,
    SUM(CASE WHEN blob1 = 'token_usage' THEN double5 END) as total_cost_usd,
    COUNT(CASE WHEN index2 LIKE 'security_%' THEN 1 END) as security_events,
    COUNT(CASE WHEN blob1 = 'error' AND double1 >= 3 THEN 1 END) as error_events
  FROM naelao_analytics
  WHERE timestamp > NOW() - INTERVAL '1 hour'
`;

<span class="cm">// Error rate by component — which Worker is failing?</span>
const ERROR_RATE_BY_COMPONENT = `
  SELECT
    index3 as component,
    COUNT(*) as total_events,
    COUNT(CASE WHEN blob1 = 'error' THEN 1 END) as errors,
    ROUND(100.0 * COUNT(CASE WHEN blob1 = 'error' THEN 1 END) / COUNT(*), 2) as error_rate_pct
  FROM naelao_analytics
  WHERE timestamp > NOW() - INTERVAL '1 hour'
  GROUP BY index3
  ORDER BY error_rate_pct DESC
  LIMIT 10
`;

<span class="cm">// LLM latency percentiles — model performance tracking</span>
const LLM_LATENCY_PERCENTILES = `
  SELECT
    blob2 as model,
    COUNT(*) as call_count,
    AVG(double1) as avg_ttft_ms,
    PERCENTILE_CONT(0.95) WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY double1) as p95_ttft_ms,
    PERCENTILE_CONT(0.99) WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY double1) as p99_ttft_ms
  FROM naelao_analytics
  WHERE blob1 = 'llm_response' AND timestamp > NOW() - INTERVAL '1 hour'
  GROUP BY model
`;

<span class="cm">// Top spending spaces — 24h cost breakdown</span>
const TOP_SPACES_BY_COST = `
  SELECT
    index1 as space_id,
    SUM(CASE WHEN blob1 = 'token_usage' THEN double5 ELSE 0 END) as total_cost_usd,
    COUNT(CASE WHEN blob1 = 'agent_run_start' THEN 1 END) as run_count
  FROM naelao_analytics
  WHERE timestamp > NOW() - INTERVAL '24 hours'
  GROUP BY index1
  ORDER BY total_cost_usd DESC
  LIMIT 20
`;

<span class="cm">// Security event timeline — detect attack patterns</span>
const SECURITY_EVENT_TIMELINE = `
  SELECT
    DATE_TRUNC('minute', timestamp) as minute,
    blob2 as event_type,
    COUNT(*) as count,
    COUNT(DISTINCT index1) as unique_spaces
  FROM naelao_analytics
  WHERE timestamp > NOW() - INTERVAL '1 hour'
    AND index2 LIKE 'security_%'
  GROUP BY 1, 2
  ORDER BY 1 DESC, 3 DESC
`;

<span class="cm">// Queue health — DLQ depth and processing rate</span>
const QUEUE_HEALTH = `
  SELECT
    blob2 as queue_name,
    COUNT(CASE WHEN blob1 = 'queue_message_sent'  THEN 1 END) as sent,
    COUNT(CASE WHEN blob1 = 'queue_message_ack'   THEN 1 END) as processed,
    COUNT(CASE WHEN blob1 = 'queue_message_retry' THEN 1 END) as retried,
    COUNT(CASE WHEN blob1 = 'queue_message_dlq'   THEN 1 END) as dead_lettered
  FROM naelao_analytics
  WHERE timestamp > NOW() - INTERVAL '1 hour'
  GROUP BY queue_name
`;</code></pre>

    <h3>Logpush Configuration — Exporting to External SIEM</h3>
    <p>For Enterprise Spaces with compliance requirements (HIPAA, SOC 2), CF Logpush streams all Worker logs to an
      external SIEM (Splunk, Datadog, S3). Configure once at the CF account level:</p>
    <pre><code><span class="cm"># CF Logpush to Datadog — run during initial account setup</span>
curl -X POST "https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/$CF_ACCOUNT_ID/logpush/jobs" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $CF_API_TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "name": "naelao-workers-logpush",
    "dataset": "workers_trace_events",
    "destination_conf": "datadog://https://http-intake.logs.datadoghq.com/api/v2/logs?header_DD-API-KEY='$DD_API_KEY'&ddsource=cloudflare&ddtags=env:prod,service:naelao",
    "logpull_options": "fields=Event,EventTimestampMs,Outcome,Logs,ScriptName&timestamps=rfc3339",
    "filter": "{\"where\":{\"and\":[{\"key\":\"ScriptName\",\"operator\":\"StartsWith\",\"value\":\"naelao-\"}]}}",
    "enabled": true
  }'</code></pre>

    <h3>On-Call Runbook — Top 5 Alert Responses</h3>
    <table class="t">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Alert</th>
          <th>Immediate Action</th>
          <th>Recovery</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl"><strong>High Agent Run Failure Rate</strong></td>
          <td>Check status.cloudflare.com for Container incidents. If containers are down: set
            <code>NAELAO_CONTAINER_DISABLED=1</code> in CF env vars — agents will reject container-tier tasks gracefully
            instead of hanging.</td>
          <td>When containers recover, remove the env var. Sweeper auto-retries queued runs.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl"><strong>Sweeper Not Running</strong></td>
          <td>CF Dashboard → Workers → naelao-sweeper → Triggers tab. If cron is missing, redeploy:
            <code>npx wrangler deploy</code>. Check Workers Logs for crash in the sweeper's main handler.</td>
          <td>Once running, abandoned runs clean up within 5 minutes (next sweeper cycle).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="tl"><strong>SpaceDO SQLite Performance Degradation</strong></td>
          <td>Check DO metrics in Cloudflare dashboard. For large products hitting DO SQLite limits (&gt;10GB), consider promoting sub-spaces to separate products. Run
            TOP_SPACES_BY_COST to check if one space is in a DB-hammering loop.</td>
          <td>If a workflow is causing the spike: <code>POST /_admin/workflows/{id}/pause</code>.</td>
        </tr>
