      <h3>The Content Agent Loop</h3>
      <p>The <code>content</code> loop differs from chat because the ultimate output is a file (Markdown) rather than a
        message sent to the user. It enforces a structured pipeline: Outline &rarr; Draft &rarr; SEO Review &rarr;
        Publish.</p>

      <pre><code><span class="cm">// agentpress/loops/content.ts</span>

export async function executeContentLoop(
  topic: string,
  agentDO: NaelaoAgentDO,
  env: Env
): Promise&lt;void&gt; {
  
  <span class="cm">// Stage 1: Research & Outline</span>
  const outlineResp = await agentDO.callLLM({
    messages: [{ role: 'user', content: `Research and outline a comprehensive article about: ${topic}` }],
    tools: [getToolDef('web_search')]
  });
  
  <span class="cm">// Stage 2: Drafting</span>
  <span class="cm">// Write the draft directly to the R2 workspace via Tier 1 operation</span>
  const draftResp = await agentDO.callLLM({
    messages: [
      { role: 'user', content: `Based on this outline, draft the article in Markdown: \n${outlineResp.content}` }
    ]
  });
  
  const filePath = `content/posts/drafts/${topic.replace(/\s+/g, '-')}.md`;
  await executeWorkspaceTool({
    toolName: 'write_file',
    parameters: { path: filePath, content: draftResp.content }
  }, agentDO.spaceId, agentDO.projectId);

  <span class="cm">// Stage 3: SEO Review (Self-Correction)</span>
  const seoReview = await agentDO.callLLM({
    messages: [{ role: 'user', content: `Review this draft for SEO best practices. Focus on headers, keyword density, and meta description. Suggest edits. \n\n${draftResp.content}` }]
  });

  <span class="cm">// Apply edits to the file</span>
  const finalContent = applyEdits(draftResp.content, seoReview.content);
  await executeWorkspaceTool({
    toolName: 'write_file',
    parameters: { path: filePath, content: finalContent }
  }, agentDO.spaceId, agentDO.projectId);

  <span class="cm">// Stage 4: Trigger CF Pages Deployment</span>
  <span class="cm">// The agent uses the `deploy-expose` skill to tell Cloudflare Pages to rebuild the site</span>
  await agentDO.executeTools([{
    toolName: 'trigger_pages_build',
    parameters: { commitMessage: `Auto-draft: ${topic}` }
  }]);
}</code></pre>

      <div class="box box-am">
        <div class="box-lbl">CF Pages Direct Integration</div>
        <p>Because the Sites manifest declares <code>externalPortal.deploymentType: 'cf-pages'</code>, the Naelao
          provisioner creates a real Cloudflare Pages project bound to this Space's R2 bucket. When the Agent writes
          Markdown to <code>spaces/{spaceId}/workspace/content/posts/</code> and calls <code>trigger_pages_build</code>,
          Cloudflare Pages pulls the R2 content, runs Astro/Next.js to build static HTML, and pushes it to the global
          edge network. This guarantees sub-millisecond TTFB for the public website, completely decoupled from Naelao's
          internal API latency.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

