        <span class="sec-ey">A6 — Public Surface</span>
        <h2>External Portals — {slug}.naelao.com &amp; Custom Domains</h2>
        <div class="bar"></div>
        <p class="lead">For Space Types like <code>Sites</code>, <code>Launchpad</code>, and <code>Workers</code>, the
          public-facing UI <em>is</em> the product. Naelao provisions a dedicated, zero-chrome public endpoint for every
          Space instance that declares <code>"externalPortal": { "enabled": true }</code> in its manifest. The agent can
          build and publish a live website, storefront, or API in a single turn — without the user ever seeing the
          Naelao management interface.</p>

        <h3>URL Structure</h3>
        <p>Every portal-enabled Space gets a subdomain on <code>naelao.app</code> derived from a user-chosen slug chosen
          at Space creation. Custom domains are supported via Cloudflare for SaaS:</p>

        <table class="t">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>URL Type</th>
              <th>Example</th>
              <th>How It Works</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td class="tl"><strong>Platform subdomain</strong></td>
              <td><code>my-shop.naelao.app</code></td>
              <td>Automatic. Provisioned when the Space is created. Immutable slug.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="tl"><strong>Custom domain</strong></td>
              <td><code>shop.mybrand.com</code></td>
              <td>User adds a CNAME pointing to <code>portal.naelao.app</code>. TXT verification required. SSL managed
                by CF for SaaS.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="tl"><strong>Preview URL</strong></td>
              <td><code>preview-{hash}.naelao.app</code></td>
              <td>Auto-generated for each agent deployment before it goes live. Expires in 24h.</td>
