          <div class="box box-am">
            <div class="box-lbl">Why We Don't Block on Credits Exhausted</div>
            <p>When <code>deductCredits()</code> finds insufficient balance, we mark the space and notify — but we don't
              block the current response. The agent already ran. Blocking it creates a terrible UX (the user's message
              is lost) without recovering any cost. The block happens on the <em>next</em> run's pre-flight check in
              <code>AgentDO.startRun()</code>. This separation of accounting from access control is intentional.</p>
          </div>

