          <h2>Appendix A10: Custom Durable Objects & the Security Scanner Pipeline</h2>
          <div class="bar"></div>
          <p class="lead">The eight built-in DO types handle the universal platform. But some Space Types need DOs with
            domain-specific state: a <strong>Launchpad</strong> space needs a <code>CartDO</code> that holds a
            customer's shopping cart for 30 minutes. A <strong>Verticals</strong> legal space needs a
            <code>CaseFileDO</code> tracking litigation status. A <strong>Sites</strong> space needs a
            <code>PublishLockDO</code> preventing two agents from writing to the same CMS slot simultaneously.</p>
          <p>This appendix defines: how manifests declare custom DOs; how the provisioner wires them; and the
            <strong>Security Scanner Pipeline</strong> — a required gate that every Space Type passes before entering
            the registry.</p>

          <h3>Declaring a Custom DO in a Manifest</h3>
