            <p>The kill switch is stored in KV. AgentDO checks
              <code>env.NAELAO_CONFIG_KV.get('emergency:kill-all-agents')</code> at the top of every LLM loop iteration.
              Because KV reads are ~1ms at the edge, this adds negligible latency. If the key is present and
              <code>active: true</code>, the agent immediately writes <code>status='emergency_halted'</code> to D1 and
              throws an <code>AgentEmergencyHaltError</code>, which the run loop catches to drain the WebSocket
              gracefully.</p>
