          <div class="box box-rd">
            <div class="box-lbl">⚠ Legal Callout — conversationLogAccess Is a Legally Significant Decision</div>
            <p><strong>This is not a simple boolean toggle.</strong> Whether a builder can read their end users'
              conversations has direct legal implications under GDPR Article 13, CCPA Section 1798.100, and potentially
              HIPAA and sector-specific regulations. The following requirements are mandatory.</p>
            <p><strong>1. Explicit Terms of Service disclosure.</strong> The product's Terms of Service must explicitly
              state that the builder or their designated admins may access conversation content. Vague language about
              "service improvement" is not sufficient.</p>
            <p><strong>2. Consent checkbox at signup.</strong> The user signup flow must include a dedicated checkbox —
              not bundled with the general Terms acceptance — that specifically mentions conversation access. This
              checkbox state is recorded in <code>product_users.conversation_access_consented</code> with a timestamp.
              If this column is false or null, builder-admin conversation access is blocked at the API level regardless
              of the product config flag.</p>
            <p><strong>3. Immutable audit trail.</strong> Every conversation access event by a builder-admin — every
              single one — must write an append-only record to CF Analytics Engine with: adminUserId, targetUserId,
              targetThreadId, accessTimestamp, IP address, justification (free text that admin must fill before access
              is granted). This cannot be disabled or batch-deleted.</p>
            <p><strong>4. Naelao-level policy gatekeeping.</strong> The <code>conversationLogAccess</code> flag can only
              be set to <code>true</code> if: (a) the builder's plan tier is Enterprise or higher, (b) the builder has
              acknowledged legal obligations in a separate checkbox during product setup, (c) a Naelao platform admin
              has manually reviewed and approved. Any attempt to enable this flag via the API without this approval
              chain returns HTTP 403: "conversationLogAccess requires platform-level approval. Submit a request at
              platform.naelao.app/access-review."</p>
            <p><strong>5. GDPR Article 13 compliance.</strong> At the time of data collection (signup), the builder must
              have informed users of: the identity of the data controller, the purposes of processing, the legal basis,
              the recipients, and the retention period. Naelao provides a template disclosure but the builder is legally
              responsible for its accuracy.</p>
