          <h3>Naelao Platform Aesthetic — Design System</h3>
          <p>The Naelao Platform and Builder Dashboard follow a deliberate design language: <strong>dark, precise,
              infrastructure-grade</strong>. Not consumer. Not playful. Not generic SaaS. The aesthetic communicates:
            this is serious infrastructure, and the numbers on this screen are real things in a real system.</p>

          <div class="box box-gr">
            <div class="box-lbl">Platform Aesthetic Principles — Non-Negotiable</div>
            <p><strong>Builder Dashboard:</strong> Dark theme (<code>#060D1A</code> base), monospace system values (DM
              Mono), orange accent (<code>#E8682A</code>), status badges using traffic-light colors,
              infrastructure-first information hierarchy. Identical to the aesthetic of this specification document. No
              purple gradients. No illustration libraries. No hero sections. Data tables, cards, code blocks, and
              precise metric displays only.</p>
            <p><strong>Product Shell templates:</strong> Neutral base, responsive to the builder's
              <code>brandColor</code>. Two template families: Chat-first (for builder products targeting consumer AI or chat use cases — Team space type) and
              Workspace-first (Developer, Verticals). Both professionally designed but intentionally unopinionated — the
              builder's branding is the dominant visual identity, not Naelao's.</p>
            <p><strong>The contrast is intentional.</strong> The Builder Dashboard looks like a well-designed technical
              document made interactive — because that is what it is. Builder products look like their own products —
              because that is what they are. Naelao's aesthetic never bleeds through into builder products. That is the
              promise of the platform.</p>
          </div>

          <h3>What Builders Never See — The Infrastructure That Runs Their Products</h3>
          <p>The Builder Dashboard deliberately hides: raw credit costs (builders see credits consumed, not CF compute
            costs in dollars), infrastructure topology (no DO instance IDs, no Worker names, no KV namespace IDs
            exposed), other builders' products and users (the entire API is scoped to the authenticated builderId), and
            Naelao's internal tooling and platform configuration. A builder building a legal AI product never needs to
            think about Cloudflare at all. They think about their product, their users, and their pricing. Naelao thinks
            about everything else.</p>

          <p>This is the same relationship a merchant has with Shopify: they configure their store, manage their
            products, and run their marketing. They never interact with Stripe's infrastructure even though Stripe
            processes every payment. The infrastructure is invisible by design. Its invisibility is not an accident — it
            is the product.</p>

        </div>


