          <div class="bar"></div>

          <p class="lead">Studio is the space type for people and teams that produce creative output professionally:
            writers, designers, video producers, musicians, marketers, and creative agencies. Where Launchpad automates
            a <em>business</em>, Studio automates a <em>production pipeline</em>. The agents are not customer-facing —
            they are collaborators in a craft. Studio is the answer to the question: what does an AI-native creative
            tool look like when the infrastructure is serious?</p>

          <div class="pull">"Launchpad runs a business with zero employees. Studio runs a production line with zero
            junior staff."</div>

          <div class="box box-pu">
            <div class="box-lbl">Why Studio Is a Separate Space Type — Not a Launchpad Template</div>
            <p>Launchpad's execution model is fulfillment: a customer order arrives, agents deliver a product, owner
              reviews. Studio's execution model is iterative production: a brief arrives, agents produce a draft, the
              creative director revises, agents incorporate feedback, the cycle repeats. The approval model is different.
              The knowledge base is different (brand guidelines, style references, past work, tone documents). The output
              artifacts are different (files, not messages). The billing model is different (project-scoped credit
              consumption, not per-order). A Studio Space cannot be reduced to a Launchpad template without losing its
              core execution model. It requires its own space type manifest, its own agent definitions, and its own UI
              layout — the <strong>Production Board</strong>.</p>
          </div>

