          <h3>The Production Board — Studio's Core UI</h3>
          <p>Studio replaces the thread-first layout of Team and Developer spaces with the
            <strong>Production Board</strong>: a Kanban-style project view where each card is a creative brief. Cards
            move through stages: <code>Brief → In Production → Review → Approved → Published</code>. The agent thread
            for each card is accessible from a slide-over panel — it's not the primary view, it's the audit trail.
            What the creative director sees first is the artifact: the draft, the asset, the script. Not the
            conversation that produced it.</p>

