          <div class="box box-bl">
            <div class="box-lbl">Studio vs Launchpad — The Decision Boundary</div>
            <p>If the end user is a <strong>customer receiving a deliverable</strong> → Launchpad. The agent serves the
              customer. The owner reviews before the customer sees it.</p>
            <p>If the end user is a <strong>creative professional producing a deliverable</strong> → Studio. The agent
              is a collaborator in the production process. The creative professional and the agent are on the same team,
              not in a vendor/customer relationship. The output goes to a client or channel outside the Space — not to
              the end user who is working inside the Space.</p>
            <p style="margin-top:8px;font-size:13px;color:var(--mt);">Ambiguous case: a solo creator selling custom
              content (e.g., ghostwriting). If they review every artifact and their client never logs in → Studio.
              If their client receives auto-generated output via a portal with their client's logo → Launchpad with a
              Studio-like template. The sub-space-to-product promotion path exists precisely for when this outgrows
              a template.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

