          <h2>Temples — Pre-Built Products on the Naelao Platform</h2>
          <div class="bar"></div>

          <p class="lead">A Temple is a fully configured, ready-to-launch NaelaoProduct. Where the Create Product
            Wizard gives a builder a blank Space and a configuration form, a Temple gives them a complete product:
            agents pre-installed, knowledge base structure defined, UI configured, pricing suggested, and a working
            demo they can explore before committing. Temples are to Naelao what Shopify themes are to Shopify — except
            a Temple includes the business logic, not just the visual design.</p>

          <div class="box box-am">
            <div class="box-lbl">Architectural Position of Temples</div>
            <p>A Temple is not a separate infrastructure concept. It is a <strong>snapshot of a fully configured
              NaelaoProduct</strong> — a serialized combination of: a NaelaoProduct record (with space type, auth
              config, pricing config, feature flags, user permissions), an agent definition bundle (the specific agents
              pre-installed into the Space), a knowledge base schema (which document types are expected, which are
              required), and a UI extension set (any custom views or components the builder needs to install on top of
              the product shell). When a builder selects a Temple, the platform executes the same
              <code>POST /builder/products</code> flow as the manual wizard — but pre-populated from the Temple
              snapshot. The builder reviews, adjusts pricing and branding, and launches. No new infrastructure
              primitive is introduced. Temples are configuration, not code.</p>
          </div>

