          <p>postMessage Origin Allowlist — Shell Validates App Messages But Apps Never Validate Shell Messages The Operator Shell uses a `postMessage` protocol between the host shell (`app.naelao.dev`) and injected app iframes (`ui.naelao.app`). The spec shows the message type contract but does not show origin validation in the receiving iframe. The shell sends `CONTEXT`, `TOKEN_REFRESH`, and `THEME_CHANGE` messages to the iframe. If the iframe does not validate that `event.origin === 'https://app.naelao.dev'`, a malicious third-party page that embeds the app iframe can spoof these messages and inject a fake `TOKEN_REFRESH` payload with a forged JWT, granting the app iframe access to the malicious…</p>
