      <div id="G-SEC-07" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;margin-bottom:6px;">
          <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);background:rgba(232,105,42,.12);padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;">G-SEC-07</span>
          <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;">Path Validation — '..' and Absolute Paths Checked Only in Skill Description, Not At Runtime</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="box box-rd">
          <div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
          <p>Path Validation — '..' and Absolute Paths Checked Only in Skill Description, Not At Runtime The file-manager SKILL.md says: "IMPORTANT: All paths are relative to /workspace. Do NOT use absolute paths or paths starting with /. Do NOT use '..' in paths." This is a guideline in the skill description, but there is no runtime validation. An agent could call `read_file('/etc/passwd')` or `read_file('../../../etc/passwd')` and the skill would attempt to execute the request without checking. The SpaceR2 helper might still prevent access (if it prefixes with `spaces/{spaceId}/workspace/`), but the path validation relies on implicit string concatenation, not explicit validation.</p>
