          <div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
          <p>Memory Context Injection — Max 20 Items; Older Memories Silently Discarded Without Archival The buildMemoryContext() function limits memory to 20 items: `memory.slice(0, 20)`. When an agent has more than 20 memories, the oldest ones are discarded from the prompt without any archival or notification. The agent won't know about these memories and can't access them. Over time, important memories (like "user's preferred coding style" or "previous project decisions") are lost silently. The 20-item limit is arbitrary and not tunable.</p>
