          <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);background:rgba(232,105,42,.12);padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;">G-SEC-09</span>
          <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;">Skill 27-Pattern Scanner — Detects Obvious `process.env.` Patterns; Misses Obfuscated Variants</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="box box-rd">
          <div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
          <p>Skill 27-Pattern Scanner — Detects Obvious `process.env.` Patterns; Misses Obfuscated Variants The launch checklist requires "27-pattern skill scanner active for all unverified skills." The scanner is mentioned but not implemented in the spec. Assuming it scans for patterns like `process.env.`, `require('`, `import('`, it catches obvious attempts to access secrets or execute code. However, it can be bypassed by obfuscation: `process['en' + 'v']`, `({}).constructor.prototype` (to access global), `atob('...')` to decode shell commands. The scanner would miss these obfuscated patterns.</p>
