          <p>Audit Query SQL Injection — Unparameterized Event Type Filter The audit query endpoint constructs a SQL query with string interpolation: `AND blob1 = '${eventType}'`. The eventType comes from the query parameter and is not parameterized. An attacker could pass `eventType = "token_usage' OR blob1 = '"` to bypass the filter and retrieve audit logs from all event types, including security events and wallet transactions they shouldn't see. This is a classic SQL injection vulnerability.</p>
