          <p>Webhook Secret Validation — No Rotation Or Expiry; Compromised Secrets Never Invalidated Webhook secrets are stored in naelao-credentials and fetched on each webhook verification. Once set, they never expire or rotate. If a webhook secret is exposed (e.g., logged in an error message, leaked via a developer's GitHub repo), an attacker can forge valid webhooks indefinitely. There is no mechanism to rotate or expire the secret. A developer would have to manually generate a new secret in the UI and update the third-party provider's webhook configuration.</p>
