        <div class="box box-rd">
          <div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
          <p>Portal Slug Uniqueness — 30s TTL Lock Not Sufficient; Race Allocates Duplicate Slugs Slug reservation uses a KV lock with 30s TTL: `await env.PORTAL_ROUTES.put(\`slug-lock:${slug}\`, spaceId, { expirationTtl: 30 })`. Between the KV write and the return, two concurrent provisioning requests could both succeed at writing the lock. KV puts are eventually consistent in some Cloudflare configs, or the TTL could expire between the check and the write. Once provisioned, both Spaces would have the same slug. When a user visits the portal, it's ambiguous which Space to serve. The custom domain mapping breaks.</p>
