        <div class="box box-rd">
          <div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
          <p>Product Slug Uniqueness — No UNIQUE Constraint; Concurrent Creates Can Allocate Duplicate Slugs Product slugs are required to be unique (`slug TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE` in the schema), but the creation flow generates the slug in the application code and inserts it. Between the generation and the insert, two concurrent requests could generate the same slug (e.g., both hash the product name to "lexspace", both try to insert). The first INSERT succeeds, the second fails with a constraint violation. However, if the constraint isn't enforced or the application doesn't validate the slug upfront, duplicate slugs could be inserted. The constraint is there, but the error handling might swallow the…</p>
