          <p>x402 AI Crawler Payment Gate — No Rate Limiting; Attackers Can Exhaust Wallet Via Repeated 402 Responses The x402 payment middleware on the Sites CF Pages deployment checks for a payment header and returns 402 Payment Required if missing. Each 402 response is routed through the wallet credit endpoint. There is no rate limiting on the 402 handler. An attacker can make thousands of requests to the same Sites page without the payment header, triggering thousands of 402 responses and wallet-credit attempts. These requests could: (a) exhaust the API rate limit quota if the wallet endpoint is rate-limited; (b) if not rate-limited, accumulate zero-amount credits in the wallet transaction log,…</p>
