          <p>Required Fix Add rate limiting to the 402 handler: e.g., max 10 requests per IP per minute. Return 429 Too Many Requests after the limit. Batch the wallet credit calls: don't call wallet-credit for every 402 response. Queue them and process in bulk every 5 minutes. Cache the 402 response for 30 seconds per IP + User-Agent combination to avoid repeated requests from the same crawler in the same minute. Severity: Medium — Attackers can flood the 402 handler and wallet credit endpoint. Legitimate crawler payments could fail under attack due to exhausted rate limits or unavailable wallet endpoint. T-144 — Skills System</p>
