      <div id="G-OPE-02" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;margin-bottom:6px;">
          <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);background:rgba(232,105,42,.12);padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;">G-OPE-02</span>
          <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;">Global Rate Limiting — No Ingress Protection, Noisy Neighbour Possible</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="box box-rd">
          <div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
          <p>Global Rate Limiting — No Ingress Protection, Noisy Neighbour Possible The spec specifies per-space AI Gateway rate limits but has no global ingress rate limiting at the naelao-router layer. A single product receiving a sudden traffic spike — a launch-day surge, a DDoS, or a misconfigured client sending in a loop — can exhaust Cloudflare Workers request budget and increase latency for every other product on the platform simultaneously. This is the noisy neighbour problem. It is not hypothetical: it is the first production incident category for every multi-tenant platform. The Three Missing Rate Limit Layers Layer What It Limits Current State Required Global ingress (per product) HTTP…</p>
        </div>
        <div class="box box-gr" style="margin-top:12px;">
          <div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
          <p>-RateLimit-Limit: {limit} // + X-RateLimit-Reset: {nextWindowTimestamp} Infinite Tool Loop — The Missing Hard Stop The AgentDO orchestrator loop has no maximum iteration count. An agent that enters a tool-call loop (calls tool A, gets result, decides to call tool A again, indefinitely) will run until it exhausts the builder's credit balance. The spec has no hard stop. Required: a per-turn tool call counter (max 50) and a per-run wall-clock timeout (max 10 minutes for isolate tier, 30 minutes for container tier) after which the run is marked 'cancelled' and the user is notified. Gap T-45 — High</p>
        </div>
        <pre style="background:var(--bg3);border:1px solid var(--brd);border-radius:8px;padding:16px;overflow-x:auto;margin-top:12px;"><code style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--cy);line-height:1.6;">// naelao-router: KV token bucket rate limiting per productId
// Simple sliding window — 1000 req/min per product (configurable per tier)

async function checkRateLimit(productId: string, env: Env): Promise&lt;boolean&gt; {
  const key = `rl:${productId}:${Math.floor(Date.now() / 60000)}`; // 1-min window
  const current = await env.NAELAO_CONFIG_KV.get(key);
  const count = current ? parseInt(current) : 0;

  const limits: Record&lt;string, number&gt; = {
    starter: 200, growth: 1000, scale: 5000, enterprise: 20000
  };
  const tier = await getProductTier(productId, env); // cached in KV
  const limit = limits[tier] ?? 200;

  if (count &gt;= limit) return false; // rate limited

  // Increment atomically — KV doesn&#x27;t support atomic increment
  // Use DO for true atomicity in high-traffic scenarios
  await env.NAELAO_CONFIG_KV.put(key, String(count + 1), { expirationTtl: 120 });
  return true;
}

// Response when rate limited:
// HTTP 429 + Retry-After: 60 + X-RateLimit-Limit: {limit}
// + X-RateLimit-Reset: {nextWindowTimestamp}</code></pre>
