          <p>Unhandled Errors — Fallthrough Default; Agents Never Know What Failed The error processor has a 30+ case switch with patterns for known error types. At the end, there is an implicit fallthrough: if an error doesn't match any pattern, a generic message is returned: `agentMessage: "Unknown error occurred. Check the logs."`. This is unhelpful to the agent. A tool fails with a custom error message from a third-party API that the error processor doesn't recognize. The agent has no context about what failed and no way to self-correct. The logs are only visible to platform engineers, not to the agent or user.</p>
