        <div class="box box-rd">
          <div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
          <p>Compensation Race — Async Cleanup Can Fail; Partial Rollbacks Leave Orphans The compensation log stores async cleanup functions. When provisioning fails, they are replayed in reverse: `for (const rollback of [...compLog].reverse()) { await rollback().catch(...) }`. Each rollback is awaited, but errors are caught and logged. If a rollback fails (e.g., R2 deletion times out, DO destroy request fails), the loop continues. The Space ends up partially provisioned: some DOs were destroyed, some R2 objects remain, the SpaceDO row was deleted but the KV slug lock expired. The user sees "provisioning failed", but behind the scenes, there are orphaned resources that Naelao pays for.</p>
