          <div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
          <p>Required Fix Use a CF Workflow for provisioning, not a single Worker request. Each compensation step is checkpointed. If a rollback fails, the Workflow retries it until it succeeds, rather than continuing and leaving orphans. Or, implement a "garbage collection" cron job that periodically scans for orphaned DOs and R2 prefixes and cleans them up. Log every failed rollback to an alerting system so ops can manually intervene. Severity: Medium — Async rollbacks can fail. Failed compensation steps are logged but not retried. Orphaned resources left behind increase storage costs. T-178 — Provisioner</p>
