          <p>Lifecycle Hooks — No Timeout Or Failure Recovery; Hook Hang Blocks Entire Provisioning Lifecycle hooks (onProvision, onDeprovision) are called synchronously within provisioning steps: `await provisionExternalPortal(...)`. If a hook hangs (makes an HTTP request that never completes, gets stuck in an infinite loop), the entire provisioning is blocked. There is no timeout. The user's browser times out waiting for the Space to be created, but behind the scenes, the provisioner is still waiting for the hook. The Space may be partially provisioned (DOs created, R2 seeded) but the UI never confirms success. A subsequent deprovision attempt would be triggered manually, adding to the orphan problem.</p>
