        <div class="box box-gr" style="margin-top:12px;">
          <div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
          <p>Required Fix Add a timeout to hook execution: `await Promise.race([hookPromise, timeoutPromise])`. If a hook times out, treat it as a recoverable failure and continue provisioning (don't block). Or, invoke hooks asynchronously via a queue (naelao-lifecycle-queue) so provisioning returns immediately. Hooks run in the background. Log hook execution time and failures. Alert on timeouts so the ops team can investigate. Severity: Medium — Lifecycle hooks have no timeout. A hanging hook blocks entire provisioning indefinitely. No recovery mechanism. User sees no response. T-180 — naelao-spaces Worker</p>
