          <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;">Space Hierarchy Depth Check — Race Between Recursive Query And Parent Deletion</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="box box-rd">
          <div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
          <p>Space Hierarchy Depth Check — Race Between Recursive Query And Parent Deletion When creating a sub-space, naelao-spaces runs a recursive CTE query to check the depth of the parent space. If the depth is &gt;= 3, creation is rejected. Between the depth check and the INSERT, another request could delete the parent space or change its parent. The depth check becomes stale. A Space could be created with a parent that no longer exists, violating the hierarchy constraint. Alternatively, two concurrent creates could pass the depth check and both succeed, resulting in a space tree deeper than 3 levels.</p>
