          <p>Required Fix Use a transaction with SELECT...FOR UPDATE on the parent space row to lock it during the depth check and insert: `SELECT * FROM spaces WHERE id = ? FOR UPDATE`. Or, add a CHECK constraint at the database level that enforces the depth limit: CHECK (depth . Let the database reject violations atomically. Verify parent existence in the same transaction before allowing the insert. Severity: Medium — Depth check is not atomic. Parent space can be deleted between check and insert. Concurrent creates can bypass depth limit. T-181 — naelao-spaces Worker</p>
