          <p>Notification Batch Failure — Promise.all() Blocks All Deliveries If Any Channel Fails The processNotification() function uses `Promise.all(deliveries)` to send across all requested channels (email, push, voice). If one channel fails (e.g., Resend email API is down), the entire Promise.all() rejects and the whole function throws. The message is retried. However, if the email API is temporarily down but push is working, the user still gets the push notification but the retry waits for email to recover. Meanwhile, subsequent notifications queue up. The idempotency lock prevents double-delivery only AFTER a successful send, so partial failures leave the system in an inconsistent state.</p>
