          <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;">Domain Classifier LLM — Called Every Query, No Cache; Hallucinates Domain IDs Outside Access</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="box box-rd">
          <div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
          <p>Domain Classifier LLM — Called Every Query, No Cache; Hallucinates Domain IDs Outside Access The `query()` method calls an LLM on every question to classify which data domains the question needs. The LLM is given the list of available domains. However: (a) there is no caching — identical questions are reclassified every time, wasting tokens; (b) the LLM can hallucinate and return domain IDs that don't exist in the available list; (c) the spec does not validate that the returned domain IDs are real — it just uses them directly in the `checkAccess()` call. An attacker or confused user could craft a question that tricks the LLM into returning a domain ID it shouldn't access, and if that domain…</p>
        </div>
        <div class="box box-gr" style="margin-top:12px;">
          <div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
          <p>Required Fix Cache domain classifications per question. Store: `{ question_hash → [domain_ids, timestamp] }`. Reuse for identical or similar questions (use semantic similarity, not exact match). After the LLM returns domain IDs, validate each ID against the actual domains table . Filter out hallucinated IDs. If the user's question requires a domain that doesn't exist in this Mini-AGI, mention that in the response. Add a debug flag to the response: which domains were classified vs which were available vs which were denied. This helps identify LLM hallucination in logs. Severity: Medium — LLM can hallucinate domain IDs. Every query pays the cost of a fresh LLM call. Hallucinations are hidden behind generic access denial. T-142 — Space Assistants</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="G-MIS-12" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;margin-bottom:6px;">
