<div style="margin:48px 0 0;padding:24px 0 0;border-top:1px solid #1E293B;">
  <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">CRITICAL SEVERITY — 6 GAPS</span>
</div>

<div id="G-F01" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F01</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">ConcurrencyDO</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">ConcurrencyDO Alarm Contention — Noisy-Neighbour Starvation Under Burst Load</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">ConcurrencyDO uses a single ctx.storage.setAlarm() to sweep stale runs. Every active run in a space hits the same DO, and a single space with many concurrent runs keeps the alarm firing continuously, starving the alarm handler of time to process heartbeat checks for other spaces sharing the same Cloudflare account&#x27;s alarm concurrency budget. With thousands of spaces each having a ConcurrencyDO, a burst of concurrent agents (e.g., a viral Launchpad product) can cause alarm queue backup across the entire platform.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Key ConcurrencyDOs by {spaceId} and enforce a platform-level MAX_CONCURRENT_AGENT_RUNS_PER_SPACE hard cap before reserving a slot, preventing any single space from exhausting the alarm budget. Implement exponential backoff on alarm rescheduling when no stale runs are found. Monitor ConcurrencyDO.alarm() latency via Analytics Engine — alert when P99 exceeds 500ms.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F02" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F02</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">WalletDO</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">No Platform-Level Daily Spending Cap — Runaway Agent Can Exhaust Credits Without Ceiling</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The spec defines per-space monthly_budget and max_single_spend policies in WalletDO, but these are builder-configurable defaults, not platform-enforced hard ceilings. An agent in an infinite loop calls deductCredits() on every LLM turn. Blocking happens on the next run&#x27;s pre-flight, not mid-run — meaning an in-flight loop burns balance unchecked. There is no platform-level absolute ceiling (e.g. $500/day/space) that Naelao enforces independent of builder policy.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add PLATFORM_DAILY_CREDIT_CEILING_USD (e.g. $500) enforced in WalletDO.deductCredits() independent of builder policy. Track daily_spent in the wallet table, reset at UTC midnight via DO alarm. If daily_spent + amount &gt; PLATFORM_CEILING, reject with { success: false, reason: &#x27;platform_daily_limit_exceeded&#x27; } and emit a security_rate_limit analytics event. naelao-sweeper should scan for wallets with daily_spent &gt; 0.8 * CEILING and alert ops.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F03" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F03</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">SpaceDO / naelao-auth</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">No Negative Auth-Result Caching — Banned User Can DoS SpaceDO with Auth Stampede</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">SpaceDO.authCheck() explicitly avoids caching negative lookups to allow fast invite propagation. This means every rejected request from a banned or uninvited user performs a full recursive CTE query against SpaceDO SQLite. A single banned user making 100 requests/second generates 100 recursive CTE queries per second against the SpaceDO for that product. Since SpaceDO is single-threaded, this serialises all auth checks for all users of that product, making it effectively unavailable during the attack.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Cache negative auth results in DO memory with a 30-second TTL (fast enough for invite propagation). Key: deny:{userId}:{spaceId}. On invalidateUser() call, clear both positive and negative cache entries. Add a per-IP rate limit (from CF-Connecting-IP header) upstream in naelao-auth: max 20 auth attempts per IP per 10 seconds stored in NAELAO_CIRCUIT_KV, returning HTTP 429 before the SpaceDO is ever contacted.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F04" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F04</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-workflows / Dynamic Workflow</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Workflow SpaceId Binding Is Not Cryptographically Verified — Tenant Code Execution Forgery</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The workflow loader reads event.payload.spaceId to determine which R2 path (spaces/{spaceId}/workflows/{name}.ts) to load. If an attacker forges the spaceId field in a CF Workflow event payload (e.g. via queue message injection), the loader executes another tenant&#x27;s workflow code under the attacker&#x27;s credentials. The validation is only a string equality check on untrusted input with no cryptographic binding between the loaded R2 code and the requesting spaceId.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Before loading workflow code from R2, verify spaceId against the user&#x27;s JWT via SpaceDO.authCheck(). Additionally, store a HMAC of {spaceId}:{workflowName}:{createdAt} in WorkflowRegistryDO at registration time and verify it matches before code execution. This creates a two-factor check — string equality + cryptographic binding — that cannot be forged without access to NAELAO_JWT_SECRET.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F05" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F05</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">LocalTunnelDO</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Pending Tool-Call Resolve Functions Stored in JS Map — Lost on DO Eviction, Agent Hangs Forever</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">LocalTunnelDO.execOnLocal() stores resolve functions in this.pendingCalls (a JS Map) with a 30-second setTimeout. If the DO is evicted before the local agent responds, the pendingCalls Map is destroyed. When the DO is recreated, the local agent&#x27;s response arrives as a WebSocket message but this.pendingCalls.get(callId) returns undefined. The AgentDO is waiting on a Promise that will never resolve — a silent hang that the sweeper won&#x27;t detect for 5 minutes.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Persist pending call state in ctx.storage.sql with columns (call_id, agent_run_id, started_at, timeout_ms). In webSocketMessage(), check the DB first. Use ctx.storage.setAlarm() instead of setTimeout — alarms survive DO eviction, setTimeout does not. In alarm(), sweep expired pending calls and resolve them with a timeout error, triggering WAL-based recovery in AgentDO.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F06" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F06</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-credentials</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Static NAELAO_INTERNAL_TOKEN Allows Cross-Space Credential Exfiltration if Any Worker Is Compromised</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">NAELAO_INTERNAL_TOKEN is a static secret shared across all Workers. If any Workflow template or Dynamic Worker can call the credentials endpoint with this token via direct fetch(), it bypasses Service Binding isolation. Compromise of any one Worker exposes all credentials for all spaces. The token has no per-request expiry, no spaceId binding, and no audit trail.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Replace NAELAO_INTERNAL_TOKEN for credential access with a short-lived, per-request HMAC signed with NAELAO_JWT_SECRET that includes {spaceId}:{agentId}:{timestamp} and expires in 60 seconds. The credentials Worker must verify HMAC signature and timestamp freshness before returning any credential. Disallow fetching credentials for any spaceId not matching the HMAC-embedded spaceId, preventing horizontal access between spaces.</p></div>
</div>

<div style="margin:48px 0 0;padding:24px 0 0;border-top:1px solid #1E293B;">
  <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">HIGH SEVERITY — 13 GAPS</span>
</div>

<div id="G-F07" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F07</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">NaelaoAgentDO / SQLite</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Missing Index on run_wal(run_id, status) — O(n) Full Table Scan on Every Fiber Recovery</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">onFiberRecovered() queries run_wal to find pending tool calls for a given run_id. The schema only has a primary key on id (the WAL entry UUID). A query like SELECT * FROM run_wal WHERE run_id = ? AND status = &#x27;pending&#x27; performs a full table scan. An agent that has run 10,000 tool calls will have 10,000 WAL rows. Recovery after DO eviction takes O(n) time proportional to total WAL history, which can exceed the CPU limit for long-running agents.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_wal_run_status ON run_wal(run_id, status) in initSchema(). Also add CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_wal_started_at ON run_wal(started_at) to support the sweeper&#x27;s cleanup query. Add a WAL compaction step that deletes rows older than 7 days where status IN (&#x27;complete&#x27;, &#x27;failed&#x27;), preventing unbounded table growth.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F08" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F08</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">SpaceDO / naelao-billing</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Billing Schema Split-Brain — space_credits Specified in Both PostgreSQL Migration and SpaceDO SQLite</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Section §22 shows space_credits and token_usage as PostgreSQL RLS-backed tables in migration 0012_billing_schema.sql. But the architecture simultaneously states &#x27;no external PostgreSQL — data layer is SpaceDO SQLite per product&#x27;. naelao-billing Worker code calls db.query() with $1/$2 parameterization (PostgreSQL syntax) against what appears to be Hyperdrive. This is a fundamental contradiction — the billing schema exists in two specified backends simultaneously, and a developer implementing this will create a split-brain billing system.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Explicitly declare that space_credits and token_usage live exclusively in SpaceDO SQLite. Remove all db.query() calls in naelao-billing that touch these tables and replace them with spaceDO.deductCredits() and spaceDO.recordTokenUsage() typed methods. Remove all PostgreSQL migration files for billing tables from the spec. Add a CI test: &#x27;billing Worker never imports or references a Hyperdrive/D1 binding&#x27;.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F09" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F09</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">Artifact Worker</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Template Literal Interpolation in wrapArtifactCode() — Backtick Injection Escapes to Dynamic Worker Code</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">For the React artifact type, user-controlled code is interpolated as ${code} directly into the worker body without escaping, inside a template literal for the HTML string. A React artifact containing backtick or ${...} sequences in string literals or comments will break out of the template context, potentially executing arbitrary code in the Dynamic Worker serving the artifact, which runs under naelao-artifact Worker&#x27;s permissions.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Never use template literal interpolation for user-controlled code in wrapArtifactCode(). Store the code string as a base64-encoded constant and decode at runtime: const userCode = atob(&#x27;${btoa(code)}&#x27;). For React artifacts, use a code-splitting approach: store the component code in R2 and import via await import(r2SignedUrl) rather than inlining into the harness. The code scanner should reject artifacts containing ${...} outside of string literals.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F10" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F10</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">wrangler.jsonc / Portal router</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">NAELAO_PORTAL_ROUTES KV Binding Absent from wrangler.jsonc — Portal Routing Broken at Deploy</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The portal router uses env.PORTAL_ROUTES — a KV namespace binding that appears in portal code but is absent from the wrangler.jsonc spec. Only three KV namespaces are declared: NAELAO_CONFIG_KV, NAELAO_CIRCUIT_KV, and NAELAO_ARTIFACT_KV. If portal keys are stored in NAELAO_CONFIG_KV as a fallback, a space with slug &#x27;skill-signature&#x27; creates a key colliding with the skill signature key pattern. Portal routing will throw &#x27;binding not found&#x27; on first deploy.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add { &#x27;binding&#x27;: &#x27;NAELAO_PORTAL_ROUTES&#x27;, &#x27;id&#x27;: &#x27;YOUR_PORTAL_ROUTES_KV_ID&#x27; } to kv_namespaces in wrangler.jsonc. Update all portal router and provisioner code to use env.NAELAO_PORTAL_ROUTES exclusively. Document the key namespace for each KV binding in a spec section. Add a CI test that verifies no KV binding writes a key matching another binding&#x27;s prefix pattern.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F11" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F11</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">R2 / naelao-workspace</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">R2 Object Versioning Not Enabled — Partial Writes Silently Destroy Live File Content</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The spec uses R2 for the agent filesystem and version history. However, R2 object versioning (CF&#x27;s built-in feature, distinct from the app-level .versions/ folder) is never mentioned as enabled. Without it, a partial write (connection drop mid-upload, Worker timeout during large file write) replaces the live key with a zero-byte or truncated object. The app-level version history only captures successfully completed writes — a failed write creates no version entry and destroys current content permanently.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Enable R2 object versioning via wrangler r2 bucket versioning enable naelao-workspace. Update writeFileWithVersioning() to specify ifMatch ETag on overwrite operations for optimistic concurrency. Add a restore_version endpoint in the file-manager skill using R2&#x27;s versioned object API. Document the R2 versioning strategy in the disaster recovery section and add it to the pre-launch checklist.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F12" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F12</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">FinetuneJobDO</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">alarm() Uses PostgreSQL-Style db.query() in a Durable Object — Throws Runtime Error After Eviction</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">FinetuneJobDO.alarm() uses await db.query(&#x27;UPDATE fine_tune_jobs SET status = $1 ...&#x27;) with $1/$2/$3 PostgreSQL parameterization. A DO cannot hold a reference to an external database connection across hibernation events. The db variable treated as a persistent module-level reference will throw a runtime error when the alarm fires after a DO eviction. Additionally, fine_tune_jobs is defined in the SpaceDO SQLite schema — the correct data access path is a Service Binding call, not a direct DB connection.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Replace db.query() in FinetuneJobDO.alarm() with a Service Binding call to SpaceDO: const spaceDO = this.env.NAELAO_SPACE_DO.get(this.env.NAELAO_SPACE_DO.idFromName(this.rootSpaceId)); await spaceDO.updateFinetuneJob({ jobId, status, resultModel }). Store rootSpaceId and spaceId in DO storage (this.ctx.storage.put()) during init() so they survive eviction. Add an integration test that verifies alarm() succeeds after a simulated DO eviction.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F13" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F13</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-mcp-hub</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">No Idempotency Key on MCP Tool Calls — Retries Cause Duplicate External Actions</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">When NaelaoAgentDO calls an App&#x27;s MCP tool via naelao-mcp-hub and the HTTP response times out or returns 5xx, AgentDO&#x27;s retry logic (CF queue retry or WAL-based recovery) re-invokes the tool. The MCP protocol has no idempotency key in the spec — no X-Idempotency-Key header, no deduplication window, and no guidance about making handlers idempotent. A payment tool called twice charges the customer twice. An email tool called twice sends two emails.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add X-Naelao-Idempotency-Key: {runId}:{walEntryId} header to all MCP tool calls made through naelao-mcp-hub. The WAL entry ID is already written before tool execution and is stable across retries. Document this header in the App developer guide and provide a checkIdempotency(key, env) helper in the Naelao Apps SDK that stores processed keys in KV with 24-hour TTL. Mark it REQUIRED for App tools that perform external write operations.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F14" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F14</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">SpaceTypeRegistryDO</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Canary Promotion Has No Minimum Sample Size Guard — 0/2 Error Rate Triggers Full Rollout</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">processCanaryRollouts() checks errorRate &lt; 0.05 before promoting a canary. If a Space Type is newly published with canary_pct = 5% and there is minimal traffic (e.g., 2 provisioning events), an error rate of 0/2 = 0% passes the check and the canary is promoted to 20% then 100%. A latent bug not triggered by the 2 test events is then deployed to all users. The spec shows no minimum sample count guard.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add a minimum sample size check before allowing canary promotion: if (sampleCount &lt; MIN_CANARY_SAMPLE_SIZE) { continue; } where MIN_CANARY_SAMPLE_SIZE = 50. Also require hoursSincePublish &gt;= 48 before full promotion to 100%. Add a canary_sample_count column to the versions table. If a canary has been stuck at 5% for more than 7 days (insufficient traffic), auto-promote with an ops alert rather than holding indefinitely.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F15" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F15</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">NaelaoAgentDO / token_buffer</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">token_buffer Table Grows Unbounded — Long-Running Agents Exhaust DO SQLite Storage Limit</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Every streaming token from the LLM is inserted into token_buffer(run_id, delta, created_at). There is no LIMIT enforced on insertion and no cleanup mechanism. A multi-hour background agent generating 2M output tokens inserts 2M rows into this table. At ~50 bytes per row, 10 concurrent long-running agents can approach the 1GB DO SQLite storage limit. Additionally, the reconnect replay query SELECT * FROM token_buffer WHERE run_id = ? returns millions of rows, causing multi-second context switches on reconnect.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add cleanup in the insertToken() path: after every 1000 inserts, delete rows beyond the last 500: DELETE FROM token_buffer WHERE run_id = ? AND id NOT IN (SELECT id FROM token_buffer WHERE run_id = ? ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 500). Add a token_buffer_watermark column to fibers table to track the last replayed token position, enabling incremental replay rather than full-table scan.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F16" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F16</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-notifications</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">sendPush() Calls fetch(spaceDO.getActiveDeviceTokens()) — API Misuse, Push Delivery Broken</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">In sendPush(), the code is: const resp = await fetch(spaceDO.getActiveDeviceTokens(payload.userId)). spaceDO.getActiveDeviceTokens() is a DO method that returns unknown[] directly, not a URL string. Passing its return value to fetch() throws TypeError at runtime. This means push notification delivery is broken by a fundamental API misuse in the spec&#x27;s reference implementation, caught by Promise.allSettled as a silent error — notifications are never delivered.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Replace with the correct Service Binding pattern: const stub = this.env.NAELAO_SPACE_DO.get(this.env.NAELAO_SPACE_DO.idFromName(rootSpaceId)); const tokenResp = await stub.fetch(new Request(&#x27;http://space/device-tokens&#x27;, { method: &#x27;POST&#x27;, body: JSON.stringify({ userId: payload.userId }) })); const tokens = await tokenResp.json(). Add device_tokens table to SpaceDO SQLite schema with columns (user_id, token, platform, registered_at) and add this endpoint to the SpaceDO spec section and test suite.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F17" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F17</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">wrangler.jsonc</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Commented-Out Hyperdrive Block Creates JSONC Parse Ambiguity — Ghost Bindings on Some Wrangler Versions</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The wrangler.jsonc spec shows a // comment on line 1 of a multi-line block, but // only comments out the remainder of that single line. The multi-line content on subsequent lines (containing { &#x27;binding&#x27;: &#x27;SPACE_DO&#x27;, &#x27;class_name&#x27;: &#x27;SpaceDO&#x27;, ... }) is NOT commented out. Some wrangler versions reject the file with a parse error; others silently include a duplicate SPACE_DO binding name that conflicts with the DO binding of the same name.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Remove the commented-out Hyperdrive block entirely from wrangler.jsonc. Replace with a single-line comment: // Hyperdrive binding removed — see SpaceDO per-product DB architecture (§22). Add a CI step that runs wrangler deploy --dry-run and fails on any wrangler parse error. Add a test that parses wrangler.jsonc with a strict JSONC parser and verifies no duplicate binding names exist.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F18" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F18</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">AssistantDO / WorkflowRegistryDO</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Custom Cron Parser Skips Day-of-Month Field, No Timezone Support, No Input Validation</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">nextCronFire() uses a custom parser: const [min, hour, , month, dow] = cron.split(&#x27; &#x27;). The destructure skips the day-of-month field with a comma. Monthly crons (0 0 1 * *) silently run daily instead. All times are treated as UTC — a user configuring &#x27;9am&#x27; means their local timezone. No validation at store time — invalid cron like &#x27;every day&#x27; is stored without error and nextCronFire() returns Date.now() + 86_400_000 (fallback), causing the job to run every 24h from save time, not midnight.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Replace the custom cron parser with a CF-compatible ESM library (e.g. croner, no Node dependencies). Add timezone field to cron job configuration: { schedule: &#x27;0 9 * * 1-5&#x27;, timezone: &#x27;America/New_York&#x27; }. Validate at registration time by calling nextCronFire(schedule) — if it throws or returns implausibly far future, reject with HTTP 400 and a human-readable error. Add Suite test: &#x27;Monthly cron 0 0 1 * * fires on the 1st, not daily&#x27;.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F19" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F19</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">NaelaoAgentDO / WebSocket</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">acceptWebSocket() Not Called in Upgrade Handler — DO Hibernation API Not Activated</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">CF WebSocket Hibernation requires explicitly calling ctx.acceptWebSocket(server, tags) in the DO before returning the 101 response. The spec&#x27;s handleWebSocketUpgrade() in websocket.ts creates a WebSocketPair and returns the client in the response, but never passes the server-side WebSocket to the DO&#x27;s hibernation API. This is done correctly in LocalTunnelDO but skipped in the main agent WebSocket upgrade path. Without acceptWebSocket(), messages during hibernation are not delivered to webSocketMessage(), breaking reconnect replay for users who go offline and come back.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">In handleWebSocketUpgrade(), after security checks pass, route to the target NaelaoAgentDO and call ctx.acceptWebSocket(server, [spaceId, agentId]) within the DO context — not in an intermediary Worker. Document in the spec that acceptWebSocket() must be called in the DO that will handle the messages. Add a test: &#x27;WebSocket message received after DO hibernation is delivered to webSocketMessage() handler&#x27;.</p></div>
</div>

<div style="margin:48px 0 0;padding:24px 0 0;border-top:1px solid #1E293B;">
  <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EAB308;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">MEDIUM SEVERITY — 7 GAPS</span>
</div>

<div id="G-F20" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F20</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EAB308;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EAB30818;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-analytics</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Positional Analytics Engine Fields Have No Schema Registry — Adding a Field Silently Corrupts All Queries</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Analytics Engine data points use positional indexing: TOKEN_USAGE_BY_MODEL queries blob4 as model and double5 as total_cost_usd. The mapping from position to field name is only defined in mapEventToDataPoint(). If a developer adds a new field at position 3 in the doubles array, double5 (total_cost_usd) shifts to double6 — all existing Analytics queries silently return wrong values for cost (likely zero). No schema versioning, no compile-time check, and query strings are raw SQL with no type safety.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Create a typed schema registry file analytics-schema.ts that exports named constants: export const TOKEN_USAGE = { doubles: { inputTokens: 0, outputTokens: 1, costUsd: 4 }, blobs: { eventType: 0, userId: 1, model: 3 } }. Use these constants in both mapEventToDataPoint() and all query strings. Add a CI test that generates a data point and verifies positional values match the schema registry. Version the schema (e.g. v1_ prefix) so breaking changes require explicit migration.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F21" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F21</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EAB308;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EAB30818;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">All Workers (API design)</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">No API Versioning Strategy — All Endpoints at Root Path, Breaking Changes Impossible to Deploy Safely</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">All API endpoints are defined without a version prefix: POST /spaces, GET /spaces/:spaceId, POST /agents/:agentId/run. When apps are built against this API, changing any endpoint signature breaks all existing clients simultaneously. There is no mechanism for a builder&#x27;s SDK to target a specific API version. Error response format is also inconsistent between endpoints — some return { error: &#x27;message&#x27; }, others { error: &#x27;CODE&#x27;, message: &#x27;text&#x27; }.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add /v1/ prefix to all Naelao HTTP API routes. Define a standard error envelope: { error: { code: &#x27;SNAKE_CASE_CODE&#x27;, message: &#x27;Human readable&#x27;, details?: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt; } } and enforce it via a shared errorResponse(code, message) helper. Add API-Version: 1 response header to all responses. Declare a stability policy: /v1/ endpoints are stable for 12 months; breaking changes increment to /v2/. Add to pre-launch checklist: &#x27;All 22 Workers return { error: { code, message } } format — verified by integration test&#x27;.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F22" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F22</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EAB308;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EAB30818;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">SpaceDO / naelao-threads</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">getLlmFormattedMessages Uses LIMIT Without Cursor and WalletDO Uses O(n) Offset Pagination</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">SpaceDO.getLlmFormattedMessages(threadId, limit=100) returns the most recent 100 messages with no cursor or before_id parameter. For threads with 500+ messages, the context manager can only see the last 100 — earlier tool results and decisions are invisible to the agent. WalletDO.getTransactions() uses LIMIT/OFFSET pagination — offset pagination is O(n), scanning 10,000 transactions to reach offset 9,900 is a full SQLite table scan.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add cursor (a message_id) parameter to getLlmFormattedMessages(): SELECT * FROM messages WHERE thread_id = ? AND id &lt; ? ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT ?. Return nextCursor in the response when more messages exist. Replace offset pagination in WalletDO.getTransactions() with keyset pagination: WHERE id &lt; ? ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT ?. Update ContextManager to use cursor pagination when building long-context windows, fetching earlier pages only when the token budget allows.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F23" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F23</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EAB308;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EAB30818;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-admin / KV</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">KV-Based Emergency Kill Switch Has 60-Second Propagation Delay — Agents Continue Running During Incidents</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">AgentDO checks env.NAELAO_CONFIG_KV.get(&#x27;emergency:kill-all-agents&#x27;) at the top of every LLM loop iteration. CF KV is eventually consistent with up to 60-second propagation SLA to all edge nodes. During a security incident requiring immediate agent halt, agents at edge nodes that haven&#x27;t received the KV update continue executing for up to 60 seconds. For an agent actively exfiltrating data via tool calls, 60 seconds is significant damage.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Supplement the KV kill switch with a DO-based kill signal for immediate propagation: maintain a KillSwitchDO singleton (idFromName(&#x27;global-kill-switch&#x27;)) that AgentDO checks via Service Binding before each LLM call. Service Binding calls propagate in under 1ms. Keep the KV check as secondary for steady-state (lower cost). Document the dual-check pattern in the security architecture section and add a test: &#x27;Kill switch activation halts agent within 1 LLM iteration&#x27;.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F24" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F24</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EAB308;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EAB30818;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">FinetuneJobDO / AssistantDO</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Alarm Handlers Not Idempotent — CF At-Least-Once Delivery Causes Duplicate Notifications and Status Updates</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">CF&#x27;s alarm system guarantees at-least-once delivery. FinetuneJobDO.alarm() calls Together AI API → UPDATE fine_tune_jobs → send notification. If the alarm fires twice (CF retry on timeout), two notifications are sent and NAELAO_NOTIFICATIONS_QUEUE.send() produces duplicate messages downstream. The UPDATE itself is idempotent, but notification sends are not — they produce duplicate emails/push messages to the builder.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add idempotency guard to all alarm handlers. Store last_alarm_executed_at in DO storage. At the start of every alarm: const lastExec = await this.ctx.storage.get(&#x27;last_alarm_executed_at&#x27;); if (lastExec &amp;&amp; Date.now() - lastExec &lt; 60_000) return;. Update after execution: await this.ctx.storage.put(&#x27;last_alarm_executed_at&#x27;, Date.now()). For notification sends, pass a deterministic id: id: `finetune-complete:${jobId}` rather than a random UUID, using the existing KV idempotency check with 24-hour TTL.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F25" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F25</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EAB308;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EAB30818;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-credentials</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Single Global Encryption Key for All Tenant MCP Credentials — No Per-Tenant Key Isolation</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">naelao-credentials encrypts all MCP credentials (Stripe keys, GitHub tokens, CRM credentials) using a single platform-wide NAELAO_MCP_ENCRYPTION_KEY. Key rotation requires re-encrypting all credentials for all spaces simultaneously. A side-channel attack extracting the key from any Worker instance exposes all tenant credentials. The spec&#x27;s BYOK section shows HKDF per-space key derivation but this pattern is not applied to the main credential store.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Adopt the BYOK HKDF pattern: derive a per-space encryption key using HKDF(masterKey, salt=spaceId, info=&#x27;mcp-credentials&#x27;). Store only the master key as NAELAO_MCP_MASTER_KEY. Per-space derived keys are never stored — recomputed on each decrypt. This means compromise of any single worker instance does not expose all credentials. Version the HKDF info string (mcp-credentials-v2) to allow rotation without full re-encryption.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-F26" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-F26</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EAB308;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EAB30818;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">All systems / Observability</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">No Distributed Trace ID Propagation Across 22-Worker Call Chain — Cross-Worker Debugging Is Impossible</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">An agent run involves: naelao-router → naelao-agents → NaelaoAgentDO → naelao-mcp-hub → [App Worker] → naelao-billing → naelao-analytics. Each Worker logs independently with its own request IDs. There is no X-Trace-ID header propagated through Service Binding calls. Analytics Engine records runId for agent events but not for billing or MCP events, breaking the correlation chain. Debugging a failed agent run requires manually correlating logs from 6+ Workers by matching timestamps — slow and error-prone.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Generate traceId = crypto.randomUUID() at naelao-router entry point for every request. Propagate as X-Trace-ID header in all Service Binding calls (Service Binding fetch() accepts custom headers). Add traceId to the AnalyticsEvent base interface so all Analytics Engine events include the trace. Add CF-Ray correlation to link CF&#x27;s own request traces. Add to pre-launch checklist: &#x27;Query Analytics Engine for a single traceId — confirm events from all 22 Workers appear in the result&#x27;.</p></div>
</div>

<div style="margin:60px 0 0;padding:32px;background:#0A1628;border:1px solid #1E293B;border-radius:8px;">
  <p style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:#64748B;margin:0;line-height:1.8;">
    Appendix F complete. Combined gap audit total: A (125) + B (30) + C (22) + D (22) + E (24) +
    F (26) = <strong style="color:var(--or);">249 documented technical gaps</strong> with required fixes.
    Recurring themes in this pass: <strong style="color:#94A3B8;">DO eviction not accounted for</strong>
    (G-F05, G-F07, G-F12), <strong style="color:#94A3B8;">missing KV binding declarations</strong>
    (G-F10, G-F17), <strong style="color:#94A3B8;">alarm handler at-least-once semantics ignored</strong>
    (G-F24), and <strong style="color:#94A3B8;">per-tenant isolation gaps</strong> (G-F03, G-F25).
  </p>
</div>
</section>


<section id="appendix-g" style="margin:80px 0 0;padding:60px 0 0;border-top:3px solid var(--or);">
<div style="margin-bottom:32px;">
  <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;display:block;margin-bottom:8px;">Appendix G · Sixth-Pass Audit</span>
  <h2 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,40px);font-weight:700;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 12px;">Architecture Contradictions, Missing Infrastructure &amp; Runtime Correctness Gaps</h2>
  <p style="color:#94A3B8;max-width:720px;line-height:1.7;">
    26 additional gaps from the deepest audit pass yet. A critical architectural contradiction runs
    through this entire pass: the spec simultaneously declares "no PostgreSQL, data layer is SpaceDO
    SQLite" while containing PostgreSQL-syntax queries, plpgsql stored functions, and undefined
    <code style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;color:var(--or);">db.query()</code>
    calls across 56 call sites in Worker code. The PostgreSQL-to-SpaceDO migration was never completed
    in the spec itself. This pass also surfaces missing wiring (canary rollout never called, Vectorize
    binding absent, extractEventType undefined), Stripe billing race conditions, and GDPR erasure gaps.
  </p>
  <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:16px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;background:#EF444422;color:#EF4444;border:1px solid #EF444444;padding:4px 10px;border-radius:4px;">6 CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;background:#E8692A22;color:#E8692A;border:1px solid #E8692A44;padding:4px 10px;border-radius:4px;">13 HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;background:#EAB30822;color:#EAB308;border:1px solid #EAB30844;padding:4px 10px;border-radius:4px;">7 MEDIUM</span>
  </div>
</div>

<div style="margin:48px 0 0;padding:24px 0 0;border-top:1px solid #1E293B;">
  <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">CRITICAL SEVERITY — 6 GAPS</span>
</div>

<div id="G-G01" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G01</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">All Workers (naelao-billing, naelao-spaces, naelao-mcp-hub, naelao-sweeper, naelao-admin, naelao-knowledge, naelao-triggers)</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">rootSpaceId Used in 56 Call Sites Across Workers But Never Declared — Universal ReferenceError on First Request</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The spec declares the data layer as &#x27;SpaceDO SQLite, no Hyperdrive, no external PostgreSQL.&#x27; However, 56 occurrences of getProductDO(rootSpaceId, c.env) appear in Worker handler bodies where rootSpaceId is never assigned before use. The db variable used in subsequent db.query() calls is also never declared. In naelao-billing&#x27;s /token-usage handler, const spaceDO = getProductDO(rootSpaceId, c.env) appears before any rootSpaceId assignment — this is a ReferenceError at the first request. naelao-spaces calls db.query() using INTERVAL &#x27;7 days&#x27; and gen_random_uuid() — PostgreSQL-only syntax that cannot execute against DO SQLite. Every Worker that touches data will throw at runtime.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">For each Worker, rootSpaceId must be extracted from the validated JWT context (c.get(&#x27;rootSpaceId&#x27;) from the auth middleware) before any data call. The db variable must be replaced with a typed SpaceDO stub obtained via env.NAELAO_SPACE_DO.get(env.NAELAO_SPACE_DO.idFromName(`space:${rootSpaceId}`)). All PostgreSQL-syntax queries (DATE_TRUNC, INTERVAL, auth.users, FOR UPDATE, RETURNING) must be rewritten as DO SQLite statements using this.ctx.storage.sql.exec() with SQLite equivalents (strftime, integer comparisons, separate SELECT then UPDATE patterns). create_space_with_defaults must use crypto.randomUUID() and a SpaceDO typed method. Add an ESLint rule banning db.query in Worker code outside DO files.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G02" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G02</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">SpaceDO Methods / naelao-billing / naelao-spaces</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Five plpgsql Stored Functions with SECURITY DEFINER and auth.uid() Cannot Execute in DO SQLite</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The &#x27;SpaceDO Methods — Replacing All Stored Functions&#x27; section contains five CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION blocks written in plpgsql with SECURITY DEFINER, LANGUAGE plpgsql, auth.uid(), auth.users, FOR UPDATE, and RETURNING clauses. SQLite in Durable Objects does not support stored functions, plpgsql, LANGUAGE clause, or auth.uid(). The deduct_space_credits function uses SELECT ... FOR UPDATE (PostgreSQL row-level locking), which has no SQLite equivalent and would silently fail. naelao-sweeper queries auth.users to fan out heartbeats — a table that only exists in Supabase/PostgreSQL. These five functions will fail at ctx.storage.sql.exec() with syntax errors, making credit deductions, space creation, and heartbeats non-functional.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">All five stored function bodies must be converted to TypeScript methods on the SpaceDO class using this.ctx.storage.sql.exec() with SQLite syntax. deduct_space_credits must use the WalletDO.deductCredits() pattern (single-threaded DO = no FOR UPDATE needed). create_space_with_defaults becomes a SpaceDO.createSpace() method using SQLite transactions via this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(&#x27;BEGIN&#x27;). auth.users and auth.uid() references must be replaced with the naelao-auth JWT validation path and SpaceDO space_members table. naelao-sweeper must query active assistants from a dedicated SpaceDO.getActiveSpaceMembers() method, not via raw SQL against auth.users.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G03" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G03</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-billing / Stripe webhook</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Stripe Webhook Handler Has No Idempotency Protection — Duplicate checkout.session.completed Events Double-Credit Users</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">CF Queues and Stripe both guarantee at-least-once delivery. The Stripe webhook handler handles checkout.session.completed by executing INSERT INTO space_credits ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE SET balance_usd = balance_usd + EXCLUDED.balance_usd. If Stripe retries the same event (it retries for up to 72 hours on 2xx responses), the credit is added again — a direct financial loss. invoice.payment_failed also triggers a notification queue message on each delivery, so the builder receives duplicate emails. The naelao-notifications consumer has a KV idempotency key but the billing handler never sets it or checks it before queuing notifications.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Before processing any Stripe event, write a KV idempotency record: const key = `stripe-event:${event.id}`; if (await env.NAELAO_CONFIG_KV.get(key)) return c.json({ received: true }); await env.NAELAO_CONFIG_KV.put(key, &#x27;1&#x27;, { expirationTtl: 86400 * 7 }). Place this check at the top of the webhook handler before the switch(event.type) block. For additional safety, the credit upsert must include the Stripe event ID as a unique constraint: INSERT INTO stripe_events (event_id) VALUES ($1) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING RETURNING id — if this returns 0 rows, skip processing.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G04" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G04</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-billing / Stripe subscription events</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">invoice.payment_failed Reads spaceId from subscription_details.metadata — null for Most Stripe Invoice Shapes, Payment Failures Silently Ignored</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The invoice.payment_failed handler reads: const spaceId = invoice.subscription_details?.metadata?.spaceId. Stripe only populates subscription_details when the invoice is directly linked to a subscription. For checkout-session invoices, metadata is on invoice.metadata directly. For subscription invoices, subscription_details.metadata may be null if metadata was set on the subscription object rather than the invoice. spaceId is undefined in several real billing scenarios, the if (spaceId) guard silently passes through, the UPDATE spaces SET status=&#x27;payment_failed&#x27; never runs, and the space continues serving traffic despite a failed payment. This also affects subscription lifecycle events which read sub.metadata?.spaceId — if spaceId was placed on the Checkout Session metadata but not copied to the Subscription metadata, all subscription lifecycle events silently no-op.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">When creating Stripe Checkout Sessions, set metadata: { spaceId } on both the Checkout Session AND the Subscription via subscription_data: { metadata: { spaceId } }. In the webhook handler, implement a multi-path resolver: const spaceId = invoice.metadata?.spaceId ?? invoice.subscription_details?.metadata?.spaceId ?? (await stripe.subscriptions.retrieve(invoice.subscription)).metadata?.spaceId. Log a structured error to Analytics Engine whenever spaceId cannot be resolved from a billing event — this catches metadata configuration bugs in staging before they reach production.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G05" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G05</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-spaces / space provisioning</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Concurrent POST /api/spaces Requests Have No Serialization Lock — Race Creates Duplicate DOs and Half-Provisioned Spaces</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The space creation flow does three non-atomic operations with no lock: INSERT INTO spaces, then spaceDO.fetch(&#x27;http://space/init&#x27;), then c.executionCtx.waitUntil(registryDO.fetch(&#x27;provision&#x27;)). If two simultaneous requests arrive, both pass quota checks (reading the same counts before either commits), both attempt the DB insert (one fails on unique violation), but if one fails the DB insert the other proceeds to call spaceDO.fetch(init). Worse, provisioning is fired via waitUntil — if the HTTP response returns before provisioning completes and the user immediately navigates to the space, they hit a SpaceDO that hasn&#x27;t called initSpaceType() yet.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Route POST /api/spaces through a per-user SpaceCreationDO via idFromName(`space-create-lock:${userId}`) — the DO&#x27;s single-threaded guarantee serializes concurrent creation attempts. Inside the DO, check for an in-progress creation before starting a new one. Alternatively, use a KV NX lock: await env.NAELAO_CONFIG_KV.put(`creating-space:${spaceId}`, &#x27;1&#x27;, { expirationTtl: 30 }) using a conditional write that fails if the key exists. The provisioning step must complete synchronously before returning 201, not via waitUntil — the client must not receive success until provisioning is confirmed complete.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G06" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G06</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-billing / naelao-admin</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">db.query(&#x27;BEGIN&#x27;) / db.query(&#x27;ROLLBACK&#x27;) Pattern Used in Workers — Cannot Execute Against SpaceDO, Atomic Billing Invariant Broken</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The spec&#x27;s most emphasized invariant is &#x27;atomic-or-nothing credit deduction.&#x27; The billing Worker shows await db.query(&#x27;BEGIN&#x27;); try { ... await db.query(&#x27;COMMIT&#x27;); } catch { await db.query(&#x27;ROLLBACK&#x27;); }. In the CF DO model there is no db object — data access goes through this.ctx.storage.sql.exec() inside the DO. If db is undefined, this throws ReferenceError on the first request. If someone implements db as a wrapper around SpaceDO calls, BEGIN/COMMIT/ROLLBACK have no meaning outside a direct SQLite connection. The actual atomic pattern in DO SQLite is a single this.ctx.storage.sql.exec() call with all statements in one string — which is not what the spec shows.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Move all credit deduction logic into a SpaceDO.deductCredits() typed method that uses this.ctx.storage.sql.exec() with a single multi-statement transaction block: this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(`BEGIN; INSERT INTO token_usage ...; UPDATE space_credits ...; COMMIT`). The AgentDO and billing Worker call this single DO method via Service Binding — the DO&#x27;s single-threaded guarantee provides the atomicity that PostgreSQL&#x27;s FOR UPDATE provided before. The three-step transaction (INSERT token_usage, UPDATE space_usage_monthly, UPDATE space_credits) must be combined into a single exec() call. Remove all db.query(&#x27;BEGIN&#x27;) / db.query(&#x27;ROLLBACK&#x27;) patterns from Worker-level code.</p></div>
</div>

<div style="margin:48px 0 0;padding:24px 0 0;border-top:1px solid #1E293B;">
  <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">HIGH SEVERITY — 13 GAPS</span>
</div>

<div id="G-G07" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G07</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">NaelaoAgentDO / webSocketMessage</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">JSON.parse(message) Without try/catch in webSocketMessage — Malformed Frame Crashes DO and Terminates All Active Runs</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The webSocketMessage handler calls const data = JSON.parse(message as string) with no try/catch. If the client sends a binary frame, message is an ArrayBuffer and JSON.parse throws SyntaxError. If the client sends a partial JSON frame (network truncation), JSON.parse also throws. An unhandled exception in webSocketMessage inside a Durable Object will cause CF to close the WebSocket connection and may trigger DO eviction. Since the agent loop runs inside the DO, an eviction mid-run triggers fiber recovery — but if the DO evicts during an active await (e.g., during an LLM call), the fiber state may not have been stashed yet (stash happens at the top of each iteration), losing the current LLM response.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Wrap the entire webSocketMessage body in try/catch: try { if (typeof message !== &#x27;string&#x27;) { ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: &#x27;error&#x27;, message: &#x27;Binary frames not supported&#x27; })); return; } const data = JSON.parse(message); ... } catch (e) { ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: &#x27;error&#x27;, message: &#x27;Invalid message format&#x27; })); return; }. Also define the webSocketClose handler to handle client disconnections cleanly rather than leaving the agent loop running headlessly with no recipient for token stream broadcasts.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G08" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G08</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">GitHub Actions CI / wrangler deploy</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">All Workers Deployed in a Single wrangler deploy Command With No Dependency Ordering — Service Binding Resolution Fails on First Deploy</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The CI pipeline runs npx wrangler deploy --env production as a single step. Cloudflare Service Bindings require the referenced Worker to already exist at deployment time. If naelao-router is deployed before naelao-auth, the Service Binding { &#x27;binding&#x27;: &#x27;NAELAO_AUTH&#x27;, &#x27;service&#x27;: &#x27;naelao-auth&#x27; } in naelao-router&#x27;s wrangler config will fail validation. On a first deploy to a fresh account (staging setup, new developer onboarding), the correct dependency order is: (1) DO-hosting Workers, (2) leaf Workers (naelao-auth, naelao-billing, naelao-knowledge), (3) aggregator Workers (naelao-mcp-hub, naelao-agents), (4) naelao-router last. A single wrangler deploy deploys in alphabetical order — not the dependency graph order.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The CI pipeline must deploy Workers in dependency order. Add a deploy-production GitHub Actions job that runs wrangler deploy for each Worker in sequence: first all DO-hosting Workers, then leaf service Workers, then aggregator Workers, then the router. Use wrangler deploy --config workers/auth/wrangler.jsonc, wrangler deploy --config workers/billing/wrangler.jsonc, etc., in order with &amp;&amp; chaining. Add a validation step that runs wrangler publish --dry-run for each Worker to catch binding resolution errors before they reach production.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G09" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G09</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-triggers / webhook security</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Stripe Webhook Signature Verification in naelao-triggers Returns true Unconditionally — Anyone Can Trigger Agent Runs</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The verifySignature function has a full GitHub HMAC-SHA256 implementation followed by // Stripe uses a custom timestamped signature, implemented similarly... return true. This means any POST request to /webhooks/stripe/{spaceId} with any payload and any signature will pass verification and trigger workflows or agent runs in the target space. An attacker who discovers the URL pattern can forge Stripe events targeting any space, triggering agent runs, waking sleeping agents, and consuming billing credits. The spaceId is in the URL and can be correlated from public portal URLs.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Implement Stripe&#x27;s timestamp-based webhook signature immediately. Stripe&#x27;s format is t=&lt;timestamp&gt;,v1=&lt;signature&gt; where v1 is HMAC-SHA256(secret, &#x27;{timestamp}.{payload}&#x27;). Enforce a timestamp tolerance: reject requests where |now - t| &gt; 300 seconds to prevent replay attacks. The verifySignature function must throw or return false for unrecognized providers — never default to return true. Add a PROVIDER_VERIFIED allowlist: only providers with implemented verification (github, stripe) are accepted; all others return 401 until implemented.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G10" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G10</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-knowledge / Vectorize</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Vectorize Binding Missing from wrangler.jsonc — env.NAELAO_VECTORIZE Is undefined, All Knowledge Upserts and Queries Throw TypeError</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The knowledge Worker upserts to c.env.NAELAO_VECTORIZE and queries the same binding. The wrangler.jsonc does not define any vectorize binding. The spec&#x27;s architecture text says &#x27;Vectors stored in Vectorize index naelao-kb-{spaceId}&#x27; suggesting per-tenant indexes, but CF Vectorize indexes are static infrastructure defined in wrangler.jsonc at deploy time — they cannot be created programmatically at runtime. With no vectorize binding in wrangler.jsonc, c.env.NAELAO_VECTORIZE is undefined and every call to .upsert() or .query() throws TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined. The entire RAG/knowledge feature is broken before a single line of application logic runs.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Define a single shared Vectorize index in wrangler.jsonc: &quot;vectorize&quot;: [{ &quot;binding&quot;: &quot;NAELAO_VECTORIZE&quot;, &quot;index_name&quot;: &quot;naelao-knowledge-base&quot; }]. Create this index before first deploy: wrangler vectorize create naelao-knowledge-base --dimensions=768 --metric=cosine. Use spaceId metadata filter on every query (filter: { spaceId }) for tenant isolation. Add index creation to the workspace setup checklist as a required one-time step. For document deletion, call NAELAO_VECTORIZE.deleteByIds() for all chunk IDs — this must be part of the deprovisioning workflow which currently does not call Vectorize at all.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G11" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G11</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">SpaceTypeRegistryDO / canary rollout</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">processCanaryRollouts() Is Never Called by Any Scheduler — Canary Versions Stuck at 5% Forever</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The processCanaryRollouts function exists as an async function inside SpaceTypeRegistryDO but is never registered as a DO alarm handler, never called from naelao-sweeper, and the global singleton DO has no alarm() method defined in the spec. The sweeper tasks are sweepAssistantHeartbeats, sweepAbandonedAgentRuns, sweepExpiredFileLocks, sweepDeadLetterQueue, and sweepStaleFineTuneJobs — no sweepCanaryRollouts. The rollbackInstances function referenced inside processCanaryRollouts is also never defined. The canary_pct field starts at 0 per the schema default and is only set to 5 at publish time via a code path that is also absent. The entire canary mechanism is specified but not wired up.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add sweepCanaryRollouts to the naelao-sweeper&#x27;s Promise.allSettled task list. Inside that task, fetch the global SpaceTypeRegistryDO and call processCanaryRollouts() on it. Define the missing rollbackInstances(typeId, version) function which must query the instances table for spaces on the failing version and update them to the last stable version. Set canary_pct = 5 explicitly in registerSpaceType() when change_type = &#x27;minor&#x27;. Add a checkErrorRateForVersion() implementation that queries Analytics Engine for the error_rate of the specific version over the past hour. Add a minimum sample size guard (min 50 provisioning events) before allowing promotion.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G12" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G12</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">RevenueCat / naelao-billing</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">RevenueCat Webhook Endpoint Has No Public Route — RevenueCat Cannot POST to an Internal Service Binding Worker</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The RevenueCat handler authenticates via Authorization header comparison. naelao-billing is an internal Worker called via Service Binding — it has no public HTTP route (all endpoints are internal, naelao-router does NOT expose these routes). But the RevenueCat webhook must be publicly accessible for RevenueCat to POST to it. If there&#x27;s an undocumented public route in naelao-router passing the Authorization header through, the JWT middleware that validates Bearer tokens would reject the RevenueCat request (which uses a shared secret, not a user JWT) with 401 before it reaches billing. RevenueCat&#x27;s webhook Authorization header conflicts with standard Bearer JWT auth patterns.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The RevenueCat webhook must have a dedicated public route: POST /api/billing/revenuecat/webhook exposed through naelao-router with auth middleware explicitly bypassed for this path (whitelisted alongside /api/auth/*). Validate the RevenueCat shared secret using a constant-time comparison (timingSafeEqual via Web Crypto) to prevent timing attacks. Alternatively, use RevenueCat&#x27;s X-RevenueCat-Signature header (HMAC-SHA256 of the body) rather than the Authorization header to avoid conflicts with JWT middleware.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G13" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G13</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">All Durable Objects / schema evolution</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS Silently Ignores New Columns on Existing DOs — Schema Evolution Is Broken for Live DOs</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The constructor calls ctx.blockConcurrencyWhile(() =&gt; this.initSchema()) on every DO instantiation. initSchema() uses CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS for all tables. If a new deployment adds a column (e.g., tool_args_hash TEXT to run_wal), the CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS run_wal statement is a no-op because the table already exists — the new column is never added. Code that writes to tool_args_hash receives &#x27;table run_wal has no column named tool_args_hash&#x27; SQLite error, crashing the agent loop. There is no migration versioning, no schema version table, and no ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS pattern specified. DOs can live for months between evictions, meaning old-schema DOs coexist with new code indefinitely.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add a schema_version table: CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS schema_version (version INTEGER PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT 0). In initSchema(), after creating tables, check the current version and apply migrations sequentially: const v = sql.exec(&#x27;SELECT version FROM schema_version&#x27;).one()?.version ?? 0; if (v &lt; 1) { sql.exec(&#x27;ALTER TABLE run_wal ADD COLUMN tool_args_hash TEXT&#x27;); sql.exec(&#x27;UPDATE schema_version SET version = 1&#x27;); }. Each new column addition becomes a numbered migration. SQLite supports ADD COLUMN without table recreation for non-destructive schema changes. Add a &#x27;DO Schema Migration Pattern&#x27; section to the spec documenting this as required for all DO schema changes.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G14" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G14</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-analytics / Queue consumer</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">naelao-analytics Queue Consumer Has No DLQ — Analytics Batch Failures Permanently Drop Events Including Security Audit Logs</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The wrangler.jsonc queue consumers section shows { &#x27;queue&#x27;: &#x27;naelao-analytics&#x27;, &#x27;max_batch_size&#x27;: 100 } with no max_retries and no dead_letter_queue. CF Queues with no DLQ permanently delete messages after max retries (default 3). The analytics Worker writes 100-event batches to Analytics Engine. If Analytics Engine has a transient outage, the entire batch fails, retries 3 times, then disappears. Because Analytics Engine is the only place analytics data is written, lost analytics means lost billing audit trail, missing security event logs, and incomplete admin dashboard data — all of which have compliance implications under GDPR Article 30 (records of processing activities).</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add max_retries: 5, dead_letter_queue: &#x27;naelao-analytics-dlq&#x27; to the naelao-analytics queue consumer in wrangler.jsonc. Create the naelao-analytics-dlq queue. Add a naelao-admin endpoint to replay analytics DLQ messages after Analytics Engine outages. For security events specifically, add a secondary KV write as a backup: await env.NAELAO_CONFIG_KV.put(`sec-event:${event.timestamp}:${event.type}`, JSON.stringify(event), { expirationTtl: 86400 * 30 }) so security events are never lost even if Analytics Engine is down.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G15" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G15</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-mcp-hub / tool route resolution</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">resolveToolRoute() Always Looks Up &#x27;unknown&#x27; AgentId Cache Key — Installed App Tools Return 404 for All Real Agents</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">resolveToolRoute() fetches tool-schemas:${spaceId}:unknown — with the agentId hardcoded as the literal string &#x27;unknown&#x27;. The GET /tools endpoint caches with cacheKey = `tool-schemas:${spaceId}:${agentId}` where agentId comes from the request query parameter. If two agents in the same space have different tool permissions, their schemas are cached at tool-schemas:{spaceId}:agentA and tool-schemas:{spaceId}:agentB respectively. resolveToolRoute always looks up tool-schemas:{spaceId}:unknown, which only exists if a tools discovery request was made with agentId=unknown. For all normal agents, route resolution finds no cache entry and returns null, causing every installed MCP app tool call to return &#x27;Tool not found: {toolName}&#x27; with 404. Platform tools are unaffected; all installed App tools become unreachable.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">resolveToolRoute() must accept the agentId parameter and look up tool-schemas:${spaceId}:${agentId}. The POST /execute endpoint already receives agentId in the request body — pass it through to resolveToolRoute. Add a fallback: if no cache entry exists for agentId, call the /tools endpoint internally to refresh before returning null. The /tools/invalidate cache-clearing endpoint must delete all agent-specific cache keys, not just the &#x27;unknown&#x27; key — use list({ prefix: `tool-schemas:${spaceId}:` }) and delete all.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G16" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G16</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">file-manager skill / append_to_file</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">append_to_file Is O(n) in File Size — Reads and Rewrites the Entire File to Append a Few Bytes, Hits 30s CPU Limit on Large Files</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The append_to_file handler reads the full existing file with r2.get(), calls existing.text() (fully buffering in memory), concatenates new content as a string, then writes the entire result back. For a log file that accumulates 10,000 append operations during a long agent run, each append must read and rewrite the entire file. At 50KB per append (common for agent output logs), the 10,000th append reads and writes ~500MB — well beyond what a Worker can do in 30 seconds. The agent&#x27;s todo.md maintenance pattern involves constant appends, making this a hot code path that degrades until it breaks.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">For files intended for append operations, store content as versioned chunks in R2: workspace/logs/{filename}/{chunkIndex}.txt, with a manifest object listing all chunks. read_file assembles chunks on read. Alternatively, enforce MAX_APPEND_FILE_SIZE_MB (e.g., 10MB) and rotate the file when exceeded: rename file.txt to file.1.txt and start a fresh file.txt. Update the SKILL.md instruction: &#x27;Use write_file with full updated content for small files (&lt;1MB); use append_to_file only for write-only logging where you will never read back the full history.&#x27;</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G17" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G17</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">SpaceTypeRegistryDO / global singleton</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Global SpaceTypeRegistryDO Singleton Serializes All Space Creation at Scale — 1000 Concurrent Creates = 5 Seconds of Head-of-Line Blocking</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The SpaceTypeRegistryDO getSpaceType() method is called for every space creation. CF Durable Objects are single-threaded and process one request at a time. On KV cache miss (after 1-hour TTL expiry), all concurrent space creations hit the DO simultaneously and queue behind each other. For a SaaS platform with viral growth (1000 spaces created in an hour after a Product Hunt launch), all 1000 requests queue serially through a single DO. Each DO request takes ~5ms, so 1000 queued requests = 5 seconds of head-of-line blocking for the last request, violating the latency budget for space creation.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Implement a stale-while-revalidate pattern: set KV TTL to 24 hours but include a staleAt timestamp set to 1 hour in the cached value. Workers that read a stale-but-not-expired entry return it immediately and trigger background revalidation via ctx.waitUntil(). This means the DO is only hit by the first request per hour, not all requests on cache expiry. The per-typeId KV shard (space-type-manifest:{typeId}) should be the primary read path — the singleton DO becomes a cache-miss path only.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G18" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G18</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-triggers / webhook event routing</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">extractEventType() Referenced But Never Defined — All Webhook-Triggered Workflows Silently Dispatch Zero Agents</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The extractEventType(provider, payload) function is called in the triggers handler to determine which registered trigger to fire. This function is never defined in the spec. If stub-implemented as return &#x27;unknown&#x27;, then the query WHERE event_type = &#x27;unknown&#x27; matches no registered triggers and zero workflows are dispatched for any webhook. Additionally, rawBody is correctly passed to verifySignature, but JSON.parse(rawBody) is called with no try/catch. For non-JSON webhooks (form-urlencoded Shopify, plain-text GitHub ping), JSON.parse throws, crashing the handler and returning 500 — causing the external service to retry indefinitely.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Implement extractEventType(provider, payload) with provider-specific mappings: for Stripe, return payload.type (e.g., &#x27;invoice.paid&#x27;); for GitHub, return ${req.header(&#x27;X-GitHub-Event&#x27;)}.${payload.action} (e.g., &#x27;push.created&#x27;). Add try/catch around JSON.parse with fallback to URLSearchParams: let payload; try { payload = JSON.parse(rawBody); } catch { payload = Object.fromEntries(new URLSearchParams(rawBody)); }. Return 200 immediately when the payload cannot be parsed but was signature-verified to prevent infinite retries from the provider.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G19" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G19</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">ConcurrencyDO / alarm management</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Concurrent checkAndReserve() Calls Each Invoke setAlarm() — Each Overwrites the Previous, Leaving Only One Alarm for N Concurrent Runs</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">CF DO alarms support only one alarm at a time per DO. Calling setAlarm when an alarm is already scheduled overwrites it. In checkAndReserve, every new run reservation calls ctx.storage.setAlarm(Date.now() + 5 * 60 * 1000). If a user starts 10 concurrent runs in rapid succession, the 10th setAlarm call overwrites all previous ones. If no new reservations arrive after the alarm fires, the remaining active runs never get their alarm-based cleanup triggered — stale run slots remain occupied, eventually blocking all new agent runs for that space until the slots naturally expire.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">In checkAndReserve, only call setAlarm if no alarm is currently scheduled: const existingAlarm = await ctx.storage.getAlarm(); if (!existingAlarm) { await ctx.storage.setAlarm(Date.now() + 5 * 60 * 1000); }. This prevents N concurrent reservations from overwriting each other&#x27;s alarms. The alarm() handler must always reschedule if any active runs remain: check remaining count AFTER deleting stale runs (not before), then call setAlarm unconditionally if remaining &gt; 0.</p></div>
</div>

<div style="margin:48px 0 0;padding:24px 0 0;border-top:1px solid #1E293B;">
  <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EAB308;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">MEDIUM SEVERITY — 7 GAPS</span>
</div>

<div id="G-G20" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G20</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EAB308;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EAB30818;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-knowledge / Vectorize filter</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Vectorize filter: { spaceId } Shorthand May Not Enforce Tenant Isolation — Silent Cross-Tenant Leak Depending on Binding Version</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The knowledge search calls env.NAELAO_VECTORIZE.query(embedding, { topK, filter: { spaceId }, returnMetadata: &#x27;all&#x27; }). Cloudflare Vectorize&#x27;s metadata filtering API requires filter expressions in the form { spaceId: { $eq: spaceId } } rather than { spaceId: value } shorthand. If the plain object form is not supported by the Vectorize binding version in use, the filter is silently ignored — all vector neighbors are returned regardless of tenant. With thousands of spaces and millions of knowledge chunks, the first 5 results may include documents from a completely different space — a cross-tenant knowledge leak.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Use the explicit filter operator syntax: filter: { spaceId: { $eq: spaceId } }. Add a post-query assertion: results.matches = results.matches.filter(m =&gt; m.metadata?.spaceId === spaceId). Add a test in Suite 04 (Space Isolation): upload a document to space A, query from space B, assert zero results are returned. This test must run against a real Vectorize index (not miniflare) in the integration test suite.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G21" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G21</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EAB308;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EAB30818;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-notifications / idempotency</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Notification Idempotency Keys Written With No TTL — Permanent KV Keys Block Legitimate Admin Resends Forever</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The notif_lock:{payload.id} KV write has no expirationTtl. CF KV with no TTL retains the key forever. For subscription lifecycle events (sub-cancelled-{spaceId}), if Stripe fires the same webhook twice, the second notification is correctly dropped. However, if an admin wants to manually re-trigger a notification (e.g., resend the &#x27;credits exhausted&#x27; email after a bug fix), the permanent idempotency key blocks it. There is no admin endpoint to clear idempotency keys, making manual notification resends impossible without direct KV deletion.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Set a 7-day TTL on idempotency keys: await env.NAELAO_CONFIG_KV.put(idempotencyKey, &#x27;1&#x27;, { expirationTtl: 86400 * 7 }). This covers Stripe&#x27;s maximum webhook retry window (72 hours) while allowing manual resends after a week. Add a naelao-admin endpoint DELETE /notifications/idempotency/{notificationId} that deletes the KV key, allowing admin-triggered resends. For subscription lifecycle events, use composite IDs including the Stripe event ID: sub-cancelled-{spaceId}-{event.id} so natural key expiry handles re-delivery without ever blocking legitimate resends.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G22" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G22</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EAB308;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EAB30818;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-knowledge / GDPR compliance</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Vectorize Vectors Not Deleted on Space Deprovisioning — GDPR Article 17 Right to Erasure Violated for Embedded Knowledge</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The DeprovisionWorkflow deletes R2 objects (Step C), calls spaceDO.purge() to cascade SpaceDO SQLite records (Step D), and cleans KV entries (Step E). It does not call Vectorize to delete embedded vectors. Knowledge document chunks are stored in Vectorize with IDs in the format {docId}:chunk:{index} and metadata containing spaceId. After deprovisioning, all vector data for the space remains in the shared Vectorize index indefinitely. Under GDPR Article 17, right to erasure requires deletion of all copies of personal data, including derived data — embeddings are derived from user-uploaded documents.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add deprovisioning Step C2: query SpaceDO SQLite for all knowledge_docs records for the space to get all docId values, construct Vectorize IDs ({docId}:chunk:0, {docId}:chunk:1, ...) up to the stored chunk_count for each doc, and call NAELAO_VECTORIZE.deleteByIds(ids) in batches of 1000 (Vectorize API limit per call). For individual document deletion, DELETE /knowledge/{docId} must also call Vectorize deletion. Add a GDPR compliance note documenting that Analytics Engine data cannot be deleted by design — provide a DSAR API that returns all Analytics Engine data for a spaceId without deleting it.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G23" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G23</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EAB308;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EAB30818;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-billing / deduct_space_credits concurrency</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">deduct_space_credits Uses PostgreSQL FOR UPDATE Pattern That Is Unsafe Outside a Durable Object — Spec Shows Both Safe and Unsafe Implementations Simultaneously</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The spec shows deduct_space_credits as a PostgreSQL stored function with SELECT ... FOR UPDATE, which would be a race condition if implemented as a Worker-level function against any database other than a single-threaded DO: two concurrent calls both read balance=100 before either commits, both deduct 80, resulting in balance=-60. The spec simultaneously shows the correct safe SpaceDO pattern (DO single-threading provides atomicity) and the unsafe PostgreSQL pattern, creating ambiguity for the implementer. If a developer follows the PostgreSQL version without understanding the DO guarantee, they implement a double-spend vulnerability.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Explicitly document that deductCredits must only ever be a SpaceDO method and that the safety guarantee comes from DO single-threading. Add a comment: &#x27;This method is safe from race conditions ONLY because it runs inside a Durable Object. If you move this logic into a Worker or serverless function, you MUST use a distributed lock or CAS operation.&#x27; Remove the PostgreSQL stored function version entirely to eliminate implementer ambiguity. Add an ESLint rule flagging any deductCredits-pattern outside of DO class files.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G24" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G24</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EAB308;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EAB30818;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">wrangler.jsonc / broken JSONC</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">wrangler.jsonc Contains Malformed JSONC With Multi-Line // Comment and Invalid localConnectionString on DO Binding — wrangler deploy Fails to Parse</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The wrangler.jsonc queues section has no max_retries or dead_letter_queue for naelao-notifications. The hyperdrive section shows // No Hyperdrive binding on line 1 of a multi-line block, but // only comments out the remainder of that single line — subsequent lines containing { &#x27;binding&#x27;: &#x27;SPACE_DO&#x27;, &#x27;localConnectionString&#x27;: &#x27;postgresql://...&#x27; } are NOT commented out. localConnectionString is not a valid wrangler property for DO bindings (it only exists for Hyperdrive). Some wrangler versions reject the file with a parse error; others include a duplicate SPACE_DO binding that conflicts with the existing DO binding of the same name.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Remove the entire malformed comment block and the localConnectionString entry — DO bindings only need name and class_name. Replace with a single-line comment: // Hyperdrive binding removed — see SpaceDO per-product DB architecture (§22). Add max_retries: 3 and dead_letter_queue: &#x27;naelao-dlq&#x27; to the naelao-notifications consumer. Add max_retries: 3 to naelao-analytics consumer so failed analytics batches don&#x27;t silently drop. Validate the complete wrangler.jsonc by running npx wrangler deploy --dry-run in CI before any test step.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G25" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G25</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EAB308;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EAB30818;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-analytics / Analytics Engine schema</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Analytics Engine Positional Fields Have No Schema Registry — Adding a Field Silently Shifts All Subsequent Fields and Corrupts Existing Queries</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Analytics Engine data points use positional indexing: TOKEN_USAGE_BY_MODEL queries blob4 as model and double5 as total_cost_usd. The mapping from position to field name is only defined in mapEventToDataPoint(). If a developer adds a new field at position 3 in the doubles array, double5 (total_cost_usd) shifts to double6 — all existing Analytics queries silently return wrong values for cost (likely zero). No schema versioning, no compile-time check, and query strings are raw SQL with no type safety.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Create a typed schema registry file analytics-schema.ts exporting named constants: export const TOKEN_USAGE = { doubles: { inputTokens: 0, outputTokens: 1, cacheReadTokens: 2, cacheWriteTokens: 3, costUsd: 4, cacheHitRate: 5 }, blobs: { eventType: 0, userId: 1, agentId: 2, model: 3, runId: 4 } }. Use these constants in both mapEventToDataPoint() and all query strings. Add a CI test that generates a data point and verifies positional values match the schema registry. Version the schema (e.g. v1_ prefix on index names) so breaking changes require explicit migration.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-G26" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-G26</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EAB308;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EAB30818;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">naelao-knowledge / search correctness</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Knowledge Full-Text Search Uses LIKE &#x27;%term%&#x27; With No Index — O(n) Scan Over All Documents, Breaks at Scale</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The knowledge Worker&#x27;s text search fallback (used when Vectorize is unavailable or for exact-match queries) executes SELECT * FROM knowledge_docs WHERE content LIKE &#x27;%{term}%&#x27; against SpaceDO SQLite. LIKE with a leading wildcard cannot use a B-tree index and performs a full table scan. At 10,000 knowledge documents per space (common for a large knowledge base), this is a 10,000-row full scan per search query inside a DO with strict CPU budget. Additionally, the term is interpolated directly into the LIKE pattern with no escaping — a search for &#x27;50%&#x27; would be interpreted as LIKE &#x27;%50%%&#x27; (SQL wildcard) not as literal &#x27;50%&#x27;, returning incorrect results.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Enable SQLite FTS5 (full-text search) for the knowledge_docs table: CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE knowledge_fts USING fts5(title, content, content=&#x27;knowledge_docs&#x27;, content_rowid=&#x27;rowid&#x27;). Use FTS5 queries: SELECT * FROM knowledge_fts WHERE knowledge_fts MATCH ? — this is O(log n) with a full-text index. For the LIKE fallback, escape the search term before interpolation: const escaped = term.replace(/[%_\\]/g, c =&gt; `\\${c}`); then use LIKE ? ESCAPE &#x27;\\&#x27; with the escaped term as a parameter. CF DO SQLite supports FTS5 as of the 2025-01-01 compatibility date.</p></div>
</div>

<div style="margin:60px 0 0;padding:32px;background:#0A1628;border:1px solid #1E293B;border-radius:8px;">
  <p style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:#64748B;margin:0;line-height:1.8;">
    Appendix G complete. Combined gap audit total: A (125) + B (30) + C (22) + D (22) + E (24) + F (26) + G (26)
    = <strong style="color:var(--or);">275 documented technical gaps</strong> with required fixes.
    The most systemic finding in this pass: the spec contains an incomplete PostgreSQL→SpaceDO migration
    with undefined variables at 56 call sites, 5 plpgsql stored functions that cannot execute in SQLite,
    and db.query('BEGIN') transaction syntax that has no valid CF DO equivalent.
    These are not isolated bugs — they represent an architectural schism that must be resolved
    before implementation begins, or every Worker that touches data will throw on first request.
  </p>
</div>
</section>


<section id="appendix-h" style="margin:80px 0 0;padding:60px 0 0;border-top:3px solid var(--or);">
<div style="margin-bottom:32px;">
  <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;display:block;margin-bottom:8px;">Appendix H · Billing Provider Strategy</span>
  <h2 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,40px);font-weight:700;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 12px;">Lemon Squeezy Primary / Stripe Future — Provider-Agnostic Billing Architecture</h2>
  <p style="color:#94A3B8;max-width:720px;line-height:1.7;">
    The current spec hardcodes Stripe throughout the billing layer. Stripe is unavailable in many regions,
    requiring <strong style="color:var(--tx);">Lemon Squeezy as the primary provider</strong> with Stripe
    as a future addition. This appendix documents: (1) a provider-agnostic BillingProvider interface
    that makes both work without code duplication, (2) every place the spec must change to support
    Lemon Squeezy, and (3) a clean migration path for when Stripe becomes available.
  </p>

  <div style="margin:24px 0;padding:24px;background:#0A1628;border:1px solid #1E3B6A;border-radius:8px;">
    <div style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:var(--or);margin-bottom:12px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;">Provider Abstraction Interface</div>
    <pre style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;color:#94A3B8;line-height:1.7;margin:0;overflow-x:auto;"><code>// workers/naelao-billing/src/providers/types.ts
interface NormalizedBillingEvent {
  type:           'payment.success' | 'payment.failed' | 'subscription.created'
                | 'subscription.updated' | 'subscription.cancelled'
                | 'subscription.paused' | 'subscription.resumed' | 'refund.issued';
  provider:       'lemon_squeezy' | 'stripe';
  spaceId:        string;
  customerId:     string;
  subscriptionId: string | null;
  variantOrPriceId: string;
  amountCents:    number;   // always integer, always cents
  currency:       string;
  metadata:       Record&lt;string, string&gt;;
}

interface BillingProvider {
  verifyWebhook(rawBody: string, headers: Headers): Promise&lt;boolean&gt;;
  parseWebhookEvent(rawBody: string): NormalizedBillingEvent;
  createCheckout(params: CheckoutParams): Promise&lt;{ url: string }&gt;;
  getCustomerPortalUrl(subscriptionId: string): Promise&lt;string&gt;;
  cancelSubscription(subscriptionId: string): Promise&lt;void&gt;;
}

// Runtime provider selection — change BILLING_PROVIDER env var to switch
const provider: BillingProvider =
  env.BILLING_PROVIDER === 'stripe'
    ? new StripeProvider(env)
    : new LemonSqueezyProvider(env);</code></pre>
  </div>

  <div style="margin:24px 0;padding:24px;background:#0A1628;border:1px solid #1E3B6A;border-radius:8px;">
    <div style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:#22C55E;margin-bottom:12px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;">Lemon Squeezy Event Mapping</div>
    <pre style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;color:#94A3B8;line-height:1.7;margin:0;overflow-x:auto;"><code>// Lemon Squeezy → Normalized
order_created                → payment.success
order_refunded               → refund.issued
subscription_created         → subscription.created
subscription_updated         → subscription.updated
subscription_cancelled       → subscription.cancelled
subscription_paused          → subscription.paused    ← no Stripe equiv
subscription_unpaused        → subscription.resumed
subscription_payment_success → payment.success
subscription_payment_failed  → payment.failed
subscription_payment_recovered → payment.success

// spaceId path in LS webhooks
event.meta.custom_data.spaceId           // order events
event.data.attributes.custom_data.spaceId // subscription events

// Amount parsing — always parse as integer
const amountCents = parseInt(event.data.attributes.total, 10); // NOT parseFloat</code></pre>
  </div>

  <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:16px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;background:#EF444422;color:#EF4444;border:1px solid #EF444444;padding:4px 10px;border-radius:4px;">4 CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;background:#E8692A22;color:#E8692A;border:1px solid #E8692A44;padding:4px 10px;border-radius:4px;">8 HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;background:#EAB30822;color:#EAB308;border:1px solid #EAB30844;padding:4px 10px;border-radius:4px;">3 MEDIUM</span>
