  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The naelao-workflows worker loads user workflow code from R2 (const code = await codeObj.text()) then calls env.DISPATCH_NAMESPACE.get(spaceId + '-' + workflowId) to dispatch it. dispatchNamespace.get(name) retrieves a pre-deployed script by its registered script name — it does not accept or execute code dynamically. The script named spaceId + '-' + workflowId does not exist in the dispatch namespace unless it was previously uploaded via the Cloudflare Workers for Platforms Upload API. The prompt acknowledges eval() and dynamic import() are prohibited but never includes the required upload step. Every workflow dispatch call throws "Worker not found" at runtime. The prompt stores code in R2 as the "source of truth" but CF Workers for Platforms requires the code to be uploaded to the namespace separately via the CF API before dispatch is possible.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add a workflow deployment step to naelao-workflows. When a user saves or updates a workflow, the worker must upload the script to the dispatch namespace via the CF Workers for Platforms API before any dispatch can occur:

// workers/naelao-workflows/src/index.ts – deployWorkflow()
async function deployWorkflow(workflowId: string, code: string, env: Env): Promise&lt;void&gt; {
  const scriptName = env.DISPATCH_NAMESPACE_NAME + '-' + workflowId;
  const res = await fetch(
    `https://api.cloudflare.com/client/v4/accounts/${env.CF_ACCOUNT_ID}/workers/dispatch/namespaces/${env.DISPATCH_NAMESPACE_NAME}/scripts/${scriptName}`,
    { method: 'PUT', headers: { 'Authorization': 'Bearer ' + env.CF_API_TOKEN, 'Content-Type': 'application/javascript' }, body: code }
  );
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error('Deploy failed: ' + await res.text());
}
// Call deployWorkflow() on POST /workflows/:id (create/update) BEFORE storing to R2.
// Add CF_ACCOUNT_ID, CF_API_TOKEN, DISPATCH_NAMESPACE_NAME to Env and wrangler secrets.</p></div>
