  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">WorkflowRegistryDO's alarm() body ends with this.ctx.storage.setAlarm(Date.now() + 60_000) unconditionally. The register() handler also calls setAlarm() but the prompt says "set alarm if not already set" without showing the getAlarm() guard. Under concurrent workflow registrations that arrive before the first alarm fires, each registration calls setAlarm() — each call replaces the previous scheduled time. The last writer wins. If ten workflows register simultaneously and the final setAlarm() is called 59 seconds from now while earlier ones expected 10 seconds, the earlier workflows miss their window. CF Durable Objects explicitly state that setAlarm() replaces any existing alarm.</p></div>
