  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">deprovisionSpace KV Credential Deletion Issues 2000+ Individual KV Deletes — Exceeds 1000 Subrequest Limit</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">deprovisionSpace Step E enumerates credentials with kv.list({ prefix: 'cred:' + spaceId + ':' }) and deletes them individually. For a space with 2000 stored credentials this produces 2 KV list calls (1000 keys each) plus 2000 individual KV delete subrequests. Combined with R2 list/delete pagination, Vectorize batch deletes, SpaceDO calls, and registry calls, the total subrequest count easily exceeds Cloudflare's hard limit of 1000 subrequests per Worker invocation. The Worker is killed mid-execution, leaving the space in a partially deprovisioned state with orphaned credentials in KV. Additionally, kv.list() is only called once (no cursor loop), so only the first 1000 credentials are even attempted.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Use kv.list() with cursor pagination AND batch the deletes:

// workers/naelao-provisioner/src/deprovision.ts
async function deleteSpaceCredentials(spaceId: string, kv: KVNamespace): Promise&lt;void&gt; {
  let cursor: string | undefined;
  const BATCH = 100; // well under subrequest budget per iteration
  do {
    const listed = await kv.list({ prefix: 'cred:' + spaceId + ':', limit: 1000, cursor });
    // Use CF KV bulk delete if available, otherwise delete in small batches
    // to stay within subrequest budget across the full Worker invocation
    for (let i = 0; i &lt; listed.keys.length; i += BATCH) {
      await Promise.all(listed.keys.slice(i, i + BATCH).map(k =&gt; kv.delete(k.name)));
    }
