  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Admin impersonation tokens include a scope array such as ['read:spaces','read:threads','read:agents']. The naelao-agents auth middleware validates the JWT signature and extracts userId and spaceId but never reads or enforces the scope field. An impersonation token scoped to read:agents can be used to call POST /agents/run/start (start a run), POST /agents/run/:runId/cancel (cancel a run), or any other write endpoint in the agents worker. This allows an admin impersonating a user to perform actions outside the declared scope, violating least-privilege and potentially creating audit log confusion.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add scope enforcement to the agents worker auth middleware. Define a route-to-required-scope map and check it when the JWT contains a scope field:

// workers/naelao-agents/src/middleware/auth.ts
const ROUTE_SCOPES: Record&lt;string, string&gt; = {
  'POST:/agents/run/start':          'write:agents',
  'POST:/agents/run/:runId/cancel':  'write:agents',
  'GET:/agents/runs':                'read:agents',
  'GET:/agents/run/:runId':          'read:agents',
};
// In middleware, after JWT validation:
const jwt = c.get('jwt');
if (jwt.scope) { // only impersonation tokens carry scope
  const required = ROUTE_SCOPES[method + ':' + pattern];
  if (required &amp;&amp; !jwt.scope.includes(required)) {
    return c.json({ error: { code: 'FORBIDDEN_SCOPE', message: 'Token scope insufficient' } }, 403);
  }
}
