  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Lemon Squeezy Billing Webhooks Processed by Both naelao-billing and naelao-triggers — Duplicate Credit Grants</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">naelao-billing handles POST /v1/billing/webhook and credits users on payment.success events. naelao-triggers handles POST /v1/webhooks/lemon_squeezy/:spaceId and also has LEMON_SQUEEZY_WEBHOOK_SECRET in its env. The naelao-router sends /v1/billing/webhook to NAELAO_BILLING and /v1/webhooks/* to naelao-triggers — both paths are active simultaneously. When Lemon Squeezy sends an order_created event, the billing platform must only send it to one endpoint. But if a space registers a trigger on the lemon_squeezy provider in naelao-triggers, and the same event arrives at /v1/billing/webhook, both consumers execute. The naelao-billing worker grants credits AND naelao-triggers fires user-configured workflows. The billing worker grants credits correctly; the triggers worker should only fire user automation, not billing logic. The problem is if a developer misconfigures the LS webhook URL to /v1/webhooks/lemon_squeezy/:spaceId instead of /v1/billing/webhook, billing is silently skipped.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Clearly separate the two webhook surfaces in documentation and wrangler config. naelao-billing /v1/billing/webhook is the only endpoint that should be registered in the Lemon Squeezy dashboard for billing events. naelao-triggers /v1/webhooks/lemon_squeezy/:spaceId is for user-configured space-level automation (not billing). To prevent accidental double-billing, naelao-billing should forward a copy of the normalized event to naelao-triggers after credit processing is complete (fan-out pattern), rather than having LS deliver to both independently:

// 15_naelao_billing.md — after credit grant
await env.NAELAO_TRIGGERS_SERVICE.fetch('/internal/billing-event', {
  method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify({ provider: 'lemon_squeezy', event: normalizedEvent })
});
// naelao-triggers then fans out to any matching user-registered triggers — no credit logic runs there.</p></div>
