  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Queue Consumers Use Promise.allSettled Without Per-Message ack()/retry() — Failed Messages Silently Dropped</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Both naelao-notifications and naelao-analytics queue consumers use Promise.allSettled(batch.messages.map(msg =&gt; handle(msg.body, env))). allSettled() never throws, so the queue handler always returns normally. Cloudflare Queues interpret a normal return as "all messages ACKed". Failed messages (push service down, Analytics Engine timeout, etc.) are silently ACKed and permanently lost — they never enter the dead-letter queue. The DLQ configuration in wrangler is never triggered because messages are ACKed before they can be retried. The naelao-analytics fix of "send to DLQ on error" in the catch block also fails because the non-awaited writeDataPoints() (see GAP-316) means the catch block never fires.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Use explicit per-message acknowledgment:

// workers/naelao-notifications/src/index.ts
export default {
  async queue(batch: MessageBatch&lt;NotificationPayload&gt;, env: Env): Promise&lt;void&gt; {
    for (const msg of batch.messages) {
      try {
        await handleNotification(msg.body, env);
        msg.ack();
      } catch (err) {
        console.error('Notification failed, will retry:', msg.body, err);
        msg.retry(); // returns message to queue for redelivery
      }
    }
  }
};

Apply the same pattern to naelao-analytics. For the analytics worker specifically, if Analytics Engine is unavailable, retry the entire batch rather than losing data. Ensure max_retries and dead_letter_queue are set in wrangler so permanently failed messages land in the DLQ instead of disappearing.</p></div>
</div>

