  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">ctx.waitUntil() Credit Settlement Not Guaranteed — Worker Eviction Before Settlement Causes Permanent Revenue Leak</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">naelao-together-ai settles the WalletDO credit reservation via ctx.waitUntil(walletDO.settle(reservationId, actualCredits)) after returning the streaming response. CF Workers guarantee that waitUntil() extends the worker lifetime, but this is not absolute: platform incidents, aggressive eviction, or timeout overruns can terminate the worker before the settlement resolves. If settlement never completes, the 300-second reservation sweep in WalletDO refunds the credits. The user received LLM inference for free. Under high-volume concurrent streaming this is an exploitable revenue leak: a client that opens thousands of simultaneous streams and aborts them immediately forces reservations that never settle, each refunding after 5 minutes.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Make credit settlement durable by writing a settlement record to a Queue before returning the response. The Queue guarantees at-least-once delivery even if the Worker is evicted:

// workers/naelao-together-ai/src/index.ts — after streaming completes
// Instead of: ctx.waitUntil(walletDO.settle(reservationId, actualCredits))
// Do:
ctx.waitUntil(
  env.NAELAO_ANALYTICS_QUEUE.send({
    type: 'wallet_settle',
    reservationId,
    actualCredits,
    userId,
    spaceId,
    timestamp: Date.now()
  })
);
// A queue consumer (can be a new handler in naelao-analytics or a dedicated settlement worker)
// calls walletDO.settle() with at-least-once guarantee.
// WalletDO settle() must be idempotent on reservationId to handle duplicate deliveries.</p></div>
</div>

