  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">space_credits Table Defined Differently in SpaceDO vs schema.ts — Missing Columns Cause NULL Reads at Runtime</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">07b_SpaceDO.md defines space_credits with columns: space_id, balance_credits, daily_spent_credits, daily_reset_at (TEXT), monthly_budget_credits, platform_daily_ceiling, updated_at (TEXT). 07c_schema.ts defines space_credits with: space_id, balance_credits NOT NULL, reserved_credits NOT NULL, daily_spent_credits NOT NULL, daily_limit_credits NOT NULL DEFAULT 1000000, daily_reset_at INTEGER NOT NULL, updated_at INTEGER NOT NULL. The two schemas diverge on: (1) 07b has monthly_budget_credits and platform_daily_ceiling not in 07c; (2) 07c has reserved_credits and daily_limit_credits not in 07b; (3) timestamp type is TEXT in 07b vs INTEGER in 07c; (4) 07c has NOT NULL constraints absent from 07b. The deployed DO will use one schema. Code from the other prompt reading non-existent columns gets NULL silently. Credit limit enforcement via daily_limit_credits will always pass (NULL &gt; any integer is false in SQLite comparisons with NULL = no enforcement).</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Canonicalize on the 07c_schema.ts definition as the source of truth. Update 07b_SpaceDO.md to use the identical column set:

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS space_credits (
  space_id            TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  balance_credits     INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
  reserved_credits    INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
  daily_spent_credits INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
  daily_limit_credits INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1000000,
  daily_reset_at      INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,   -- unix ms
  updated_at          INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0    -- unix ms
);

Remove monthly_budget_credits and platform_daily_ceiling from the space_credits table — these belong in a separate space_billing_config table if needed. Read PLATFORM_DAILY_CREDIT_CEILING from the env var (already done in WalletDO). Ensure all timestamp reads/writes in SpaceDO use Date.now() (integer) not new Date().toISOString() (text).</p></div>
</div>

