  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">deprovisionSpace KV Credential Deletion Uses Single kv.list() — No Cursor Pagination, First 1000 Only</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Separate from the subrequest budget issue in GAP-302, Step E of deprovisionSpace calls kv.list({ prefix: 'cred:' + spaceId + ':' }) once with no cursor loop. KV list returns a maximum of 1000 keys per call. For enterprise spaces with more than 1000 stored credentials, only the first 1000 are deleted. The remaining credentials persist in KV indefinitely as orphaned data. For GDPR compliance (right to erasure), this is a data leak: deleted space data survives in KV with no cleanup mechanism. The R2 deletion in the same function correctly implements cursor pagination with do { } while (cursor) — the same pattern is absent for KV.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add cursor pagination to the KV credential deletion loop in deprovision.ts:

// workers/naelao-provisioner/src/deprovision.ts – Step E
let cursor: string | undefined;
do {
  const listed = await env.NAELAO_CONFIG_KV.list({
    prefix: 'cred:' + spaceId + ':',
    limit: 1000,
    cursor
  });
  await Promise.all(listed.keys.map(k =&gt; env.NAELAO_CONFIG_KV.delete(k.name)));
  cursor = listed.list_complete ? undefined : listed.cursor;
} while (cursor);

Note: for spaces with &gt;1000 credentials, combine this fix with the subrequest budget fix from GAP-302 (staged deletion via queue messages) to avoid hitting the 1000-subrequest-per-invocation ceiling.</p></div>
</div>

