  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Analytics Engine writeDataPoints() Called Without await — Rejections Unhandled, DLQ Fallback Never Fires</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">In 19_naelao_analytics.md the queue consumer calls env.NAELAO_ANALYTICS.writeDataPoints(points) without await. Analytics Engine writeDataPoints() is asynchronous. Without await: (1) if the call rejects, the rejection is unhandled — the surrounding try/catch does not catch asynchronous rejections from non-awaited promises; (2) the catch block that sends failed events to the DLQ never executes even when Analytics Engine is down; (3) the queue handler returns before the write completes, so the message is ACKed (per allSettled) before it is known whether the write succeeded. The entire DLQ fallback mechanism is broken.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add await and combine with the per-message ack fix from GAP-307:

// workers/naelao-analytics/src/index.ts
export default {
  async queue(batch: MessageBatch&lt;AnalyticsEvent&gt;, env: Env): Promise&lt;void&gt; {
    const points = batch.messages.map(m =&gt; mapEventToDataPoint(m.body));
    for (const msg of batch.messages) {
      try {
        await env.NAELAO_ANALYTICS.writeDataPoints([mapEventToDataPoint(msg.body)]);
        msg.ack();
      } catch (err) {
        console.error('Analytics write failed:', err);
        msg.retry(); // requeue for retry up to max_retries, then DLQ
      }
    }
  }
};
// If batching writes is important for throughput, write in groups of 20 and retry the group on failure.</p></div>
</div>

