  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">KV Rate Limit Counter is Non-Atomic — Concurrent Burst Allows Brute Force Bypass</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">naelao-auth rate-limits login attempts via a KV counter keyed rl:login:&lt;ip&gt;. The implementation reads the current count, checks it against the limit, increments, and writes back. KV writes are not atomic. Under concurrent requests: 100 simultaneous login attempts all read count=0, all pass the check, and all write count=1. The effective limit is never enforced against burst traffic. An attacker sending 100 parallel requests to /v1/auth/login can brute force passwords indefinitely by always sending requests in concurrent bursts, as each burst sees count=0.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Replace the KV counter with a Durable Object for atomic counting, or use Cloudflare's built-in Rate Limiting API (if available on the plan):

Option A — Rate Limiting DO (always available):
// workers/naelao-auth/src/rate-limit.ts
export class RateLimitDO implements DurableObject {
  private count = 0; private resetAt = 0;
  async fetch(req: Request): Promise&lt;Response&gt; {
    const now = Date.now();
    if (now &gt; this.resetAt) { this.count = 0; this.resetAt = now + 900_000; }
    this.count++;
    return Response.json({ allowed: this.count &lt;= 10, count: this.count });
  }
}
// In naelao-auth login handler:
const id = env.RATE_LIMIT_DO.idFromName('rl:login:' + ip);
const { allowed } = await env.RATE_LIMIT_DO.get(id).fetch('/').then(r =&gt; r.json());
if (!allowed) return c.json({ error: { code: 'RATE_LIMITED' } }, 429);

Option B — Cloudflare Rate Limiting binding (requires paid plan):
Add to wrangler.jsonc: { "rate_limits": [{ "binding": "LOGIN_RATE_LIMIT", "namespace_id": "&lt;id&gt;" }] }</p></div>
</div>

<div id="GAP-315" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
