    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">25_naelao_router.md / 05_naelao_auth.md</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Router Auth Middleware Double-Hops Every Request Through naelao-auth — Revocation Check Inconsistency and Single Point of Failure</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">naelao-router's auth middleware calls NAELAO_AUTH service binding GET /v1/auth/me on every authenticated request to verify the JWT. This is a double-hop: router validates the JWT via auth-worker, then the router forwards the request to the target worker. Every authenticated request incurs 2x latency. More critically: if naelao-auth is down or cold-starting, 100% of authenticated requests fail — naelao-auth becomes a single point of failure for the entire platform. Additionally, naelao-router performs a KV revocation check (revoked:userId:spaceId) before calling auth-worker. Service Binding calls that bypass the router (worker-to-worker internal calls) skip both the revocation check and the auth-worker verification entirely, creating a gap where a revoked member can still reach internal endpoints.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Verify JWTs locally in naelao-router without calling naelao-auth. The JWT secret (NAELAO_JWT_SECRET) is already an env var. Use Web Crypto to verify HMAC-SHA256 inline:

// workers/naelao-router/src/middleware/auth.ts
import { verifyJwt } from '../../naelao-auth/src/jwt'; // shared util via package
// OR inline the verification — it's 10 lines of Web Crypto
const payload = await verifyJwtLocally(token, env.NAELAO_JWT_SECRET);
// No network hop needed — JWT is self-contained.

Reserve naelao-auth calls for token refresh, login, and logout only. For revocation, write revoked:userId:spaceId into SpaceDO (strongly consistent) and check it via a SpaceDO stub in the router middleware. This removes the auth-worker as a SPOF and cuts per-request latency by ~10ms.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="GAP-316" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
