    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">GAP-316</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#E8692A;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">20_naelao_triggers.md / 14_naelao_mcp_hub.md</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">SSRF via MCP Hub App Worker URL — User-Controlled App Worker URLs Fetch Internal CF Metadata Endpoints</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">naelao-mcp-hub forwards tool calls to "App Workers" via fetch() using a URL retrieved from SpaceDO. If the App Worker URL is user-controllable (set when registering an app), an attacker who can register an app with a malicious URL causes the MCP hub to fetch arbitrary URLs. Cloudflare Workers can reach internal metadata endpoints (169.254.169.254 on some CF network paths), other internal CF services, or other customers' workers. The prompt does not show URL validation before the fetch() call. Similarly, naelao-triggers webhook forwarding uses :provider from the URL path — if the trigger configuration allows a user to set an arbitrary forwarding URL, the triggers worker can be used as an SSRF proxy.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Validate App Worker URLs at registration time and at call time:

// workers/naelao-mcp-hub/src/index.ts – before fetch()
function validateAppWorkerUrl(url: string): void {
  const parsed = new URL(url); // throws on invalid URL
  // Only allow HTTPS
  if (parsed.protocol !== 'https:') throw new Error('App Worker URL must use HTTPS');
  // Block internal/private IP ranges and CF metadata endpoints
  const blocked = ['169.254.', '10.', '172.16.', '192.168.', 'localhost', '127.'];
  if (blocked.some(prefix =&gt; parsed.hostname.startsWith(prefix))) {
    throw new Error('App Worker URL cannot target internal addresses');
  }
  // Only allow *.workers.dev or customer-registered domains (stored in an allowlist)
  if (!parsed.hostname.endsWith('.workers.dev') &amp;&amp; !isAllowlistedDomain(parsed.hostname)) {
    throw new Error('App Worker URL not in allowlist');
  }
}
// Apply the same validation in naelao-triggers for any user-configurable forwarding URLs.</p></div>
</div>
