<div id="GAP-317" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">GAP-317</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EAB308;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EAB30818;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">26_naelao_portal_router.md</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Portal Router In-Memory Route Cache Is Not Shared Across Worker Instances — Cache Is Ineffective and Inconsistent</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">naelao-portal-router caches portal route lookups in a module-level Map with a 60-second TTL to reduce KV reads. Cloudflare Workers are not singletons: Cloudflare runs multiple isolate instances simultaneously across PoPs and scales them horizontally. Each instance has its own independent Map. A request routed to isolate A sees the cached route; a request routed to isolate B sees nothing. The cache provides no meaningful hit rate benefit. Worse, when a portal route is updated in KV, some isolates continue serving the old route for up to 60 seconds while others immediately serve the new route, creating inconsistent behavior visible to end users depending on which CF PoP handles their request.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Remove the in-memory Map cache. KV reads are fast (~1ms) and globally consistent within 60 seconds. For a portal router whose purpose is mapping slugs/hostnames to spaceIds, the KV read cost is negligible and consistency is more important than a cache that provides no real benefit across isolates. If caching is truly needed, use a Durable Object as a shared cache (one DO instance per portal slug, with a short TTL stored in DO SQLite). Alternatively, accept the KV eventual consistency window and document it as expected behavior — routes take up to 60 seconds to propagate globally after update.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="GAP-318" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
