    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">GAP-318</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EAB308;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EAB30818;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">27_naelao_artifact.md</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Artifact R2 Key and KV Metadata Key Lack Namespace — Artifact IDs Are Not Scoped per Space, Enabling Enumeration</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Artifacts are stored in R2 under artifacts/&lt;spaceId&gt;/&lt;artifactId&gt;.&lt;ext&gt; and metadata in KV under artifact:&lt;artifactId&gt;. The artifactId is presumably a UUID, but the KV metadata key includes no spaceId prefix. Two consequences: (1) the KV namespace is flat across all spaces — if any service leaks an artifactId, the metadata is accessible without knowing the spaceId; (2) listing KV keys with prefix artifact: exposes artifact IDs from all spaces. The ownership check "verify requester's spaceId matches artifact.spaceId" is correct for direct access but fails to prevent enumeration by an attacker who guesses or lists artifact IDs. Additionally, the artifact content-type detection from file extension in the GET handler, if the extension comes from user-supplied type stored in KV metadata without strict validation, could serve crafted MIME types.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Namespace the KV metadata key by spaceId:

// Change KV key from: artifact:&lt;artifactId&gt;
// To: artifact:&lt;spaceId&gt;:&lt;artifactId&gt;

// GET /v1/artifacts/:artifactId — extract spaceId from JWT, build scoped key:
const meta = await env.NAELAO_ARTIFACT_KV.get('artifact:' + spaceId + ':' + artifactId, 'json');
if (!meta) return c.json({ error: { code: 'NOT_FOUND' } }, 404);

// POST /v1/artifacts — store with scoped key:
await env.NAELAO_ARTIFACT_KV.put('artifact:' + spaceId + ':' + artifactId, JSON.stringify(metadata));

For content-type, use an explicit allowlist: const ALLOWED_TYPES = { html: 'text/html', js: 'text/javascript', css: 'text/css', json: 'application/json', png: 'image/png', jpg: 'image/jpeg' }; Never serve application/octet-stream for unknown types — return 400 instead.</p></div>
</div>

