  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">billingProvider Created Outside Handler for Reuse — No Problem With Reuse, But Secret Selection Logic for verifyWebhook Is Undocumented</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">naelao-billing creates the billingProvider instance at module scope ("CRITICAL: billingProvider const must be created outside the handler to reuse"). The provider instance is reused across requests correctly. However, the verifyWebhook(rawBody, headers, secret) call in the webhook handler never specifies which secret variable to pass. For BILLING_PROVIDER='lemon_squeezy' the correct secret is env.LEMON_SQUEEZY_WEBHOOK_SECRET; for 'stripe' it is env.STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET. Without explicit documentation, a code generator may pass the wrong secret (e.g., always passing LEMON_SQUEEZY_WEBHOOK_SECRET regardless of provider), which would cause webhook verification to silently fail for Stripe webhooks (signature mismatch) or to succeed with the wrong secret for LS webhooks during provider migration. This is low severity because the fix is trivially obvious once flagged, but it is a real failure mode during a provider switch.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Make the secret selection explicit in 15_naelao_billing.md. The BillingProvider interface's verifyWebhook should not take a secret parameter — each provider implementation reads its own secret from the Env it was constructed with:

// packages/billing-providers/src/types.ts
interface BillingProvider {
  verifyWebhook(rawBody: string, headers: Headers): Promise&lt;boolean&gt;; // no secret param
  // ...
}

// packages/billing-providers/src/lemon-squeezy.ts
class LemonSqueezyProvider implements BillingProvider {
  constructor(private env: { LEMON_SQUEEZY_WEBHOOK_SECRET: string }) {}
  async verifyWebhook(rawBody: string, headers: Headers): Promise&lt;boolean&gt; {
    return verifyHmacSha256(rawBody, headers.get('X-Signature') ?? '', this.env.LEMON_SQUEEZY_WEBHOOK_SECRET);
  }
}

// workers/naelao-billing/src/index.ts
const provider = createBillingProvider(env); // provider self-selects its own secret
const verified = await provider.verifyWebhook(rawBody, request.headers); // no secret arg needed</p></div>
