  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">SandboxDO Eviction Leaves containerRef=null While SQLite Says "running" — All exec() Calls Return 409 After DO Wakes</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">SandboxDO stores the running container reference as an in-memory class field: private containerRef: SandboxStub | null = null. When the DO is evicted from memory (after ~30s idle or under memory pressure) and then woken by a subsequent request, the DO is reconstructed fresh with containerRef = null. The container_state SQLite table still says status = 'running' because the container itself may still be alive in CF's container infrastructure.

ensureRunning() checks: if (status === 'running' && this.containerRef) — because containerRef is null after reconstruction, this check fails even though the container is running. ensureRunning() then calls getSandbox() and mountBucket() again, potentially creating a duplicate container or re-mounting.

exec() checks: if (!this.containerRef) return 409 — but ensureRunning() was already called and returned 'already_running' (state said running) without re-populating containerRef. So exec() will return 409 every time after a DO eviction, permanently blocking any sandbox tool execution for that project until the container is explicitly stopped and restarted.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">ensureRunning() must re-acquire containerRef whenever it is null, regardless of what the state table says:

private async ensureRunning(request: Request): Promise&lt;Response&gt; {
  const { spaceId, projectId } = await request.json();
  const status = this.ctx.storage.sql
    .exec("SELECT value FROM container_state WHERE key = 'status'").one()?.value as string;

  if (status === 'running' &amp;&amp; this.containerRef) {
    this.lastActiveAt = Date.now();
    return Response.json({ status: 'already_running' });
  }

  // CRITICAL FIX: containerRef is null after DO eviction — re-acquire even if state says 'running'
  const containerName = this.buildContainerName(spaceId, projectId);
  const sandbox = getSandbox(this.env.NAELAO_SANDBOX, containerName);
  this.containerRef = sandbox;  // re-acquire the stub
  this.lastActiveAt = Date.now();

  if (status === 'running') {
    // Container was already running; stub re-acquired — no need to re-mount
    return Response.json({ status: 'reconnected' });
  }

  // ... normal start path: mountBucket, exec sync script, update state, setAlarm
}</p></div>
</div>

