  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">validateContainerPath() Uses Node.js require('path') — Throws ReferenceError in CF Workers</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The validateContainerPath() function in §25 (called by exec() on every Tier 5 tool call) uses:

function validateContainerPath(agentPath: string): string {
  const { resolve, normalize } = require('path');
  ...
}

CF Workers do not support CommonJS require(). Node.js built-in modules like 'path' are not available via require() in CF Workers runtime. This code throws ReferenceError: require is not defined on the very first Tier 5 tool execution. Path traversal is therefore completely unprotected — any path passed by the agent executes in the container without sanitization.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Implement path traversal validation without require('path') using pure string operations valid in CF Workers:

function validateContainerPath(agentPath: string): string {
  const WORKSPACE_ROOT = '/workspace';
  // Resolve '..' segments manually — no require('path') needed
  const parts = agentPath.split('/');
  const resolved: string[] = [];
  for (const part of parts) {
    if (part === '..') resolved.pop();
    else if (part !== '.' &amp;&amp; part !== '') resolved.push(part);
  }
  const normalized = resolved.join('/');
  const absolute = agentPath.startsWith('/')
    ? '/' + normalized
    : WORKSPACE_ROOT + '/' + normalized;
  // Canonicalize and block traversal outside /workspace
  if (!absolute.startsWith(WORKSPACE_ROOT + '/') &amp;&amp; absolute !== WORKSPACE_ROOT) {
    throw new Error('Path traversal blocked: "' + agentPath + '" resolves outside /workspace');
  }
  return absolute;
}</p></div>
