  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">wrapArtifactCode() React Type Generates Worker Script Containing JSX — JSX Cannot Execute at Runtime in CF Workers</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The wrapArtifactCode() function in §18 generates a React artifact serving Worker:

return `
import { renderToString } from 'react-dom/server';
${code}

export default {
  fetch(request) {
    const html = renderToString(&lt;App /&gt;);  // ← RAW JSX
    ...
  }
}`;

Two fatal problems: (1) JSX syntax (&lt;App /&gt;) is not valid JavaScript — it requires a transpilation step (Babel or esbuild) to convert to React.createElement() calls. CF Workers execute JavaScript/WASM, not JSX. The runtime will throw a SyntaxError when it tries to parse the &lt;App /&gt; expression. (2) import { renderToString } from 'react-dom/server' — this npm package is not available in CF Workers without explicit bundling. Dynamic imports of npm packages at runtime in Workers for Platforms scripts are not supported unless the package was bundled at upload time. Both issues make React artifacts completely non-functional.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">React artifacts must be transpiled at artifact creation time, not wrapped in raw JSX. wrapArtifactCode() for 'react' type must:

1. Use esbuild (available in CF Workers via the esbuild WASM build) or pre-bundle react/react-dom into the script.
2. Transpile JSX to React.createElement() before storing in R2.
3. The simplest practical fix: React artifacts are stored as pre-rendered static HTML (the agent renders them server-side during creation using a Node.js build step), not as dynamic Worker scripts.

// Recommended: treat React artifacts as static HTML, not dynamic Workers
function wrapReactArtifact(renderedHtml: string): string {
  // renderedHtml is pre-rendered HTML passed from the agent's build step
  const escaped = renderedHtml
    .replace(/&amp;/g, '&amp;amp;').replace(/"/g, '&amp;quot;')
    .replace(/&lt;/g, '&amp;lt;').replace(/&gt;/g, '&amp;gt;');
  return `&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style="margin:0"&gt;
    &lt;iframe sandbox="allow-scripts" srcdoc="${escaped}"
      style="width:100%;height:100%;border:0;"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;`;
}</p></div>
