  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">naelao-analytics Queue Consumer ACKs All Messages Before writeDataPoints() — DLQ Fallback Is Bypassed on AE Write Failure</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The §56 naelao-analytics Worker implementation shows:

for (const msg of batch.messages) {
  const dp = mapEventToDataPoint(msg.body);
  if (dp) dataPoints.push(dp);
  msg.ack();  // ← ACK happens here, BEFORE writeDataPoints
}
if (dataPoints.length > 0) {
  await env.NAELAO_ANALYTICS.writeDataPoints(dataPoints);  // ← failure here loses all data
}

All messages are ACKed before the batch write to Analytics Engine. If writeDataPoints() fails (AE outage, malformed data, rate limit), all messages have already been positively acknowledged and will not be redelivered. The catch block that sends to DLQ is unreachable because the messages are already committed. This silently drops the entire analytics batch with no retry path — billing events, agent run events, and security events are lost permanently.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Attempt the write BEFORE ACKing. Use per-message retry on failure:

export default {
  async queue(batch: MessageBatch&lt;NaelaoAnalyticsEvent&gt;, env: Env): Promise&lt;void&gt; {
    const dataPoints = batch.messages.map(msg =&gt; mapEventToDataPoint(msg.body)).filter(Boolean);
    try {
      if (dataPoints.length > 0) {
        await env.NAELAO_ANALYTICS.writeDataPoints(dataPoints);
      }
      // Only ACK after successful write
      for (const msg of batch.messages) msg.ack();
    } catch (err) {
      // Write failed — retry all messages (they have not been ACKed)
      console.error('[analytics] writeDataPoints failed, retrying batch:', err);
      for (const msg of batch.messages) msg.retry();
      // DLQ fallback for security events if retry budget is exhausted (handled by queue dead-letter config)
    }
    // Security event KV backup (unchanged — runs after AE write attempt)
    for (const msg of batch.messages) {
      if (msg.body.event_type?.startsWith('security_')) {
        await env.NAELAO_CONFIG_KV.put('sec-event:' + Date.now() + ':' + msg.body.event_type,
          JSON.stringify(msg.body), { expirationTtl: 86400 * 30 });
      }
    }
  }
};</p></div>
