  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Admin Dashboard AE SQL Uses PostgreSQL INTERVAL Syntax — Invalid in Workers Analytics Engine SQL Dialect</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The four admin dashboard queries in §56 all use PostgreSQL-style interval arithmetic:

WHERE timestamp > NOW() - INTERVAL '30 days'
WHERE timestamp > NOW() - INTERVAL '7 days'
WHERE timestamp > NOW() - INTERVAL '24 hours'

Workers Analytics Engine uses a custom SQL dialect that is NOT PostgreSQL. The INTERVAL '30 days' syntax is PostgreSQL-specific and will cause a parse error in AE SQL. All four dashboard queries — token usage by model, run success rate, tool usage heatmap, and security events — will fail to execute, returning zero data for the admin dashboard.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Use the correct AE SQL time-filtering syntax. Workers AE supports toTimestamp() and integer arithmetic on the timestamp field:

-- WRONG (PostgreSQL):
WHERE timestamp > NOW() - INTERVAL '30 days'

-- CORRECT (Workers AE SQL):
WHERE timestamp > toTimestamp(toUnixTimestamp(NOW()) - 30 * 86400)

-- Or use the AE-native date_diff approach:
WHERE date_diff('day', timestamp, NOW()) &lt;= 30

-- Practical fix — use epoch arithmetic (most portable):
WHERE timestamp > toTimestamp(toUnixTimestamp(NOW()) - 2592000)  -- 30 * 86400 = 2592000

Apply this substitution in all four query constants:
  TOKEN_USAGE_BY_MODEL: 30 * 86400
  RUN_SUCCESS_RATE: 7 * 86400
  TOOL_USAGE_HEATMAP: 7 * 86400
  SECURITY_EVENTS_24H: 86400</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-J09" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
