  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">listMarketplace() Directly Interpolates filter.maxPrice Into SQL String — SQL Injection in DO SQLite</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">SpaceTypeRegistryDO.listMarketplace() builds a SQL query with direct string interpolation:

if (filter?.maxPrice !== undefined) {
  query += ` AND price_usd <= ${filter.maxPrice}`;
}
return this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(query).toArray();

Although the TypeScript type says maxPrice: number, any value that survives JSON.parse() deserialization and reaches this code — including NaN, Infinity, -Infinity, or a crafted input on an unvalidated API — gets interpolated directly into the SQL string. SQLite will evaluate `price_usd &lt;= NaN` as always-false (no rows) or `price_usd &lt;= Infinity` as always-true (all rows). More critically, if an API boundary fails to enforce the numeric type, a string like `0 OR 1=1` would turn the query into a tautology, bypassing the status/visible filters and returning unapproved or suspended space types.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Use parameterized queries for all runtime values, including numeric filters:

async listMarketplace(filter?: { tags?: string[]; maxPrice?: number }): Promise&lt;SpaceTypeListing[]&gt; {
  const params: (string | number)[] = ['approved', 1];
  let where = "WHERE status = ? AND visible = ?";

  if (filter?.maxPrice !== undefined) {
    const maxPrice = Number(filter.maxPrice);  // enforce numeric, rejects NaN/Infinity
    if (!isFinite(maxPrice) || maxPrice &lt; 0) throw new Error('Invalid maxPrice');
    where += ' AND price_usd &lt;= ?';
    params.push(maxPrice);
  }

  const query = `SELECT id, name, description, author, current_version,
    price_usd, install_count, rating_avg, rating_count
    FROM space_types ${where} ORDER BY install_count DESC LIMIT 100`;

  return this.ctx.storage.sql.exec&lt;SpaceTypeListing&gt;(query, ...params).toArray();
}</p></div>
