    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">§45 — WalletDO (x402 Inter-Space Payment)</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">x402 Payment Flow Is Non-Atomic — Debit Can Succeed While Creator Credit Fails, With No Rollback</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The x402 inter-space payment flow in §45 consists of three sequential DO-to-DO RPC calls:

1. POST http://wallet/deduct → company WalletDO (deducts full amountUsd)
2. POST http://workerdef/record-earning → creator WorkerDefinitionDO (credits amountUsd * 0.85)
3. NAELAO_ANALYTICS_QUEUE.send() → platform fee recorded

The spec itself notes "(NOT atomic — sequential RPCs)" but provides no fix. If step 1 succeeds but step 2 fails (creator DO unavailable, network error, creator DO evicted mid-call), the user pays but the creator is never paid. There is no compensation transaction, no idempotency key, and no retry mechanism. This creates an invisible fund leak: money leaves the payer's wallet and disappears into the platform's accounting gap. At scale, this silently accumulates as unresolvable accounting discrepancies.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Implement a saga pattern with compensation. Use an idempotency key and a payment coordinator record:

// WalletDO.processX402Payment(params) — transactional saga
async processX402Payment(params: {
  paymentId: string;  // idempotency key — include in both debit and credit
  amountUsd: number;
  creatorSpaceId: string;
  workerDefId: string;
}): Promise&lt;{ success: boolean; error?: string }&gt; {
  // Check idempotency — already processed?
  const existing = this.ctx.storage.sql
    .exec('SELECT status FROM payment_log WHERE id = ?', params.paymentId).one();
  if (existing?.status === 'complete') return { success: true };

  // Record intent BEFORE debit
  this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(
    'INSERT OR IGNORE INTO payment_log (id, amount_usd, creator_space_id, status) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)',
    params.paymentId, params.amountUsd, params.creatorSpaceId, 'pending'
  );

  // Step 1: Debit
  const debitResult = await this.deductCredits({ amount: params.amountUsd, reason: 'x402:' + params.paymentId });
  if (!debitResult.success) return { success: false, error: debitResult.error };

  // Step 2: Credit creator — retry up to 3 times
  let credited = false;
  for (let attempt = 0; attempt &lt; 3 &amp;&amp; !credited; attempt++) {
    try {
      const creatorDO = this.env.NAELAO_WALLET_DO.get(
        this.env.NAELAO_WALLET_DO.idFromName('wallet:' + params.creatorSpaceId));
      await creatorDO.fetch(new Request('http://wallet/credit', {
        method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify({ paymentId: params.paymentId, amount: params.amountUsd * 0.85 })
      }));
      credited = true;
    } catch { /* retry */ }
  }
  if (!credited) {
    // Compensate: refund the debit
    await this.creditCredits({ amount: params.amountUsd, reason: 'x402-refund:' + params.paymentId });
    this.ctx.storage.sql.exec("UPDATE payment_log SET status='failed' WHERE id=?", params.paymentId);
    return { success: false, error: 'Creator credit failed after 3 attempts — payment refunded' };
  }
  this.ctx.storage.sql.exec("UPDATE payment_log SET status='complete' WHERE id=?", params.paymentId);
  return { success: true };
}</p></div>
</div>

