In CF Workers, when the outer fetch() handler returns a Response, the runtime terminates any pending microtasks or promises that were not registered with ctx.waitUntil(). A bare void expression is not registered. The HTTP response is sent to the client ({"messageId":..., "mode":"foreground"}) and then the agentDO.fetch() call is silently abandoned. The agent run never executes. The UI shows the user message as sent, the runId is returned, but no LLM call ever happens. This is a silent hang — users see their message accepted but never get a response.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Register the foreground dispatch with ctx.waitUntil() so it survives the Response return:

// In POST /threads/:id/messages handler — context must be passed to the route handler
app.post('/threads/:id/messages', async (c) =&gt; {
  // ...validate, persist user message, check concurrency...
  const runId = crypto.randomUUID();

  // Foreground mode: fire-and-keep-alive with ctx.waitUntil
  const agentDO = c.env.NAELAO_AGENT_DO.get(
    c.env.NAELAO_AGENT_DO.idFromName(spaceId + ':' + projectId + ':' + threadId)
  );
  c.executionCtx.waitUntil(
    agentDO.fetch(new Request('http://agent/run', {
      method: 'POST',
      body: JSON.stringify({ threadId, runId, spaceId, userId })
    }))
  );

  return c.json({ messageId, runId, mode: 'foreground' });
});

