<section id="appendix-k" style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(32px,6vw,80px) clamp(16px,4vw,48px);">
<h2 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(22px,4vw,36px);font-weight:700;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 8px;">Appendix K — Additional Technical Gap Audit (Third Pass)</h2>
<p style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;color:#64748B;margin:0 0 32px;line-height:1.7;">
  Third-pass gap analysis of the full Naelao architecture spec (naelao_expanded_gaps_resolved.html). This pass covered sections not fully analyzed in prior passes: §04 AgentDO, §05 AssistantDO, §17 fine-tuning, §22 artifacts, §29 billing, §30 ConcurrencyDO, §31 knowledge, §35 SandboxDO, §40 LocalTunnelDO, §43 sweeper, §45 WalletDO skills, §49 MiniAGIDO, §56 bootstrap, §57 SpaceDO methods, §62 provisioner, §70–71 enterprise wallet/x402, §72 Mini-AGI, §76 canary, §77 apps, §78 admin, §79 notifications, §80 eval, §81 categorizer/feedback, §82 templates/workflows/FinetuneJobDO, §84 SpaceDO, §85 AssistantSandboxDO.
  This pass identified 51 new gaps: 12 CRITICAL, 25 HIGH, 13 MEDIUM, 1 LOW.
  Gaps G-K14, G-K25, and G-K29 confirm findings from G-J14, G-J09, and G-J04 respectively — same root cause, different spec sections.
</p>

<div id="G-K01" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-K01</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">§29 — naelao-billing Worker</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">naelao-billing Uses PostgreSQL Manual Transaction Syntax That Has No Effect in SpaceDO SQLite — Non-Atomic Billing Updates</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The billing worker executes three sequential INSERT/UPDATE statements wrapped in:
  await db.query('BEGIN');
  // ... three INSERT/UPDATE queries ...
  await db.query('COMMIT');
  // catch: await db.query('ROLLBACK');

On D1 or SpaceDO SQLite, multi-statement manual transactions via separate .query() calls are not supported — D1 requires db.batch([...stmts]) for atomicity, and SpaceDO SQLite uses this.ctx.storage.sql.exec() which auto-commits each statement. The BEGIN/COMMIT/ROLLBACK calls will either throw or execute as no-ops. The three statements (writing token_usage, space_usage_monthly, space_credits) run non-atomically. A crash between steps 2 and 3 deducts from the monthly total without deducting from the balance, causing silent billing inconsistency with no recovery path.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Replace the BEGIN/COMMIT/ROLLBACK block with a single this.ctx.storage.sql.exec() invocation using multiple statements separated by semicolons. SpaceDO Durable Objects are single-threaded: all operations within a single fetch() handler are automatically serialized, providing the atomicity guarantee without explicit transaction syntax. Example:
  this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(`
    INSERT INTO token_usage (space_id, model, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost_usd, created_at)
    VALUES (?,?,?,?,?,unixepoch('now')*1000);
    INSERT INTO space_usage_monthly (space_id, month, total_tokens, total_cost_usd)
    VALUES (?,?,?,?) ON CONFLICT (space_id, month) DO UPDATE SET
      total_tokens = total_tokens + excluded.total_tokens,
      total_cost_usd = total_cost_usd + excluded.total_cost_usd;
    UPDATE spaces SET credits_usd = credits_usd - ? WHERE id = ?;
  `, ...params);
Remove all db.query('BEGIN'), db.query('COMMIT'), db.query('ROLLBACK') calls.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-K02" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-K02</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">§29 — naelao-billing Worker</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">naelao-billing Uses $1 PostgreSQL Placeholders and NOW() / DATE_TRUNC() — All Five SQL Queries Throw at Runtime</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Every SQL query in the billing worker uses $1, $2... positional parameters (PostgreSQL syntax) and calls NOW() / DATE_TRUNC('month', NOW()). SQLite requires ? positional parameters and datetime('now') / strftime('%Y-%m-01', 'now'). At runtime, every single billing query will throw a SQLite syntax error. This makes ALL credit tracking, monthly usage aggregation, and credit deduction completely non-functional. No token usage is recorded, no monthly totals accumulate, and no credits are deducted — the entire billing system silently fails on every call.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Apply a systematic replacement across all five SQL queries in the billing flow:
  • $1, $2, $N → ? (positional placeholders)
  • NOW() → datetime('now')
  • DATE_TRUNC('month', NOW()) → strftime('%Y-%m-01', 'now')
  • TIMESTAMPTZ → INTEGER (store as milliseconds: unixepoch('now')*1000)
  • RETURNING id INTO variable → not needed in SQLite; use lastInsertRowId

The ON CONFLICT ... DO UPDATE SET ... excluded.column syntax IS valid SQLite and can be kept. Add a lint rule or CI check that flags $N placeholder syntax in any .sql file or SQL template string that targets SpaceDO.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-K03" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-K03</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">§57 — SpaceDO Methods</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">All Five 'Replacement' SpaceDO Methods Are Written as PostgreSQL plpgsql Stored Functions — Section Heading Claims Migration But Body Still Contains Supabase Source</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The spec section is titled "SpaceDO Methods — Replacing All Stored Functions" but all five functions (get_llm_formatted_messages, get_stale_projects_for_categorization, create_space_with_defaults, get_active_assistants, deduct_space_credits) are written as CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION ... LANGUAGE plpgsql SECURITY DEFINER. These are PostgreSQL RPCs using auth.uid(), DECLARE v_slug TEXT; v_slug :=, SELECT ... FOR UPDATE, RAISE EXCEPTION, gen_random_uuid(), REGEXP_REPLACE(..., 'g'), TIMESTAMPTZ, INTERVAL '24 hours', and RETURNING id INTO variable — none of which are valid SQLite. The provisioner (provisionSpace) calls db.query('SELECT create_space_with_defaults($1,...)') at Step 1. This call will fail at runtime with a SQLite error, aborting every single space creation on the platform. (See also G-K22 for the provisioner call site.)</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Rewrite all five as TypeScript methods on the SpaceDO class using this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(sql, ...params) with ? placeholders, datetime('now'), lower(hex(randomblob(16))) for UUIDs, and plain string operations for slug generation. Example for create_space_with_defaults:
  createSpaceWithDefaults(name: string, ownerId: string, spaceType: string, planTier: string) {
    const spaceId = crypto.randomUUID();
    const slug = name.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-').slice(0, 50);
    this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(
      `INSERT INTO spaces (id, name, slug, owner_id, space_type, plan_tier, created_at)
       VALUES (?,?,?,?,?,?,unixepoch('now')*1000)`,
      spaceId, name, slug, ownerId, spaceType, planTier
    );
    return spaceId;
  }
Remove all plpgsql function definitions from the spec.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-K04" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-K04</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">§40 — LocalTunnelDO</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">LocalTunnelDO.pendingCalls Is an In-Memory Map Destroyed on DO Hibernation — All In-Flight Local PC Tool Calls Hang Permanently</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">LocalTunnelDO stores pending tool-call promise resolvers in:
  private pendingCalls = new Map&lt;string, (result: ToolResult) =&gt; void&gt;();

The DO uses this.ctx.acceptWebSocket(server) (hibernation API), which means the DO hibernates between WebSocket messages. When it hibernates, the entire class instance is destroyed and pendingCalls resets to an empty Map. Any in-flight execOnLocal() call whose promise resolver was in that Map is permanently unresolvable — the agent loop hangs until the 30-second setTimeout fires (but setTimeout callbacks are also destroyed on hibernation). The sweeper marks the run abandoned after 10 minutes. Every local PC tool call that spans a DO hibernation event silently hangs.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Replace the in-memory pendingCalls Map with a SQLite table:
  CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS pending_calls (
    call_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    tool_name TEXT NOT NULL,
    params TEXT NOT NULL,
    created_at INTEGER DEFAULT (unixepoch('now')*1000)
  );

On webSocketMessage (when the local PC returns a result), look up call_id in SQLite and use a response queue or alarm-based polling instead of in-memory promise resolution. Implement a dedicated GET /poll/{callId} endpoint that the agent loop calls with retries. Add a timeout cleanup: delete FROM pending_calls WHERE created_at &lt; unixepoch('now')*1000 - 30000 in the alarm() handler.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-K05" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-K05</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">§85 — AssistantSandboxDO</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">AssistantSandboxDO.lastCommandAt and sandboxRef Are In-Memory — Alarm Fires with lastCommandAt=0 After Restart, Immediately Terminating Container and NPE-Crashing</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">private lastCommandAt = 0 and private sandboxRef: SandboxStub | null = null are both in-memory instance fields. After any DO eviction or restart: (1) alarm() fires with lastCommandAt = 0, so Date.now() - 0 &gt;= idleTimeoutMs is always true, meaning the alarm immediately tries to terminate the container; (2) this.sandboxRef is null, so this.sandboxRef.terminate() throws a null-pointer TypeError. The alarm handler crashes, is not retried, and the container may be orphaned (running but unreachable). Enterprise workloads with idleTimeoutMs = -1 (infinite) skip the terminate check, but sandboxRef is still null after restart, so any subsequent exec() call fails with "Container not running." This is the same class of bug as in SandboxDO (§35, confirmed by G-J03) but with an additional NPE in the alarm path.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Persist both lastCommandAt and container status in the DO's SQLite state table:
  // On every exec() call:
  this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(
    `INSERT OR REPLACE INTO state (key, value) VALUES ('last_command_at', ?)`,
    Date.now().toString()
  );
  // In alarm():
  const rows = [...this.ctx.storage.sql.exec('SELECT value FROM state WHERE key = ?', 'last_command_at')];
  const lastCommandAt = rows[0] ? parseInt(rows[0].value) : 0;
  if (this.sandboxRef === null) {
    const status = this.ctx.storage.sql.exec('SELECT value FROM state WHERE key = ?', 'container_status');
    if (status[0]?.value === 'running') {
      // Re-acquire sandbox reference before attempting terminate
      this.sandboxRef = await this.env.SANDBOX.get(this.ctx.storage.sql.exec('SELECT value FROM state WHERE key = ?', 'container_id')[0]?.value);
    } else return; // Nothing to terminate
  }</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-K06" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-K06</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">§29 WalletDO / §71 — x402 Inter-Space Payments</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">x402 Three-Step Cross-DO Payment Is Non-Atomic — Debit Succeeds but Credit Can Permanently Fail, Destroying Funds</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The x402Payment() function executes three sequential, independent operations:
  (1) companyWalletDO.fetch('http://wallet/deduct')
  (2) workerDefDO.fetch('http://workerdef/record-earning')
  (3) NAELAO_ANALYTICS_QUEUE.send(...)

If step 1 succeeds and step 2 fails (network error, DO unavailable, timeout), the company is permanently debited amountUsd while the creator is never paid and the platform fee is never logged. There is no saga log, no idempotency key, no compensation transaction, and no retry mechanism. The txId returned comes from the debit transaction, not a coordinated payment ID, so there is no way to reconcile the half-completed state. This can be triggered under normal production load whenever the workerDefDO is briefly unavailable.

Note: G-J12 documented a related non-atomic issue in §45 WalletDO. This gap documents the specific mechanism by which the three-step RPC fails non-atomically at the inter-space level.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Introduce a PaymentCoordinatorDO that logs a saga before any step executes:
  INSERT INTO payments (saga_id, status, debit_amount, debit_wallet, credit_wallet, credit_amount, created_at)
  VALUES (?, 'pending', ?, ?, ?, ?, unixepoch('now')*1000);

After each successful step, update status: 'pending_credit' → 'pending_log' → 'complete'. The sweeper retries rows with status='pending_credit' older than 60 seconds. Add a self-payment guard: if fromSpaceId === toCreatorSpaceId, return 400 immediately to prevent the nested DO call deadlock documented in G-K07.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-K07" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-K07</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">§29 WalletDO / §70 — Enterprise Wallet</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Nested WalletDO Calls Within the Same Request Chain Deadlock Cloudflare's Single-Threaded DO Model — Funds Lost on Self-Payment</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">When a Worker agent pays another Worker in the same space (self-hire, or same-space sub-agent), the orchestrator calls companyWalletDO.fetch(). Inside that DO's deductCredits(), the spec calls void this.recordCreatorEarning(amount * 0.15) which calls workerDefDO.fetch('http://workerdef/record-earning'). If workerDefDO and companyWalletDO happen to be the same DO instance (same idFromName result due to self-payment), the outer request holds the DO's single-thread lock while the inner fetch() waits for the same lock — permanent deadlock. The request times out at 30 seconds, the debit is already committed to SQLite, the credit never executes, and funds are permanently lost. CF Durable Objects do not support reentrant locking.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">In x402Payment(), add a guard before executing the three-step flow:
  if (fromSpaceId === toCreatorSpaceId && fromWalletId === toWorkerId) {
    return { success: false, error: 'Self-payment not allowed: same space cannot both debit and credit' };
  }

For the recordCreatorEarning call inside deductCredits(), restructure to use a fire-and-forget after the current request completes. Since DurableObjectState does not have waitUntil(), schedule the creator credit via a setAlarm(Date.now() + 1000) with the credit details persisted to SQLite, then process it in alarm(). This breaks the reentrant call chain entirely.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-K08" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-K08</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">§78 — naelao-admin</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">naelao-admin Analytics Engine Queries Are Vulnerable to SQL Injection via Unparameterized spaceId, eventType Template Interpolation</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The admin audit route constructs the Analytics Engine SQL query by string interpolation:
  WHERE index1 = '${spaceId}' AND blob1 = '${eventType}' ... LIMIT ${parseInt(limit)}

The spaceId and eventType values come directly from query parameters. An authenticated admin can inject arbitrary SQL through these parameters (e.g., spaceId = "' OR '1'='1" or eventType = "'; DROP TABLE...") to exfiltrate data across all spaces or crash the analytics pipeline. parseInt(limit) mitigates the limit injection but not the others. Since Analytics Engine SQL is a read-only query API that does not support parameterized queries, the fix requires server-side validation.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Validate spaceId against /^[0-9a-f-]{36}$/ (UUID format) before interpolation. Reject requests with non-conforming spaceId values with a 400 error. Validate eventType against a strict allowlist of known event type strings (e.g., ['agent_run', 'token_usage', 'portal_view', ...]). Validate limit with Math.min(Math.max(parseInt(limit) || 100, 1), 1000). Never interpolate free-form user input into Analytics Engine SQL strings. Implement a shared sanitizeAEParam() helper used by all Analytics Engine query builders in the admin worker.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-K09" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-K09</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">§04 AgentDO / §05 AssistantDO</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">runFiber(), fiberCtx.stash(), and onFiberRecovered() Are Not Cloudflare Platform Primitives and Do Not Exist — Every Background Agent Run Throws TypeError</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The entire background agent execution model, crash recovery, and heartbeat checkpoint system is built on this.runFiber(), fiberCtx.stash({ iteration, sessionId }), and async onFiberRecovered(ctx: FiberContext). These are described as "Project Think primitives" but are not part of the Cloudflare Durable Objects API. Cloudflare DOs have ctx.storage.setAlarm() for scheduled wakeups and CF Workflows for durable step execution, but no runFiber() method, no stash() snapshot mechanism, and no onFiberRecovered() callback. Any implementation that ships this code will throw TypeError: this.runFiber is not a function on every background agent run, making the entire async agent execution model non-functional.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Map background agent execution to CF Workflows: each step.do('iteration-N', async () => { ... }) within a Workflow provides the durability and crash-resume semantics described. Agent state (iteration count, sessionId, tool results, message history) is stored in SpaceDO SQLite as before — only the execution continuation mechanism changes. Remove all runFiber(), stash(), and onFiberRecovered() references and replace with WorkflowStep.do() calls that read/write the existing SQLite agent_runs and agent_wal schemas. Declare the agent execution Workflow class in wrangler.jsonc with [[workflows]] binding.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-K10" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-K10</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">§06 WorkerDefinitionDO / §49 MiniAGIDO</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">NAELAO_AI_GATEWAY Used as a Direct DO/SDK Binding Throughout — CF AI Gateway Is a URL Proxy, Not a Binding Type</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Throughout the spec, DOs and Workers call this.env.NAELAO_AI_GATEWAY.messages.create({ model: '...', max_tokens: 200 }) as if NAELAO_AI_GATEWAY were a Workers AI binding or SDK object. Cloudflare AI Gateway is a URL-based proxy, not a binding type — it has no binding interface and exposes no messages.create() method. The correct pattern (documented in shared/ai-client.ts) is to pass a modified baseURL to the Anthropic SDK. Two different binding name variants (env.AI_GATEWAY and env.NAELAO_AI_GATEWAY) also appear in the same codebase, one of which will be undefined at runtime. Every DO or Worker that calls .messages.create() via this binding will throw TypeError: this.env.NAELAO_AI_GATEWAY.messages is undefined.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Remove all env.NAELAO_AI_GATEWAY.messages.create() calls from DO code. Every LLM call must go through shared/ai-client.ts's createAnthropicClient(env) which sets baseURL to the gateway URL:
  const client = createAnthropicClient(env); // sets baseURL = env.NAELAO_AI_GATEWAY_URL
  const response = await client.messages.create({ model: env.MODEL_ID, ... });

Standardize on NAELAO_AI_GATEWAY_URL as a plain environment variable (string, not a binding) containing the gateway URL. Remove NAELAO_AI_GATEWAY from the wrangler.jsonc bindings sections entirely. Audit all sections using env.AI_GATEWAY vs env.NAELAO_AI_GATEWAY and consolidate to a single name.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-K11" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-K11</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#EF444418;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">§31 naelao-knowledge / §49 MiniAGIDO</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Vectorize Filter Uses Flat Object Syntax { spaceId, projectId } — Must Use { field: { $eq: value } } Operators — Silent Cross-Tenant Data Leakage</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The knowledge search queries Vectorize with filter: { spaceId: spaceId, projectId: projectId } (flat object). The actual Cloudflare Vectorize metadata filter API requires operator syntax: { spaceId: { $eq: spaceId }, projectId: { $eq: projectId } }. The flat syntax { field: value } is not valid and will either silently ignore the filter (returning unscoped results across all tenants) or throw a runtime error. If silently ignored, every knowledge search returns results from ALL spaces — causing cross-tenant data leakage where one tenant's knowledge base content is visible in another tenant's agent responses.

