  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Vectorize returnMetadata:'all' Is Not a Valid API Value — Causes Runtime Error or Silent Metadata Loss on All Knowledge Queries</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The Vectorize query call uses returnMetadata: 'all' (a string). The Cloudflare Vectorize API accepts returnMetadata: true (boolean) to return all metadata, or returnMetadata: false (default). The string value 'all' is not valid. At runtime this will either throw a type error or be coerced to true in a truthy context — but the spec cannot rely on coercion behavior. If the query returns without metadata, every match.metadata?.docName, match.metadata?.text, and match.metadata?.spaceId will be undefined, producing empty knowledge base context for every agent query across the entire platform.</p></div>
