  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">AssistantDO Uses this.ctx.waitUntil() — waitUntil() Is on ExecutionContext, Not DurableObjectState — Slack Webhook Handler Crashes</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The Slack webhook handler calls:
  this.ctx.waitUntil(asyncDODispatch());

In a Durable Object, this.ctx is DurableObjectState, which does NOT have a waitUntil() method. waitUntil() is a method on ExecutionContext (the third argument ctx in Worker fetch handlers). Calling this.ctx.waitUntil() throws TypeError: this.ctx.waitUntil is not a function, meaning the Slack webhook handler crashes before ACKing Slack's 3-second requirement. Slack retries the webhook up to 3 times, and the DO processes duplicate messages — causing duplicate agent runs for every Slack message.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">DurableObjectState does not expose waitUntil(). Restructure the Slack handler to respond immediately and then process asynchronously using DO's natural single-threaded model:
  async handleSlack(request: Request): Promise&lt;Response&gt; {
    const payload = await request.json();
    // Persist the Slack event to SQLite for async processing
    this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(
      'INSERT INTO slack_event_queue (event_id, payload, created_at) VALUES (?,?,unixepoch('now')*1000)',
      payload.event_id, JSON.stringify(payload)
    );
    // Schedule immediate alarm to process it
    this.ctx.storage.setAlarm(Date.now() + 100);
    return new Response('ok', { status: 200 }); // ACK Slack immediately
  }</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-K35" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-K35</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#F9731618;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">§72 — Mini-AGI Federated Query Loop</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Mini-AGI executeFederatedQueryLoop() Synthesizes Answer Before Writing Audit Log — DO Eviction Between Steps Permanently Loses Mandatory Audit Trail</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">executeFederatedQueryLoop() executes sequentially: (1) build secure query plan, (2) run Vectorize queries, (3) call Claude Opus synthesis (~800–1200ms), (4) call miniAgiDO.logQuery() for the mandatory audit log. Total wall-clock time: 2–5 seconds. If the DO is evicted between step 3 (answer synthesized) and step 4 (audit logged), the answer has already been sent to the user but the audit log is never written. For regulated industries (HR data, financial data), this missing audit trail is a compliance violation. The in-memory memoryContexts array containing sensitive HR/financial data is also silently lost with no recovery path.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Reverse the order to write-before-synthesize for audit integrity:
  // Step 1: Write preliminary audit entry BEFORE synthesis
  await miniAgiDO.logQuery({ queryId, status: 'in_progress', query: userQuery, timestamp: Date.now() });

  // Step 2: Synthesize answer
  const answer = await claudeClient.messages.create({ ... });

  // Step 3: Update audit entry with completed result
  await miniAgiDO.updateQueryLog({ queryId, status: 'complete', answer: answer.content });

This ensures the audit trail exists even if the DO is evicted mid-synthesis. The sweeper cleans up status='in_progress' entries older than 5 minutes.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-K36" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-K36</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#F9731618;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">§43 — naelao-sweeper</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">Sweeper Enumerates Active Assistants via KV list() with No Pagination — All Spaces Beyond 1,000 Silently Skipped</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The sweeper's sweepAssistantHeartbeats task queries the active assistant list with:
  const { keys } = await env.PRODUCT_DB_REGISTRY.list({ prefix: 'assistant:' });

KV list() returns a maximum of 1,000 keys per call. Without cursor-based pagination, any platform with more than 1,000 active spaces silently skips their assistants during heartbeat sweeps. Skipped assistants miss their scheduled cron jobs, sub-agent status checks, and memory consolidation. The keys.truncated boolean flag from the KV response is not checked, so there is no indication that keys were missed.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Implement cursor pagination to process all spaces:
  let cursor: string | undefined;
