    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-K37</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#F9731618;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">§77 — Naelao Apps / §62 SpaceTypeRegistryDO</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">AppRegistryDO and SpaceTypeRegistryDO Are Global Singleton DOs — Single-Threaded Bottleneck Under Concurrent Platform Load</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">AppRegistryDO uses idFromName('global-app-registry') and SpaceTypeRegistryDO uses idFromName('global-space-type-registry') — single DO instances serving all app installs and space type queries for the entire platform globally. Durable Objects are single-threaded. Every app install from any user anywhere in the world must be processed sequentially by this one DO. Under load (e.g., a popular app launch, a viral space type), all install requests queue up behind this single-threaded bottleneck, causing P99 latencies measured in seconds and timeout failures for concurrent installs. At 100+ concurrent installs/second, requests queue up faster than the DO can process them.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Shard the registry by a consistent hash of app_id or space_type_id. Use multiple AppRegistryDO instances:
  const shardId = parseInt(appId.slice(-2), 16) % 16; // 16 shards
  const registryDO = env.APP_REGISTRY_DO.get(
    env.APP_REGISTRY_DO.idFromName('app-registry-shard-' + shardId)
  );

Use KV to cache read-heavy operations (per-app install counts, manifests) with a 5-minute TTL. The DO only handles write operations (installs, publishes). Reads that don't require strong consistency should bypass the DO and read from KV cache directly.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-K38" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
