    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-K39</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#3B82F6;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#3B82F618;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">§24 naelao-workflows / AgentDO</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">NaelaoAgentDO ID Constructed from Three Unsanitized Components — Colon Collisions Between spaceId:projectId:threadId Can Point to Wrong DO</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">NaelaoAgentDO is named idFromName('${spaceId}:${projectId}:${threadId}') with no separator escaping. If spaceId, projectId, or threadId ever contain colons (e.g., from legacy migration data or a validation gap), two different (spaceId, projectId, threadId) triples can produce the same concatenated string:
