</div>
<div id="G-K41" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#E8692A18;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">G-K41</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#3B82F6;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;background:#3B82F618;padding:3px 8px;border-radius:3px;white-space:nowrap;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;">§82 — WorkflowRegistryDO</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">WorkflowRegistryDO sweepSchedules() Has No Idempotency Guard — Concurrent Sweeper Invocations Trigger Duplicate Workflow Runs</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">sweepSchedules() queries workflows with next_run &lt;= now, creates workflow instances, then updates next_run. If two sweeper cron invocations overlap (CF Cron is at-least-once), both reads may return the same set of due workflows before either updates next_run. Both instances then call env.NAELAO_WORKFLOW.create() for the same workflow, creating duplicate runs. CF Cron Triggers can fire multiple times within a given window if previous invocations haven't completed, making this race practically guaranteed on any busy platform.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Use SQLite atomic compare-and-swap in sweepSchedules():
  // Atomic: only update if next_run hasn't changed since we read it
  const result = this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(
    'UPDATE workflows SET next_run = ?, last_run = ? WHERE id = ? AND next_run = ?',
    nextRunTime, Date.now(), workflowId, readNextRun
  );
  // Only create workflow instance if we won the CAS
  if (result.rowsWritten > 0) {
    await env.NAELAO_WORKFLOW.create({ id: workflowRunId, params: { spaceId: this.spaceId, workflowPath: wf.r2_path } });
  }
