  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">VAPI Voice Call Configuration Hardcodes Deprecated claude-3-haiku-20240307 Model ID — Voice Alerts Will Fail or Route to Stale Model</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The VAPI phone call configuration hardcodes "model": "claude-3-haiku-20240307" (an April 2024 model). The current model lineup uses claude-haiku-4-5 (consistent with the rest of the spec). The old model ID will either be rejected by Anthropic's API (returning a model-not-found error), causing all critical voice alert calls to silently fail, or it will route to a deprecated model that may be phased out without notice. During a critical production incident, failed voice alerts can delay emergency response.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Replace "model": "claude-3-haiku-20240307" with "model": "claude-haiku-4-5" in the VAPI assistant configuration. Consider reading the model name from an environment variable:
  assistantConfig.model.model = env.VAPI_MODEL ?? 'claude-haiku-4-5';

