  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:clamp(16px,2.5vw,22px);font-weight:600;color:var(--tx);margin:0 0 16px;">SpaceDO.spaceId and rootSpaceId Are In-Memory Instance Properties Never Persisted — Lost on Every DO Restart</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">this.spaceId and this.rootSpaceId are used throughout SpaceDO methods (auth check, sub-space hierarchy queries, credential lookups) but are never persisted or re-initialized from storage in the shown code. After any DO eviction/restart, both properties are undefined, causing every method that references them to throw or return incorrect results. The auth cache's recursive CTE query WHERE id = $1 would use undefined as the spaceId, returning empty results and denying access to all space members. This bug silently breaks the entire SpaceDO on every cold start.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">In the SpaceDO constructor, initialize from persistent storage:
  constructor(ctx: DurableObjectState, env: Env) {
    this.ctx = ctx; this.env = env;
    this.ctx.blockConcurrencyWhile(async () => {
      const stored = await ctx.storage.get&lt;string&gt;('spaceId');
      if (stored) this.spaceId = stored;
    });
  }
On first POST /init: await ctx.storage.put('spaceId', spaceId); this.spaceId = spaceId;

As a resilient fallback, extract spaceId from the DO's own name string: const match = ctx.id.name?.match(/^space:([0-9a-f-]+)/); if (match) this.spaceId = match[1];</p></div>
