  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The file manager skill's write_file handler correctly acquires an advisory lock via projectDO.fetch('/acquire-lock') before modifying R2 content. However, append_to_file does NOT acquire the lock: it directly reads the R2 object, concatenates the new content, and writes it back without any lock or ETag check. Two concurrent appends to the same file will both read the same original content and each write back only their own addition — one of the two appended entries is silently discarded.</p></div>
