  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The operator shell processes postMessage events from embedded App iframes:
  if (msg.type === 'WRITE_LEARNING') {
    await uiInstructionsDO.writeLearning(msg.key, msg.value);
  }

There is no validation of msg.key against an allowlist, no maximum length on msg.value, no rate limiting, and event.origin is not verified. A malicious or compromised App iframe can: (1) flood the DO with arbitrary key/value pairs causing unbounded storage growth and cost; (2) overwrite system-level shell instruction keys that control agent behavior; (3) inject malicious content into the operator's UI learning state. Any document in the operator's browser (not just registered Apps) can send this message.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add three layers of defense:
  window.addEventListener('message', (event) => {
    // 1. Verify origin
    if (event.origin !== registeredAppOrigin) return;
    const msg = event.data;
    if (msg.type !== 'WRITE_LEARNING') return;
    // 2. Validate key against allowlist
    const ALLOWED_KEYS = ['theme-pref', 'layout-pref', 'shortcut-pref'];
    if (!ALLOWED_KEYS.includes(msg.key)) return;
    // 3. Enforce value length
    if (typeof msg.value !== 'string' || msg.value.length &gt; 512) return;
    await uiInstructionsDO.writeLearning(msg.key, msg.value);
  });
Add KV-based rate limiting: max 10 WRITE_LEARNING writes per App per minute.</p></div>
