  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">ConcurrencyDO Has No fetch() Handler But Callers Invoke It via fetch — Concurrency Gate Never Fires</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">`ConcurrencyDO` exposes only RPC-style methods (`checkAndReserve`, `heartbeat`, `releaseSlot`) and no `fetch()` handler. But naelao-threads calls `concurrencyDO.fetch(new Request('http://concurrency/check'))` and the sweeper calls `http://concurrency/release`. With no `fetch()` method the request hits the default handler (500/empty), so `if (!concurrencyCheck.ok)` never actually gates anything — the concurrency limit is silently unenforced. The `/check` call also passes no `billingTier`, so tier defaults to free regardless of plan.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Either add a `fetch()` router to ConcurrencyDO that maps `/check`→`checkAndReserve` and `/release`→`releaseSlot`, or switch all callers to direct RPC method calls on the stub. Pass the real `billingTier` so per-plan concurrency limits apply. Add a test asserting that an over-limit reservation is actually rejected.</p></div>
