  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">`read_file` with `encoding:'base64'` does `String.fromCharCode(...new Uint8Array(buf))`. Spreading a multi-MB array into function arguments exceeds the call-stack / argument-count limit and throws `RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded` for any non-trivial binary file — precisely the case base64 exists for. The identical pattern appears in the credentials `encrypt`/`decrypt` (`String.fromCharCode(...new Uint8Array(ciphertext))`).</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Convert in chunks: loop over the Uint8Array in blocks (e.g. 8 KB) building the binary string, then `btoa`, or use a streaming base64 encoder. Replace every `String.fromCharCode(...spread)` over a byte array with a chunked loop. This is a hard runtime crash, not a slow path.</p></div>
