  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Billing input validation uses `if (!inputTokens || !outputTokens) return 400`. A response with `outputTokens === 0` (a refusal, a pure tool-stop, or a cache-only turn) is falsy and gets rejected with HTTP 400, so it is never billed and the usage is lost. Conversely, legitimate accounting for zero-output turns silently disappears. Zero is a valid token count, not a missing value.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Validate type and presence, not truthiness: `if (typeof inputTokens !== 'number' || typeof outputTokens !== 'number') return 400`. Allow zero as a valid value. Bill zero-output turns at their actual input cost so cache and refusal turns are accounted for.</p></div>
