  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Vectorize Upsert and Metadata Insert Not Atomic — Orphaned Vectors on Partial Failure</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">After upserting embeddings to Vectorize, the upload handler records document metadata via a separate SpaceDO write. If the metadata insert fails (or, per other gaps, references an undefined `spaceDO`/`db`), the vectors are already stored in Vectorize but no SpaceDO row exists. The result is orphaned vectors: searchable embeddings with no owning document record, which cannot be deleted, re-indexed, or attributed, and which leak into results with no metadata to scope them.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Sequence the writes so the durable metadata record is created first (or use a compensating delete). On metadata-insert failure, delete the just-upserted vectors by ID before returning an error, so Vectorize and SpaceDO never diverge. Record a reconciliation job that periodically lists vectors with no matching SpaceDO row and removes them.</p></div>
