  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Promise.race Timeout Leaks the Timer and Never Cancels the Container exec</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">`exec()` races `sandboxRef.exec(...)` against a `setTimeout` reject. On success the timer is never cleared (leaked); on timeout the underlying container exec is never cancelled — no `AbortController` is wired in — so a 'timed-out' command keeps running inside the container, accruing billing and holding the slot, while the caller is told it failed. Wall-clock billing and the reported slot state diverge.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Wire an `AbortController` (or `AbortSignal.timeout`) into `sandboxRef.exec` so the timeout actually aborts the container command, and `clearTimeout` in a `finally` block so the timer never leaks. Reconcile billing to the actual aborted duration, not the full timeout window.</p></div>
