  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Cutover Checks Query pg_tables/auth.users — Meaningless Against DO SQLite</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">`runCutoverChecks` runs `SELECT ... FROM pg_tables WHERE rowsecurity=false`, references `auth.users`, and verifies RLS state. These are Postgres/Supabase catalogs and concepts; the target architecture is per-product DO SQLite with no `pg_tables`, no RLS, and no `auth.users`. The 'SpaceDO per-product isolation verified' check always errors or returns meaningless results, so the cutover gate provides false assurance.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Replace catalog-based checks with SpaceDO health-check method calls (per-DO row counts, schema-version reads). Drop the RLS/`pg_tables` verification entirely — isolation in this architecture is the DO boundary, not row-level security. The cutover gate must test what actually exists in production.</p></div>
