  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">SpaceDO.fetch(req) Body References Undefined `request` — ReferenceError on Hottest Path</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">`async fetch(req: Request)` declares the parameter as `req`, but the body does `const url = new URL(request.url)` referencing `request`, which is not in scope. Because `authCheck` runs on almost every platform request, this throws `ReferenceError: request is not defined` at the entry of the single hottest code path on the platform — effectively a total outage the moment the DO is exercised.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Rename to `const url = new URL(req.url)` (or rename the parameter to `request`) and audit the entire DO for `req`/`request` inconsistency. Add a smoke test that issues one real request through SpaceDO.fetch — a typo this load-bearing must be caught by the most basic test.</p></div>
