    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-O28</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§77 AppRegistryDO — handleInstall</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">App Install Count Incremented Non-Atomically — Inflates on Duplicate/Failed Installs</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">`handleInstall` inserts into `installs` and runs `UPDATE apps SET install_count = install_count + 1`, then separately writes the space-side record. The count increment is not conditioned on a genuinely new install: a re-install or a downstream failure path can still increment the counter, and the second (cross-store) write has no compensation, so the registry can show 'installed' while the SpaceDO has no record. Install counts drift upward and the two stores diverge.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Use `INSERT OR IGNORE` into `installs` and increment `install_count` only when `changes() === 1` (a real new row). Move the space-side install record into the same SpaceDO via a typed RPC within one serialized method, with rollback if it fails, so the count, the install row, and the space record commit together or not at all.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-O29" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
