<section id="appendix-p" style="padding:60px 0 40px;">
  <div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 24px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.15em;text-transform:uppercase;">Appendix P</span>
    <h2 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:36px;font-weight:700;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.02em;margin:8px 0 6px;">Eighth-Pass Technical Gap Analysis</h2>
    <p style="color:var(--tx);font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 48px;">35 new critical and high-severity gaps discovered in the eighth full-spectrum audit pass: hibernation state loss across AssistantDO, SandboxDO and ConcurrencyDO; non-atomic cross-DO payment flows; PostgreSQL DDL and DML syntax throughout DO SQLite tables; security vulnerabilities in APNs JWT generation, BYOK key exposure, webhook signature bypass, and Analytics Engine SQL injection; Hono framework spread export destroying the fetch handler; and Cloudflare platform API correctness issues in Vectorize filters, CF Workflows stubs, and token-usage billing.</p>

  <div id="G-P01" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P01</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§launchpad — NaelaoAgentDO.requestApproval() / handleApprovalDecision()</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">pendingApprovals Map Lost on DO Hibernation — Agent Hangs Forever</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">this.pendingApprovals = new Map() stores {resolve, reject} Promise callbacks for human-approval pauses. When the DO hibernates between the approval request and the owner's response, all class fields are wiped. On wake, this.pendingApprovals.get(approvalId) returns undefined, the resolver is gone, and the agent run hangs permanently waiting for a callback that can never fire — no timeout, no error, just silence.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Persist approval records to DO SQLite with a status column (pending/approved/rejected). On wake, query for status='pending' rows and implement polling via a DO alarm rather than an in-memory Promise resolver. The alarm fires every N seconds, checks the SQLite record, and proceeds if the admin has updated it. Remove all in-memory Map usage for cross-request state.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P02" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P02</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§schema — SpaceDO.initSchema() — §22 canonical DDL block</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">SpaceDO Canonical §22 Schema Uses PostgreSQL — Incompatible with DO SQLite</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The §22 canonical schema block uses gen_random_uuid(), auth.users foreign keys, JSONB, TIMESTAMPTZ, DEFAULT NOW(), ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY, CREATE POLICY, and ALTER TABLE … ADD CONSTRAINT — none of which exist in SQLite. Executing this DDL via this.ctx.storage.sql.exec() throws a parse error immediately, preventing any SpaceDO from initialising its schema on first wake.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Rewrite the entire canonical DDL to valid SQLite: replace gen_random_uuid() with crypto.randomUUID() in application code passed as a ? parameter, replace TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW() with INTEGER DEFAULT (unixepoch()*1000), replace JSONB with TEXT (store as JSON.stringify), delete all ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY and CREATE POLICY statements, and remove all auth.users references. Tenant isolation is enforced via space_id column checks in application logic, not DB-level RLS.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P03" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P03</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§naelao-os — createSpace() in workers/spaces/index.ts</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">createSpace() Calls spaceDO.query() Before Declaration — ReferenceError + PostgreSQL $N Placeholders</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">spaceDO.query('INSERT INTO spaces ... VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4, $5)', [...]) is called several lines before the spaceDO variable is instantiated, producing a ReferenceError at runtime. The $1/$2/$N PostgreSQL positional placeholders are also invalid in DO SQLite which requires ? for all bound parameters. Additionally spaceDO.query() is a non-existent method — DO SQLite uses this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(sql, ...params).</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Move the spaceDO instantiation before any call to it. Replace all $N placeholders with ? and use this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(sql, ...params) spread syntax throughout. Run a global search for db.query and spaceDO.query across all Workers to find other instances of the same leftover Supabase API pattern.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P04" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P04</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§assistants — handleSlackWebhook() in naelao-router / naelao-assistant</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">handleSlackWebhook Double-Reads Consumed Request Body — Signature Always Fails</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">await request.json() consumes the body stream as parsed JSON. The subsequent verifySlackSignature(..., await request.text(), ...) call re-reads the already-consumed body, returning an empty string. Slack HMAC-SHA256 verification is computed over the raw request body bytes; using an empty string produces a signature that never matches, causing every legitimate Slack event to be rejected as 401 Unauthorized.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Read the body exactly once as text: const rawBody = await request.text(). Verify the Slack signature against rawBody, then parse the event with JSON.parse(rawBody) for application use. Never call both .json() and .text() on the same request — the first call to consume the body makes the stream unreadable for all subsequent reads.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P05" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P05</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§assistants — AssistantDO constructor and all public methods</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">AssistantDO this.spaceId and this.userId Not Persisted — Undefined After Hibernation, Cross-Tenant R2 Paths</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Every AssistantDO method references this.spaceId and this.userId (e.g., R2 path spaces/${this.spaceId}/..., DO ID lookups). The constructor and initSchema() never INSERT or SELECT these values from SQLite. After DO hibernation and wake, both fields are undefined, causing every method to construct the path spaces/undefined/... — reading from and writing to the wrong R2 prefix and potentially blending data across tenants silently.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Persist spaceId and userId to a config table in initSchema() immediately after first construction. Add an ensureLoaded() guard called at the top of every public method that reads them back from SQLite if not already set: if (!this.spaceId) { const row = this.ctx.storage.sql.exec("SELECT value FROM config WHERE key = ?", 'spaceId').one(); this.spaceId = row?.value as string; }. Add a similar guard for userId.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P06" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P06</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§walletdo-deep — x402Payment() in workers/billing/x402.ts</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">x402Payment Non-Atomic Two-DO Debit-Then-Credit — Money Lost If Credit Call Fails</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Step 1 debits companyWalletDO and Step 2 separately credits workerDefDO via two independent DO fetch() calls with no transaction wrapping or compensation record. If Step 2 fails (network error, DO crash, 5xx), the company is debited but the creator is never credited. The platform fee (Step 3) is also sent to a Queue independently. There is no idempotency key, no retry log, and no rollback path.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Implement two-phase commit: (1) write an x402_transfer record with status='pending' to a TransferLedgerDO before debiting, (2) debit with an idempotency key referencing the transfer ID, (3) credit with the same key, (4) mark status='settled' after both succeed. A sweeper alarm retries any status='pending' records older than N minutes. The idempotency key on both DOs prevents double-debit or double-credit on retry.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P07" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P07</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§concurrency-do — ConcurrencyDO.checkAndReserve()</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">ConcurrencyDO setAlarm Replaced on Every Reservation — Zombie Slots Never Cleaned</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">checkAndReserve() calls this.ctx.storage.setAlarm(Date.now() + HEARTBEAT_WINDOW) on every invocation. CF Durable Objects support only one alarm at a time; each setAlarm() call replaces the previous one. Under concurrent reservations, the cleanup alarm is continuously pushed forward. Expired reservations are never collected because the alarm never fires, and the concurrency ceiling is permanently consumed by zombie slots.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Implement an alarm multiplexer: store the current earliest-deadline timestamp in SQLite. Only call setAlarm() if the newly computed deadline is earlier than the currently stored one. The alarm handler should re-schedule itself if unexpired slots still exist after cleanup, using the earliest remaining expiry as the next alarm target.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P08" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P08</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§analytics — AnalyticsWorker queue handler</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Analytics Queue msg.ack() Called Before writeDataPoints — Events Permanently Lost on Error</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The queue message handler calls msg.ack() before the await writeDataPoints(...) call completes. CF Queues provide at-least-once delivery only when ack() is deferred until after successful processing. Acknowledging first means any exception or transient failure in writeDataPoints() permanently silently drops the analytics event — no retry, no dead-letter, no error log. All billing, usage metering, and observability data in transit is at risk.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Move msg.ack() to after await writeDataPoints(...) succeeds. Wrap the write in try/catch; on failure, do not call ack() — the queue will redeliver automatically. Add a retry counter in the message metadata to apply exponential back-off and route persistently failing events to the dead-letter queue after max_retries is exceeded.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P09" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P09</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§naelao-threads-impl — POST /threads/:id/messages handler in workers/threads/index.ts</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">billingTier Never Passed to ConcurrencyDO — Paid Spaces Throttled to Free-Tier Limits</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The threads handler calls concurrencyDO.checkAndReserve() with only { spaceId, agentId } in the request body — it never reads or forwards billingTier from the space record. ConcurrencyDO applies different concurrency slot limits per billing tier; with the tier always absent, it defaults to the 'free' limit for every space regardless of subscription. Enterprise workspaces with 10-agent concurrency entitlements are incorrectly limited to 1-2 free-tier slots.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Before calling checkAndReserve(), fetch the space record from SpaceDO to extract billingTier, then include it in the request body: { spaceId, agentId, billingTier }. In ConcurrencyDO, treat a missing or unrecognised tier as an error that returns 400 rather than silently defaulting to 'free'. Add a unit test asserting that maker/business/enterprise spaces receive their correct slot allocations.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P10" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P10</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§naelao-admin / §naelao-admin-full — handleAdminAuditLog in naelao-admin worker</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Admin Audit Analytics Engine Query Built via String Interpolation — SQL Injection</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The audit log query builds a CF Analytics Engine SQL string via template literals: WHERE index1 = '${spaceId}' and ${eventType ? `AND blob1 = '${eventType}'` : ''}. Both spaceId and eventType are taken directly from c.req.param() / c.req.query() without sanitisation. An attacker with admin credentials can exfiltrate arbitrary Analytics Engine data by injecting SQL fragments. The LIMIT ${parseInt(limit)} coercion provides no protection against the string-based filter fields.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Parameterise all dynamic values using the CF Analytics Engine SQL binding syntax (? positional params). Replace template-literal construction with a static query string and pass [spaceId, eventType, parsedLimit] as the params array to env.ANALYTICS.query(). Validate eventType against an allowlist of known event-type strings before including it in any query context.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P11" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P11</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§naelao-notifications-full — generateAPNsJWT in naelao-notifications worker</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">APNs JWT Signed with DER-Encoded ECDSA Signature — iOS Push Always Rejected</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">crypto.subtle.sign({ name: 'ECDSA', hash: 'SHA-256' }, signingKey, data) returns a DER-encoded ECDSA signature on all Web Crypto implementations. APNs requires raw P1363 format (two 32-byte big-endian integers R||S concatenated, 64 bytes total). The code immediately base64url-encodes the DER blob without conversion, producing a JWT signature that APNs always rejects with HTTP 403. Every iOS push notification silently fails.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">After obtaining the DER-encoded rawSig, parse the ASN.1 DER structure: locate the two INTEGER TLV fields in the SEQUENCE, extract the R and S integers, left-pad each to exactly 32 bytes, concatenate them into a 64-byte buffer, and base64url-encode the result. Implement a derToP1363(buf, coordSize) helper and add a test asserting the output is exactly 64 bytes when coordSize=32.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P12" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
