      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§naelao-notifications-full — sendPush in naelao-notifications worker</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">sendPush References spaceDO Variable Never Defined in Scope — ReferenceError on Every Call</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">sendPush calls spaceDO.getActiveDeviceTokens(payload.userId) but spaceDO is not declared or passed anywhere in the function signature or its enclosing scope. This is a ReferenceError that crashes the function on every invocation, making all push notification delivery completely non-functional at runtime. No test catches this without an end-to-end push path exercise.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add env: Env to the sendPush signature and construct the SpaceDO stub inside the function: const id = env.NAELAO_SPACE_DO.idFromName(payload.spaceId); const spaceDO = env.NAELAO_SPACE_DO.get(id);. Then call spaceDO.fetch(new Request('https://internal/devices/active', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify({ userId: payload.userId }) })) using the standard Service Binding .fetch() pattern.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P13" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
