      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P13</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§naelao-billing-full / §naelao-together-ai-full — Worker default export in naelao-billing and naelao-together-ai</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">export default { ...app, scheduled } Spread Destroys Hono Fetch Handler</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Spreading a Hono app instance with { ...app, scheduled } copies only enumerable own properties of the app object. The fetch method is defined on Hono's prototype chain and is therefore not an enumerable own property — it is not copied by the spread. The resulting export object has a scheduled property but no callable fetch handler, causing all HTTP requests to these workers to receive an unhandled-fetch error. The scheduled handler also breaks because the spread loses the correct this binding for app.fetch.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Export an explicit object literal: export default { fetch: app.fetch.bind(app), scheduled: async (event, env, ctx) =&gt; { ctx.waitUntil(runDailyMaintenance(env)); } }. This preserves the Hono fetch handler with the correct binding and adds the scheduled handler independently. Never spread a class or framework instance — prototype methods are invisible to the spread operator.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P14" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
