      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§space-templates — space_templates DDL in SpaceDO / template-installer worker</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">space_templates DDL Uses PostgreSQL RLS, TIMESTAMPTZ, auth.users — SQLite Incompatible</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The space_templates schema DDL includes author_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES auth.users(id), created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(), ALTER TABLE space_templates ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY, and CREATE POLICY ... USING (status = 'approved'). None of these are valid SQLite syntax. Executing this DDL via this.ctx.storage.sql.exec() throws a parse error on first contact, making the entire Space Templates system inoperable from cold start.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Rewrite the DDL for SQLite: use TEXT for all UUID and timestamp columns, replace TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW() with INTEGER DEFAULT (unixepoch()*1000), remove all REFERENCES auth.users(id) constraints, and delete the ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY and CREATE POLICY statements entirely. Enforce access control in application logic by filtering on space_id and checking membership. Apply the same audit to installTemplate and every related stored function.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P15" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
