      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§naelao-billing-full — GET /byok/:spaceId/anthropic in naelao-billing worker</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">BYOK Endpoint Returns Decrypted API Key in Plaintext JSON Response — Secret Exposed</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The BYOK retrieval route decrypts the stored AES-GCM ciphertext and returns c.json({ hasByok: true, apiKey }) where apiKey is the fully decrypted secret. Any intermediary that can read the response body — CDN edge logs, Cloudflare dashboard request logging, client-side JavaScript — now has the plaintext key. The decrypted value is included unconditionally regardless of call context.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Return only { hasByok: true } from the GET endpoint and never include the decrypted key in any response body. If the key must be used downstream, implement a proxy pattern where the billing worker makes the LLM call on behalf of the space using the key server-side and returns only the result. If the user must see the key (e.g., for rotation UI), mask it to sk-ant-...XXXX and gate the unmasked display behind a separate admin-scoped endpoint with full audit logging.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P16" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P16</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§naelao-apps-registry — handleInstall in AppRegistryDO</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">AppRegistryDO.handleInstall Uses PostgreSQL db.query + $N Params — App Installation Broken</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">handleInstall executes await db.query('INSERT INTO space_app_installs ... VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4)', [spaceId, appId, ...]) using PostgreSQL positional parameter syntax. Durable Objects use SQLite via this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(sql, ...params) which requires ? placeholders. The db variable is undefined in the DO runtime (no Postgres client exists), causing a ReferenceError that crashes every app install attempt.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Replace db.query(sql, paramsArray) with this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(sql, ...paramsArray) and change all $1/$2/$3/$4 placeholders to ?. Ensure the space_app_installs table DDL is created in blockConcurrencyWhile() during AppRegistryDO's first init via this.ctx.storage.sql.exec('CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS ...').</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P17" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
