    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">installTemplate Uses gen_random_uuid() + $N Params + NOW() — SQLite Incompatible</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">installTemplate executes await db.query('INSERT INTO agent_definitions (id, ...) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), $1, $2, ...)', [...]) and await db.query('INSERT INTO space_template_installs ... VALUES ($1, $2, NOW())', [...]). gen_random_uuid() and NOW() are PostgreSQL functions with no SQLite equivalents. The $N positional syntax is also incompatible. All three constructs throw errors when executed via this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(), making template installation completely broken.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Generate UUIDs in application code using crypto.randomUUID() and pass as a ? parameter. Replace NOW() with unixepoch()*1000 or pass Date.now() as a bind parameter. Rewrite all queries to use ? placeholders: this.ctx.storage.sql.exec('INSERT INTO agent_definitions (id, space_id, name, ...) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ...)', uuid, spaceId, agent.name, ...). Run a global search for gen_random_uuid() and NOW() across all DDL and DML in the spec.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P18" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P18</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§naelao-triggers — verifySignature in naelao-triggers worker</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Non-GitHub Webhook Providers Return true from verifySignature — Auth Bypass</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">verifySignature implements real HMAC-SHA256 verification only for the 'github' provider. All other providers — Stripe, Linear, Jira, and any future webhook sources — fall through to return true unconditionally. Any unauthenticated HTTP POST to a non-GitHub trigger endpoint is accepted as a valid signed webhook. An attacker can trigger arbitrary automation workflows by posting crafted payloads to any Stripe or Linear trigger URL without knowing the webhook secret.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Implement provider-specific HMAC verification for each supported provider before any fallback. For Stripe, verify using the Stripe-Signature header with 5-minute timestamp-tolerance validation. For Linear and Jira, verify their respective HMAC-SHA256 header signatures using the stored webhook secret. Add an explicit throw new Error(`Unsupported provider: ${provider}`) as the final fallback to prevent silent acceptance of unknown providers.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P19" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P19</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§naelao-spaces-full — POST /spaces/:spaceId/archive handler in naelao-spaces worker</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Duplicate const spaceDO in Archive Handler — SyntaxError Prevents Worker from Loading</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Within the same async route handler function, spaceDO is declared twice with const: first as const spaceDO = getProductDO(rootSpaceId, c.env) and then again as const spaceDO = c.env.NAELAO_SPACE_DO.get(...). In strict-mode JavaScript (all CF Workers run in strict mode) redeclaring a const in the same lexical scope throws a SyntaxError at parse time. The entire naelao-spaces worker fails to load and all space management routes return 500 errors.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Rename the second declaration to a distinct identifier (e.g., const spaceDOStub = ...) or consolidate both into a single declaration if they refer to the same object. Audit all other route handlers in naelao-spaces/index.ts for duplicate variable declarations — a single redeclared const in any handler prevents the entire worker module from loading.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P20" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P20</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§space-type-versioning — processCanaryRollouts in SpaceTypeRegistryDO / canary cron</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">processCanaryRollouts Standalone Function Accesses this.ctx — TypeError on Every Invocation</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">processCanaryRollouts is declared as async function processCanaryRollouts(env: Env) — a standalone function, not a class method — but its body calls this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(...) and this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(`UPDATE versions ...`). In strict-mode JS, this inside a regular function call is undefined, so this.ctx throws TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'ctx'). The canary rollout engine is entirely broken; no rollout percentage ever advances.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Either convert processCanaryRollouts to a method on the DO class (async processCanaryRollouts() using this.env and this.ctx stored at construction), or refactor it to accept the DO's sql storage context as an explicit parameter: async function processCanaryRollouts(sql: SqlStorage, env: Env) and replace all this.ctx.storage.sql.exec() calls with sql.exec(). If called from a cron handler, pass the DO stub explicitly.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P21" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P21</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§naelao-billing-deep — POST /token-usage handler in naelao-billing worker</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">naelao-billing Token-Usage Handler Uses PostgreSQL BEGIN/COMMIT + db.query — Billing Writes Never Execute</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The token-usage handler issues await db.query('BEGIN'), multiple db.query(INSERT/UPDATE ...) calls, and await db.query('COMMIT') / await db.query('ROLLBACK'). This is PostgreSQL transaction syntax via a db client that does not exist in a Cloudflare Worker. Workers have no persistent database connection and no db global. The entire billing-write path throws a ReferenceError on db, meaning token usage is never recorded and credit deduction never occurs — allowing unbounded free usage.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Move all billing state into a BillingDO where SQLite transactions are available. Inside the DO, use this.ctx.storage.sql.exec('BEGIN') / COMMIT for atomicity, or wrap all writes in a single this.ctx.blockConcurrencyWhile() block which provides DO-level serialisation. Replace all $1/$2 placeholders with ? and all db.query(sql, arr) calls with this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(sql, ...arr).</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P22" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P22</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§ai-gateway — getAvailableModels() in workers/agents/models.ts</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">getAvailableModels() References Undeclared spaceDO and Uses Non-Existent .rows on SQLite Result</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">const fineTunedModels = await spaceDO.query(...) uses spaceDO which is never declared in that function's scope, producing a ReferenceError. Additionally, DO SQLite .exec() returns an object exposing .toArray() and .one() — not a .rows property — so result.rows.map(...) throws TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'map') at runtime. Both errors combine to make fine-tuned model listing completely broken.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Pass a spaceDO: DurableObjectStub parameter into getAvailableModels() or instantiate it from env inside the function. Replace all .rows with .toArray() on DO SQLite exec results. Apply a project-wide search for .rows on sql.exec() results to find and fix all other occurrences of this pattern.</p></div>
