      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P25</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§skills — loadSkillsFromR2() in shared/skill-loader.ts; list_files in file-manager handler</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">loadSkillsFromR2() and list_files Both Truncate at 1000 R2 Objects — Skills and Files Silently Lost</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Both implementations call bucket.list({ prefix, delimiter: '/' }) without checking listing.truncated or following the cursor. R2 list() returns at most 1000 objects per call. Spaces with more than 1000 installed skills or workspace files silently lose all objects beyond the first 1000 with no error, no log, and no indication to the caller that the result is incomplete.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Wrap every r2.list() call in a cursor loop: let listing = null; const results = []; do { listing = await bucket.list({ prefix, cursor: listing?.cursor, limit: 1000 }); results.push(...listing.objects); } while (listing.truncated); Apply the same pattern to VerticalFinetuneWorkflow, archiveSpace, and every other R2 list() call in the codebase.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P26" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
