      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P26</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§workers-sp — WalletDO.deductCredits() / recordCreatorEarning()</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">WalletDO Creator Earning Fired as Bare void in DO Handler — Silently Lost on Response Return</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">void this.recordCreatorEarning(params.amount * 0.15) inside a DO fetch() handler fires an unregistered Promise. When the DO returns its Response the runtime can cancel the in-flight Promise. DOs do not have ExecutionContext.waitUntil(). Creator earnings that represent 15% of every paid agent run are silently lost on any DO eviction or Worker recycle.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Write the creator earning record synchronously to DO SQLite inside deductCredits() before returning the Response: this.ctx.storage.sql.exec('INSERT INTO pending_earnings (id, amount, created_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?)', ...). A separate alarm-based sweeper then processes pending_earnings in bulk and credits the creator wallet. The initial record must be durable before the DO response returns.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P27" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P27</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§workflows — WorkflowRegistryDO in workers/workflows/index.ts</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">WorkflowRegistryDO Calls Non-Existent instance.id() on CF Workflows Stub — Workflow Creation Throws</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">After const instance = await env.NAELAO_WORKFLOW.create({ id: workflowId, ... }), the code calls await instance.id() to register the workflow. The CF Workflows WorkflowInstance stub does not expose an .id() method. This throws TypeError: instance.id is not a function at runtime on every workflow creation, making the entire Workflows feature non-functional.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Use workflowId directly — it is the value already passed to .create(). The CF Workflows API exposes .status(), .pause(), .resume(), and .abort() on the instance stub, not .id(). Immediately register the workflow ID in WorkflowRegistryDO using the workflowId local variable: await registryDO.fetch(new Request('http://registry/register', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify({ workflowId }) })).</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P28" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P28</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§naelao-threads-impl — GET /threads Hono handler in workers/threads/index.ts</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">GET /threads Uses PostgreSQL $N Placeholders + Dead db.query Reference — ReferenceError on Every List Request</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The GET /threads implementation builds a SQL string with $1, $${params.length+1} (PostgreSQL positional syntax) and calls await db.query(query, params) where db is the removed Supabase client. The comment // SpaceDO replaces Hyperdrive appears but db.query() is used anyway. At runtime db is undefined and db.query() throws ReferenceError immediately, making thread listing completely non-functional.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Replace all db.query(sql, params) calls with the SpaceDO Service Binding pattern: await spaceDO.fetch(new Request('http://space/query', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify({ sql, params }) })). Replace all $N placeholders with ? for SQLite compatibility. Run a project-wide search for db.query to find all other leftover Supabase call sites.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P29" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P29</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§naelao-threads-impl — createSSEStream() in workers/threads/index.ts</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">createSSEStream Bare void IIFE Killed When Response Returns — Zero SSE Tokens Delivered</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The SSE stream driver uses void (async () =&gt; { ... })() — a bare unregistered Promise. When createSSEStream() returns its Response, the Workers runtime recycles the execution context and cancels the in-flight async IIFE before any tokens are forwarded to the client. The text/event-stream response closes immediately with no events, making the SSE fallback permanently broken for all clients.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Use ctx.waitUntil(streamDriverPromise) on the ExecutionContext to keep the Worker alive until the stream completes. Thread the ExecutionContext down to wherever the SSE Response is constructed and ensure the entire async streaming loop is registered with waitUntil before the Response is returned.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P30" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P30</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§execution-ladder — SandboxDO.alarm() in durable-objects/sandbox-do.ts</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">SandboxDO Alarm Reads this.lastActiveAt Class Field — Always 0 After Hibernation, Stops Every Container</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">private lastActiveAt: number = 0 is a class field that resets to 0 after every DO hibernation. The alarm() handler checks Date.now() - this.lastActiveAt &gt;= IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS. Since this.lastActiveAt is always 0 on wake, Date.now() - 0 always exceeds 10 minutes, and the container is stopped on every alarm regardless of actual recent activity — destroying any long-running container session.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Persist lastActiveAt to DO SQLite on every activity event: this.ctx.storage.sql.exec("UPDATE container_state SET value = ? WHERE key = 'last_active'", Date.now()). In alarm(), read it back before computing the idle delta: const lastActive = parseInt(this.ctx.storage.sql.exec("SELECT value FROM container_state WHERE key = 'last_active'").one()?.value ?? '0'). Default to Date.now() (not 0) when the key is absent to avoid false-positive idle detection.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P31" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P31</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§sandbox-do — SandboxDO in durable-objects/sandbox-do.ts</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">SandboxDO sandboxRef In-Memory Field Nulled on Hibernation — Container Orphaned, All Exec Calls Fail</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">private sandboxRef = null is a class-level field never persisted to SQLite. When the DO hibernates between exec() calls, sandboxRef is wiped. On wake, ensureRunning() has no mechanism to re-attach to an already-running external container — it only starts new ones. The previously active container is silently orphaned, and subsequent exec() calls start a duplicate container or fail, leaking container resources.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Persist the container's unique identifier string to SQLite (INSERT OR REPLACE INTO container_state (key, value) VALUES ('sandbox_id', containerId)) whenever a container is started. In ensureRunning(), first query SQLite for an existing sandbox_id and attempt re-attachment before launching a new container. Gate the entire ensureRunning() body inside this.ctx.blockConcurrencyWhile() to prevent concurrent duplicate starts.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P32" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P32</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§naelao-credentials — getCredentialForUrl() in workers/credentials/index.ts</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">getCredentialForUrl endsWith Domain Check — Subdomain Bypass Forwards Credentials to Attacker</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The domain validation uses domains.some(d =&gt; parsedUrl.hostname.endsWith(d)). A hostname like evilnaelao.com satisfies endsWith('naelao.com'), bypassing the allowlist entirely. The credential routing forwards matching credentials (API keys, OAuth tokens) to any domain sharing the suffix with an allowed domain, enabling SSRF and credential theft by an attacker who registers a suffix-matching domain.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Replace the endsWith check with the correct prefix-anchored subdomain test: hostname === d || hostname.endsWith('.' + d). This ensures the match is against the domain itself or a proper subdomain, not an arbitrary suffix. Apply the same fix to every domain validation in the credentials worker and add a unit test asserting that evilnaelao.com does not match naelao.com.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P33" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P33</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§naelao-knowledge — knowledge/index.ts GET /knowledge/search</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Vectorize Filter Uses Flat Object — Cross-Space Knowledge Returned, Tenant Data Leak</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The vector search query passes filter: { spaceId } — a flat key-value object. Cloudflare Vectorize requires filter expressions using explicit operator syntax: { spaceId: { $eq: spaceId } }. A flat object is not a valid filter expression and is either silently ignored or returns an API error. In the ignore case, the search returns results across all spaces rather than scoping to the requesting space, exposing cross-tenant knowledge base content.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Change the filter to { spaceId: { $eq: spaceId } } (and similarly for all other filter fields such as agentId, projectId, domainId). Verify that all filtered fields are declared as metadata indexes at Vectorize index creation time — undeclared fields silently produce unfiltered results. Add an integration test asserting that results returned by any search belong only to the authenticated space.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P34" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P34</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§stored-functions — deduct_space_credits stored function</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">deduct_space_credits Uses SELECT FOR UPDATE Row Lock — Invalid Syntax in SQLite, Billing Deduction Broken</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The deduct_space_credits function uses SELECT ... FOR UPDATE to lock the credits row before the deduction. FOR UPDATE is a PostgreSQL row-level locking clause that does not exist in SQLite. Executing this statement via this.ctx.storage.sql.exec() throws a syntax error, causing every credit deduction to fail. Because this function gates all paid AI operations, the entire billing enforcement layer is inoperable.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Remove FOR UPDATE entirely. In Durable Objects, concurrency is serialised by the single-threaded execution model — row locks are unnecessary. Wrap the read-modify-write in this.ctx.blockConcurrencyWhile() if atomicity across awaited calls is needed within the same handler. Use a single atomic SQL UPDATE: UPDATE space_credits SET balance = balance - ? WHERE space_id = ? AND balance &gt;= ? RETURNING balance to perform the deduction atomically without a separate lock.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div id="G-P35" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-P35</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
      <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§naelao-notifications-full — initiateVoiceCall / VAPI webhook handler in naelao-notifications</span>
    </div>
    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">VAPI Voice Escalation Has No Approval-Outcome Webhook Handler — Call Result Never Processed</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">initiateVoiceCall posts a call to VAPI and stores callId in KV, but there is no registered POST /vapi/webhook route to receive the VAPI call.ended or call.transcript callback. Without this handler the platform never learns whether the human approved or rejected the escalation, so all downstream logic gated on the call outcome (resuming paused workflows, logging approval decisions) never executes. KV entries for pending calls also accumulate indefinitely with no TTL.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Register a POST /vapi/webhook route that verifies the VAPI HMAC signature, reads callId from the payload, fetches the KV record, determines the outcome from call.status or the call transcript, and either resumes the paused workflow via WorkflowRegistryDO or logs a rejection. Set a TTL of &lt;= 24 hours on all KV entries written by initiateVoiceCall to prevent unbounded accumulation.</p></div>
  </div>
  </div>


