    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The spec loads skills from three tiers and concatenates their instructions into the system prompt with Tier 3 (Personal) taking precedence over Tier 2 (Space) which takes precedence over Tier 1 (Platform). If a Personal skill says "always respond in French" but a Platform skill says "always respond in the user's detected language", the conflict is silently resolved by instruction ordering — the last instruction wins, but no one knows why the agent is behaving oddly. Conflicting skill instructions produce unpredictable LLM behavior because the model tries to satisfy contradictory constraints.</p></div>
