    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">AssistantSandboxDO creates a single CF Container per assistant and routes all sandbox tasks (Python execution, bash scripts, browser automation, Node.js code) through it sequentially. When a long-running Python data analysis fiber is executing, it blocks bash command execution, browser screenshot tasks, and all other sandbox work for that assistant. The Moltworker architecture defines a multi-container pool: multiple specialized containers per agent with independent execution, sharing a single R2 workspace as the source of truth. The spec never defines container pool management, container type specialization, or cross-container task routing.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Redesign AssistantSandboxDO to manage a container pool:
```typescript
interface ContainerSlot {
  id: string;
  type: 'python' | 'node' | 'browser' | 'bash';
  status: 'idle' | 'busy' | 'starting';
  containerRef: DurableObjectStub | null;
  lastUsedAt: number;
}

class AssistantSandboxDO extends DurableObject {
  private pool: ContainerSlot[] = [];
  private maxContainers = 3; // configurable per space plan

  async executeTask(task: SandboxTask): Promise&lt;TaskResult&gt; {
    const slot = await this.acquireContainer(task.type);
    try {
      return await slot.containerRef!.execute(task);
    } finally {
      this.releaseContainer(slot.id);
    }
  }

  async acquireContainer(type: ContainerSlot['type']) {
    // Find idle container of matching type, or create new one
    let slot = this.pool.find(
      s =&gt; s.type === type &amp;&amp; s.status === 'idle'
    );
    if (!slot &amp;&amp; this.pool.length &lt; this.maxContainers) {
      slot = await this.createContainer(type);
    }
    if (!slot) throw new Error('Container pool exhausted');
    slot.status = 'busy';
    return slot;
  }
}
```
Expose pool status in AssistantDO.getHealth() for observability.</p></div>
