    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The spec mentions FUSE-mounted R2 as the container workspace but never specifies: (1) which R2 bucket prefix each container mounts, (2) how FUSE write-back is triggered (write-through vs. write-behind), (3) how a second container reading a file written by the first container avoids a stale cache read, and (4) what happens when two containers write to the same file concurrently. In the Moltworker model, R2 is the source of truth: containers use FUSE write-through (every write is immediately PUT to R2), and cache invalidation uses R2 event notifications (R2 PUT fires an event that all containers with the affected key in their FUSE cache must invalidate).</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Define the filesystem sync protocol in the spec:
```
Write path:
  Container write → FUSE driver → R2.put(key, data) (synchronous)
  On R2.put success → FUSE confirms write to container
  On R2.put failure → FUSE returns EIO to container

Read/cache invalidation path:
  Container read → FUSE checks local cache → cache miss: R2.get(key)
  R2 PUT event → naelao-r2-notifier Worker →
    AssistantSandboxDO.onR2Event(key) →
    broadcast invalidation to all active containers via
    container.invalidateCache(key)

Conflict resolution:
  R2 object versioning enabled on workspace bucket
  Concurrent writes: last-writer-wins (R2 conditional PUT not used)
  Conflict detection: container can opt-in to R2 conditional
  PUT (If-Match: etag) for critical files
```
Document this explicitly in the Moltworker integration spec section. Add a conflict_log table in AssistantSandboxDO SQLite to record R2 write conflicts for debugging.</p></div>
