    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">env.SANDBOX.create() is called in the spec without a network policy option. CF Containers support configurable network policies: full (default, internet access), restricted (only egress to allowlisted hostnames), or none (no network). Agent-executed user code (Python scripts, bash commands from LLM tool calls) runs in a container with full internet access by default. A prompt-injected agent could exfiltrate secrets, make unexpected external API calls, or participate in a DDoS attack from within the container.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add network policy to container creation:
```typescript
async createContainer(
  type: ContainerSlot['type'],
  taskContext: TaskContext
): Promise&lt;ContainerSlot&gt; {
  const networkPolicy = this.resolveNetworkPolicy(
    type, taskContext
  );
  const container = await this.env.SANDBOX.create({
    image: CONTAINER_TYPES[type].image,
    network: networkPolicy,
    memory: CONTAINER_TYPES[type].memoryMb * 1024 * 1024,
    cpu: CONTAINER_TYPES[type].cpuMilli
  });
  return {id: crypto.randomUUID(), type, containerRef: container, status: 'idle', lastUsedAt: 0};
}

resolveNetworkPolicy(
  type: ContainerSlot['type'],
  ctx: TaskContext
): NetworkPolicy {
  if (ctx.userProvided) {
    // User-submitted code: restricted egress only
    return {
      type: 'restricted',
      allowedHostnames: this.spaceConfig.sandboxAllowedHosts ?? []
    };
  }
  // Agent-generated code: allow access to declared tools only
  return { type: 'restricted', allowedHostnames: ctx.requiredHosts };
}
```
Allow space admins to configure sandboxAllowedHosts in space settings for legitimate external API access from containers.</p></div>
