    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">In shared agent mode, all users' memories are inserted into the same Vectorize index (Layer 5 of the Memory OS) with no user_id metadata. A vector similarity search for User B's question may return embedding neighbors from User A's stored memories. Because vector similarity is semantic (not syntactic), the leakage is invisible: User B's agent may surface personal facts about User A without any obvious indicator that the data came from a different user.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add user_id to all Vectorize inserts and filter on all queries:
```typescript
// Write path:
async storeVectorMemory(
  text: string, userId: string, metadata: Record&lt;string, string&gt;
) {
  const embedding = await this.env.AI.run(
    '@cf/baai/bge-small-en-v1.5', {text}
  );
  await this.env.VECTORIZE.upsert([{
    id: `${userId}-${crypto.randomUUID()}`,
    values: embedding.data[0],
    metadata: {
      userId, // REQUIRED for isolation
      spaceId: this.spaceId,
      ...metadata
    }
  }]);
}

// Read path — ALWAYS include userId filter:
async recallVectorMemory(query: string, userId: string) {
  const embedding = await this.env.AI.run(
    '@cf/baai/bge-small-en-v1.5', {text: query}
  );
  return await this.env.VECTORIZE.query(
    embedding.data[0],
    {
      topK: 10,
      filter: {userId, spaceId: this.spaceId} // user isolation filter
    }
  );
}
```
