    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">In shared agent mode, the sessions table tracks active sessions by channel type (Slack, Discord, etc.) but has no user_id column. When User A and User B both send Slack messages in the same channel, the agent creates one session for the Slack channel. Both users' messages are appended to the same session, interleaving their conversations. The agent responds to User B's message with context from User A's conversation and vice versa — complete conversation isolation failure.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add user_id to the sessions table and use channel+user as the session key:
```typescript
