    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Max-Instances Enforcement Race Condition — Concurrent Creation Requests Both Pass Limit Check Before Either Commits</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The spec enforces the per-user max-5-instances limit by reading the current count from DO SQLite and comparing it to the limit. If two concurrent creation requests both read count=4 (under the limit of 5), both pass the check, and both proceed to create a new instance. The user ends up with 6 instances. This is a classic read-check-write race condition. Durable Objects are single-threaded per I/O boundary, but two independent HTTP requests to the SpaceDO can interleave: Request A reads count, Request B reads count, Request A writes, Request B writes — both see count=4.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Use an atomic INSERT to enforce the limit:
```typescript
async createAssistantInstance(
  spaceId: string, userId: string, config: AssistantConfig
): Promise&lt;string&gt; {
  // Atomic: the INSERT fails if count &gt;= 5
  try {
    const result = this.sql&lt;{id: string}[]&gt;`
      WITH check_limit AS (
        SELECT COUNT(*) as cnt FROM assistant_instances
        WHERE space_id = ${spaceId} AND user_id = ${userId}
          AND status != 'deleted'
      )
      INSERT INTO assistant_instances
        (id, space_id, user_id, config_json, created_at)
      SELECT
        ${crypto.randomUUID()}, ${spaceId}, ${userId},
        ${JSON.stringify(config)}, unixepoch('now')*1000
      FROM check_limit
      WHERE cnt &lt; ${MAX_INSTANCES_PER_USER}
      RETURNING id
    `;
    if (result.length === 0) {
      throw new Error('Max instances reached');
    }
    return result[0].id;
  } catch (e: unknown) {
    if (e instanceof Error &amp;&amp; e.message === 'Max instances reached') {
      throw new Error(`Max ${MAX_INSTANCES_PER_USER} assistant instances per user`);
    }
    throw e;
  }
}
```
The CTE + INSERT WHERE cnt &lt; N is atomic within SQLite; no external lock needed.</p></div>
