    <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">No Graceful State Flush on DO Hibernation — In-Flight Fiber State Lost When DO Is Evicted</h3>
    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">When a Durable Object is hibernated (evicted after 70-140 seconds of inactivity), any in-memory state not written to SQLite is lost. AssistantDO holds in-memory: active fiber execution context, the current LLM streaming state, pending approval Map entries, and the skill cache. If the DO is evicted mid-fiber (e.g., while awaiting a slow tool call), the fiber is silently lost — the user never receives a response and the task is never retried. The spec has no alarm-based pre-eviction flush pattern to checkpoint fiber state before hibernation.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Use DO alarms as a pre-eviction checkpoint:
```typescript
// When a fiber starts, set an alarm to flush its state
async startFiber(fiber: Fiber) {
  await this.sql`UPDATE fibers
    SET status = 'running', started_at = unixepoch('now')*1000
    WHERE id = ${fiber.id}`;
  // Set alarm 60s from now to checkpoint (hibernation starts at ~70s)
  await this.ctx.storage.setAlarm(
    Date.now() + 60_000,
    {type: 'fiber_checkpoint', fiberId: fiber.id}
  );
}

async alarm() {
  const meta = await this.ctx.storage.get&lt;{type: string; fiberId: string}&gt;('alarmMeta');
  if (meta?.type === 'fiber_checkpoint') {
    await this.checkpointFiber(meta.fiberId);
    // Reschedule while fiber is still running
    const fiber = await this.getFiber(meta.fiberId);
    if (fiber?.status === 'running') {
      await this.ctx.storage.setAlarm(Date.now() + 60_000, meta);
    }
  }
}
```
On wake after hibernation, onStart() checks for fibers with status='running' and restarts them from their last checkpoint.</p></div>
