    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">AssistantDO sets this.spaceId and this.userId in the constructor from the DO's name (parsed from assistant:{spaceId}:{userId}). If this parsing logic has a bug after hibernation (e.g., the constructor is called differently on cold wake), these instance variables could be undefined, empty strings, or stale values. All R2 paths use these variables: a corrupted this.spaceId causes the DO to read/write another space's R2 prefix — cross-tenant data leakage. The spec never defines how instance variables are validated after hibernation or what happens if DO naming conventions change during a migration.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Validate and restore spaceId/userId on every wake, not just construction:
```typescript
class AssistantDO extends AIChatAgent&lt;Env, AssistantState&gt; {
  private _spaceId: string | null = null;
  private _userId: string | null = null;

  get spaceId(): string {
    if (!this._spaceId) throw new Error('spaceId not initialized');
    return this._spaceId;
  }

  async onStart() {
    // Parse from DO name (format: assistant:{spaceId}:{userId})
    const name = this.ctx.id.name;
    if (!name) throw new Error('AssistantDO must be created with idFromName');
    const parts = name.split(':');
    if (parts.length !== 3 || parts[0] !== 'assistant') {
      throw new Error(`Invalid AssistantDO name format: ${name}`);
    }
    this._spaceId = parts[1];
    this._userId = parts[2];
    if (!this._spaceId || !this._userId) {
      throw new Error(`Empty spaceId/userId in DO name: ${name}`);
    }
    // Cross-check against SQLite if previously initialized
    const stored = this.sql&lt;{space_id: string}[]&gt;`
      SELECT space_id FROM assistant_meta LIMIT 1
    `[0];
    if (stored &amp;&amp; stored.space_id !== this._spaceId) {
      throw new Error('spaceId mismatch between DO name and stored metadata');
    }
    // ... rest of schema init
  }
}
```
