    <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The spec defines Layer 5 (Vectorize) as long-term semantic memory that can be searched by embedding similarity. The retrieval path is described (embed the query, search Vectorize, return top-K results). The write path is never defined: when does a memory get written to Vectorize? After every message? After every turn? Only for certain memory types (facts, not session summaries)? What chunk size? What embedding model? What Vectorize namespace? Without a defined write path, vectors are never inserted and Layer 5 returns empty results on every query — silently degraded to a broken layer.</p></div>
    <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Define the Vectorize write path explicitly:
```typescript
async extractAndStoreMemories(
  turn: CompletedTurn, userId: string
) {
  // Extract memorable facts from the turn using LLM
  const facts = await this.llm([{
    role: 'system',
    content: 'Extract 0-5 durable facts worth remembering long-term. Return JSON: [{fact, importance: 1-5}]'
  }, {
    role: 'user',
    content: JSON.stringify(turn.messages)
  }]);

  const parsedFacts: {fact: string; importance: number}[] =
    JSON.parse(facts);

  // Only store high-importance facts (importance &gt;= 3) in Vectorize
  const important = parsedFacts.filter(f =&gt; f.importance &gt;= 3);

  for (const {fact, importance} of important) {
    const embedding = await this.env.AI.run(
      '@cf/baai/bge-small-en-v1.5', {text: fact}
    );
    await this.env.VECTORIZE.upsert([{
      id: `${userId}-${crypto.randomUUID()}`,
      values: embedding.data[0],
      metadata: {userId, spaceId: this.spaceId, fact, importance, turnId: turn.id}
    }]);
  }
}
