<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Replace KV rate limiting with one of two correct primitives:

**Option A — CF Rate Limiting (recommended for simple limits):**
```toml
# wrangler.jsonc
[[rules]]
binding = "RATE_LIMITER"
namespace = "naelao-api-rl"
simple = { limit = 100, period = 60 }
```
```typescript
const { success } = await env.RATE_LIMITER.limit({ key: clientIp });
if (!success) return new Response("Too Many Requests", { status: 429 });
```

**Option B — Durable Object counter (for complex per-user limits across tiers):**
```typescript
const rateLimiterId = env.RATE_LIMITER_DO.idFromName(`user:${userId}`);
const limiter = env.RATE_LIMITER_DO.get(rateLimiterId);
const { allowed } = await limiter.check(100, 60); // 100 req/min
