<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Dynamic tool execution has no per-tool timeout — hanging tools block agent turn indefinitely</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Dynamic Worker Loader executes user-defined TypeScript tools in V8 isolates. There is a 30-second Worker request timeout, but this is the GLOBAL timeout for the entire agent turn, not a per-tool timeout. A dynamic tool that makes a slow external HTTP call, enters an infinite loop, or waits for a resource that never responds will consume the full 30-second budget, leaving zero time for the agent's LLM reasoning, other tool calls, and response streaming. No partial result is salvageable; the entire turn fails with a 504.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Wrap each dynamic tool execution in a `Promise.race()` with a configurable per-tool deadline:
```typescript
const TOOL_TIMEOUT_MS = {
  default: 10_000,
  web_search: 15_000,
  exec_script: 25_000,
};

async function executeToolWithTimeout(
  toolName: string,
  toolFn: () =&gt; Promise&lt;unknown&gt;
): Promise&lt;unknown&gt; {
  const timeoutMs = TOOL_TIMEOUT_MS[toolName] ?? TOOL_TIMEOUT_MS.default;
  const timeoutPromise = new Promise((_, reject) =&gt;
    setTimeout(() =&gt; reject(new Error(`Tool ${toolName} timed out after ${timeoutMs}ms`)), timeoutMs)
  );
  return Promise.race([toolFn(), timeoutPromise]);
}
```
Return a structured error to the LLM on timeout: `{ error: "tool_timeout", toolName, timeoutMs }` — the agent can retry with different parameters or skip the tool call.</p></div>
