<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">No onChatEnd / onChatError boundary — locks, sub-agents, and metrics leak on error paths</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The hand-rolled loop has no defined post-turn boundary. When a turn ends — normally or via exception — there is no guaranteed cleanup: temporary file locks acquired by failed tool execution are never released, sub-agents spawned during the turn are never reconciled, billing events are emitted best-effort inline (and skipped entirely on the error path), and metrics are not reliably written. A turn that throws halfway leaves orphaned state that accumulates across the DO's lifetime.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Implement onChatEnd and onChatError hooks (native in CF Think) with finally-style guarantees:
```typescript
async onChatEnd(ctx: TurnContext) {
  await this.releaseLocks(ctx.turnId);
  await this.flushBilling(ctx.turnId);      // always bill, even on partial turns
  await this.emitMetrics(ctx.turnId, "ok");
}
async onChatError(ctx: TurnContext, error: Error) {
  await this.releaseLocks(ctx.turnId);
  await this.flushBilling(ctx.turnId);      // bill for tokens already consumed
  await this.reconcileSubAgents(ctx.turnId);
  await this.emitMetrics(ctx.turnId, "error");
  this.broadcast(JSON.stringify({ type: "turn_error", message: error.message }));
}
```
If staying with the hand-rolled loop, wrap the body in try/finally and call these explicitly.</p></div>
</div>
