<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">System prompt rebuilt with volatile memory inline every turn — defeats Anthropic prompt caching (≈10x cost)</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The system prompt is reassembled every turn with the Memory OS injection (often thousands of tokens) concatenated into a single string. Anthropic prompt caching keys on an exact prefix match up to a cache breakpoint. Because the memory section changes between turns (a fact updated, a recall reordered), the cached prefix is invalidated and every turn is a cache MISS, billed at the full uncached input rate — roughly 10x the cost of a cache hit on the static instruction prefix. The static base instructions, which never change, are not isolated behind a cache breakpoint.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Separate the immutable prefix from the volatile suffix and set an explicit cache breakpoint:
```typescript
const messages = [
  {
    role: "system",
    content: [
      // Static base instructions — cached
      { type: "text", text: BASE_INSTRUCTIONS,
        providerOptions: { anthropic: { cacheControl: { type: "ephemeral" } } } },
      // Volatile memory — placed AFTER the breakpoint so it never invalidates the cache
      { type: "text", text: assembleMemoryContext(spaceId, userId) },
    ],
  },
  ...conversationHistory,
];
```
Keep skills and tool definitions (also stable) before the breakpoint with base instructions. Only genuinely per-turn content goes after it.</p></div>
