<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Document deletion removes SQLite metadata but never deletes vectors — search poisoning + GDPR breach</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">When a knowledge document is deleted, its row is removed from SpaceDO SQLite but `vectorize.deleteByIds()` is never called for the document's chunk vectors. The vectors remain in the index permanently, so semantic search continues returning content from documents the user explicitly deleted. This poisons retrieval with stale/removed content and is a direct GDPR Article 17 (right to erasure) violation when the deleted document contained personal data.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Delete vectors as part of document deletion, with retry compensation:
```typescript
async deleteDocument(docId: string, spaceId: string) {
  const chunkIds = [...this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(
    "SELECT vector_id FROM knowledge_chunks WHERE doc_id = ?", docId
  )].map(r =&gt; r.vector_id);
  // Delete vectors first; only remove metadata after success
  await env.NAELAO_VECTORIZE.deleteByIds(chunkIds);
  this.ctx.storage.sql.exec("DELETE FROM knowledge_chunks WHERE doc_id = ?", docId);
  this.ctx.storage.sql.exec("DELETE FROM knowledge_docs WHERE id = ?", docId);
}
```
Add a nightly reconciliation sweep comparing SQLite chunk IDs against Vectorize to catch any orphans from partial failures.</p></div>
</div>
