<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">No embedding model version stored — a model upgrade silently turns all existing vectors into noise</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Chunks are embedded with `@cf/baai/bge-base-en-v1.5` (768-dim) but neither the chunk metadata nor the Vectorize vectors record which embedding model produced them. If the platform ever upgrades the embedding model, new query vectors live in a different semantic space (and possibly a different dimension) than the existing stored vectors. Cosine similarity between old and new vectors becomes meaningless noise, silently degrading every search with no error raised.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Stamp the embedding model on every vector and gate queries on it:
```typescript
const EMBEDDING_MODEL = "@cf/baai/bge-base-en-v1.5";
await env.NAELAO_VECTORIZE.upsert([{
  id: chunkId,
  values: embedding,
  metadata: { spaceId, docId, embedding_model: EMBEDDING_MODEL },
}]);
```
On model upgrade, run a re-embedding job: query all vectors with the old `embedding_model`, re-embed their source chunks with the new model, upsert, and only then switch query traffic. Provide an admin `/knowledge/reembed` endpoint that drives this as a CF Workflow.</p></div>
</div>
