<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">topK hardcoded with no re-ranking — relevant chunks ranked just below the cutoff are dropped</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Knowledge search returns a fixed `topK` (≈20) of raw vector matches and injects them directly into context. For large knowledge bases, a highly relevant chunk can rank 25th by raw cosine similarity and fall below the cutoff, making the agent appear to have amnesia about content that is actually present. There is no cross-encoder re-ranking step to recover relevant-but-lower-ranked chunks, and topK is not configurable per query.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Over-fetch, then re-rank to select the final context set:
```typescript
// 1. Over-fetch candidates
const candidates = await env.NAELAO_VECTORIZE.query(queryVector, {
  topK: 50, returnMetadata: "all",
  filter: { spaceId: { $eq: spaceId } },
});
// 2. Re-rank with a cross-encoder (Workers AI reranker)
const reranked = await env.AI.run("@cf/baai/bge-reranker-base", {
  query: userQuery,
  contexts: candidates.matches.map(m =&gt; ({ text: m.metadata.text })),
});
// 3. Inject only the top 5-8 after re-ranking
const final = reranked.slice(0, 8);
```
Make the candidate count and final count configurable per space tier.</p></div>
