<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Vector upsert and metadata insert are not atomic — partial failure leaves orphaned vectors</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Ingestion upserts vectors to Vectorize and separately inserts chunk metadata into SpaceDO SQLite. These are two systems with no shared transaction. If the SQLite insert fails after the Vectorize upsert succeeds (DO eviction, CPU limit, error), the vectors exist in the index with no corresponding metadata row — they can be returned by search but can never be deleted (deletion is driven by the metadata table) and are invisible to reconciliation.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Write metadata first, then vectors, and compensate on failure:
```typescript
async ingestChunk(chunk: Chunk, embedding: number[]) {
  const vectorId = crypto.randomUUID();
  // 1. Metadata first — establishes the deletion record
  this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(
    "INSERT INTO knowledge_chunks (id, doc_id, vector_id, text, status) VALUES (?,?,?,?,'pending')",
    chunk.id, chunk.docId, vectorId, chunk.text
  );
  try {
    await env.NAELAO_VECTORIZE.upsert([{ id: vectorId, values: embedding,
      metadata: { spaceId: chunk.spaceId, docId: chunk.docId } }]);
    this.ctx.storage.sql.exec("UPDATE knowledge_chunks SET status='active' WHERE id=?", chunk.id);
  } catch (e) {
    this.ctx.storage.sql.exec("DELETE FROM knowledge_chunks WHERE id=?", chunk.id);
    throw e;
  }
}
```
A nightly job deletes any chunk stuck in `pending` for &gt; 1 hour and any Vectorize ID with no `active` row.</p></div>
