<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">There is no idempotency key or content-hash dedup on ingestion. Uploading the same document twice (a common user action, or an automatic retry after a perceived failure) creates two complete sets of chunk vectors with identical content but different IDs. Search then returns near-duplicate results, wasting context budget and skewing relevance, and the duplicate vectors double the storage and embedding cost.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Key ingestion on a content hash and skip or replace on match:
```typescript
async ingestDocument(docId: string, content: ArrayBuffer, spaceId: string) {
  const contentHash = await sha256(content);
  const existing = [...this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(
    "SELECT id, content_hash FROM knowledge_docs WHERE id = ?", docId
  )][0];
  if (existing?.content_hash === contentHash) {
    return { skipped: true, reason: "unchanged" };
  }
  if (existing) {
    // Content changed — delete old chunks/vectors before re-ingesting (see G-V09)
    await this.deleteDocument(docId, spaceId);
  }
  // ... chunk, embed, upsert, store content_hash
}
```</p></div>
