<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">PDF/DOCX parse failures have no error path — documents silently ingest with zero vectors</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Ingestion calls `extractPdfText()` and `extractDocxText()` but specifies no failure handling. A corrupt PDF, a password-protected file, or an unsupported DOCX variant causes extraction to return empty or throw. The spec does not define whether the upload fails, whether a `knowledge_docs` row is created with no chunks, or whether the user is told. The likely outcome is a document that appears successfully uploaded in the UI but contributes nothing to search — a silent data-loss failure.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Make parse failures explicit and never create a doc record without content:
```typescript
async function parseDocument(buffer: ArrayBuffer, mime: string): Promise&lt;string&gt; {
  let text: string;
  try {
    if (mime === "application/pdf") text = await extractPdfText(buffer, env);
    else if (mime.includes("wordprocessingml")) text = await extractDocxText(buffer);
    else throw new UnsupportedFormat(mime);
  } catch (e) {
    throw new ParseError(`Failed to parse ${mime}: ${e.message}`);
  }
  if (!text || text.trim().length &lt; 10) {
    throw new ParseError("Document produced no extractable text (scanned image? empty file?)");
  }
  return text;
}
// Caller returns HTTP 422 with the reason; no knowledge_docs row is written on failure.
```
For scanned PDFs, offer an OCR fallback (Workers AI image-to-text) before failing.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-V16" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-V16</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#3B82F6;background:#3B82F618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">MEDIUM</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§naelao-knowledge — RAG — naelao-knowledge / embedding limits + billing</span>
