<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Embedding batch limits unhandled and embedding token cost is never billed</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Ingestion batches chunks in groups of 100 (the Vectorize upsert limit) and calls Workers AI embedding per batch, but Workers AI embedding has its own batch and rate limits that are neither documented nor handled — an oversized batch can fail or be silently truncated. Separately, embedding consumes real tokens (a 5MB document is ~1M embedding tokens) and the spec never records embedding token usage against billing, so this cost is entirely unaccounted.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Bound embedding batches independently, handle 413/429, and bill embedding tokens:
```typescript
const EMBED_BATCH = 25; // conservative for Workers AI embedding
let embeddingTokens = 0;
for (let i = 0; i &lt; chunks.length; i += EMBED_BATCH) {
  const batch = chunks.slice(i, i + EMBED_BATCH);
  const res = await withBackoff(() =&gt; env.AI.run("@cf/baai/bge-base-en-v1.5",
    { text: batch.map(c =&gt; c.text) }));
  embeddingTokens += batch.reduce((n, c) =&gt; n + estimateTokens(c.text), 0);
  // upsert in Vectorize-sized sub-batches of 100
}
await env.NAELAO_BILLING_QUEUE.send({
  type: "embedding_usage", spaceId, tokens: embeddingTokens,
  costMicroCents: BigInt(embeddingTokens) * EMBED_PRICE_MICRO_CENTS,
});
```</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-V17" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-V17</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Frontend — WebSocket — client / DO hibernation</span>
</div>
<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">handleWebSocketUpgrade never calls acceptWebSocket — hibernation drops messages, reconnect replay broken</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The WebSocket upgrade handler creates a `WebSocketPair` and returns the client socket but never calls `this.ctx.acceptWebSocket(server, tags)`. Without the hibernation-API accept call, the DO holds the socket only in memory: when the DO hibernates (which it will, aggressively), the socket is dropped and any messages the client sends afterward are never routed to `webSocketMessage()`. This silently breaks long-lived chat sessions and makes the reconnect-replay path unreachable, because the server side of the connection no longer exists after the first hibernation.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Use the hibernation WebSocket API so sockets survive eviction:
```typescript
async handleWebSocketUpgrade(request: Request): Promise&lt;Response&gt; {
  const pair = new WebSocketPair();
  const [client, server] = Object.values(pair);
  // Accept with the hibernation API — REQUIRED for messages to route post-hibernation
  this.ctx.acceptWebSocket(server, [`space:${spaceId}`, `user:${userId}`]);
  return new Response(null, { status: 101, webSocket: client });
}
// Implement the hibernation handlers (not in-memory addEventListener):
async webSocketMessage(ws: WebSocket, message: string | ArrayBuffer) { /* ... */ }
async webSocketClose(ws: WebSocket, code: number, reason: string) { /* ... */ }
```</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-V18" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-V18</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Frontend — WebSocket — client / message parsing</span>
</div>
<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">webSocketMessage parses JSON with no try/catch — a malformed frame evicts the DO mid-run</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The `webSocketMessage` handler calls `JSON.parse(message)` directly with no error handling. A binary frame, a truncated message from a flaky connection, or a malicious client sending non-JSON throws an uncaught exception inside the DO. An uncaught throw in a DO handler can tear down the DO, taking any in-flight agent turn with it. A single bad frame from one client thus aborts that user's running agent.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Guard parsing and handle non-JSON frames gracefully:
```typescript
async webSocketMessage(ws: WebSocket, message: string | ArrayBuffer) {
  if (typeof message !== "string") {
    ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: "error", message: "binary frames not supported" }));
    return;
  }
  let parsed: ClientMessage;
  try {
    parsed = JSON.parse(message);
  } catch {
    ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: "error", message: "invalid JSON" }));
    return;
  }
  try {
    await this.handleClientMessage(ws, parsed);
  } catch (e) {
    ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: "error", message: "internal error" }));
    // swallow — never let a single message crash the DO
  }
}
```</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-V19" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-V19</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Frontend — Streaming — client / disconnect billing</span>
