<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Token usage is billed only when the final SSE chunk reaches the client — disconnect = free inference</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Token accounting is performed when the terminal stream chunk (carrying usage totals) is delivered to the client. If the user disconnects before that chunk arrives — browser close, network drop, or deliberately — the usage is never recorded and the tokens consumed from the upstream model are never debited from the wallet. A user can obtain unlimited free inference simply by closing the connection just before completion. Billing must be tied to server-side completion, not client delivery.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Bill server-side on completion, independent of client delivery:
```typescript
// In the agent loop, on stream finish (server-side event, always fires)
onStepFinish: async ({ usage }) =&gt; {
  this.accumulatedUsage.input += usage.promptTokens;
  this.accumulatedUsage.output += usage.completionTokens;
},
// And in onChatEnd / onChatError (see G-V06) — always flush, even if client gone
async onChatEnd() {
  await env.NAELAO_BILLING_QUEUE.send({
    type: "token_usage", spaceId, userId,
    costMicroCents: calculateCostMicroCents(this.accumulatedUsage.input, this.accumulatedUsage.output),
  });
}
```
The client receiving the usage chunk becomes a display concern only; billing no longer depends on it.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-V20" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-V20</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#3B82F6;background:#3B82F618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">MEDIUM</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Frontend — Streaming — client / token buffer growth</span>
