<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Stream replay buffer grows unbounded — long runs create 100MB+ of rows and slow reconnects</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Every streamed token inserts a row into the replay buffer with no `LIMIT`, TTL, or cleanup. A long-running agent emitting 2M tokens creates 2M rows (~100MB) in the DO's SQLite. On reconnect, replay reads the entire buffer at once, causing multi-second reconnection stalls and blocking the agent loop while the read completes. The buffer is also never trimmed after the turn ends.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Bound the buffer to the current turn and trim aggressively:
```typescript
// Trim old turns when a new turn starts
async startTurn(turnId: string) {
  this.currentTurnId = turnId;
  // Keep only the current turn's buffer
  this.ctx.storage.sql.exec("DELETE FROM stream_buffer WHERE turn_id != ?", turnId);
}
// On reconnect, replay only events after the client's last-seen seq (see G-V03),
// and cap the replay to the most recent N events:
const tail = [...this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(
  "SELECT event_json FROM stream_buffer WHERE turn_id=? AND seq&gt;? ORDER BY seq DESC LIMIT 2000",
  turnId, lastSeq
)].reverse();
```
For very long outputs, checkpoint completed text to the messages table and clear the per-token buffer.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-V21" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-V21</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#3B82F6;background:#3B82F618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">MEDIUM</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Frontend — API — client / pagination cursor</span>
</div>
<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Pagination cursors on created_at collide on same-millisecond inserts — page 2 silently skips messages</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Thread pagination uses `WHERE created_at &gt; ?` with `created_at` as the cursor. Multiple messages inserted in the same millisecond (common during multi-agent runs where several tool results land together) share an identical `created_at`. When the cursor lands on that timestamp, the next page's `&gt; ?` filter skips ALL messages with that exact timestamp, silently dropping them from the UI. Users see gaps in their conversation that do not correspond to any deletion.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Use a compound, strictly-monotonic cursor (timestamp + tiebreaker id):
```sql
-- Cursor encodes both created_at and id
SELECT * FROM messages
WHERE space_id = ?
  AND (created_at, id) &gt; (?, ?)   -- compound comparison, no collisions
ORDER BY created_at ASC, id ASC
LIMIT ?;
```
```typescript
// Cursor = base64({ createdAt, id }) of the last row on the previous page
const cursor = { createdAt: lastRow.created_at, id: lastRow.id };
```
Alternatively use a monotonic auto-increment `seq` column as the sole cursor — guaranteed unique and ordered.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-V22" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-V22</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Finetune — Pipeline — FinetuneJobDO / SpaceDO wiring</span>
