<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Fine-tune jobs submitted to Together AI but never tracked locally — sweeper polls a 404 endpoint</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The fine-tune worker successfully submits jobs to Together AI, then calls a SpaceDO endpoint (`/finetune/*`) to record the job — but SpaceDO has no `finetune_jobs` table and no such route, so the call returns 404 and the job is never tracked locally. The sweeper's `sweepStaleFineTuneJobs()` queries the same missing endpoint and also 404s. The result: jobs run and bill on Together AI with zero local visibility, no status updates, no completion handling, and no way to surface results to the user.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add the table and route to SpaceDO and wire the worker to it:
```sql
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS finetune_jobs (
  id              TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  space_id        TEXT NOT NULL,
  provider_job_id TEXT,
  status          TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'queued'
                  CHECK (status IN ('queued','running','completed','failed','cancelled')),
  error_message   TEXT,
  result_model    TEXT,
  cost_micro_cents INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
  created_at      INTEGER DEFAULT (unixepoch('now')*1000),
  updated_at      INTEGER
);
```
```typescript
// SpaceDO route
case "/finetune/create": { /* INSERT row, return job */ }
case "/finetune/update": { /* UPDATE status/result by provider_job_id */ }
case "/finetune/stale":  { /* SELECT running jobs older than N for the sweeper */ }
```</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-V23" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-V23</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Finetune — Pipeline — FinetuneJobDO / alarm idempotency</span>
</div>
<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Polling alarm fires at-least-once with no idempotency guard — duplicate completion notifications</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">CF Durable Object alarms guarantee at-least-once delivery; an alarm handler can fire more than once for the same scheduled time (e.g., after a timeout-and-retry). The fine-tune polling `alarm()` sends a completion notification and updates downstream state each time it observes a finished job. Without a guard, a double-fire sends the user two "training complete" notifications and may re-trigger any completion side-effects (model registration, billing settlement).</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Guard the alarm with a last-handled marker and make completion handling idempotent:
```typescript
async alarm() {
  const lastAt = (await this.ctx.storage.get&lt;number&gt;("alarm_handled_at")) ?? 0;
  if (Date.now() - lastAt &lt; 5000) return; // collapse duplicate fires
  await this.ctx.storage.put("alarm_handled_at", Date.now());

  const status = await pollProvider(this.providerJobId);
  if (status === "completed" &amp;&amp; !(await this.ctx.storage.get("completion_handled"))) {
    await this.ctx.storage.put("completion_handled", true);
    await notifyUser(this.spaceId, "finetune_complete");
    await settleBilling(this.jobId);
    return; // do not reschedule
  }
  await this.ctx.storage.setAlarm(Date.now() + this.pollInterval);
}
```</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-V24" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-V24</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Finetune — Pipeline — FinetuneJobDO / budget + concurrency</span>
</div>
<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">No concurrent-job cap or pre-submission budget check — a user can exhaust the space budget with parallel jobs</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The fine-tune handler validates dataset format and a 50-example minimum but never checks how many jobs the space already has running, nor reserves credits before submission, nor estimates cost up front. A user (or a buggy client retry loop) can start dozens of long-running training jobs in parallel; each bills on Together AI for hours, and the space's monthly budget is blown to thousands of dollars before anyone notices, because the only billing signal arrives at job completion.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Enforce a concurrency limit and reserve estimated cost before submitting:
```typescript
async createFinetuneJob(spaceId: string, dataset: Dataset) {
  const MAX_CONCURRENT = 3;
  const running = await spaceDO.countRunningFinetuneJobs(spaceId);
  if (running &gt;= MAX_CONCURRENT) {
    throw new Error(`Concurrent fine-tune limit (${MAX_CONCURRENT}) reached`);
  }
  const estCents = estimateFinetuneCostCents(dataset);
  const reservation = await walletDO.reserveCredits(estCents); // throws if insufficient
  try {
    const providerJobId = await submitToProvider(dataset);
    await spaceDO.createFinetuneJob({ spaceId, providerJobId, reservation });
  } catch (e) {
    await walletDO.releaseReservation(reservation);
    throw e;
  }
}
```</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-V25" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-V25</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#3B82F6;background:#3B82F618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">MEDIUM</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Finetune — Pipeline — FinetuneJobDO / dataset validation</span>
</div>
<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Dataset validation checks format and count only — no size, sequence-length, or schema-consistency checks</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Validation confirms JSONL format and a 50-example minimum but does not check: maximum file size, maximum sequence length per example (examples exceeding the model's context are rejected by the provider mid-job), per-example token counts, or schema consistency across examples (some examples missing the `assistant` turn). A dataset that passes Naelao's validation can still fail partway through training on Together AI, wasting the reserved budget and the user's time with a cryptic provider error.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add comprehensive pre-submission validation:
```typescript
function validateDataset(lines: string[]): ValidationResult {
  const errors: string[] = [];
  if (lines.length &lt; 50) errors.push("min 50 examples");
  if (lines.length &gt; 100_000) errors.push("max 100k examples");
  let totalBytes = 0;
  for (const [i, line] of lines.entries()) {
    const ex = JSON.parse(line);
    if (!ex.messages?.some(m =&gt; m.role === "assistant"))
      errors.push(`example ${i}: missing assistant turn`);
    const tokens = estimateTokens(JSON.stringify(ex));
    if (tokens &gt; MAX_SEQ_LEN) errors.push(`example ${i}: ${tokens} tokens &gt; ${MAX_SEQ_LEN}`);
    totalBytes += line.length;
  }
  if (totalBytes &gt; 500 * 1024 * 1024) errors.push("dataset &gt; 500MB");
  return { valid: errors.length === 0, errors };
}
```</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-V26" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-V26</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§MiniAGI — Federated — MiniAGIDO / result merging</span>
</div>
<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Federated query concatenates domain results with no dedup or conflict resolution</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">MiniAGIDO's `query()` fetches matching records from each granted data domain in R2 and concatenates them into a single LLM prompt. The same record present in two domains (e.g., order #123 in both "sales" and "customer" domains) appears twice, wasting context and biasing the model toward duplicated facts. When two domains hold conflicting values for the same entity (domain A: price=$100, domain B: price=$150), both are injected with no resolution strategy, leaving the model to guess which is authoritative.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Deduplicate by record key and resolve conflicts before injection:
```typescript
function mergeDomainResults(results: DomainRecord[][]): MergedRecord[] {
  const byKey = new Map&lt;string, MergedRecord&gt;();
  for (const domainResults of results) {
    for (const rec of domainResults) {
      const existing = byKey.get(rec.id);
      if (!existing) { byKey.set(rec.id, { ...rec, sources: [rec.domain] }); continue; }
      // Conflict: keep higher-trust domain, record the discrepancy
      existing.sources.push(rec.domain);
      if (DOMAIN_TRUST[rec.domain] &gt; DOMAIN_TRUST[existing.domain]) {
        byKey.set(rec.id, { ...rec, sources: existing.sources, conflicts: existing });
      }
    }
  }
  return [...byKey.values()];
}
```
Surface conflicts to the model explicitly (`&lt;conflict&gt;` markers) so it can flag uncertainty rather than silently picking one.</p></div>
