<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Federated fetch has no size cap — a large domain overflows the prompt and OOMs the DO</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">`fetchDomainData()` pulls all matching records from a granted domain with no pagination, streaming, or size cap. A domain backed by a 1M-row CSV loads entirely into the DO's memory and is injected into a single LLM prompt, exceeding both the DO memory budget and the model's context window. There is no cursor-based fetch and no early termination once enough relevant context is gathered.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Cap fetched data and use relevance-bounded retrieval instead of full scans:
```typescript
async function fetchDomainData(domain: string, query: string, env: Env) {
  const MAX_RECORDS = 200;
  const MAX_BYTES = 256 * 1024;
  // Prefer a vector/index lookup scoped to the domain over a full scan
  const hits = await env.NAELAO_VECTORIZE.query(await embed(query, env), {
    topK: MAX_RECORDS,
    filter: { domain: { $eq: domain }, spaceId: { $eq: spaceId } },
  });
  let bytes = 0;
  const records = [];
  for (const h of hits.matches) {
    const r = await loadRecord(h.id, env);
    bytes += JSON.stringify(r).length;
    if (bytes &gt; MAX_BYTES) break;
    records.push(r);
  }
  return records;
}
```</p></div>
