<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">User deletion only soft-deletes SpaceDO — no cross-system erasure across R2, Vectorize, Analytics, KV, AI cache</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">User data lives in at least six systems: SpaceDO/AssistantDO SQLite, R2 (files, skills, workspace), Vectorize (memory and knowledge vectors), Analytics Engine (events), KV (caches), and the AI Gateway response cache. A right-to-deletion request only soft-deletes the SpaceDO row. The personal data in R2, Vectorize, Analytics Engine, and caches remains, which is a direct GDPR Article 17 violation. Analytics Engine in particular cannot delete individual rows at all, so it needs a distinct strategy (avoid storing PII, or pseudonymize).</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Implement an erasure saga as a CF Workflow that fans out across every store:
```typescript
export class ErasureWorkflow extends WorkflowEntrypoint {
  async run(event, step) {
    const { userId, spaceId } = event.payload;
    await step.do("purge-do-sqlite", () =&gt; purgeUserRows(userId, spaceId));
    await step.do("purge-r2", () =&gt; deleteR2Prefix(`spaces/${spaceId}/assistants/${userId}/`));
    await step.do("purge-vectorize", async () =&gt; {
      const v = await env.NAELAO_VECTORIZE.query([0], { topK: 1000,
        filter: { spaceId: { $eq: spaceId }, userId: { $eq: userId } } });
      await env.NAELAO_VECTORIZE.deleteByIds(v.matches.map(m =&gt; m.id));
    });
    await step.do("purge-kv", () =&gt; deleteUserKVKeys(userId));
    await step.do("emit-erasure-certificate", () =&gt; recordErasure(userId, Date.now()));
  }
}
```
For Analytics Engine: never write raw PII; store a salted user hash that can be disassociated, and document the 90-day rolling window after which events age out.</p></div>
