<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Analytics Engine fields are positional with no schema registry — inserting a field corrupts every existing query</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Analytics Engine data points are positional: `blobs[0..19]` and `doubles[0..19]`. Naelao writes data points across many call sites with hand-maintained field ordering. Adding a new field in the middle (or a developer guessing the wrong index) silently shifts every subsequent field, so existing dashboards and queries that read `blobs[3]` now read different data with no error. There is no central schema registry mapping field names to indices.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Centralize the field schema and write through a typed helper:
```typescript
// Single source of truth for field positions
const ANALYTICS_SCHEMA = {
  blobs:   { eventType: 0, spaceId: 1, userId: 2, component: 3, detail: 4 },
  doubles: { count: 0, latencyMs: 1, tokens: 2, costMicroCents: 3 },
  index1: "eventType",
} as const;

function writeAnalytics(env: Env, event: TypedAnalyticsEvent) {
  const blobs = new Array(20).fill("");
  const doubles = new Array(20).fill(0);
  blobs[ANALYTICS_SCHEMA.blobs.eventType] = event.eventType;
  blobs[ANALYTICS_SCHEMA.blobs.spaceId]   = event.spaceId;
  doubles[ANALYTICS_SCHEMA.doubles.tokens] = event.tokens ?? 0;
  env.NAELAO_ANALYTICS.writeDataPoint({ blobs, doubles, indexes: [event.eventType] });
}
```
New fields only ever append at the next free index; never reorder. Version the schema and document each index.</p></div>
