<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">22 Workers with zero W3C trace-context propagation — cross-Worker requests cannot be correlated</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Naelao spans ~22 Workers plus many Durable Objects, communicating via Service Bindings, queues, and HTTP. No `traceparent` (W3C Trace Context) header is propagated across these boundaries. When a request fans out (router → agent → tool → MCP hub → billing queue), there is no correlation ID linking the spans, so debugging a slow or failed request across Workers is impossible — each Worker's logs are an isolated island.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Generate a trace ID at the edge and propagate it through every hop:
```typescript
// At naelao-router (edge): create or accept a traceparent
const traceId = request.headers.get("traceparent") ?? crypto.randomUUID().replace(/-/g, "");
// Propagate on every downstream call
await env.NAELAO_AGENTS.fetch(new Request(url, {
  headers: { ...headers, "traceparent": `00-${traceId}-${spanId}-01` },
}));
// On queue sends, include it in the message body
await env.NAELAO_BILLING_QUEUE.send({ ...payload, traceId });
// Every log line and Analytics Engine event includes traceId in a fixed blob slot
```
Forward all logs to a Tail Worker that indexes by `traceId` for end-to-end request reconstruction.</p></div>
