<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Static shared NAELAO_INTERNAL_TOKEN for all inter-Worker calls — one compromised Worker exposes every space</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Inter-Worker calls across at least eight call sites authenticate with a single static `NAELAO_INTERNAL_TOKEN` shared by all Workers. It has no expiry, no per-request scope, and no caller identity. If any Worker is compromised — for example via a malicious dynamic tool or skill that achieves code execution in a Worker isolate — the attacker holds a token that authorizes calls to every internal API for every space, and nothing in the audit trail distinguishes the malicious calls from legitimate platform traffic.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Replace the static token with short-lived, caller-scoped service JWTs:
```typescript
// Caller mints a 5-minute JWT identifying itself and the target scope
async function mintServiceToken(env: Env, caller: string, scope: string) {
  return await signJWT({ iss: caller, aud: "naelao-internal", scope,
    exp: Math.floor(Date.now()/1000) + 300 }, env.SERVICE_SIGNING_KEY);
}
// Callee verifies signature, issuer, audience, scope, and expiry
const { payload } = await jwtVerify(token, key, {
  audience: "naelao-internal", algorithms: ["HS256"],
});
if (!payload.scope?.includes(requiredScope)) return new Response("forbidden", { status: 403 });
```
Log `iss` (calling Worker) and `scope` on every internal call so compromised callers are attributable.</p></div>
</div>
