<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Webhook signing secrets lack per-integration isolation and rotation grace period</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Webhook signing secrets (Slack signing secret, Stripe webhook secret, etc.) are stored with no documented per-integration scoping or rotation support. If stored under the shared platform encryption key, a key compromise exposes all of them; if a provider regenerates its signing secret (a routine security action), Naelao has no way to accept both the old and new secret during a transition, so verification breaks for every event the moment the secret rotates.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Version webhook secrets and accept overlapping secrets during rotation:
```sql
CREATE TABLE webhook_secrets (
  id           TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  integration  TEXT NOT NULL,        -- 'slack' | 'stripe' | ...
  secret_enc   TEXT NOT NULL,        -- per-space DEK encrypted
  version      INTEGER NOT NULL,
  active       INTEGER DEFAULT 1,
  created_at   INTEGER, rotated_at INTEGER
);
```
```typescript
// During rotation, mark old secret active for a grace window and verify against both
for (const s of activeSecretsFor(integration)) {
  if (verifySignature(body, sig, decrypt(s.secret_enc))) return true;
}
return false;
```
Expire the old secret after a 30-day grace period.</p></div>
