<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-W17</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Email — Inbound — naelao-notifications / sender verification</span>
</div>
<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Inbound email is processed with no SPF/DKIM/DMARC verification — spoofed mail triggers agent actions</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">If inbound email handling is enabled (email as a channel into the assistant), there is no documented verification of sender authenticity. An attacker can spoof the From address of a trusted user or system and send an email that the assistant treats as a legitimate instruction — triggering agent actions, approvals, or data access under the spoofed identity. SPF, DKIM, and DMARC results are available on inbound mail but are never checked.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Verify authentication results before acting on any inbound email:
```typescript
async function handleInboundEmail(msg: ForwardableEmailMessage, env: Env) {
  const authResults = msg.headers.get("Authentication-Results") ?? "";
  const spfPass   = /spf=pass/.test(authResults);
  const dkimPass  = /dkim=pass/.test(authResults);
  const dmarcPass = /dmarc=pass/.test(authResults);
  if (!(spfPass &amp;&amp; dkimPass &amp;&amp; dmarcPass)) {
    await quarantine(msg, "failed_email_auth");
    return;
  }
  // Map the verified From to a known user; reject if unmapped
  const user = await resolveVerifiedSender(msg.from, env);
  if (!user) return quarantine(msg, "unknown_sender");
  await routeToAssistant(user, msg);
}
```
Never bind email-sender identity to an account on the From header alone.</p></div>
</div>
