<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">No email loop prevention — an auto-responder on the other end creates an unbounded reply storm</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The system sends transactional and assistant emails but has no safeguard against reply loops. If the assistant emails a user (or another system) that has an auto-responder or auto-forward configured, the auto-reply arrives inbound, the assistant responds, that response is auto-replied, and so on. This exhausts the email quota, damages sender reputation, and can spiral within minutes.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add loop-detection headers and a per-thread send budget:
```typescript
// On every outbound email, set anti-loop headers
headers.set("Auto-Submitted", "auto-generated");
headers.set("X-Naelao-Loop-Token", threadLoopToken);
// On inbound, drop machine-generated replies and enforce a count cap
if (/auto-(replied|generated)/.test(msg.headers.get("Auto-Submitted") ?? "")) return;
if (msg.headers.get("Precedence") === "bulk") return;
const count = await incrThreadEmailCount(threadId);
if (count &gt; MAX_EMAILS_PER_THREAD_PER_HOUR) { await pauseThread(threadId); return; }
```</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-W19" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
