<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Uploaded images are not size/dimension-checked before base64 vision encoding — token explosion and OOM</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Images supplied as agent input are base64-encoded and inlined into the model prompt with no prior size or dimension validation. A user uploading a 100MB or 12000×12000 image produces an enormous base64 string that explodes token usage (and cost) and can OOM the Worker (128MB memory limit) when several large images are processed concurrently. There is no downscaling or rejection path.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Validate and downscale before encoding:
```typescript
const MAX_BYTES = 5 * 1024 * 1024;     // 5MB
const MAX_DIM = 2048;
async function prepareImage(buf: ArrayBuffer, env: Env) {
  if (buf.byteLength &gt; MAX_BYTES) throw new InputError("image exceeds 5MB");
  const meta = await probeImage(buf);    // dimensions + real format
  if (meta.width &gt; MAX_DIM || meta.height &gt; MAX_DIM) {
    buf = await env.IMAGES.input(buf).transform({ width: MAX_DIM, fit: "scale-down" }).output();
  }
  return { data: bytesToBase64(buf), mediaType: meta.mime };
}
```
Prefer referencing images by URL (CF Images / R2) where the model supports it, instead of inlining base64.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-W21" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-W21</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Files — Upload Safety — file-manager / magic-byte validation</span>
