<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">File uploads trust the declared MIME type — polyglot files bypass downstream type assumptions</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The write/upload path accepts a declared content type (and a base64 `encoding` flag) but never validates that the file's actual magic bytes match the declared type. A ZIP or HTML file can be uploaded as `image/png`, or an executable disguised as `.txt`. Any downstream consumer that trusts the declared type (a vision model, a previewer, another user downloading the file) is exposed to a polyglot/confused-type attack.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Sniff magic bytes and reject mismatches:
```typescript
import { fileTypeFromBuffer } from "file-type";
async function validateUpload(buf: ArrayBuffer, declaredType: string) {
  const detected = await fileTypeFromBuffer(buf);
  const ALLOWED = new Set(["image/png","image/jpeg","application/pdf","text/plain", /*...*/]);
  if (!detected || !ALLOWED.has(detected.mime)) {
    throw new InputError(`unsupported or undetectable file type`);
  }
  if (detected.mime !== declaredType) {
    throw new InputError(`declared ${declaredType} but content is ${detected.mime}`);
  }
  return detected.mime; // trust the sniffed type downstream, not the declared one
}
```</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-W22" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-W22</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Files — Upload Safety — file-manager / presigned URL TTL</span>
