<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Presigned R2 upload URLs have no documented expiration — a leaked URL grants indefinite write access</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Direct-to-R2 uploads use presigned URLs but the spec does not define an expiration TTL or path scoping. A presigned URL that never expires (or expires far in the future) is a standing write capability: if it leaks (browser history, logs, a shared link), an attacker can inject arbitrary files into the space's workspace at the signed path for as long as the URL is valid.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Issue short-lived, tightly-scoped presigned URLs:
```typescript
async function getUploadUrl(spaceId: string, filename: string, env: Env) {
  // Constrain the key to the caller's workspace prefix — no traversal
  const key = `spaces/${spaceId}/uploads/${crypto.randomUUID()}/${sanitize(filename)}`;
  const url = await env.R2.createPresignedUrl({
    bucket: "naelao-workspace", key, method: "PUT",
    expiresIn: 300,                 // 5 minutes
    conditions: { contentLengthRange: [1, 50 * 1024 * 1024] }, // size cap
  });
  return { url, key };
}
```
Validate the uploaded object (magic bytes, size) server-side after upload before treating it as usable.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-W23" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-W23</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#3B82F6;background:#3B82F618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">MEDIUM</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Files — Download — file-manager / content-type sniffing</span>
</div>
<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Download content-type comes from stored metadata without re-sniffing — enables type-confusion on download</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">On download, the file-manager returns the `contentType` from R2 object metadata, which was set at upload time from the (untrusted) declared type. If a user uploaded a mislabeled file (e.g., an HTML file stored as `text/plain`), downstream agents or users receive it with a content type that does not match its bytes, enabling type-confusion attacks (HTML served as something benign, then rendered).</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Re-derive the content type from content, and set safe download headers:
```typescript
async function downloadFile(key: string, env: Env) {
  const obj = await env.R2.get(key);
  const buf = await obj.arrayBuffer();
  const detected = (await fileTypeFromBuffer(buf))?.mime ?? "application/octet-stream";
  return new Response(buf, {
    headers: {
      "Content-Type": detected,                 // trust content, not stored metadata
      "Content-Disposition": "attachment",        // never inline-render user files
      "X-Content-Type-Options": "nosniff",
    },
  });
}
```</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-W24" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-W24</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#3B82F6;background:#3B82F618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">MEDIUM</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Files — Path Safety — file-manager / path enforcement layer</span>
</div>
<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Relative-path validation is enforced only in app code — no R2-prefix enforcement as defense in depth</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Path traversal is blocked by a `validateRelativePath()` check at tool-execution time that rejects `..` and absolute paths. This is a single layer: any code path that forgets to call it, or a bug in the check, allows a crafted path to escape the space's workspace prefix and read/write another tenant's objects. There is no second enforcement boundary that constrains all R2 operations to the space prefix regardless of the application path.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Wrap R2 access in a per-space client that hard-prefixes every key:
```typescript
class SpaceScopedR2 {
  constructor(private bucket: R2Bucket, private prefix: string) {}
  private resolve(path: string): string {
    const key = `${this.prefix}/${path}`.replace(/\/+/g, "/");
    // Normalize and assert containment — defense in depth
    if (!normalize(key).startsWith(this.prefix + "/")) throw new Error("path escape");
    return key;
  }
  get(p: string)  { return this.bucket.get(this.resolve(p)); }
  put(p: string, v: any) { return this.bucket.put(this.resolve(p), v); }
}
// All file ops go through SpaceScopedR2(bucket, `spaces/${spaceId}`), never raw bucket.
```</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-W25" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-W25</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Orchestration — State — NaelaoAgentDO / setState conflicts</span>
