<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Whole state object is broadcast on every change — large state floods every connected client per token</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">State sync broadcasts the entire serialized state object to all connected WebSocket clients whenever it changes. If the agent accumulates a large state (megabytes of session context), every incremental update — potentially every streamed token — re-sends the full object to every client. This wastes bandwidth, stalls clients, and scales quadratically with state size × update frequency × client count.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Send deltas, not whole-state, and cap synced state size:
```typescript
// Maintain synced state as a small view; keep bulk data in SQLite (queryable, not synced)
const SYNC_BUDGET = 64 * 1024; // 64KB cap on the synced object
// Broadcast JSON-patch deltas instead of the full object
import { compare } from "fast-json-patch";
const patch = compare(prevSyncedState, nextSyncedState);
if (patch.length) this.broadcast(JSON.stringify({ type: "state_patch", patch }));
```
Keep transcripts, tool outputs, and large blobs out of synced state entirely — clients fetch them on demand by ID.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-W27" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
<div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-W27</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
<span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Orchestration — State — NaelaoAgentDO / state ownership boundary</span>
