<h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Sub-agent spawn passes only a task description — conversation, memory, and intermediate context are lost</h3>
<div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">When the assistant spawns a sub-agent, the only context transferred is the task description string. The parent's conversation history, relevant Memory OS facts, system prompt, and any intermediate results are not handed off. A sub-agent asked to "research the competitor mentioned earlier" has no access to "earlier," so it either fails or hallucinates. There is no atomic handoff primitive that snapshots and transfers the needed context.</p></div>
<div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div>
<p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Define a handoff payload that snapshots scoped context atomically:
```typescript
async spawnSubAgent(task: SubAgentTask) {
  const handoff = {
    task: task.description,
    // Curated, scoped context — not the whole history
    relevantMemory: await this.recallForTask(task.description, { topK: 8 }),
    recentMessages: await this.getRecentMessages(10),
    parentRef: { spaceId: this.spaceId, threadId: this.threadId, agentId: this.id.toString() },
    handoffId: crypto.randomUUID(),
  };
  // Persist the handoff so it survives parent eviction (see G-W30)
  this.ctx.storage.sql.exec("INSERT INTO handoffs (id, payload, status) VALUES (?,?,'sent')",
    handoff.handoffId, JSON.stringify(handoff));
  return dispatchSubAgent(handoff);
}
```</p></div>
