<h2 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:32px;font-weight:700;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.02em;margin:0 0 6px;">Appendix X — Sixteenth Pass</h2>
<p style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 32px;">Rate Limiting &amp; Abuse · RAG Pipeline · WebSocket Protocol · Observability · Skills Security · Multi-Tenancy Isolation</p>

<div id="G-X01" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X01</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Agent Runtime — Tool Execution — AgentDO / tool dispatch</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Per-Tool-Call Rate Limit Missing — Unbounded Recursive Tool Loops Drain Credits</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The spec defines agent tiers and allowed tools but places no ceiling on how many times an agent may call a single tool within one run. A misbehaving agent can issue web_search 10,000 times recursively before the run is manually cancelled, consuming the entire space credit balance in minutes. The MAX_ITERATIONS guard exists for agentic reasoning loops but is never applied to individual tool invocation counts.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add maxToolCallsPerTool (default 100) and maxToolCallsPerRun (default 500) counters to AgentDO per-run state, enforced in the tool dispatch layer before each invocation. Return a structured error and mark the run failed-rate-exceeded when exceeded. Log the event to Analytics Engine for billing reconciliation and admin alerting.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X02" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X02</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Queue Consumers — naelao-notifications — CF Queues / maxConcurrency</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Queue Consumer Unbounded Parallelism — Burst Traffic Causes Thundering Herd on Downstream APIs</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">CF Queues dispatches all messages in a batch to the consumer Worker in parallel when maxConcurrency is unset. A space completing a large batch job can enqueue 10,000 notification events simultaneously, triggering 10,000 concurrent downstream API calls (APNs, FCM, Slack) and immediately rate-limiting those services. The cascade affects all spaces sharing the consumer Worker, not just the offending space.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Set maxConcurrency: 50 and maxBatchSize: 100 on every queue consumer binding in wrangler.jsonc. Implement a per-space semaphore inside the consumer: allow at most 10 concurrent deliveries per spaceId. Log consumer queue depth to Analytics Engine every minute as a capacity-alerting metric.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X03" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X03</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§AI Gateway — Model Invocation — callAIGateway / retry logic</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">AI Gateway 429 Response Not Caught at Worker Level — No Per-Space Exponential Backoff</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">When a space exhausts its AI Gateway token-per-minute quota the gateway returns HTTP 429 with a Retry-After header. The agent Workers do not inspect this header; they either surface the error immediately to the user or retry in a tight synchronous loop, burning the remaining quota and locking the space out for the entire minute. No backoff is stored across requests.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Wrap all callAIGateway() calls in a retry helper that detects status 429, reads the Retry-After header (default 60 s), and stores a per-space backoff timestamp in KV (TTL = backoff seconds). Reject subsequent calls for that space until the backoff expires. Surface a structured error to clients: { type: "quota_exceeded", retry_after_ms }.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X04" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X04</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Billing — Credit Enforcement — SpaceDO / billing queue</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">No Pre-Run Credit Reservation — Asynchronous Billing Enables Unbounded Overspend</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Credit checks occur after each LLM call via the billing event queue, which is processed asynchronously. Between the first LLM call and the billing event being consumed by naelao-billing, dozens more LLM calls can be issued. Under high concurrency a space with zero remaining credits can accumulate a large negative balance before the first billing event closes the account, incurring real API cost with no immediate enforcement.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Pre-reserve credits synchronously at run start: deduct a worst-case reservation (e.g., 10,000 tokens x tier rate) from the SpaceDO SQLite credit ledger before the first LLM call. Refund the unused portion at run end. Reject run start with a user-facing quota error if available_credits &lt; minimum_reservation.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X05" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X05</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#3B82F6;background:#3B82F618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Personalisation — Apps Economy — KV TTL / cache expiry</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Personalisation Cache TTL Has No Jitter — Simultaneous Expiry Causes Hourly Rate-Limit Spike</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">UI personalisation profiles are cached with a fixed 3600-second TTL set at first authentication. All users who authenticated around the same time expire their caches simultaneously, issuing hundreds of synchronous LLM personalisation calls to the AI Gateway at the same clock second. This spikes per-space token consumption and triggers quota limits, degrading experience for all concurrent users.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Apply jitter at cache-write time: ttl = 3600 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 600). Store next_regen_at = Date.now() + ttl * 1000 in the cached KV value. Derive TTL from last cache write rather than user login time, so rolling updates spread expirations uniformly across a 10-minute window.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X06" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X06</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Billing — naelao-billing queue consumer — Analytics Engine / SpaceDO ledger</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Billing Events Lost on Analytics Engine Unavailability — No Durable Fallback Ledger</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The billing pipeline writes credit deduction events to Analytics Engine via the naelao-billing queue consumer. If Analytics Engine is unavailable the consumer nacks the message; after maxRetries is exhausted the message is dead-lettered. The credit ledger in SpaceDO SQLite is never updated, leaving the space with phantom credits — balances that were spent but never deducted.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Make SpaceDO SQLite the authoritative billing ledger: subtract credits synchronously from SQLite at the moment of LLM call, before enqueuing to Analytics Engine. AE receives analytics-only copies; AE loss is cosmetic. Reconcile monthly by querying AE against SpaceDO and alerting on divergence above a threshold.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X07" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X07</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Knowledge — naelao-knowledge — chunker / embedding pipeline</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Chunker Uses Word Count Not BPE Token Count — Chunks Overflow Embedding Model Context Window</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The chunker splits documents at 512 "tokens" measured as whitespace-separated words. One word averages 1.3–1.8 BPE subword tokens for the @cf/baai/bge-base-en-v1.5 model, whose maximum context is 512 subword tokens. A 512-word chunk routinely exceeds 700 subword tokens, causing the embedding call to silently truncate the tail of each chunk and losing the last ~30% of information before indexing.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Replace word-count splitting with a BPE tokenizer matching the embedding model (e.g., gpt-tokenizer, ~20 kB WASM). Target 400 subword tokens per chunk with 50-token overlap. Validate chunk.tokenCount &lt;= 512 before calling ai.run(); log a warning and split further if exceeded. This applies to all content types including code and non-Latin documents.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X08" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X08</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Knowledge — Vectorize — embedding model metadata</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">No Embedding Model Version Tracked in Vectorize — Upgrade Causes Silent Vector Space Drift</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Vectors are upserted to Vectorize with no embedding_model metadata field. When the platform upgrades from bge-base-en-v1.5 to a newer model, new document embeddings occupy a different vector space than existing ones. Cosine similarity between old and new vectors is meaningless noise; semantic search quality degrades silently across all spaces that contain pre-upgrade knowledge documents.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add embedding_model TEXT NOT NULL to the knowledge_chunks SQLite table and to every Vectorize vector's metadata. On model upgrade, run a background migration job that re-embeds all chunks with the new model, upserts to Vectorize, and deletes old vectors. Gate query paths to compare only vectors whose model version matches the query embedding's model.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X09" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X09</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Knowledge — Vectorize — document update / vector cleanup</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Stale Vectors Accumulate on Document Updates — Old Chunk Versions Permanently Indexed</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">When a knowledge document is edited, new chunks are upserted by ID but if the new version produces fewer chunks than the old version, surplus old-version vector IDs are never deleted. After ten edits, up to ten versions of the same document are simultaneously indexed, causing semantic search to return duplicates, outdated content, and potentially confidential draft material that has since been revised or deleted.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Maintain a vector_ids JSON column in knowledge_chunks SQLite. On each document update, read the old vector IDs, call vectorize.deleteByIds(oldIds) before upserting new chunks, then write the new IDs back in the same SQLite transaction so a partial failure does not orphan vectors. Schedule a nightly reconciliation job to detect and remove any orphaned vectors.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X10" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X10</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Knowledge — RAG Pipeline — retrieval quality / re-ranking</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">No Relevance Score Threshold or Re-ranking — Low-Quality Chunks Injected into Prompt</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The RAG pipeline queries Vectorize for top-K results and injects all K into the system prompt regardless of similarity scores. A weak semantic match at 0.55 is injected alongside a strong match at 0.95, diluting answer quality with irrelevant context. For large knowledge bases the true answer may rank beyond the hardcoded retrieval window, making it invisible to the agent.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Set a minimum relevance threshold (default 0.72, configurable per space). After Vectorize returns topK=20 candidates, filter out scores below the threshold. Optionally pass the shortlist to a cross-encoder re-ranker for final scoring before injection. Log retrieved chunk IDs, scores, and the injected count in run telemetry to enable quality debugging.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X11" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X11</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#3B82F6;background:#3B82F618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Knowledge — ContextManager — system prompt / context assembly</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Knowledge Block Has No Token Budget — Context Overflow Crashes Turn With Unspecified Error</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The ContextManager inserts retrieved knowledge chunks into the system prompt with no declared token budget. If five chunks total 12,000 tokens and the model's context window is 32,000 tokens, the combined system prompt plus conversation history overflows and the model API returns a context-length error that surfaces as an opaque run failure with no user-visible explanation about what happened.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Define max_knowledge_tokens (default 4,000, configurable in space settings) for the knowledge block. ContextManager sorts chunks by relevance DESC, appends chunks until the budget is exhausted, then stops. Log { chunks_available, chunks_injected, tokens_used } per turn and surface a user-visible notice when knowledge was truncated due to context limits.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X12" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X12</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EF4444;background:#EF444418;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">CRITICAL</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Knowledge — GDPR / Vectorize — right-to-erasure / deleteByIds</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Deleted Knowledge Documents Leave Vectors in Vectorize — GDPR Article 17 Violation</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The knowledge deletion endpoint removes rows from SpaceDO SQLite and the R2 object but never calls vectorize.deleteByIds(). Deleted documents' chunk vectors remain indexed and searchable indefinitely. Semantic queries against the space may return content from legally erased records, violating GDPR Article 17 right to erasure and exposing the platform to regulatory liability.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">On knowledge document deletion, retrieve all vector IDs from the knowledge_chunks.vector_ids column and call await env.VECTORIZE.deleteByIds(vectorIds) before returning 200. Confirm deletion in the response. Add a nightly reconciliation job that cross-checks Vectorize metadata against SpaceDO knowledge_chunks and deletes any orphaned vectors with no matching document record.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X13" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X13</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#3B82F6;background:#3B82F618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Knowledge — Vectorize — topK / retrieval configuration</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">topK Hardcoded at 5 — Builders Cannot Tune Retrieval Depth for Larger Knowledge Bases</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The knowledge search endpoint reads topK from the query string but falls back to 5 with no upper-bound cap or builder-level configuration. Vectorize supports up to 100 results. Builders debugging why their agent misses known information have no way to increase retrieval depth without modifying platform code, and the default of 5 frequently misses relevant chunks in knowledge bases larger than 500 documents.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add knowledge.retrieval_top_k (range 5–50, default 10) to space configuration in SpaceDO. Expose it in the builder dashboard. The knowledge search endpoint reads this config and clamps topK: Math.min(requested, space.retrieval_top_k). Document the trade-off in the builder docs: higher topK increases retrieved tokens and context cost per turn.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X14" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X14</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§WebSocket — AgentDO streaming — token broadcast / message envelope</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Token Stream Has No Sequence Numbers — Clients Cannot Detect Dropped or Duplicate Messages</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Token streaming broadcasts { type: "token", delta, runId } with no sequence counter. If a client loses connectivity for 200 ms and reconnects, it receives a replay from the token_buffer but has no way to determine whether replayed messages overlap with ones already received. Duplicate tokens silently render twice in the UI; dropped tokens create invisible gaps in the streamed response with no way for the client to detect them.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Maintain a per-run seqId counter (auto-incrementing integer) in AgentDO state. Include seqId in every outbound message: { type: "token", delta, runId, seqId }. On reconnect the client sends its lastSeqId; the server replays only messages with seqId &gt; lastSeqId. The client detects gaps when incoming seqId !== lastSeqId + 1 and requests explicit re-sync from the server.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X15" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X15</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§WebSocket — AgentDO broadcast — ws.send / backpressure</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Broadcast Blocks on Slow Socket — One Lagging Client Stalls Token Delivery for All Others</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The token broadcast loop calls ws.send() synchronously for each connected WebSocket via getWebSockets(). If one client is on a throttled connection, its TCP send buffer fills and ws.send() blocks the Durable Object thread. While the LLM continues generating tokens, other clients stop receiving updates until the slow client drains or disconnects, potentially timing out the entire agent run.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Wrap each ws.send() in a non-blocking check: if the socket's bufferedAmount exceeds 65,536 bytes, skip that socket for the current batch and log a slow-client event. After three consecutive skips, close the socket with code 4002 and notify it to reconnect. Store unsent messages in a per-socket ring buffer (max 200 messages) so they are available on immediate reconnect.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X16" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X16</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§WebSocket — DO eviction recovery — reconnect / subrequest limits</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Reconnect Storm After DO Eviction — Simultaneous Reconnects Exhaust CF Subrequest Limit</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">When a Durable Object is evicted from memory, all connected WebSockets receive close events simultaneously and all clients attempt reconnection within the same millisecond. A space with 200 connected clients triggers 200 simultaneous DO hydration requests, each performing SQLite reads and potentially KV reads, exceeding Cloudflare's subrequest limits and returning 429 errors for the majority of clients.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Clients must reconnect with full jitter: delay = Math.random() * 10000 ms. The server sets a retry hint in the WebSocket close reason: { code: 4003, retryAfterMs: Math.floor(Math.random() * 10000) }. Cap concurrent DO instantiations per space to 5 using a KV-based semaphore so the hydration load is throttled even if all clients ignore the retry hint.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X17" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X17</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#3B82F6;background:#3B82F618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§WebSocket — Auth / DO hibernation — JWT / session token refresh</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">JWT Expires During Hibernated Long-Lived WebSocket — No Re-Auth Path for Service Bindings</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The WebSocket upgrade validates a JWT from the query string but the token is not stored in DO state. If the DO hibernates and wakes hours later (while CF Hibernation holds the WebSocket open), outgoing calls to other Workers via Service Bindings require a valid access token; the DO has no valid token to present. Authenticated context is stale; downstream Workers reject the calls silently.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Store the decoded JWT payload and its exp in SpaceDO SQLite on WebSocket accept. Define a { type: "auth_refresh", jwt: newToken } client-to-server message type that clients send proactively 30 s before token expiry. The DO validates the new token, updates stored claims in SQLite, and uses the refreshed token for all subsequent Service Binding calls.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X18" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X18</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#3B82F6;background:#3B82F618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§WebSocket — Network reliability — ping/pong / keepalive</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">No Ping/Pong Keepalive — Network Proxies Drop Idle WebSocket Connections After 60 s</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The spec does not implement WebSocket ping frames. HTTP proxies, CDNs, and mobile network gateways commonly close idle TCP connections after 60–90 seconds of inactivity. During a long agent tool execution where no tokens are streamed for 2+ minutes, intermediary proxies silently close the socket. The client is unaware until it next tries to send and discovers the connection is dead, having missed the entire tool result.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Send a WebSocket ping frame every 20 seconds from the DO: ctx.getWebSockets().forEach(ws =&gt; ws.ping()). Track last-pong timestamp per socket in DO memory. If a socket has not ponged within 30 seconds of the last ping, close it with code 4004 (keepalive timeout), log to Analytics Engine, and let clients auto-reconnect.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X19" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X19</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#3B82F6;background:#3B82F618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§WebSocket — Message framing — onMessage / frame type guard</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Binary WebSocket Frame Silently Coerced to String — Causes Spurious Client Disconnects</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The onMessage handler casts the incoming frame as string: const data = message as string; JSON.parse(data). If a client sends a binary frame (opcode 0x82), ArrayBuffer coercion produces "[object ArrayBuffer]", which throws a JSON parse error. The catch block sends a JSON error response, but some clients interpret a server-sent message during a binary send as a framing error and close the connection, causing spurious disconnects.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add an explicit type guard before parsing: if (message instanceof ArrayBuffer || message instanceof Uint8Array) { ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: "error", code: "BINARY_NOT_SUPPORTED" })); return; }. Place this check before the try/catch to prevent ArrayBuffer coercion. Document in the client SDK that only UTF-8 text frames are accepted.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X20" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X20</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#10B981;background:#10B98118;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">LOW</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§WebSocket — Protocol versioning — Sec-WebSocket-Protocol header</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">No WebSocket Subprotocol Negotiation — Clients Cannot Detect Incompatible Message Types</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The WebSocket upgrade does not negotiate a subprotocol via the Sec-WebSocket-Protocol header. When new message types are added to the wire protocol, existing clients receive unknown types they cannot handle gracefully. There is no versioned handshake; both new and old clients connect on the same endpoint with no compatibility signal, making it impossible to introduce breaking protocol changes safely.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Define named subprotocols: naelao.agent.v1 (current), naelao.agent.v2 (next). Clients include supported versions in the Upgrade request. The server selects the highest mutually supported version and responds with it in the Sec-WebSocket-Protocol header. The server sends only message types defined in the negotiated version. Increment version on any new message type.</p></div>
</div>

