    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X21</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Observability — Distributed Tracing — Service Bindings / X-Trace-Id</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">No Trace ID Propagated Across 22 Workers — Cross-Service Errors Cannot Be Correlated</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">A single user request routes through multiple Workers (naelao-api → naelao-agents → naelao-ai → naelao-knowledge). No trace ID is generated at the edge and propagated via headers (X-Trace-Id or W3C traceparent). When an error occurs in a downstream Worker there is no way to link it to the originating request; debugging requires guessing by timestamp across Worker logs in different Cloudflare accounts.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Generate a UUID trace ID at the CF edge entry point and propagate it in every Service Binding call via X-Naelao-Trace-Id. Each Worker logs { trace_id, span_id, service, duration_ms, status } to Analytics Engine. Provide an admin trace viewer: SELECT * FROM events WHERE trace_id = ? ORDER BY timestamp to reconstruct the full execution path of any request.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X22" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X22</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#3B82F6;background:#3B82F618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Observability — Logging — console.log / log schema</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">No Standard Structured Log Schema — Worker Logs Are Ad-Hoc Text Prefixes Unqueryable at Scale</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Worker logging uses ad-hoc console.log calls with text prefixes: [NAELAO], [SWEEPER], [model-fallback]. These are queryable only via substring matching in Cloudflare Workers Logs. There is no consistent JSON structure with fields like service, level, trace_id, and timestamp, making cross-Worker log aggregation and automated alerting practically impossible without expensive text parsing pipelines.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Define a log utility: log({ level, service, trace_id, event, ...context }) emitting structured JSON to stdout. All Workers import this utility instead of calling console.log directly. Require fields: level (debug|info|warn|error), service, trace_id. Provide a dashboard template for log exploration via Cloudflare Workers Analytics or an external SIEM.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X23" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
