    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X23</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#3B82F6;background:#3B82F618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Observability — Dead-Letter Queue — sweeper / DLQ retry trace</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">DLQ Retry Requeue Loses Original Failure Context — No Parent-Message Correlation</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The sweeper fetches failed messages from the dead-letter queue and requeues them via CF Queues REST API. The requeued message receives a new message ID with no reference to its original ID, failure reason, or attempt count. When the retry also fails, the second DLQ entry has no parent-message link. Operations cannot distinguish retries from new failures, making root-cause analysis for recurring failures impossible.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Enrich messages with retry metadata before requeue: { original_message_id, attempt_count, first_failure_at, last_failure_reason, dlq_ingress_at }. Log each requeue to Analytics Engine. Expose GET /admin/dlq/history?original_message_id=X returning the full retry chain. Alert when attempt_count &gt;= 3 for the same original message.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X24" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X24</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#3B82F6;background:#3B82F618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Observability — Cron Monitoring — sweeper / cron_jobs table</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Cron Job Skip Accumulation Has No SLO Threshold or Alert — Silent Starvation of Background Jobs</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">When a cron job's previous run is still active, the sweeper logs a skip and returns. No counter tracks consecutive skips. A cron job that consistently exceeds its interval (e.g., a billing reconciliation that runs 70 minutes on a 60-minute schedule) is skipped indefinitely with no alert, silently accumulating billing drift, missed cleanups, or stale state with no operational visibility.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add consecutive_skips INT and last_successful_run_at TIMESTAMP columns to the cron_jobs SQLite table. Increment on each skip; reset to 0 on successful completion. Write an Analytics Engine alert event when consecutive_skips &gt;= 3. Expose GET /admin/crons returning { jobId, lastRun, consecutiveSkips, status } for each registered job.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X25" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X25</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Observability — Skill Integrity — SkillRegistryDO / SHA256 verification</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Skill SKILL.md Hash Verified Only at Load Time — Post-Load Tampering in R2 Goes Undetected</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The skills loader computes a SHA256 hash of SKILL.md at startup and caches it. If the R2 object is subsequently overwritten via a compromised API token or insider threat, the cached skill continues executing with its original definition and the tampered version is never detected until the DO restarts or the cache expires. A tampered skill could silently exfiltrate conversation data or issue unauthorized tool calls.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Re-verify the SKILL.md SHA256 hash on each execution, not only at load. If the hash does not match the value stored in SkillRegistryDO, immediately suspend the skill, log { type: "skill_tamper_detected", skill_id, expected_hash, actual_hash } to an immutable append-only audit table, and alert the space admin. Limit hash verification cache to 5 minutes maximum.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X26" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
