    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X26</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#3B82F6;background:#3B82F618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Observability — Analytics Engine Schema — blob field positions / versioning</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Analytics Engine Blob Positions Not Versioned — Inserting a Field Silently Corrupts All Queries</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Analytics Engine events use positional arrays: blobs[0] = eventType, blobs[1] = userId, blobs[2] = agentId, etc. If a new field is inserted in the middle, all downstream queries and dashboards relying on positional indexes silently read the wrong data. There is no schema registry, migration plan, or query compatibility layer for evolving Analytics Engine event schemas across the 22 Workers.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Treat Analytics Engine blob arrays as strictly append-only: never insert a field in the middle, only append at the end. Maintain an analytics-schema.ts manifest committed to the repo documenting the exact field positions. Include schema_version (blobs[19]) in every event. On any breaking change bump the version and provide a query adapter that re-maps old field positions.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X27" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
