    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-X27</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#F97316;background:#F9731618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">HIGH</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Skills — Marketplace Security — npm integrity / SkillRegistryDO</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Community Skills Reference npm Packages Without Version Pin — Supply Chain Attack Vector</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Community skills reference npm packages without pinning to an exact version or cryptographic hash. A compromised npm account can publish a malicious patch version (e.g., 1.2.4 over 1.2.3) that is automatically pulled on next cache miss by any space using that skill. The SkillRegistryDO's SHA256 covers only the cached SKILL.md, not the npm package artifact itself, so the attack is undetected.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Require exact version strings (1.2.3, not ^1.2 or latest) in community skill manifests. Store the npm package's integrity hash from package-lock.json in SkillRegistryDO at install time. Verify the hash on each fetch. Introduce a community skill review queue: flag new versions as pending-review until a platform reviewer approves before the new version goes live to spaces.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-X28" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
