  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Mobile File Upload Path Lacks Native Camera Picker and iCloud/Google Drive Access</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The document upload UI in builder products uses a standard HTML &lt;input type="file"&gt; element. On iOS, this does not natively expose the camera roll or live camera capture with proper metadata (location, orientation correction). On Android, it lacks deep integration with Google Drive or Samsung Files. For builder products in industries where mobile-captured images are primary inputs (insurance claims with photos, healthcare with lab result pictures, real estate with property photos), the upload experience is friction-heavy and often non-functional.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Replace the raw file input with a mobile-aware upload component: (1) on mobile, show a bottom sheet with options: Camera, Photo Library, Files (iCloud/Google Drive via the Web Share Target API and File System Access API), (2) for camera capture, use the capture="environment" attribute on the input for rear camera default, (3) for images, perform client-side HEIC→JPEG conversion (heic2any library) before upload to ensure compatibility, (4) display a progress indicator with upload size and estimated time on slow connections, (5) chunk large files (&gt;10MB) using the Resumable Upload R2 multipart API for resilience on mobile connections.</p></div>
</div>
