  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Builder Canvas Has No Touch Gestures — Tablet Users Cannot Pinch-to-Zoom or Navigate by Touch</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The visual builder canvas (for configuring space layouts, agent flows, and capability connections) is designed for mouse interaction only. Tablet users (iPad, Surface) who want to build products on the go cannot pinch-to-zoom the canvas, pan with two-finger drag, or activate node operations by long-press. This severely limits the builder experience on tablets, which represent a meaningful segment of mobile-first creators and educators who are the target early builder demographic.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Add touch event handling to the builder canvas component: (1) pinch-to-zoom using the Pointer Events API (two pointer points calculating scale factor), (2) two-finger pan using pointer delta, (3) long-press (500ms) to open the context menu instead of right-click, (4) tap to select nodes, double-tap to open node settings, (5) use react-zoom-pan-pinch or similar library rather than implementing from scratch. Test on iOS Safari (WebKit) and Chrome for Android. Ensure all builder canvas keyboard shortcuts have touch equivalents documented in a "touch guide" in the builder help centre.</p></div>
</div>
