  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Platform Admin Panel Has Broken User-Ban Functionality and Cannot Perform Key Maintenance Operations</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The naelao-admin Worker has a broken user-ban endpoint (db reference error prevents execution). Beyond this, the admin panel is missing core operations: platform admins cannot view aggregated usage metrics across all builder spaces, cannot search and inspect any specific builder's space, cannot force-close a rogue agent run, cannot manually trigger the billing cycle for a specific builder, and cannot view the DLQ for failed operations. This means platform incidents require direct DO access via the Cloudflare dashboard instead of a purpose-built admin tool.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Build a comprehensive internal admin panel (restricted to Naelao staff via Cloudflare Access): (1) fix user-ban (correct the db reference, add ban audit logging), (2) space explorer (list all spaces with usage metrics, drill-down to space config, active agents, current credits), (3) agent run inspector (list active runs, force-terminate a run, view run logs), (4) manual billing operations (trigger cycle reset, issue credit grant, view ledger), (5) DLQ browser (view, replay, or discard failed messages per G-AG43), (6) platform health dashboard (error rates, queue depths, DO counts, R2 storage usage). All admin actions are logged to the compliance audit trail.</p></div>
