    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Payment / Subscriptions — Builder Product Subscription Plan Management</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">No Platform Primitive for Builders to Sell Recurring Subscription Plans to Their End-Users</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Builders who want to charge end-users a monthly or annual subscription fee for access to their product (standard SaaS model) have no platform support. There is no subscription plan definition (name, price, billing interval, feature gates), no Stripe subscription management, no billing portal for end-users to manage their plan, no proration on plan change, and no dunning for failed payments. Builders are forced to implement subscription billing from scratch in their agent instructions, which is impractical.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Implement a SubscriptionPlanDO per space: stores plan definitions (plan_id, name, price_cents, interval: "month"|"year", trial_days, feature_gates: string[]). On user subscription: create a Stripe Customer + Stripe Subscription for the end-user, store stripe_subscription_id in the user record, set plan_id and status="active". Handle Stripe subscription webhooks: invoice.payment_failed → status="past_due", customer.subscription.deleted → status="cancelled". Gate feature access in the agent by checking user.plan_id against feature_gates. Provide a Stripe-hosted billing portal link (billingPortal.sessions.create()) for users to manage their plan.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-AI42" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
