    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#3B82F6;background:#3B82F618;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Notifications — Critical Notification Delivery Confirmation</span>
  </div>
  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">No Read-Receipt or Delivery Confirmation for Critical Notifications — Platform Cannot Verify User Was Reached</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">When a billing failure notification or security alert is dispatched, the platform has no mechanism to verify whether the notification was actually delivered and read. FCM/APNs return delivery status but this is not recorded. Email opens are not tracked. In-app notifications have no read flag. If a critical alert is never seen (app uninstalled, email filtered, push disabled), the platform is unaware and does not escalate. Account suspensions can happen without the user ever being effectively notified.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Implement delivery tracking for critical notifications: (1) on FCM push: listen for the delivery receipt callback, update notifications.push_delivered_at, (2) on email: embed a 1×1 transparent tracking pixel at GET /n/{notificationId}/open that sets notifications.email_opened_at on request, (3) on in-app: mark notifications.read_at when the user opens the notification center, (4) escalation job (runs every 15 min): for critical notifications where none of the three channels has a delivery confirmation within 30 minutes, trigger the next escalation tier (G-AI29). Record the effective delivery time in Analytics Engine for SLA reporting.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-AI43" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
