  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">Service Bindings Between Workers Do Not Resolve Locally — Cross-Worker Integration Testing Requires Remote Deployment</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Cloudflare Service Bindings (env.WORKER_NAME.fetch()) are the primary inter-Worker RPC mechanism. During local development with wrangler dev, each Worker runs in an isolated local process. Bindings to other Workers attempt to reach remote production services rather than locally-running counterparts. Developers cannot test cross-Worker flows (auth → agent → billing) locally. Every test requires a staging deployment, increasing iteration time from seconds to minutes.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Use Wrangler's --config flag and workers_dev routing to simulate Service Bindings locally: define a dev.vars file mapping Service Binding names to localhost:PORT addresses for locally-running Workers. Implement a DevOrchestrator script (scripts/dev-all.sh) that starts all 22 Workers on sequential ports (3001-3022) with a shared Miniflare state directory for KV/DO persistence. Use Miniflare's serviceBindings configuration to connect Workers. Document the local development setup in the CONTRIBUTING.md with a quick-start that takes a new developer from clone to working local environment in &lt;10 minutes.</p></div>
</div>
<div id="G-AI44" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
