  <div class="box-gr" style="background:#e8f5e9;border-left:4px solid #2e7d32;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;">
    <em>Required Fix:</em> Build Naelao Builder mobile app (React Native using native SDK base AW10): core features for mobile: (1) Space health overview (traffic light per Space), (2) real-time session count and error rate push notifications (via AU08/AW34), (3) support ticket response (AU17), (4) KPI dashboard (AY08 metrics), (5) conversation review (recent sessions browsable). Out of scope for mobile: UI Builder (too complex), KB management (done on desktop). Publish to iOS App Store and Google Play. Deep linking: PagerDuty alert links open directly to affected Space in mobile app. Track mobile_dashboard_session_count and mobile_action_taken rate.
  </div>
</div>
<div id="G-AY44" style="margin-bottom:2rem;">
  <div class="box-rd" style="background:#fff3cd;border-left:4px solid #e67e22;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;margin-bottom:.5rem;">
    <strong>G-AY44 [HIGH] — Proactive Space Health Recommendations</strong><br>
    <em>The Gap:</em> Builders receive alerts when something is wrong (error rate spike, quota exhaustion) but get no proactive recommendations for improving their Space's performance, quality, or reliability before problems occur. Naelao platform intelligence is underutilized for builder success.
  </div>
  <div class="box-gr" style="background:#e8f5e9;border-left:4px solid #2e7d32;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;">
    <em>Required Fix:</em> Implement HealthAdvisorDO: weekly analysis of each Space's metrics, producing ranked recommendations: (1) "Your KB has 15 docs older than 1 year that are frequently retrieved — consider refreshing them" (AW16), (2) "Your P95 TTFT is 2.3s — enable cross-encoder re-ranking (AV37) to improve retrieval relevance and reduce unnecessary LLM calls", (3) "15% of end-users abandon after first message — try adding conversation starters (AY20)", (4) "Your Space has 3 KB docs with &gt;60% thumbs-down retrieval — remove or revise them (AV49)." Recommendations delivered via in-dashboard notification (AV21) and weekly email digest. Track recommendation_acted_on rate as engagement metric.
  </div>
</div>
<div id="G-AY45" style="margin-bottom:2rem;">
  <div class="box-rd" style="background:#fff3cd;border-left:4px solid #e67e22;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;margin-bottom:.5rem;">
    <strong>G-AY45 [HIGH] — Platform Fraud Detection for Abuse Prevention</strong><br>
    <em>The Gap:</em> Naelao faces risk from platform abuse: API key sharing (one builder key used by hundreds of users), token farming (builders creating Spaces purely to consume AI tokens then resell access), and credit card fraud (stolen cards used to purchase plans, then abuse AI compute before chargeback).
  </div>
  <div class="box-gr" style="background:#e8f5e9;border-left:4px solid #2e7d32;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;">
    <em>Required Fix:</em> Implement FraudDetectionDO: monitor behavioral signals: (1) API key sharing: requests from &gt;50 unique IPs in 24h per API key → flag SUSPICIOUS, require MFA re-auth to continue. (2) Token farming: token_consumption_rate / active_sessions &gt; 10× platform average → flag for manual review. (3) New account + immediately high AI usage + high churn risk score → hold credits for 48h verification period. (4) Card fraud: billing velocity checks via Stripe Radar integration + custom rules (VPN IP + new card + trial + high usage). On fraud detection: suspend account, email with appeal link. Track fraud_detected, fraud_confirmed (post-review), false_positive_rate monthly.
  </div>
</div>
<div id="G-AY46" style="margin-bottom:2rem;">
  <div class="box-rd" style="background:#d1ecf1;border-left:4px solid #2980b9;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;margin-bottom:.5rem;">
