</div>
<div id="G-AZ43" style="margin-bottom:2rem;">
  <div class="box-rd" style="background:#f8d7da;border-left:4px solid #c0392b;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;margin-bottom:.5rem;">
    <strong>G-AZ43 [CRITICAL] — Output Content Safety Filter</strong><br>
    <em>The Gap:</em> LLMs can generate harmful outputs despite safety training, especially when given adversarial inputs. No output safety filter validates agent responses before delivery to end-users.
  </div>
  <div class="box-gr" style="background:#e8f5e9;border-left:4px solid #2e7d32;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;">
    <em>Required Fix:</em> Implement output safety layer: post-LLM, pre-response: (1) run output through moderation check (async, &lt;100ms), (2) check for PII leakage (regex: SSN, credit card patterns), (3) check for prompt injection echo (response contains system prompt fragments). BLOCKED responses: substitute safe fallback message, alert builder, log output_blocked_event. Track output_block_rate; spikes indicate adversarial attacks requiring investigation.
  </div>
</div>
<div id="G-AZ44" style="margin-bottom:2rem;">
  <div class="box-rd" style="background:#d1ecf1;border-left:4px solid #2980b9;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;margin-bottom:.5rem;">
    <strong>G-AZ44 [MEDIUM] — User Reputation and Trust Scoring</strong><br>
