<div id="G-BA45" style="margin-bottom:2rem;">
  <div class="box-rd" style="background:#fff3cd;border-left:4px solid #e67e22;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;margin-bottom:.5rem;">
    <strong>G-BA45 [HIGH] — Developer Debug Mode for Spaces</strong><br>
    <em>The Gap:</em> When a Space behaves unexpectedly, builders have no debug mode to inspect internal agent reasoning, tool call inputs/outputs, KB retrieval chunks, and token usage in real-time. Debugging requires log analysis — slow and indirect.
  </div>
  <div class="box-gr" style="background:#e8f5e9;border-left:4px solid #2e7d32;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;">
    <em>Required Fix:</em> Implement debug mode: builder enables debug_mode per Space (not in production by default). In debug mode: agent responses include debug_context field: {reasoning_steps, tool_calls:[{name, input, output, latency_ms}], kb_chunks:[{id, content_preview, score}], token_usage:{prompt, completion, cached}, total_latency_ms}. Builder dashboard Debug tab shows expandable trace per conversation turn. Auto-disable after 1h or 1000 requests. Debug data stored 24h.
