</div>
<div id="G-BA46" style="margin-bottom:2rem;">
  <div class="box-rd" style="background:#d1ecf1;border-left:4px solid #2980b9;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;margin-bottom:.5rem;">
    <strong>G-BA46 [MEDIUM] — Request Replay and Time-Travel Debugging</strong><br>
    <em>The Gap:</em> When a production bug is reported, engineers cannot replay the exact request that triggered it. Request payloads are not persisted, making reproduction difficult especially for non-deterministic LLM responses.
  </div>
  <div class="box-gr" style="background:#e8f5e9;border-left:4px solid #2e7d32;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;">
    <em>Required Fix:</em> Implement request capture for debug sessions: when debug_mode=true or sampled at 1% in production, persist full request payload (headers, body) to R2 with 7-day TTL. Engineers can replay request via internal API: POST /debug/replay/{request_id} — exactly reproduces original request with same inputs. Compare replayed response to original. Track replay_utility (replays that led to bug fix) to justify storage cost.
  </div>
</div>
<div id="G-BA47" style="margin-bottom:2rem;">
  <div class="box-rd" style="background:#d1ecf1;border-left:4px solid #2980b9;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;margin-bottom:.5rem;">
    <strong>G-BA47 [MEDIUM] — Error Fingerprinting and Deduplication</strong><br>
    <em>The Gap:</em> Error logging captures many error events but no fingerprinting deduplicates similar errors. An LLM timeout affecting 10,000 users generates 10,000 individual error events — obscuring signal in noise.
  </div>
  <div class="box-gr" style="background:#e8f5e9;border-left:4px solid #2e7d32;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;">
    <em>Required Fix:</em> Implement error fingerprinting: extract error signature = hash(error_type + stack_frame_top3 + endpoint). Group errors by fingerprint in Analytics Engine. Dashboard shows: unique_error_types, occurrence_count_per_fingerprint, first_seen, last_seen, affected_users. New error fingerprint not seen before triggers higher-priority alert. Resolved fingerprint tracked: reopen if recurs within 7 days. Track error_fingerprint_count and mean_time_between_recurrences.
  </div>
</div>
<div id="G-BA48" style="margin-bottom:2rem;">
  <div class="box-rd" style="background:#d1ecf1;border-left:4px solid #2980b9;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;margin-bottom:.5rem;">
    <strong>G-BA48 [MEDIUM] — Distributed Context Propagation (Baggage)</strong><br>
    <em>The Gap:</em> Distributed traces (AZ29) correlate spans but context baggage (tenant_id, space_id, session_id, experiment_variant) is not propagated through all async hops: CF Queues messages, CF Workflows steps, and sub-requests from Workers.
  </div>
  <div class="box-gr" style="background:#e8f5e9;border-left:4px solid #2e7d32;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;">
    <em>Required Fix:</em> Implement W3C Baggage propagation: routing Worker sets baggage header (tenant_id, space_id, session_id, trace_id). All downstream Workers extract and re-propagate baggage. CF Queue messages include baggage JSON in metadata field. CF Workflow steps receive baggage as step input. Sub-requests (fetch calls within Workers) include propagated headers. Analytics Engine events include all baggage fields. Enables full cross-hop correlation for any request.
  </div>
</div>
<div id="G-BA49" style="margin-bottom:2rem;">
  <div class="box-rd" style="background:#fff3cd;border-left:4px solid #e67e22;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;margin-bottom:.5rem;">
    <strong>G-BA49 [HIGH] — Platform Governance and Policy Engine</strong><br>
    <em>The Gap:</em> As the platform scales to millions of Spaces, manual policy enforcement (ToS violations, content policy, usage policy) becomes impossible. No automated policy engine detects and enforces platform policies at scale.
  </div>
  <div class="box-gr" style="background:#e8f5e9;border-left:4px solid #2e7d32;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;">
    <em>Required Fix:</em> Build policy engine: policy rules defined as code (OPA — Open Policy Agent): {rule_id, condition_query, action, severity}. Evaluated at: (1) SpaceType publish (content policy check), (2) Session start (builder account in good standing?), (3) Periodic background audit (active Spaces comply with current policies). Policy violations: automated actions (warn, suspend, terminate) based on severity. Appeal process: builder disputes via ticket, human review within 48h. Track policy_violation_rate by category.
  </div>
</div>
<div id="G-BA50" style="margin-bottom:2rem;">
  <div class="box-rd" style="background:#fff3cd;border-left:4px solid #e67e22;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;margin-bottom:.5rem;">
    <strong>G-BA50 [HIGH] — Platform Health Score and Executive Dashboard</strong><br>
    <em>The Gap:</em> Platform leadership has no unified health score aggregating the most important platform metrics into a single executive view. Individual metric dashboards exist but no single "platform is healthy / degraded / critical" signal.
  </div>
  <div class="box-gr" style="background:#e8f5e9;border-left:4px solid #2e7d32;padding:1rem;border-radius:6px;">
    <em>Required Fix:</em> Build executive health dashboard: compute platform_health_score (0-100) from weighted signals: (1) p99_latency_ok (weight 20), (2) error_rate_ok (weight 20), (3) billing_processing_ok (weight 15), (4) LLM_provider_ok (weight 15), (5) active_sessions_vs_target (weight 10), (6) synthetic_monitor_ok (weight 10), (7) security_alerts_zero (weight 10). Score &lt; 80: DEGRADED, &lt; 60: CRITICAL. Weekly executive email: health score trend, top 3 risks, top 3 positive signals.
