  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The architecture includes an `mcp-hub` worker for Model Context Protocol tool integration. Without it, agents can only use built-in tools (http_get, calculate, search_web). Builders cannot extend their Spaces with external MCP tool servers (Slack, GitHub, Salesforce, etc.).</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Implement the MCP hub worker: it maintains a registry of configured MCP servers per Space (stored in D1: `mcp_servers (space_id, name, url, auth_config_encrypted)`). The agent runtime discovers available MCP tools by calling `env.MCP_HUB.fetch('/spaces/{spaceId}/tools')`. Tool calls are proxied through the MCP hub, which handles authentication and response normalisation.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-I18" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
  <div style="display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:6px;">
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--or);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;">G-I18</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#EAB308;background:#EAB30818;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;letter-spacing:.08em;">MEDIUM</span>
    <span style="font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;color:#64748B;letter-spacing:.06em;">§Integration — SpaceDO — DO upgrade</span>
