  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">No Threads Worker — Long-Running Multi-Turn Conversations Cannot Be Managed</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">The architecture includes a `threads` worker for managing conversation threads (collections of sessions that form a coherent long-running interaction). Without it, each session is isolated and cannot be linked to prior sessions for the same end-user.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Implement the threads worker: a thread is a sequence of sessions for the same `{space_id, end_user_id}` pair. `POST /v1/spaces/:spaceId/threads` creates a thread. Sessions are created within a thread context. The LLM gateway uses the thread's session history to provide continuity. Thread summaries are generated by the LLM when the context approaches the token limit.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-I21" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
