  <h3 style="font-family:'Fraunces',serif;font-size:22px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hd);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 18px;">No Credentials Worker — External Service Credentials Cannot Be Stored Securely per Space</h3>
  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Builders who configure their Spaces with external tool integrations (Salesforce, Jira, Slack) need to store API credentials. There is no secure credential storage per Space/SpaceType. Credentials cannot be stored in the SpaceType manifest (shared across Spaces) or in plain D1.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Implement the credentials worker: `POST /v1/spaces/:spaceId/credentials` stores a named credential (encrypted with the Space's DEK). `GET /v1/spaces/:spaceId/credentials` returns credential names (not values). The agent runtime calls the credentials worker at tool dispatch time to fetch the plaintext credential in memory (never logged). Credentials are scoped to Space, not shared across Spaces.</p></div>
</div>

<div id="G-I24" style="margin:40px 0 0;padding:28px 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--brd);">
