  <div class="box box-rd"><div class="box-lbl">The Gap</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Workers publish to queues and consume from queues, but message formats are ad-hoc per worker. A billing message and an analytics message might have different structures for the same logical event (e.g. `session_end`), causing the analytics consumer to silently drop events it can't parse.</p></div>
  <div class="box box-gr"><div class="box-lbl">Required Fix</div><p style="white-space:pre-wrap;">Create `packages/types/src/queue-messages.ts` with typed interfaces for every queue message type: `AnalyticsEvent`, `BillingUsageEvent`, `WebhookDeliveryEvent`, `KbIngestionEvent`. All workers import from this package. The queue consumer uses discriminated unions on the `type` field to route messages. Add JSON Schema validation on consume.</p></div>
